window.COURSES=[{"day":1,"title":"英语积累Day 1","topic":"数码产品","author":"Daiz","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/2c88882b3d534a2daae810c014f4c7f0","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/o-Bcl93OnU0?si=Zs7PMNaq6bSbnBVz","audioSize":"242.7KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-001.m4a","youtubeId":"o-Bcl93OnU0","chinese":"好多小伙伴都询问我对它们 (AirPods Max) 的真实评价，我超喜欢它能跟我的各种穿搭完美搭配，感觉整个造型都更加出彩！AirPods Max从来没出现过电量耗尽的情况。如果你一直在攒钱准备入手，我觉得还是值得的。不过，我不认为这是非得破费购买的东西。","english":"A lot of you guys have been asking me for like an honest review on them my AirPods Max. I love how it goes with all of my outfits and it just kind of upgrades your outfits. My AirPods Max have never died on me. If you've been saving up for it, I say go for it. But I don't think this is something you really need to go out of your budget for.","sentences":["A lot of you guys have been asking me for like an honest review on them my AirPods Max.","I love how it goes with all of my outfits and it just kind of upgrades your outfits.","My AirPods Max have never died on me.","If you've been saving up for it, I say go for it.","But I don't think this is something you really need to go out of your budget for."],"exercise":"A lot of you guys have been asking me for like 真实评价 on them my AirPods Max. I love how it 完美搭配 and it just kind of （更）出彩 your outfits. My AirPods Max have never 出现过电量耗尽的情况. If you've been 攒钱 I say 入手 it. But I don't think this is something you really need to 破费购买.","vocabulary":[{"id":"b6b281ee-381c-42b7-8e7a-d2e02a4e506f","english":"review","ipa":"/rɪˈvjuː/","chinese":"n. 评论，评价","usage":"The book received a favorable review. 这本书赢得了好评。"},{"id":"a2ca67a6-ed15-46b1-89d8-60a001e81e22","english":"outfit","ipa":"/ˈaʊtfɪt/","chinese":"n. 全套服装","usage":"wore a slinky outfit to the party. 穿了一件时髦的外衣去参加聚会"},{"id":"3fd0eed1-2997-469f-85df-cbe1c2553959","english":"die on sb","ipa":"","chinese":"在某人使用过程中突然失效或停止工作","usage":"My car just died on me. 我的汽车开着开着就坏了。"},{"id":"083e6730-c061-46c0-b6a3-5254393bad17","english":"save up for","ipa":"","chinese":"存钱，攒钱","usage":"Howard, you know we're saving up for a house. \nHoward，我们在存钱买房呢。"},{"id":"e8766db0-a0d5-4311-8bc8-a32df1128bf5","english":"budget","ipa":"/ˈbʌdʒɪt/","chinese":"n. 预算","usage":"Our budget has been pared to the bone. 我们的预算额已削减到最低限度。"}]},{"day":2,"title":"英语积累Day 2","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Daiz","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/9d408b94968b4a70a18b1708170e361b","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/GpieaXJ4f5s?si=co8IS8znMAdIZ7V-","audioSize":"340.0KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-002.m4a","youtubeId":"GpieaXJ4f5s","chinese":"首先，我会使用一款非常温和舒缓的爽肤水，因为我是重度敏感肌。我超爱精华液，感觉就像是一瓶浓缩维生素。这款 the Ordinary品牌的酸有助于痘肌，但我发现它对于已经冒出来的痘痘并没有太大帮助，更多地是预防长痘。它能让肤色更加均匀。","english":"First, going with the toner that's really mild and calming because I have pretty sensitive skin. I love serums. I feel like it's the perfect condensed vitamins. It’s like acid from the Ordinary and it helps with acne-prone skin but I realize that it doesn't really help with like active acne. It's more for pre-breakouts. This just evens out your skin tone so nicely.","sentences":["First, going with the toner that's really mild and calming because I have pretty sensitive skin.","I love serums.","I feel like it's the perfect condensed vitamins.","It’s like acid from the Ordinary and it helps with acne-prone skin but I realize that it doesn't really help with like active acne.","It's more for pre-breakouts.","This just evens out your skin tone so nicely."],"exercise":"First, going with the 爽肤水 that's really 温和舒缓 because I 重度敏感肌. I love 精华液. I feel like it's the perfect 浓缩维生素. It’s like 酸 from the Ordinary and it helps with 痘肌 but I realize that it doesn't really help with like 已经冒出来的痘痘. It's more for 预防长痘. This just 让肤色更加均匀.","vocabulary":[{"id":"a5151f68-3043-4c14-8827-6419b42ec8cd","english":"toner","ipa":"/'təunə/","chinese":"n. 爽肤水","usage":"And after I wash it, I put on toner, and then essence, and moisturizer.洗完后，先涂上爽肤水，再涂精华液和保湿霜。"},{"id":"f1fcedfb-9f87-4878-b2c2-1d5be7d743ef","english":"serum","ipa":"/'sɪərəm/","chinese":"n. 精华液；浆液；血清","usage":""},{"id":"560eb983-b915-40f4-b048-38eed4cc0565","english":"condense","ipa":"/kənˈdens/","chinese":"v. 浓缩","usage":"1. condensed soup. 浓汤。\n2. a condensed account of an event对某事件的简要叙述\n3. I have condensed my report. 我已缩短了我的报告。"},{"id":"766921d5-21bf-4b48-80bc-e5fe902b029b","english":"acid","ipa":"/ˈæsɪd/","chinese":"酸类（护肤品）","usage":"They're soaked with my stomach acid. 都泡在我的胃酸里了。"},{"id":"8eb1dbc4-3c9f-4b0e-b1a0-fcae2c46e322","english":"acne","ipa":"/'æknɪ/","chinese":"n. 痤疮，粉刺，痘痘","usage":"Acne is very common among teenagers. 粉刺在青少年中间很常见。"},{"id":"0fec4ac7-bd1d-421b-8462-18a7411f2d4d","english":"prone (to)","ipa":"/prəʊn/","chinese":"a. 易于遭受；有（坏事）的倾向","usage":"Some of those were prone to catching fire. 有些产品还易于起火。"},{"id":"c3666e1f-732a-4a9f-8e2f-ad255f962b0d","english":"acne-prone skin","ipa":"","chinese":"痤疮易发肌","usage":"Suitable for all skin types, acne-prone skin and sensitive skin. 适合所有皮肤类型，易痤疮皮肤和敏感肌肤。"},{"id":"f5a69fa7-28ee-47dd-a934-c97a2faa5196","english":"even out","ipa":"","chinese":"使均衡；使肤色均匀","usage":"My energy levels are starting to even out. 我的能量水平开始平衡了。"},{"id":"50755cfd-dea0-435e-b6ed-6c648751433a","english":"skin tone","ipa":"","chinese":"肤色","usage":""}]},{"day":3,"title":"英语积累Day 3","topic":"生活方式","author":"Sydney Serena","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/5864b78988c24ab28c77e818fa0fb6d9","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/bcfCeRXXrgY?si=j5jThdbi6JbD04Ao","audioSize":"326.2KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-003.m4a","youtubeId":"bcfCeRXXrgY","chinese":"我真正记得这本书的唯一原因就是它的封面太鲜亮了。它主要讲了如何在二三十岁的青年时期掌控人生。我有点想加入读书俱乐部或者类似的组织，因为我感觉这样我才能保持阅读习惯。上次我和朋友一起参加的读书俱乐部终止了，因为我拖后腿，无法按时读完书。","english":"Now only reason I really remember it (this book) is just because it's so like bright and neon. It's basically about navigating life in your young 20s and 30s. I want to join a book club or something because I feel like that's how I like stay on top of reading. The last book club I was in with my friend ended because I was the weak link. I didn't do my readings on time.","sentences":["Now only reason I really remember it (this book) is just because it's so like bright and neon.","It's basically about navigating life in your young 20s and 30s.","I want to join a book club or something because I feel like that's how I like stay on top of reading.","The last book club I was in with my friend ended because I was the weak link.","I didn't do my readings on time."],"exercise":"Now only reason I really remember it (this book) is just because it's so like 鲜亮. It's basically about 掌控人生 in your young 二三十岁. I want to join a book club or something because I feel that's how I like 保持阅读习惯. The last book club I was in with my friend ended because I 拖后腿. I didn't do my readings on time.","vocabulary":[{"id":"b20e9994-1a67-48ae-94b1-90ecbf54fba8","english":"neon","ipa":"/'niːɒn/","chinese":"a. 霓虹的","usage":"neon light  霓虹灯"},{"id":"06c25f5e-15cc-4227-b589-273cd27029fa","english":"navigate","ipa":"/ˈnævɪɡeɪt/","chinese":"v. 航行；驾驶，操纵","usage":"navigate sth 找到正确方法（对付困难复杂的情况）"},{"id":"b388a6c2-1a3f-4980-a4b1-ee42f99666c9","english":"stay on top of sth","ipa":"","chinese":"掌控，驾驭","usage":""},{"id":"9dc91415-7443-496e-ac8e-b31552589340","english":"weak link","ipa":"","chinese":"薄弱环节","usage":"I'm the weak link of this super group. 我是这个超级组合里的薄弱环节。"}]},{"day":4,"title":"英语积累Day 4","topic":"生活方式","author":"Sydney Serena","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/b91d2261f5ec48e4be0f1175bc7c3592","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/LeqjcafMu9o?si=ZfeC1qHWUzaINJDa","audioSize":"256.7KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-004.m4a","youtubeId":"LeqjcafMu9o","chinese":"睡到中午才起床会让我的一天从一开始就偏离正轨。当我早上坐在这块户外草坪时，我喜欢写手帐来代替刷手机。所以我有一本MADHAPPY品牌手账本，每天都会有不同的提示问题，另外它还有每日心情记录板块。","english":"(Getting up at noon) really makes me feel like sets my day off on the wrong foot. When I’m out here in the mornings, I also like to journal kind of as a replacement of going on my phone. So I have this MADHAPPY journal. So each day has a little bit of a different prompt. And it also has like little mood check-ins for each day.","sentences":["(Getting up at noon) really makes me feel like sets my day off on the wrong foot.","When I’m out here in the mornings, I also like to journal kind of as a replacement of going on my phone.","So I have this MADHAPPY journal.","So each day has a little bit of a different prompt.","And it also has like little mood check-ins for each day."],"exercise":"(Getting up at noon) really makes me feel like 一天从一开始就偏离正轨. When I’m out here in the mornings, I also like to 写手帐 kind of as a replacement of 刷手机. So I have this MADHAPPY journal. So each day has a little bit of a different 提示问题. And it also has like little每日心情记录板块.","vocabulary":[{"id":"2ef22b97-0b29-4595-b78d-2f05d4777afe","english":"set off","ipa":"","chinese":"出发，启程","usage":"set my day off 开启我的一天"},{"id":"fbf3455d-c2ff-42f0-8801-0194bbe7f7ed","english":"(start) on the wrong foot","ipa":"","chinese":"一开始就不顺利","usage":""},{"id":"1e993f47-4838-4cb4-b40f-0e8e105d9a53","english":"journal","ipa":"","chinese":"v. 记日记，写手帐","usage":"Try keeping a journal for one week.\n各位也可以尝试，用一个星期时间记录日志。"},{"id":"d6bb314c-826c-4e2d-b617-4904961dd1b3","english":"going on my phone","ipa":"","chinese":"刷手机","usage":""},{"id":"e52e5e6e-5ccf-476d-96c5-a98340cf911e","english":"prompt","ipa":"/ prɑːmpt /","chinese":"n. 提示 \nv. 提示，鼓励，促使","usage":"Will you prompt for us at the performance? 演出时你给我们提示台词好吗?"},{"id":"0812471d-272e-442e-a572-0a6b8fde20e4","english":"check-in","ipa":"","chinese":"登记（酒店入住）；检票","usage":"She checked in at the hotel yesterday. 她昨天在旅馆登记住宿。"}]},{"day":5,"title":"英语积累Day 5","topic":"日常,生活方式","author":"Sydney Serena","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/c680bb5fb23647738a50797e78d02176","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/kpEh8Y-Xffo?si=FnsZYwstM1BecbGg","audioSize":"242.0KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-005.m4a","youtubeId":"kpEh8Y-Xffo","chinese":"我应该给大家描述一下我的一天。最近几天，我的生活一直停滞不前，而且我有些逃避现实。有时候会觉得没有动力去做事情。唯一能让我从这种情绪中振作起来的方法就是强迫自己去做事情。今天的日程安排中，我必须办几件事。","english":"I should give you guys a little rundown of my day. I've kind of been in a rut the past few days and I get like really in funk. Sometimes I just feel really unmotivated to do things. The only way for me to really get out of it is to force myself into doing things. So on today's agenda I have to run a few errands.","sentences":["I should give you guys a little rundown of my day.","I've kind of been in a rut the past few days and I get like really in funk.","Sometimes I just feel really unmotivated to do things.","The only way for me to really get out of it is to force myself into doing things.","So on today's agenda I have to run a few errands."],"exercise":"I should give you guys 描述 of my day. I've kind of been 停滞不前 the past few days and I get like really 逃避现实. Sometimes I just feel really 没有动力to do things. The only way for me to get out of it is to force myself into doing things. So on today's 日程安排 I have to 办几件事.","vocabulary":[{"id":"00e2006b-0e1f-469b-a31b-57e4706711d9","english":"rundown","ipa":"/'rʌndaun/","chinese":"n. 裁减,纲要","usage":"1. n. ~ on/of sth 解释；描述\n2. n. ~ in/of sth（尤指商业）削减，紧缩\n3. run-down a.（建筑或地方）破败的；（商业）衰败/不景气的"},{"id":"83ac9a1d-38a9-48a1-99f2-890a9846f8d8","english":"rut","ipa":"/rʌt/","chinese":"n. 惯例；凹槽\nvt. 挖槽于；在…形成车辙","usage":"(stuck) in a rut 一成不变；停滞不前"},{"id":"b524f296-1bdc-4988-9c5f-044134db54a4","english":"funk","ipa":"/fʌŋk/","chinese":"n. (尤因处于无法控制的情形中而出现的)恐慌\nv. funk sth （因害怕而）逃避","usage":"1. And I will fall into an existential funk.\n我会陷入一种存在主义的恐惧。\n2. I could have seen him this morning but I funked it. 今天早晨我本可见到他的，但我躲开了。"},{"id":"c5935437-74dc-408b-a7c7-71b23d8f0334","english":"unmotivated","ipa":"/ʌnˈməʊtɪveɪtɪd/","chinese":"a.（对工作或学习）缺乏动机的，不感兴趣的","usage":"What if you end up overworked and unmotivated? 如果你最后疲于应付而缺乏动力怎么办?"},{"id":"84629e3c-ec9d-4828-95ec-133da8b7ad49","english":"force","ipa":"/ fɔːs /","chinese":"n. 暴力，武力；力，力量；自然力；（有某目的）一群人；有影响力的人（或事）；影响力；武装部队；警察部门；风力\nv. 强迫；用力推；使发生；勉强做出","usage":"force somebody into doing sth 强迫某人做"},{"id":"bc39adbd-42bc-4339-9214-01c0ba6337a1","english":"agenda","ipa":"/əˈdʒendə/","chinese":"n. 日程安排；会议议程","usage":"I move that we adopt the agenda as it stands. 我提议不作改变通过这个议程。"},{"id":"35e747f0-7158-4769-ae5e-2e6efb24d3b8","english":"errand","ipa":"/ˈerənd/","chinese":"n. 差事；使命","usage":"run an errand 办理差事"}]},{"day":6,"title":"英语积累Day 6","topic":"生活方式","author":"Sydney Serena","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/2afd1c8ef9474bda959217661e713e07","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/tbc2hP_fRXA?si=tdh0POQ0HLsdxrj2","audioSize":"309.5KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-006.m4a","youtubeId":"tbc2hP_fRXA","chinese":"我住在一间单身公寓，东西很容易变得凌乱，所以需要经常整理我的物品。我会断舍离，并保持物品整洁，否则就会感觉房间像一片废墟。这种情况有利有弊，因为它迫使我保持超出寻常的整洁。目前我的公寓相当干净，但我计划进行一些深度清洁。","english":"I live in a studio things get messy quickly and I really need to kind of constantly just go through a lot of my things. Toss old things, donate old things and just keep things decluttered or it just feels like a wreck. So It's kind of a blessing and a curse. It does force me to be extra clean. Right now actually my apartment is like fairly clean but I'm just gonna do some deep cleaning.","sentences":["I live in a studio things get messy quickly and I really need to kind of constantly just go through a lot of my things.","Toss old things, donate old things and just keep things decluttered or it just feels like a wreck.","So It's kind of a blessing and a curse.","It does force me to be extra clean.","Right now actually my apartment is like fairly clean but I'm just gonna do some deep cleaning."],"exercise":"I live in a 单身公寓 things get 凌乱 quickly and I need to kind of constantly just 整理 a lot of my things. I 断舍离, donate old things and just 保持 things 整洁 or it just feels like a 废墟. It's kind of 有利有弊. It does force me to be extra clean. Right now actually my apartment is like 相当 clean but I'm just gonna do some deep cleaning.","vocabulary":[{"id":"d0f7acd4-d5b6-45b1-ad21-110272310214","english":"studio","ipa":"/ ˈstjuːdiəʊ /","chinese":"「作为一种房型」\n通常是一种单间公寓。这种房屋布局将起居区、睡眠区和厨房通常都放在一个房间内，没有明确的分隔，通常适合单身或者少数人居住。","usage":""},{"id":"9fceed18-6f95-4748-a1be-cd9bb99cdd76","english":"messy","ipa":"/ˈmɛsi/","chinese":"a. 凌乱的，杂乱无章的","usage":"They straighten up messy areas of their homes.\n他们会把家里脏乱的地方收拾干净。"},{"id":"7f0b9947-36fc-4af3-91db-ce2aac77d2b2","english":"go through","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 检查、清理或整理杂物或个人物品\n2. 浏览；检查；审阅\n3. 经历；经受\n4. 消耗；使用完","usage":"1. 检查、清理或整理杂物或个人物品\n🌰Example: I need to go through things in my closet and donate what I don't need anymore. 我需要整理一下衣柜里的东西，把不需要的捐掉。\n2. 浏览；检查；审阅\n🌰Example: I need to go through these documents before the meeting. 我需要在会议之前检查这些文件。\n3. 经历；经受\n🌰Example: She went through a difficult time after her father passed away.在父亲去世后，她经历了一段困难时期。\n4. 消耗；使用完\n🌰Example: We went through three bottles of water during the hike.在徒步旅行中，我们用掉了三瓶水。"},{"id":"f1a97e7f-f527-496d-be3e-266c26e7684a","english":"toss","ipa":"/tɒs","chinese":"v. 扔，抛弃；掷（硬币）","usage":"They tossed the ball to each other. 他们把球互相扔来扔去。"},{"id":"06de7afb-c491-4536-b63f-02a683a0827b","english":"declutter","ipa":"/diːˈklʌtər/","chinese":"v. 整理，清理，去除杂物","usage":"Here are four easy tips to help you actually declutter your home. 这里有四个简单的诀窍可以帮助你有效的整理自己的家。"},{"id":"7f5b2930-4b83-4ab0-89a5-f2157cfc312f","english":"wreck","ipa":"/rɛk/","chinese":"n. 残骸；废墟；损坏或破坏状态","usage":"1. You can even check yourself before you wreck yourself. 你甚至可以在你搞砸之前先自我检查。\n2. My job's a train wreck right now, and, yes, I admit it. 我的工作现在简直一团糟，而且，是，我承认。"},{"id":"529592fa-69a4-4cd1-a7c9-a17892616b56","english":"blessing and curse","ipa":"","chinese":"直译为“祝福与诅咒”，指一种情况或事物既有好的方面，也有坏的方面。","usage":""}]},{"day":7,"title":"英语积累Day 7","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Sydney Serena","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/0e2b9c173cd14c03974a62e4800dd427","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/Z2_YXRPmkD8?si=lNMHuhIPQ3ambJJx","audioSize":"284.4KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-007.m4a","youtubeId":"Z2_YXRPmkD8","chinese":"我想开箱分享一下Skims品牌寄来的剩余部分衣物。第一件是他们Fits Everyone系列的方领紧身连体衣。当我第一次试穿的时候，简直被它的舒适度惊呆了！它完美贴合了我的身形，尤其是腰部位置。而且我超爱后背的低U型设计，简直太衬托身材了！","english":"I want to do a little haul of the rest of the Skims pieces that they sent me. The first one is their Fits Everyone square neck bodysuit. When I first tried this on, I was shocked at how comfortable it was. It hugs you in the right places, especially in the waist. And I love the lower back — how it scoops in the back. It's super flattering.","sentences":["I want to do a little haul of the rest of the Skims pieces that they sent me.","The first one is their Fits Everyone square neck bodysuit.","When I first tried this on, I was shocked at how comfortable it was.","It hugs you in the right places, especially in the waist.","And I love the lower back — how it scoops in the back.","It's super flattering."],"exercise":"I want to 开箱分享 of the rest of the Skims 衣物 that they sent me. The first one is their Fits Everyone 方领紧身连体衣. When I first tried this on, I was shocked at how comfortable it was. 它完美贴合了我的身形, especially in the waist. And I love后背的低U型设计. It's super 衬托身材.","vocabulary":[{"id":"3ab42fe9-1df8-4f0b-be3d-ecae4a57d089","english":"haul","ipa":"/hɔːl/","chinese":"v. (用力地) 拉，拖；（用运载工具）运送，运输 \nn. 拖，拉；大批赃物；一网的捕鱼量","usage":"1. do a haul 开箱\n2. a haul of  一大批，指一次性获得或收集到的大量物品或信息\n3. shopping haul 购物开箱"},{"id":"e4064762-4986-4e77-9793-cb5704e378c4","english":"piece","ipa":"","chinese":"n. 块;部分;片;部件;一件，一篇，一首，一支;（尤指一套中的）一件，一台;条;段;碎片;零件;文章，报道","usage":"1. a piece of 一片，一块；\n2. piece by piece 逐渐地；\n3. piece of cake 轻而易举的事情；轻松愉快的事"},{"id":"accf8c46-a16c-471c-a193-7186f586666b","english":"square neck","ipa":"/skweə(r)/ \n/nek/","chinese":"方领","usage":""},{"id":"1cd17e21-c403-4d28-9566-3f00a066c20e","english":"scoop","ipa":"/skuːp/","chinese":"vt. 用铲[勺]等挖(洞等)\na. (衣领)汤匙式的，大圆领的","usage":"scoop with a small shovel\n用一把小铲子挖"},{"id":"a884f6fa-f459-4102-874b-49ff58c0ead3","english":"flattering","ipa":"/'flætəriŋ/","chinese":"a. 使人显得更漂亮的，衬托人的；奉承的","usage":"the article began with some flattering words about us.\n文章开头是一些对我们的溢美之词。"}]},{"day":8,"title":"英语积累Day 8","topic":"食物","author":"Sydney Serena","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/af5c3682735344eea568a26a414a205a","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/XVKzwSYvLGA?si=xK32Hd5T-a3G_SvR","audioSize":"343.3KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-008.m4a","youtubeId":"XVKzwSYvLGA","chinese":"我们现在要去一个叫做Denbro的地方，它是一家得来速（咖啡店）。哇，回到家乡，看到这么多新店，感觉自己仿佛与这些变化脱节了。好像我错过了很多重要的经历，就像错过了一切。他们不小心给了我两杯饮料，我现在感觉自己像个美食评论家。这杯是薄荷拿铁饮料，我能欣赏它独特的风味。它真的很不错，实际上超出了我的预期。","english":"We‘re gonna go to this place called Denbro, and it’s a drive-thru (coffee shop). Wow I feel so out of touch going back to hometown and seeing all these new stores. Like I feel like I missed many chapters, I missed everything. They accidentally gave me two drinks. I feel like a food reviewer now. So this one is the peppermint latte drink. I can get behind this. This is really really good it actually exceeded my expectations.","sentences":["We‘re gonna go to this place called Denbro, and it’s a drive-thru (coffee shop).","Wow I feel so out of touch going back to hometown and seeing all these new stores.","Like I feel like I missed many chapters, I missed everything.","They accidentally gave me two drinks.","I feel like a food reviewer now.","So this one is the peppermint latte drink.","I can get behind this.","This is really really good it actually exceeded my expectations."],"exercise":"We‘re gonna go to this place called Denbro, and it’s  a 得来速(coffee shop). Wow I feel so 脱节 going back to hometown and seeing all these new stores. I feel like I 错过了很多重要的经历, like I missed everything. They 不小心 gave me two drinks. I feel like a 美食评论家 now. So this one is the 薄荷拿铁饮料 drink. I can get behind this. This is really really good it actually 超出了我的预期.","vocabulary":[{"id":"4ef01fa2-1792-4d4e-996b-44b4199a7da8","english":"drive-thru","ipa":"","chinese":"得来速（音译）","usage":"1. 指一种商业服务模式，顾客可以在不下车的情况下通过车辆驶入到服务窗口或者柜台，进行点餐、购物或取货。这种服务通常在快餐店、咖啡店、银行、药店等场所提供，方便顾客在车内交易，节省时间。\n2. ”drive-thru\" 和 \"drive-through\" 是同样的概念，只是拼写上有所不同。在美国，通常使用 \"drive-thru\" 这种拼写方式。而在一些其他地区，也会使用 \"drive-through\" 这种拼写。"},{"id":"2c3470dd-c34a-4671-ba04-de0150ac9edc","english":"out of touch","ipa":"","chinese":"不了解新情况的；失去联系的","usage":"🌰Example: I think he’s out of touch with the real world. 我认为他与现实世界脱节了。\n🌰Example: James and I have been out of touch for years.  我和詹姆斯已经多年没有联系了。"},{"id":"eb26a56a-7fe6-466d-90d9-fe64abb69a26","english":"miss many chapters","ipa":"","chinese":"遗漏了很多篇章","usage":"用来比喻错过了某个事件或经历中的重要部分。在此语境中，博主感到自己错过了家乡发生的一系列变化或重要事件，就像是错过了一本书中的很多重要内容，感到与家乡的联系有所中断"},{"id":"f06c9806-a59e-430e-9b8f-61340f90481b","english":"accidentally","ipa":"/,æksɪˈdɛntəli/","chinese":"adv. 偶然地；意外地；非故意地","usage":"🌰Example: We accidentally broke the radio. 我们不小心弄坏了收音机"},{"id":"3e46e159-d88f-4edd-9e91-028935532810","english":"reviewer","ipa":"/rɪˈvjuːə(r)/","chinese":"n. 书籍、电影、新节目、新戏剧等的评论家，评论员","usage":"food reviewer 美食评论家\ninvited reviewer杂志特邀审稿人\nbook reviewer书评撰稿人；书评家\nfilm reviewer影评人"},{"id":"6a024090-2314-4a33-a4f3-61ec1bee3f72","english":"peppermint","ipa":"/'pepəmɪnt/","chinese":"n. 薄荷","usage":"a peppermint cream. 薄荷奶油糖。"},{"id":"94ef711f-7d89-4588-9a48-da1b4894e06d","english":"latte","ipa":"/ˈlæteɪ/","chinese":"拿铁咖啡","usage":"I love a maple hot latte from there.我喜欢那里的枫糖热拿铁。"},{"id":"a1f0cebd-a8d0-4fe0-883e-0b9a3bbed587","english":"get behind sth","ipa":"","chinese":"支持…","usage":"And everyone kind of gets behind their country.\n每个人都会支持他们的国家。"},{"id":"1be21295-b982-4a43-9d18-673e83761f70","english":"get behind with","ipa":"","chinese":"落后于，拖欠：指在完成某项任务或支付某笔款项上落后于预定时间或计划。","usage":"If you get behind with the rent, you will be asked to leave.\n你要是拖欠房租，就得请你走人。"},{"id":"0628c573-8f76-44dc-a56f-a55b33a3ac47","english":"exceed","ipa":"/ɪkˈsiːd/","chinese":"v. 超过，超出某数量、数字等","usage":"exceed in 在…方面超过"},{"id":"fccae1b2-4e4b-4d5b-95f2-2d4264fbf189","english":"expectation","ipa":"/ˌekspekˈteɪʃn/","chinese":"n. 期待，预期","usage":"an unreasonable expectation; 不合理的期望；"}]},{"day":9,"title":"英语积累Day 9","topic":"数码产品","author":"Michelle Choi","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/0ec9e6f3038b46d4a84614b7642607ad","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/fQYryTwGQqc?si=wRChYex4RQVl1c9g","audioSize":"282.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-009.m4a","youtubeId":"fQYryTwGQqc","chinese":"这些新手机壳的设计超级可爱，但更重要的是非常耐用。它们是防撞手机壳，所以即使你不小心摔了手机，也会得到保护。大家都知道，我目前正在进行为期一个月的旅行，这意味着我需要随身携带所有的装备。因此，对我来说拥有一个耐用且保护性强的手机壳是必不可少的。","english":"The design of the new phone cases is super cute, but more importantly, they are very durable. These are the impact cases. So even when you drop your phone, it's protected. As far as you know, I'm on a month-long travel trip, which means I am lugging around all my equipment, laptops, bags. So it's a must-have for me to have a durable and protective phone case.","sentences":["The design of the new phone cases is super cute, but more importantly, they are very durable.","These are the impact cases.","So even when you drop your phone, it's protected.","As far as you know, I'm on a month-long travel trip, which means I am lugging around all my equipment, laptops, bags.","So it's a must-have for me to have a durable and protective phone case."],"exercise":"The design of the new 手机壳 is super cute, but 更重要的是, they are very 耐用. These are 防撞手机壳, so even if you drop your phone, it's protected. As far as you know, I'm on a 为期一个月的 travel trip, which means  I am 随身携带 around all my equipment, laptops, bags. So it's a 必不可少的（东西） for me to have a durable and 保护性强的 phone case.","vocabulary":[{"id":"0e923803-137a-41f5-8526-303ded244b7b","english":"case","ipa":"/keɪs/","chinese":"n. 当“case”作为名词时，它有多种含义：\n1.  案例（例如法律案例）\n2.  情况、状况\n3.  事件、事例\n4.  盒子、容器\n5.  套、壳（如手机壳）\n6.  病例（医学术语）","usage":"phone case手机壳"},{"id":"c985a247-028c-4c49-94e3-84c9feeb5bf2","english":"durable","ipa":"/ˈdjʊərəbl/","chinese":"a. 耐用的;持久的","usage":"🌰Example: Willow wood furniture is expensive but durable. \n柳木家具不便宜但却很耐用"},{"id":"a71eeb50-fa66-449b-a9fe-838e736988b6","english":"impact","ipa":"/ˈɪmpækt/","chinese":"n. 影响；冲击、撞击","usage":"impact case 防撞手机壳"},{"id":"ab394a06-b9d1-461c-a01c-4a8e95e8bcb6","english":"month-long","ipa":"","chinese":"","usage":"由名词\"month\"和形容词\"long\"构成的复合形容词，用于描述名词\"travel trip\"的特征。"},{"id":"d9c400a1-d7cf-4123-9fc2-7cb9f8273e52","english":"lug","ipa":"/lʌɡ/","chinese":"v. 用力拉，拖，提","usage":"lug around 费力地携带、搬运"},{"id":"59133c99-2291-491e-a9cd-9094bea26732","english":"must-have","ipa":"","chinese":"必备品，必须品","usage":"🌰Example: This jacket is a must-have for winter; it's so warm and durable.\n这件夹克是冬季必备品；它又暖和又耐用。"},{"id":"d434c2ff-e32c-4c1f-a095-67f8ccda500d","english":"protective","ipa":"/prəˈtektɪv/","chinese":"a. 保护的；防护的；","usage":"🌰Example: Protective gloves reduce the absorption of chemicals through the skin.\n防护手套可以减少皮肤对化学物质的吸收。"}]},{"day":10,"title":"英语积累Day 10","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Sydney Serena","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/3a940cac77fd46f2b3e4fa97e119ccf1","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/4AwKAHib_nc?si=G4eO5It4Y9v1eqoc","audioSize":"551.9KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-010.m4a","youtubeId":"4AwKAHib_nc","chinese":"家人们最近感觉我的头发不怎么油了。如果你们有关注我的TikTok的话，或许会知道我经常提到这件事。我一天洗一次澡，等到第二天，老实说甚至大约12小时后，头发就会再次变油。所以我开始试着逐步改变洗头的频率，变成隔一天洗一次，这样一来我确实觉得头发稍微不那么油腻了。一些粉丝在TikTok评论区建议我修剪一下头发，这似乎也有所帮助。\n我需要立刻整理一下化妆包，它已经乱到里面有太多东西，以至于我连每天实际投入使用的产品都找不到了。我的东西都跑到哪去了？这个化妆包就像一个无底洞一样。","english":"Guys, I feel like my hair has actually been a little bit less greasy recently. If you guys follow me on TikTok, then you might have seen me talk about it. I'll shower one day, and then the next day, honestly, even like 12 hours later, it gets greasy again. So, I've been kind of trying to phase out of it and push it to like every other day, and I do feel like my hair has been a bit less greasy. Some of you guys in the comments on TikTok were telling me to like trim my hair, and that kind of helps. I need to go through my makeup bag like immediately. It's to the point where there's so much stuff that I can't even find my actual products that I use every day. So maybe later today I'll go through this. Where is everything? It's like, it's like a bottomless pit in here.","sentences":["Guys, I feel like my hair has actually been a little bit less greasy recently.","If you guys follow me on TikTok, then you might have seen me talk about it.","I'll shower one day, and then the next day, honestly, even like 12 hours later, it gets greasy again.","So, I've been kind of trying to phase out of it and push it to like every other day, and I do feel like my hair has been a bit less greasy.","Some of you guys in the comments on TikTok were telling me to like trim my hair, and that kind of helps.","I need to go through my makeup bag like immediately.","It's to the point where there's so much stuff that I can't even find my actual products that I use every day.","So maybe later today I'll go through this.","Where is everything?","It's like, it's like a bottomless pit in here."],"exercise":"Guys, I feel like my hair has actually been a little bit less 油 recently. If you guys 关注我的TikTok, then you might 会知道 me talk about it. I'll shower one day, and then the next day, honestly, even like 12 hours later, it gets greasy again. So, I've been kind of trying to 逐步改变 of it and push it to like 隔一天（洗一次）, and I do feel like my hair has been a bit less greasy. Some of you guys in the comments on TikTok were telling me to like 修剪 my hair, and that kind of helps. \nI need to 整理 my 化妆包 like immediately. It's to the point where there's so much 东西 that I can't even find my 实际投入使用的产品 that I use every day. So maybe later today I'll go through this. Where is everything? It's like, it's like a 无底洞 in here.","vocabulary":[{"id":"f2d20ffe-a37b-44ad-9392-7b9b49f08892","english":"greasy","ipa":"/'griːsɪ/","chinese":"a. 1. 脂肪的,涂有脂肪的,含脂肪过多的\n2. (指人、举止)谄媚的\nn. 润滑油箱\n<机>油杯","usage":"1. greasy spoon 低级小饭馆；经济小吃店\n2. greasy skin.油性皮肤\n3. greasy food. 油腻的食品\n4. a shampoo for greasy hair 适合油性发质的洗发水"},{"id":"9d8cb962-73a4-4ddb-ad7e-aa34a89ccb39","english":"follow on","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 继续; 随之发生；\n2. （在社交媒体上）关注（某人）","usage":"Even among people that teens follow on these platforms.\n即使是青少年在这些平台上关注的人也是如此"},{"id":"3cf09afb-0707-4816-9597-43dbd6032d1a","english":"phase out","ipa":"","chinese":"逐渐停止；使逐步淘汰","usage":"I'm trying to phase out of meat.\n我正试图逐步告别肉类。"},{"id":"ae818d6f-92b8-4943-bbe0-1ff696442f89","english":"every other day","ipa":"","chinese":"每隔一天","usage":"That is about one painting every other day. 也就是说大约每隔一天画一幅画。"},{"id":"dc7f703c-d2ed-4f21-b85a-2d1c36544673","english":"trim","ipa":"/trɪm/","chinese":"vt. 1. 修剪, 整修\n2. 除去, 削减\n3. 装饰\n4. a. 整齐的, 整洁的, 匀称漂亮的\n5. n. 修剪\n6. 准备就绪, 井井有条, 整整齐齐, 状态极佳","usage":"1. trim a budget. 削减预算\n2. trim the edges of a lawn 修剪草地的边缘\n3. His hat was brushed; his wig was trim; his neckcloth was perfectly tied. 他的帽子刷过了，他的假发很整齐，他的颈巾端端正正。\n4. She went to the hairdresser's for a trim. 她到理发店理发去了。"},{"id":"c2f7cc79-ebcd-43cd-89fa-fe8cad8c736a","english":"go through","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 检查, 审查, 搜查\n2. 完成, 做完\n3. 练习\n4. 遭受, 经受, 经历\n5. 穿过, 通过\n6. 用完, 用掉\n7. 看完\n8. 讨论\n9. 整理","usage":"1. There's other people going through what you are going through, too. 很多人都在经历和你一样的事情。\n2. We workshop it. So we go through it. 我们会对其进行研习，会不断进行整理。"},{"id":"e850c2a6-c15a-4ccd-91bf-aa17d19f8c74","english":"makeup bag","ipa":"","chinese":"化妆包","usage":"I'm really excited about using this new makeup bag.\n我很兴奋够用这个新的化妆包。"},{"id":"fd065777-f2b4-475b-86ad-0877fb015954","english":"stuff","ipa":"/stʌf/","chinese":"n. 材料；东西；填充物；素材资料\nvt. 填塞；塞满；让吃饱\nvi. 吃得过多","usage":"1. stuff a pillow. 塞枕头\n2. stuff a child with food 喂饱孩子\n3. this stuff grows on you.\n这种东西会越来越吸引你。"},{"id":"b33cfffa-938f-40db-baed-81aa8f2450ed","english":"pit","ipa":"/pɪt/","chinese":"n. 深坑；矿井；陷阱；（英国剧场的）正厅后排；（物体或人体表面上的）凹陷；正厅后排的观众\nvt. 窖藏；使竞争；使凹下；去…之核；使留疤痕\nvi. 凹陷；起凹点","usage":"1. a bottomless pit 无底洞\n2. pits in a windshield. 屏风上的小麻点\n3. a chance to pit herself against him. 一个使她能跟他竞争的机会。"}]},{"day":11,"title":"英语积累Day 11","topic":"生活方式","author":"Zhirelle","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/f4f532bd382449dc90ae041565baa2f0","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/zweKYOLwf0k?si=KXXOLZEmFugB696U","audioSize":"409.7KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-011.m4a","youtubeId":"zweKYOLwf0k","chinese":"上学期间，我经常感到压力山大、不堪重负。内心总有个声音说：“我真的受够了，我不可能再熬过另一个学期了。”之后，我改变了心态，明白了上学是我人生的必经之路，所以我把精力投入到如何能享受学校生活上。在这个视频中，我会向大家展示，我是如何将上学这件事情浪漫化的，这帮我取得了更好的成绩，使我享受学习，并让我对接下来的学期感到兴奋。","english":"During the school year, I used to feel so stressed and overwhelmed all the time. I was always telling myself, \"I'm so over it, there's no way I'm getting through another semester.\" So, I shifted my mindset and understood that school was something I was going to get through, which made me put energy into how I could enjoy it. So, in this video, I'm going to show you how I romanticized school, which helped me to get better grades, enjoy learning, and made me feel excited for the next semester.","sentences":["During the school year, I used to feel so stressed and overwhelmed all the time.","I was always telling myself, \"I'm so over it, there's no way I'm getting through another semester.\"","So, I shifted my mindset and understood that school was something I was going to get through, which made me put energy into how I could enjoy it.","So, in this video, I'm going to show you how I romanticized school, which helped me to get better grades, enjoy learning, and made me feel excited for the next semester."],"exercise":"During the school year, I used to feel so stressed and 不堪重负 all the time. I was always telling myself, \"I'm so 受够了, there's no way I'm 熬过 another semester.\" So, 我改变了心态 and understood that school was something I was going to get through, which made me把精力投入到 how I could enjoy it. So, in this video, I'm going to show you how I 浪漫化 school, which helped me to get better grades, enjoy learning, and made me feel excited for the next semester.","vocabulary":[{"id":"88019189-bdcd-46ee-ba0e-22e6f5b9e089","english":"overwhelm","ipa":"/ˌəʊvəˈwelm/","chinese":"1. vt. 覆盖，淹没\n2. 压倒，制服；打败\n3. 使某人不知所措","usage":"1. an overwhelming victory 势如破竹的胜利\n2. an overwhelming tug of attraction. 极大的吸引力。"},{"id":"08ad2ef3-4a11-4f2d-95af-128d35998db6","english":"be over it","ipa":"","chinese":"受够了","usage":"I'm so over it 我受够了"},{"id":"4d6799bf-7e9a-4ede-b6cb-4b25e31de002","english":"get through","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 度过困难时期\n2. 完成某事，处理某事\n3. 与某人取得联系","usage":"1. It was tough, but we managed to get through it together.\"这很艰难，但我们熬过去了\n2. I need to get through this paperwork before the end of the day. 我需要在今天结束之前处理完这些文书工作。\n3. I couldn't get through to him on the phone. 我无法通过电话联系到他。"},{"id":"f652ffb0-504b-4466-924d-dc19ef459554","english":"shifted sb’s mindset","ipa":"","chinese":"改变心态/思维方式","usage":"After attending the workshop on mindfulness, it really shifted my mindset towards stress and relaxation. 参加了关于正念的研讨会后，我的思维方式真的发生了变化，对压力和放松有了新的看法。"},{"id":"85273777-b392-4905-90dc-ac36b9eddc4b","english":"put energy into","ipa":"","chinese":"投入精力、努力或注意力去做某事","usage":"I've been putting a lot of energy into my studies lately to prepare for the exam. 我最近在努力学习，为了备考。"},{"id":"05bd640a-9364-462a-9852-80795442ac54","english":"romanticize","ipa":"/rə(ʊ)'mæntɪsaɪz/","chinese":"1. vt. 使浪漫化；使传奇化\n2. 夸张,以浪漫手法处理\n3. vi. 沉醉于浪漫的幻想","usage":"1. I do not believe that our museum romanticizes World War Two. 我不相信我们的博物馆将浪漫化第二次世界大战。\n2. When I was in the city, I romanticized country living. 我住在都市的时候，我将乡村生活想象得很美好。"}]},{"day":12,"title":"英语积累Day 12","topic":"情感成长","author":"Michelle Choi","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/38a71dae45df43bb99ae3def3a333667","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/5Vx1NO1dxUQ?si=n2jsgDxpVzqhIz21","audioSize":"314.5KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-012.m4a","youtubeId":"5Vx1NO1dxUQ","chinese":"几天前我去心理咨询，回来之后，我总是察觉到自己在走神。是否也有人有这样的感觉？有时在经历几次心理咨询后，我会觉得自己变好很多，感觉想通了很多事情，但最近并不是这样的状态，只是觉得有点想家，想回家。","english":"I had therapy a couple of days ago, and ever since that therapy session, I've just been catching myself zoning out. Has anyone else experienced this? Some therapy sessions I feel so good after; I'm feeling like I've unpacked a lot of things, but recently it hasn't been like that. Just kind of been feeling a little homesick, wanting to go back home.","sentences":["I had therapy a couple of days ago, and ever since that therapy session, I've just been catching myself zoning out.","Has anyone else experienced this?","Some therapy sessions I feel so good after; I'm feeling like I've unpacked a lot of things, but recently it hasn't been like that.","Just kind of been feeling a little homesick, wanting to go back home."],"exercise":"I had 心理咨询 a couple of days ago, and ever since that therapy session, I've just been 察觉到 myself 在走神. Has anyone else experienced this? （有时在经历）几次心理咨询 （后） I feel so good after; I'm feeling like I've  想通了 a lot of things, but recently it hasn't been like that. Just kind of been feeling a little 想家, wanting to go back home.","vocabulary":[{"id":"23166b1f-a945-4f70-91c8-aa0736057b9f","english":"therapy","ipa":"/ˈθerəpi/","chinese":"n. 治疗，疗法","usage":"1. he is currently in therapy . 他正接受心理治疗。\n2. the therapy of fresh air and sun.\n新鲜空气与阳光的治疗能力"},{"id":"7a1c67cf-be2a-46ce-8abe-2da0374f23d9","english":"catch","ipa":"/kætʃ/","chinese":"1. vt. 忽然发觉;突然意识到；\n2. 了解","usage":"1. Would you mind repeating that? I didn't quite catch on. 请再说一遍好吗?我没听懂。"},{"id":"c8522f5b-545c-44f4-a665-b2da8dd56ca1","english":"zone out","ipa":"","chinese":"走神，发呆","usage":"So imagine hundreds of people staring at screens and zoning out in meetings. 所以想想看数百人都在眼盯屏幕或在会上发呆。"},{"id":"32033121-8bec-4376-9075-2c2d1b8c799e","english":"therapy sessions","ipa":"","chinese":"心理治疗期","usage":"心理治疗过程中的交谈。在交谈中，个人与心理健康专家（如心理医生、心理治疗师或心理咨询师）进行交流和讨论，以解决心理健康问题"},{"id":"d7130838-886f-4427-b3fc-bbd42ad9dd30","english":"unpack","ipa":"/ˌʌnˈpæk/","chinese":"1. vt. & vi. 从(包裹等)中取出(所装的东西)，打开行李取出\n2. vt. 拆包，拆解，拆开(已压缩的数据项)\n3. 解除...的负担；吐露(心事等)\n4. 卸下(车、马等)的负荷物","usage":"1. unpack one's grievances 诉苦\n2. let us unpack this question. 让我们分解一下这个问题。"},{"id":"3ea6d8ef-3248-4aba-975a-20759153590c","english":"homesick","ipa":"/'həʊmsɪk/","chinese":"adj. 想家的；思乡病的","usage":"That night they felt homesick and lonely. 那天晚上，他们都开始想家，感觉孤独极了"}]},{"day":13,"title":"英语积累Day 13","topic":"生活方式","author":"Michelle Choi","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/0b3ac6c6a7914d41be59bd6621c47f61","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/5Vx1NO1dxUQ?si=n2jsgDxpVzqhIz21","audioSize":"436.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-013.m4a","youtubeId":"5Vx1NO1dxUQ","chinese":"嗨，嗨，我马上要去上普拉提课了，这可是我今天最期待的事情。我正在去普拉提课的路上。我在拉伸机上挤到脚，都淤青了。我已经预约了这节普拉提课，不想因为取消而付费。所以，我依旧在去上课的路上，我要坚强起来，上完我的课。","english":"Hello, hello, about to go take a Pilates class. It's just been the highlight of my day. I am on my way to a Pilates class. I pinched my foot on the reformer machine, and my foot is bruised. I was already scheduled for this Pilates class, and I don't want to pay for a cancellation. So, here I am, going strong, making it to my class.","sentences":["Hello, hello, about to go take a Pilates class.","It's just been the highlight of my day.","I am on my way to a Pilates class.","I pinched my foot on the reformer machine, and my foot is bruised.","I was already scheduled for this Pilates class, and I don't want to pay for a cancellation.","So, here I am, going strong, making it to my class."],"exercise":"Hello, hello, about to go take a 普拉提课. It's just been the 最期待的事情 of my day. I am on my way to a Pilates class. I 挤到脚 on the 拉伸机, and my foot is 淤青. I was already 预约 for this Pilates class, and I don't want to 因为取消而付费. So, here I am, 坚强起来, making it to my class.","vocabulary":[{"id":"82905b0c-3fd8-405d-9443-1297a0df07c7","english":"Pilates class","ipa":"/pɪˈlɑːtiːz/","chinese":"n. 普拉提课程","usage":"pilates push-ups 普拉提俯卧撑"},{"id":"a8b30da0-ed63-419e-8ea2-48f7f125e02f","english":"highlight","ipa":"/ˈhaɪlaɪt/","chinese":"1. vt. 强调, 突出, 使显著\n2. n. 最精彩的部分, 最重要的事情","usage":"1. This highlights the potentially deadly effect of our disposable culture.\n这就凸显了丢弃文化潜在的致命影响。\n2. I'll show you the highlights of the event. 我将给你展示这个事件的最精彩的部分。"},{"id":"d1e53c15-2da8-40d7-bba0-a94256c4d34f","english":"pinch","ipa":"/pɪntʃ/","chinese":"1. vt. 捏；勒索；使苦恼；掐掉某物，修剪\n2. n. 匮乏；少量；夹痛\n3. vi. 夹痛；节省","usage":"1. feel the pinch [口语]感到经济拮据\n2. a pinch of 一撮，少许\n3. at/in a pinch 在紧要关头\n4. pinch pennies 精打细算\n5. She pinched me on the arm.她在我臂上拧了一下。"},{"id":"aaef03e2-e682-4ca4-8c35-06edc99050bd","english":"reformer machine","ipa":"","chinese":"拉伸机","usage":"健身房中常见的健身设备，主要用于进行全身训练，特别是针对核心肌群和平衡能力的训练。通常与皮带、弹簧和滑轨等组件结合在一起，形成一个多功能的训练系统。"},{"id":"f8a90af6-d0be-4e57-a51e-93d5616a62f3","english":"bruised","ipa":"/bru:zd/","chinese":"1. adj. [医]青肿的；瘀紫的\n2. v. 擦伤（bruise的过去式）","usage":"1. a bruised knee. 撞青了的膝盖。\n2. She bruised herself against the desk. 她撞到书桌上, 有些瘀青。"},{"id":"81110f46-a9a1-468f-8862-1749c83401e4","english":"schedule","ipa":"/ˈskedʒuːl/","chinese":"1. vt. 排定, 安排\n2. n. 时间表, 日程安排表\n3. 清单, 明细表","usage":"1. on schedule adv. 按时；按照预定时间\n2. ahead of schedule adv. 提前\n3. according to schedule 按照预定计划\n4. time schedule 时间表"},{"id":"69d65cf5-2a61-4027-bf7d-1effdc27efd0","english":"cancellation","ipa":"/ˌkænsə'leɪʃ(ə)n/","chinese":"1. n. 取消，注销；作废，废除；删去，划掉\n2. 被取消的事物\n3. <数>(相)约；(相)消\n4. 盖销记号；戳记","usage":"1. cancellation of registration 取消登记\n2. The cancellation of the game was a real letdown.\n比赛取消真是令人失望"},{"id":"547e8533-cc29-4c31-8b15-3f5bede25d70","english":"go strong","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 坚强起来\n2. 精力充沛","usage":"Well, check you out, still going strong.看看你，还这么有劲头。"}]},{"day":14,"title":"英语积累Day 14","topic":"情感成长","author":"Michelle Choi","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/cb7723debf2d4a69be98c54eada66e94","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/g3sdFQxSyVY?si=DaXODNN6_uyly2NV","audioSize":"288.7KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-014.m4a","youtubeId":"g3sdFQxSyVY","chinese":"作为一个博主，我不可避免地会接触到很多人的意见。从某种程度上来说，我对此心存感激，因为这让我得以成长和改进。但有时候，我会在这个过程中迷失了自我，因为它会让我产生疲惫和“冒名顶替综合症”的感觉。所以我正在努力寻找一个健康的平衡点，让我既能接受意见，又能保持自我。","english":"As someone who is on the Internet, it's inevitable for me to get a lot of people's opinions. And on one end, I'm grateful for them because it allows me to grow and improve. But sometimes, I lose myself in that process because it leads to burnouts and impostor syndrome. So I'm trying to find a happy medium where I can do both in a healthy way.","sentences":["As someone who is on the Internet, it's inevitable for me to get a lot of people's opinions.","And on one end, I'm grateful for them because it allows me to grow and improve.","But sometimes, I lose myself in that process because it leads to burnouts and impostor syndrome.","So I'm trying to find a happy medium where I can do both in a healthy way."],"exercise":"As someone who is on the Internet, it's 不可避免地 for me to get a lot of people's opinions. And 某种程度上来说, I'm grateful for them because it allows me to 成长和改进. But sometimes, I 迷失了自我 in that process because it leads to 疲惫 and 冒名顶替综合症. So I'm trying to find a 健康的平衡点 where I can do both in a healthy way.","vocabulary":[{"id":"5b26b818-a8dc-4021-8e48-8ed6a2d1526f","english":"inevitable","ipa":"/ɪnˈevɪtəbl/","chinese":"1. adj. 不可避免的, 必然发生的\n2. 〈非正〉总会发生的, 照例必有的, 惯常的","usage":"1. inevitable defeat 丧志屈服; 必然的失败;\n2. Inevitable Accident 不可避免的事故; \n3. Inevitable trend 必然趋势; 必然走向;\n4. inevitable loss 无法避免的损失; 不可避免的损失;"},{"id":"adee249d-0410-4d98-b4f8-61a6b3395921","english":"On one end","ipa":"","chinese":"某种程度上来说；一方面。**这里的end为多义词，意思为“一端，一方，一头”，如“There was silence at the other end of the line. 电话那头没有声音。”  短语\"on one end\" 常用来指代某个范围或是某个事物的一端，通常在讨论某个事物的两端、两极或是两个极端时使用。","usage":"On one end we actually realized that the bedrock of being able to build back better if you will. 一方面，我们实际上意识到，如果你愿意的话，能够重建得更好的基石。"},{"id":"71fe0f21-95ed-4af7-b495-120d7aed018a","english":"lose oneself","ipa":"","chinese":"热衷于; 迷失方向; 入迷;","usage":"Not to dare is to lose oneself, that is when we don't cope, when we avoid. 而我们不去应对，选择逃避，却步不前则会迷失自我。"},{"id":"ff233a4d-ddc8-4d78-9706-c4c5259c94d5","english":"burnout","ipa":"/'bɜːnaʊt/","chinese":"1. n. 烧坏；燃料烧尽\n2. n. 疲惫；倦怠","usage":"1. job burnout 职业倦怠; 职业枯竭;\n2. burnout syndrome 疲劳综合征"},{"id":"d5e233d9-7ec1-494a-87f5-edecb14de5d0","english":"impostor syndrome","ipa":"/ɪmˈpɒstə(r)/\n/ˈsɪndrəʊm/","chinese":"冒充者综合症","usage":"一种常见的心理状态，即个人无法内在接受自己取得的成就，并持续担心被揭穿为\"冒充者\"或\"骗子\"的感觉。即使在取得显著成就或在专业领域中获得成功的人，也可能因为内心感觉自己并不足够胜任而产生这种情绪。"},{"id":"84d3243a-a700-4f4c-825f-902e24965bb8","english":"medium","ipa":"/ˈmiːdiəm/","chinese":"1. n. 媒介, 手段, 方法, 工具\n2. 折中, 中间物\n3. 生活条件, 环境\n4. adj. 中等的, 适中的","usage":"1. a happy medium 健康的平衡点\n2. you have to strike a happy medium. 你得采取折中办法。"}]},{"day":15,"title":"英语积累Day 15","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Michelle Choi","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/7af2db78ef5e4a3e84c7410d8313f741","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/g3sdFQxSyVY?si=DaXODNN6_uyly2NV","audioSize":"413.7KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-015.m4a","youtubeId":"g3sdFQxSyVY","chinese":"我刚做完头发回来，还戴上了我在韩国地铁站买的这个可爱的小蝴蝶结。当时我不确定到底是把头发放下来还是扎上去。最后我选择了半扎半放，因为实在无法决定。我认为我在剪发这件事情上领悟到的最重要的一点是，专业的事情还是要找专业的人来做，因为我喜欢她给我剪的刘海。我不知道为什么，但留刘海让我想起了大学时代，因为我以前就留过这样的刘海。","english":"I just got back from doing my hair, and I added this little cute bow that I got in Korea in the subway station. I wasn't sure if I was going to leave my hair all down or go all up. I just set a half up half down cause I couldn't decide. I think the biggest takeaway here is to always cut your hair by a professional, cause I love how she cut my bangs. I don't know why, but having bangs just reminds me of my college days cause I used to have bangs like this.","sentences":["I just got back from doing my hair, and I added this little cute bow that I got in Korea in the subway station.","I wasn't sure if I was going to leave my hair all down or go all up.","I just set a half up half down cause I couldn't decide.","I think the biggest takeaway here is to always cut your hair by a professional, cause I love how she cut my bangs.","I don't know why, but having bangs just reminds me of my college days cause I used to have bangs like this."],"exercise":"I just got back from doing my hair, and I 戴上了 this little cute 蝴蝶结 that I got in Korea in the subway station. I wasn't sure if I was going to 把头发放下来还是扎上去. I just set a 半扎半放 cause I couldn't decide. I think the biggest 领悟到的最重要的一点 here is to always cut your hair by a professional, cause I love how she cut my 刘海. I don't know why, but having bangs just reminds me of my college days cause I 以前就留过这样的刘海.","vocabulary":[{"id":"86f89564-0066-4e7c-8431-86006e7e1420","english":"bow","ipa":"/baʊ/","chinese":"1. n. 鞋带或丝带系成的蝴蝶结  \n2. n. 弓；鞠躬；船首\n3. vi. 鞠躬；弯腰\n4. vt. 鞠躬；弯腰\n5. adj. 弯曲的","usage":"1. Add a length of ribbon tied in a bow. 再用一段丝带，系个蝴蝶结。\n2. bow in suppliance for knowledge\n为恳求知识而鞠躬"},{"id":"e29af149-7f66-4d2f-9d9c-1f0c5aed09a2","english":"leave one’s hair all down or go all up","ipa":"","chinese":"把头发放下来或者扎上去","usage":""},{"id":"173ec03e-a509-4052-b374-9fece2bf43a2","english":"takeaway","ipa":"/'teɪkəweɪ/","chinese":"1. adj. 外卖的；外吃的\n2. n. 外卖食品；外卖餐馆\n3. 从某种经验或情况中获得的主要观点或教训","usage":"All jokes set aside, we hope you walk out of this with the following few takeaways.\n抛开所有的笑话不谈，我们希望你能带着以下几个要点走出困境。"},{"id":"146d3995-8ab6-4824-a77d-d31b1d450243","english":"bang","ipa":"/bæŋ/","chinese":"1. n. 猛击, 猛撞\n2. 巨响, 爆炸声\n3. vt. 猛击, 猛撞\n4. vi. 发出砰的一声, 砰砰作响, 砰地敲[推, 扔]\n5. n. 刘海；额前短垂发","usage":"1. My bangs were cut short, but the rest of my hair was long. 我剪短了刘海，但其他地方的头发还是很长。\n2. a nasty bang on the head. 对头部的猛击。"},{"id":"00709d6a-8a8b-4cfc-9c29-2b8f71bf746c","english":"used to","ipa":"","chinese":"过去常常","usage":"I used to be a damsel in distress. 我是常常处于忧伤中的女孩。"}]},{"day":16,"title":"英语积累Day 16","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Sydney Serena","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/bb220f695e884d1880b3a5807674c217","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/4AwKAHib_nc?si=ysKwo_RAzvqn1Xe1","audioSize":"577.5KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-016.m4a","youtubeId":"4AwKAHib_nc","chinese":"首先是这件红色露背背心。我喜欢它的领口设计，而且我也超爱穿红色。我平时也经常穿黑色系，红色和黑色真的是绝配。我觉得这款背心很漂亮适合约会穿。我淘到了这件风衣，它之所以吸引我是因为版型有点臃肿，但我正喜欢这一点。这件衣服很考究，我在纽约见过好多女孩穿这种风格的衣服。接下来这一件有点超出我的舒适区，但这也正是我喜欢它的原因。我真的很佩服那些女孩，她们能够用最奇特、最古怪的单品搭配出一套非常棒的衣服。我不会说我就是那种女孩，但我正在努力成为其中之一。","english":"Starting out with this red halter neck tank. What I liked about this was the neckline, and I also have been really loving to wear red. I wear a lot of black, and red and black just go super well together. I think this will be a beautiful date night top. I got this trench coat, and this one caught my eyes because it's a bit bulky, but I like that about it. It's so sophisticated, and I see so many girls in New York wearing stuff like this. This next one is a little bit out of my comfort zone, but that's what I liked about it. I really admire those girls that can just take the most random, eccentric pieces and put them together to create a really nice outfit. I wouldn't say I'm one of those girls, but I'm trying to be.","sentences":["Starting out with this red halter neck tank.","What I liked about this was the neckline, and I also have been really loving to wear red.","I wear a lot of black, and red and black just go super well together.","I think this will be a beautiful date night top.","I got this trench coat, and this one caught my eyes because it's a bit bulky, but I like that about it.","It's so sophisticated, and I see so many girls in New York wearing stuff like this.","This next one is a little bit out of my comfort zone, but that's what I liked about it.","I really admire those girls that can just take the most random, eccentric pieces and put them together to create a really nice outfit.","I wouldn't say I'm one of those girls, but I'm trying to be."],"exercise":"Starting out with this red 露背背心. What I liked about this was the 领口设计, and I also have been really loving to wear red. I wear a lot of black, and red and black just 绝配. I think this will be 很漂亮适合约会穿. I 淘到了 this 风衣, and this one caught my eyes because it's 版型有点臃肿, but I like that about it. It's so 考究, and I see so many girls in New York wearing stuff like this. This next one is a little bit out of my 舒适区, but that's what I liked about it. I really admire those girls that can just take the most 最奇特、最古怪的单品 and put them together to create 一套非常棒的衣服. I wouldn't say I'm one of those girls, but I'm trying to be.","vocabulary":[{"id":"935f5bf8-41a6-43d0-a49c-923c62cd5157","english":"halter neck tank","ipa":"","chinese":"露肩背心","usage":"She wore a halter neck tank with a pair of jeans, looking very stylish.她穿着一件露肩背心，搭配一条牛仔裤，看起来非常时尚。"},{"id":"15c6ea3a-63b9-474c-a071-3333dcb7cb83","english":"neckline","ipa":"/'neklaɪn/","chinese":"n. 领口，领圈","usage":"She braid the neckline, hem and cuffs of the dress.她用穗带装饰连衣裙的领口、摺边和袖口。"},{"id":"408ad4ce-7caf-4e6e-881f-7a23e90b7d81","english":"go super well together","ipa":"","chinese":"非常搭配，相互非常和谐","usage":"The red blouse and black skirt go super well together.这件红色的衬衫和黑色的裙子搭配得非常和谐。"},{"id":"b4a4b46d-2d93-4992-a9d7-4ce4ddc1929e","english":"a beautiful date night top","ipa":"","chinese":"很漂亮适合约会穿","usage":""},{"id":"0dbb43df-b229-4b72-9cc6-0997d66187e8","english":"trench coat","ipa":"/trentʃ/","chinese":"风衣","usage":"Another thing, another kind of coat is a trench coat, a trench coat. 另一种外套是风衣，风衣"},{"id":"9e42b079-7f9a-4cea-b314-f6b428ea7057","english":"bulky","ipa":"/ˈbʌlki/","chinese":"adj. 庞大的；体积大的；笨重的","usage":"Bulky clothes tend to hinder movement.肥大的衣服常常碍手碍脚。"},{"id":"56570386-db43-46b5-873f-1c85ead637ed","english":"sophisticated","ipa":"/səˈfɪstɪkeɪtɪd/","chinese":"1. adj. 老练的；老于世故的\n2. 精密的，尖端的\n3. 高雅的，有教养的；善于社交的;高雅时髦的;见过世面的；","usage":"1. Recently her tastes have become more sophisticated.最近她的品位越发优雅时髦起来。\n2. These people are very sophisticated observers of the foreign policy scene. 这些人是观察外交政策领域动向的行家里手。"},{"id":"d738d8d9-fd15-4bcc-879e-80ca7a4be06b","english":"comfort zone","ipa":"","chinese":"舒适区","usage":"She decided to step out of her comfort zone and try something new. 她决定走出自己的舒适区，尝试一些新的事物。"},{"id":"c20a7769-aa86-441d-8967-c07f13496a5e","english":"random","ipa":"/ˈrændəm/","chinese":"1. adj. 任意的；胡乱的；随机的\n2. n. 随意\n3. adv. 胡乱地","usage":"1. at random 胡乱地；随便地；任意地\n2. random sampling 随机抽样；随意采样"},{"id":"46d7e166-3813-4f73-b1ad-6b0e6615cf33","english":"eccentric","ipa":"/ɪkˈsentrɪk/","chinese":"adj. 古怪的，怪癖的；异乎寻常的","usage":"she came to the defence of the eccentric professor.她开始为那个古怪教授辩护了。"},{"id":"6e02716d-9da7-4723-b391-3d80843d2ff7","english":"pieces","ipa":"/ˈpiːsɪz/","chinese":"服装的各个部分或单品，比如衣服、配饰等","usage":"She has a talent for mixing and matching different pieces to create unique and stylish outfits.她有一种天赋，能够将不同的服装单品搭配在一起，创造出独特而时尚的服装。"},{"id":"ce21441d-a139-49b5-9d4c-657e81551cf5","english":"outfit","ipa":"/ˈaʊtfɪt/","chinese":"1. n. （为特定场合或活动而穿的）全套服装，装束\n2. 全套装备；成套工具\n3. 组织；公司；团队；军事单位\n4. v. 装备，配备；为…提供设备（或服装）","usage":"1. wore a slinky outfit to the party.穿了一件时髦的外衣去参加聚会\n2. The whole outfit matches up beautifully.整套衣服搭配得很好看。"}]},{"day":17,"title":"英语积累Day 17","topic":"情感成长,生活方式","author":"Sydney Serena","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/4efbd0088a304105bc059e633bd7900e","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/Qk0uFJ-hvP0?si=Tcr9N84DUSDSRy26","audioSize":"394.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-017.m4a","youtubeId":"Qk0uFJ-hvP0","chinese":"我接下来要说的，是更日常化的习惯，那就是对外呈现自己，为迎接新的一天做好准备，无论对你来说这意味着什么。我发现，即使我只是出门办事，不会在那天见任何人，或是整天都呆在房间里，我都会化点淡妆，穿一套很可爱的运动装。虽然我知道没有人会看到我，但那不是重点。重点是为了让我接下来的一天感觉更好，稍微打扮一下，戴上一对金色的耳环。","english":"The next thing I have, this is more of a day-to-day thing, it's presenting yourself and preparing yourself for the day, whatever that means to you. I find even if I'm running errands, I'm not seeing anyone that day, or if I'm just staying in my room all day, sometimes I'll just throw on a little concealer, a really cute sweat set. No one's gonna see me, and I know that, but that's not the point. The point is really just to make me feel better for the day ahead by getting a little bit ready, throwing on some gold hoop earrings.","sentences":["The next thing I have, this is more of a day-to-day thing, it's presenting yourself and preparing yourself for the day, whatever that means to you.","I find even if I'm running errands, I'm not seeing anyone that day, or if I'm just staying in my room all day, sometimes I'll just throw on a little concealer, a really cute sweat set.","No one's gonna see me, and I know that, but that's not the point.","The point is really just to make me feel better for the day ahead by getting a little bit ready, throwing on some gold hoop earrings."],"exercise":"The next thing I have, this is more of 日常的事情, it's presenting yourself and preparing yourself for the day, whatever that means to you. I find even if I'm 出门办事, I'm not seeing anyone that day, or if I'm just staying in my room all day, sometimes I'll just 化点淡妆, a really cute 运动装. No one's gonna see me, and I know that, but 那不是重点. The point is really just to make me feel better for the day ahead by getting a little bit ready, 戴上 some 金耳环.","vocabulary":[{"id":"b6ec8e02-0549-4f2f-ba3b-85032c9595fe","english":"a day-to-day thing","ipa":"","chinese":"日常的、每天都会发生的事情","usage":"Doing laundry is just a day-to-day thing for me now. 对我来说，洗衣服已经成为了日常琐事。"},{"id":"6e0c8de5-6b49-4b42-9d57-bd6aadd46aa3","english":"run errands","ipa":"","chinese":"完成日常任务或跑腿，办理事务","usage":"I spent the morning running errands, like picking up groceries and dropping off dry cleaning.我花了上午的时间跑腿，比如买菜和送干洗衣物。"},{"id":"1778d2a9-e6ac-4cb0-8834-7f0215fadb28","english":"throw on a little concealer","ipa":"","chinese":"涂一点点遮瑕膏，句子中意思是简单地化一点淡妆","usage":"Before heading out, she decided to throw on a little concealer to cover up a few blemishes. 在出门前，她决定化个淡妆，遮住一些瑕疵。"},{"id":"ef6d72e1-0eab-486f-b7d0-7c66d22a5a2c","english":"sweat set","ipa":"","chinese":"一套运动服","usage":"She opted for a sweat set today, feeling comfortable whether she was at home or out and about. 她今天选择了一套运动服，无论她在家里还是外出都感觉舒适。"},{"id":"cb957ee3-fe81-4bcf-b686-6046fe9aca94","english":"point","ipa":"/pɒɪnt/","chinese":"n. 要点","usage":"That's not the point.\n这不是重点。"},{"id":"8d5affe3-542b-4fbd-afdb-23f98a24a4f7","english":"throw on","ipa":"","chinese":"匆匆穿上或披上衣物；戴上","usage":"I was running late, so I just threw on a sweater and dashed out the door. 我已经迟到了，所以我只是匆匆穿上一件毛衣，然后冲出了门。"},{"id":"646e3bd7-f25b-4e6d-b777-e6abfcd68d4e","english":"hoop","ipa":"/huːp/","chinese":"n. 箍；铁环；呼呼声\nvt. 加箍于；包围\nvi. 发呼呼声","usage":"hula hoop 呼拉圈\nhoop earrings 耳环"}]},{"day":18,"title":"英语积累Day 18","topic":"生活方式","author":"Anna Neubert","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/d6e56f3a1e8348b7aeb4fd722c613f49","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/20efEGXwE5I?si=foQrlDh6su_J6vTA","audioSize":"444.9KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-018.m4a","youtubeId":"20efEGXwE5I","chinese":"老实说，我不喜欢早上 5 点起床。但天气越暖和，离夏天越近，我就越容易早起。就好像当每一缕阳光洒满天空，我就会重新充满能量，也变得更有动力。我们都有过几乎一整天都离不开床的时候。我们会匆匆忙忙地完成日常事项中最必要的步骤，然后出门。这并没有错。但对我的精神和身体健康来说，我觉得一个我能坚持执行的、有条理的晨间日程大有裨益。","english":"I'll be honest, I do not like waking up at 5 am. But the warmer it gets and the closer we are to summer, the easier I find it to wake up early. It's almost as if with every ray of sunshine dancing throughout the sky, my batteries are filling up again and I'm so much more motivated. We all have days where we barely get out of bed. We rush through the steps within a routine that we do, most necessary, and out of the door we go. And there's nothing wrong with that. But for my own mental and also physical health, I find a structured morning routine that I can stick to on most days highly beneficial.","sentences":["I'll be honest, I do not like waking up at 5 am.","But the warmer it gets and the closer we are to summer, the easier I find it to wake up early.","It's almost as if with every ray of sunshine dancing throughout the sky, my batteries are filling up again and I'm so much more motivated.","We all have days where we barely get out of bed.","We rush through the steps within a routine that we do, most necessary, and out of the door we go.","And there's nothing wrong with that.","But for my own mental and also physical health, I find a structured morning routine that I can stick to on most days highly beneficial."],"exercise":"I'll be honest, I do not like waking up at 5 am. But the warmer it gets and 离夏天越近, the easier I find it to wake up early. It's almost as if with 每一缕 sunshine dancing throughout the sky, 重新充满能量 and I'm so much more motivated. We all have days where we 几乎不 get out of bed. We 匆匆忙忙 the steps within 完成日常事项, most necessary, and out of the door we go. And there's nothing wrong with that. But for my own mental and also physical health, I find a 有条理 morning routine that I can 坚持执行 on most days 大有裨益.","vocabulary":[{"id":"e645659c-c37b-4cd1-a3c7-d7fb2d74831d","english":"ray","ipa":"/reɪ/","chinese":"1. n. 光束, 光线\n2. 射线\n3. 微量, 丝毫","usage":"1. a ray of hope 一线希望}\n2. a ray of intelligence一线智慧的光芒"},{"id":"82d3cb64-e43a-4c6b-8e71-10f0f4101806","english":"battery","ipa":"/ˈbætri/","chinese":"n. 电池，蓄电池","usage":"1. battery of 一组；一套\n2. storage battery 蓄电池；蓄电池组"},{"id":"61da523e-d67b-4209-8bbf-6a12126446aa","english":"fill up","ipa":"","chinese":"vt. 装满(填写, 填充, 填塞, 堵塞)","usage":"Snow was filling up the window now. 雪正在积满窗棂。"},{"id":"c5fb2ebf-8034-4968-b3ed-76a9249ae7f1","english":"barely","ipa":"/ˈbeəli/","chinese":"adv. 仅仅，勉强；几乎不；公开地；贫乏地","usage":"1. Albeit Just Barely 虽然可以也勉强\n2. barely enough 勉强够; 仅够;\n3. barely not 几乎不\n4. barely satisfactory 差强人意"},{"id":"1b8e87ae-ddcd-4c94-ad55-6d5e0b952a57","english":"rush through","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 匆忙做完\n2. 快速通过\n3. 快速地做\n4. 赶紧做","usage":"1. rush through lunch: 匆匆吃完午餐\n2. rush through one's mind: 从脑中掠过\n3. rush things through: 急躁冒进\n4. rush the work through: 赶完工作"},{"id":"68f58867-b605-473d-b902-0e165f7f0136","english":"routine","ipa":"/ruːˈtiːn/","chinese":"1. n. 例行公事；日常工作；程序\n2. adj. 日常的；例行的","usage":"1. routine work 日常工作；常规作业\n2. daily routine 日常生活；日常工作"},{"id":"c4b3ab79-5d2a-4d07-a21f-1701387afe61","english":"necessary","ipa":"/ˈnesəsəri/","chinese":"1. adj. 必要的; 必需的\n2. 必然的; 不可避免的\n3. n. 必需品","usage":"indispensable 语气强，侧重指绝对必要性或不可缺少性。\nessential 指对事物本身性质具有决定性的重要性，暗含不可缺少，否则便无法存在。\nnecessary 最常用词，侧重由客观因素决定的某种需要，强调不可避免，但并非绝不可缺少。\nrequisite 正式用词，特指为实现某一目的或得到某种结果而应有的需要，有时可与necessary换用。"},{"id":"36e46729-fe9a-4099-ade1-362da202929a","english":"structured","ipa":"/ˈstrʌktʃə(r)/","chinese":"1. n. 结构，构造\n2. 有结构的事物；复杂的整体；建筑物\n3. vt. 组织；安排；构造；制定","usage":"1. structure a curriculum; structure one's day. 安排课程；对一天进行安排\n2. This will make it easier to keep your ideas structured and clear. 这样既有条理又清晰地表述观点就更加容易了。"},{"id":"6aac4bde-d035-46d7-8687-523bfd45f83d","english":"stick to","ipa":"/stɪk/","chinese":"v. 坚持；粘住","usage":"You have to stick to the subject, stick to the procedure, the elegant solution.\n你必须坚持主题，坚持程序以及得体的解决方案。"},{"id":"9c9cc821-8d79-4ef9-b19a-084e73e8996b","english":"beneficial","ipa":"/ˌbenɪˈfɪʃl/","chinese":"adj. 有益的, 有利的","usage":"mutually beneficial 互利的；双赢的\nbeneficial owner 受益所有人\nbeneficial use 享用，有权使用\nbe beneficial to 对…有益处"}]},{"day":19,"title":"英语积累Day 19","topic":"食物","author":"Zhirelle","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/c59631b98b874befafe67bf71079a5ca","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/FEN8lESp6-E?si=DiGMI-TDTLSjNrek","audioSize":"381.7KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-019.m4a","youtubeId":"FEN8lESp6-E","chinese":"我不喜欢做饭或烘焙，讨厌洗碗，饿了就想吃点超级方便的东西。我很少想自己动手做饭，但今天到目前为止我做得很好。我做了意大利面，然后放了鸡肉、牛油果、洋葱、西红柿和罗勒叶。我还在上面淋了些柠檬，放了盐和胡椒。这一口尝起来真的绝了，哇，太好吃了！","english":"I am not a fan of cooking or baking, I hate doing the dishes. And when I get hungry I just want something super convenient. It's very rare that I'm in the cooking mood but so far today I'm doing such a good job. So, I went with pasta and then I have chicken, avocado, onions, tomatoes, and basil. I also drizzled some lemon on top and put salt and pepper. That is the perfect bite, wow that is so good!","sentences":["I am not a fan of cooking or baking, I hate doing the dishes.","And when I get hungry I just want something super convenient.","It's very rare that I'm in the cooking mood but so far today I'm doing such a good job.","So, I went with pasta and then I have chicken, avocado, onions, tomatoes, and basil.","I also drizzled some lemon on top and put salt and pepper.","That is the perfect bite, wow that is so good!"],"exercise":"I am 不喜欢 cooking or 烘焙, I hate doing the dishes. And when I get hungry I just want something super 方便. 很少 I'm 想自己动手做饭 but so far today I'm doing such a good job. So, I 做了 pasta and then I have chicken, 牛油果, onions, tomatoes, and 罗勒叶. I also 淋 some lemon on top and put salt and pepper. 这一口尝起来真的绝了, wow that is so good!","vocabulary":[{"id":"40bb710d-eef3-4713-a5cd-1af961ae9683","english":"be a fan of","ipa":"","chinese":"是...的粉丝; 喜欢...","usage":"I'm a huge fan of basketball, and I never miss watching my favorite team's games.我是篮球的粉丝，从不错过我最喜欢的球队比赛的观看"},{"id":"c3a8b41d-f1ac-41ee-ba2c-965b44259b31","english":"bake","ipa":"/beɪk/","chinese":"vt. & vi. 烤, 烘焙","usage":"they bake their own bread and cakes.他们自己烤制面包和蛋糕。"},{"id":"575aab12-e6af-481b-8c0e-913ec7700021","english":"convenient","ipa":"/kənˈviːniənt/","chinese":"1. adj. 方便的, 便利的, 合适的\n2. 附近的, 近便的","usage":"convenient for adj. 便于…"},{"id":"6d2fcada-62bd-40e5-8306-c874be7da957","english":"in the…mood","ipa":"","chinese":"心情好，有兴致：情绪状态良好，愿意做某事。","usage":"1. Be in the mood: 想要做某事；心情舒畅\n2. not in the mood: 心情不舒畅；没有兴致；没有心情；没心情"},{"id":"40e386ce-fb9d-4a1a-91d0-cc239005350f","english":"rare","ipa":"/reə(r)/","chinese":"1. adj. 半熟的；稀有的；稀薄的\n2. adv. [口]非常；极其\n3. vi. [方]用后腿站起；[美口]渴望","usage":"1. rare air. 稀薄的空气\n2. stumble upon a rare book 偶然发现一本少见的书"},{"id":"8630b266-0b34-4810-937b-a573f560bdd9","english":"go with","ipa":"","chinese":"与…搭配；一起出现","usage":"1. I decided to go with the salmon for dinner and paired it with steamed vegetables and a side salad. 我决定晚餐吃三文鱼，搭配蒸蔬菜和一份沙拉。\n2. This new restaurant has different types of live music every night and excellent food to go with it.\n除了星期天，这家新餐馆每天晚上都有不同类型的现场音乐表演，还有与之相配的美味食物"},{"id":"92c29f4c-f43a-4bc2-9604-b297d2cbdea0","english":"avocado","ipa":"/ˌævəˈkɑ:dəʊ/","chinese":"牛油果","usage":"It was this class that made me remember the word avocado clearly! 就是这堂课，让我对牛油果这个词记忆犹新！"},{"id":"9352bb42-49e4-4aa0-8018-081d0384dfd3","english":"basil","ipa":"/'bæz(ə)l/","chinese":"n. 罗勒属植物","usage":"Prep some dough for a calzone for me, and get someone to chop some basil. 给我准备点面团做馅饼，再找个人切点罗勒。"},{"id":"d974167f-c1cc-46bc-b6ff-60d896c785a6","english":"drizzle","ipa":"/'drɪz(ə)l/","chinese":"1. (在食物上)滴，淋，洒；\n2. vi. 下蒙蒙细雨, 下毛毛雨\n3. n. 蒙蒙细雨, 毛毛雨","usage":"1. Drizzle the remaining dressing over the duck and salad...将剩下的调料淋在鸭肉和色拉上。\n2. It drizzled off and on all day. 整日在时停时续地下着毛毛雨。"}]},{"day":20,"title":"英语积累Day 20","topic":"生活方式","author":"Leyla Tavas","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/7de322d880724a40a58b8711f66ce40d","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/bANzmaUoLa4?si=J3rUZ6gtZl2WvVrJ","audioSize":"319.0KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-020.m4a","youtubeId":"bANzmaUoLa4","chinese":"不要试图通过拿起手机来唤醒自己，因为这样只会让你一刻不停地玩手机。相信我，我也曾犯过这样的错误。你其实可以准备一个晨间音乐播放列表来代替玩手机，播放几首令你感到放松的歌曲，或者选择一些能激发灵感的书籍来阅读。此外，也可以尝试听听激励人心的博客。这些都能让你以最佳状态开始新的一天。","english":"Don't make the mistake of grabbing your phone to wake yourself up because this just leads you to hourless scrolling. Trust me, I've been there before. So instead, you can make a morning playlist with chill songs and listen to it, or read a book that inspires you. You can also listen to motivational podcasts. All these things get you in the perfect mindset to start the day.","sentences":["Don't make the mistake of grabbing your phone to wake yourself up because this just leads you to hourless scrolling.","Trust me, I've been there before.","So instead, you can make a morning playlist with chill songs and listen to it, or read a book that inspires you.","You can also listen to motivational podcasts.","All these things get you in the perfect mindset to start the day."],"exercise":"Don't make the mistake of 拿起 your phone to wake yourself up because this just leads you to 一刻也停不下来地滑动屏幕. Trust me, 也曾犯过这样的错误. So instead, you can make a morning 播放列表 with 令你感到放松的歌曲 and listen to it, or read 能激发灵感的书籍 you. And here are some I really recommend. You can also listen to 激励人心 podcasts. All these things get you in the perfect 状态 to start the day.","vocabulary":[{"id":"83f15ff9-e88b-438d-a64c-fe3e9dc92625","english":"grab","ipa":"/ɡræb/","chinese":"1. vt. & vi. 抢先, 抢占\n2. vt. 抓取，拿取, 抓住\n3. 对…有好感, 对…产生影响\n4. n. 试图抓取, 有意抢夺","usage":"1. grab 在口语语境中与phone搭配，意思多为“拿起手机（玩）”或“接电话”\n2. He was clumsily trying to grab at Alfred's arms. 他笨手笨脚地想抓住艾尔弗雷德的手臂。"},{"id":"e083f5ef-34c2-49ef-9695-fb135a55f9fa","english":"lead to","ipa":"","chinese":"导致；通向","usage":"He warned yesterday that a pay rise for teachers would lead to job cuts.\n他昨天警告说，给教师们加薪会导致职位的裁减。"},{"id":"45d8dc05-ab66-419a-ab4e-6191317b1544","english":"scroll","ipa":"/skrəʊl/","chinese":"1. v. (在屏幕上)滚动(文档),滚屏\n2. n. (带有文字的)卷轴，长纸卷\n3. n. (绘制或雕刻的)涡卷形装饰","usage":"1. I scrolled down to find 'United States of America'. 我向下滚动文档搜索“美利坚合众国”。\n2. Ancient scrolls were found in caves by the Dead Sea. 死海旁边的山洞里发现了古代的卷轴。"},{"id":"3c026c28-c9ad-494d-88cd-9ea091bc99ad","english":"hourless","ipa":"","chinese":"adj．无时间限制的，无时辰的：没有特定时间或时限的。","usage":"Their conversation was so engaging that it felt hourless. 他们的谈话如此引人入胜，让人觉得时间无关紧要。”"},{"id":"4fe94444-2f2f-4846-8385-55d4fa2510c7","english":"I've been there before","ipa":"","chinese":"我曾经经历过类似的情况；我以前也有过这样的经历","usage":"I know what it feels like to lose a job unexpectedly. I've been there before. 我知道突然失去工作的感觉。我以前也有过这样的经历。"},{"id":"0fa13be8-e4fa-41e5-aba6-eb859332d60e","english":"instead","ipa":"/ɪn'sted/","chinese":"1. 代替…;而不是…；\n2. 作为替代;反而;相反地；","usage":"1. She had to spend nearly four months away from him that summer, instead of the usual two... 那个夏天她被迫离开他将近四个月而不是通常的两个月。\n2. He reached for the wine but did not drink, pushed it, instead, across the table towards Joanna...他伸手拿酒却没有喝,而是把它推给了坐在桌子对面的乔安娜。"},{"id":"9541b4ed-487d-430c-b43d-069432356138","english":"playlist","ipa":"","chinese":"1. n. 电台的音乐播放表\n2. v. 把…排入播放表；","usage":"1. Radio 1's playlist is dominated by top-selling youth-orientated groups. 广播一台主要播放一些面向年轻人的乐团所演唱的畅销曲目。\n2. We've playlisted many artists like Beth Orton who got picked up down the line by others. 我们把很多像贝丝·奥顿这样的艺术家纳入了播放表，他们之后也逐渐为其他人所认识。"},{"id":"af8d3720-116a-4200-bd24-56e9983b40a2","english":"chill","ipa":"/tʃɪl/","chinese":"1. v. 使冷却;使凉下来;冷藏；\n2. adj. 轻松的、放松的、冷静的、舒适的","usage":"1. Chill the fruit salad until serving time... 把水果色拉冰镇一下，吃的时候再拿出来。\n2. Tonight, let's just stay home, order some pizza, and listen to chill songs by the fireplace. 今晚，让我们只是待在家里，点些比萨，然后在壁炉旁听一些轻松的歌曲。"},{"id":"cc483d70-b5df-4557-bf39-4c0ffb689c74","english":"inspire","ipa":"/ɪnˈspaɪə(r)/","chinese":"1. v. 激励;鼓舞;驱使；\n2. v. 启发;使产生灵感和热情\n3. v. 作为…的为灵感来源;是…的原型；","usage":"Our challenge is to motivate those voters and inspire them to join our cause...我们面临的挑战是如何调动那些选民的积极性并鼓励他们加入我们的事业。"},{"id":"e8d20a52-fe64-4cf9-8b7f-373e98996cd6","english":"motivational","ipa":"/ˌməuti'veiʃənəl/","chinese":"adj. 动机的,有关动机的","usage":"What about the motivational side of things? 关于激励的那方面是怎样的？"},{"id":"89dbc999-df59-414b-bb5e-2de0afe386b6","english":"mindset","ipa":"/ˈmaɪndset/","chinese":"1. n. 思维模式;思想倾向；\n2. 心态","usage":"The greatest challenge for the Americans is understanding the mindset of Eastern Europeans...\n对于美国人来说，最大的挑战在于理解东欧人的思维方式。"}]},{"day":21,"title":"英语积累Day 21","topic":"生活方式","author":"Zhirelle","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/c239c5a5f7a4417c91536d5f14b2fd04","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/rZH8lnKpoGc?si=H251FTsgstmHRXdP","audioSize":"419.3KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-021.m4a","youtubeId":"rZH8lnKpoGc","chinese":"今年，我打算尝试每天早上都以写感恩日记开始。我只是非常想在开始显化愿望之前写一些我感激的事情，昨晚我花了一整晚做了一个愿景板，我待会就给你们展示一下。我还在圣诞节收到了这个——薰衣草枕头喷雾。我一直都想试试这款产品，我觉得它会对我的睡眠帮助很大。但是我昨晚忘了喷，所以今天早上喷了一下，应该能为早上写日记营造平静的氛围。","english":"I am gonna try and start this year every morning with a gratitude journal entry. I really just want to write about things that I'm grateful for before I start manifesting and I created a vision board all last night, so I'll show you guys that in a minute. I also just got this for Christmas. It's lavender pillow mist. I've been wanting to try this for so long. I think it's going to help so much with my sleep. But I forgot to spray it on last night, so I just did it this morning and it should set the mood for a calming journaling experience this morning.","sentences":["I am gonna try and start this year every morning with a gratitude journal entry.","I really just want to write about things that I'm grateful for before I start manifesting and I created a vision board all last night, so I'll show you guys that in a minute.","I also just got this for Christmas.","It's lavender pillow mist.","I've been wanting to try this for so long.","I think it's going to help so much with my sleep.","But I forgot to spray it on last night, so I just did it this morning and it should set the mood for a calming journaling experience this morning."],"exercise":"I am gonna try and start this year every morning with a 感恩日记. I really just want to write about things that I'm grateful for before I start 显化愿望 and I created a 愿景板 all last night, so I'll show you guys that 待会. I also just got this for Christmas. It's lavender pillow 喷雾. I've been wanting to try this for so long. I think it's going to help so much with my sleep. But I forgot to 喷 last night, so I just did it this morning and it should 营造氛围 a calming journaling experience this morning.","vocabulary":[{"id":"044ca124-9316-45e8-b445-4b9ff8836835","english":"start with","ipa":"","chinese":"以…开始","usage":"We are starting with a political crisis. 我们首先从一场政治危机开始。"},{"id":"a91291ec-521f-4809-93a9-07207bfae255","english":"entry","ipa":"/ˈentri/","chinese":"1. n. 入口；进入；登记；\n2. 日志、日记或记录本中的一个条目或一篇文章","usage":"I wrote a gratitude journal entry today, expressing my appreciation for the support of my friends, the beauty of nature surrounding me, and the opportunity to pursue my passions. 今天我写了一篇感恩日志，表达了对朋友们的支持、身边自然美景以及追求激情的机会的感激之情。"},{"id":"d3033177-b9b1-4ac7-bce4-d0ce6a0ff181","english":"in a minute","ipa":"","chinese":"一会儿","usage":"All right. See you in a minute. 好的 待会儿见。"},{"id":"d42ff1f5-c278-440b-b6a6-95afa80c77c6","english":"manifest","ipa":"/ˈmænɪfest/","chinese":"1. vt. 证明，表明；显示\n2. vi. 显示，出现\n3. n. 旅客名单；载货单，货单\n4. adj. 明白的；显然的，明显的\n5. 在这里翻译为“显化”意为通过改变自己内心的想法和潜意识，从而使得想法映射到现实，而成为现实的过程，叫做显化。","usage":"1. He doesn't manifest much interest in his his studies. 他表现出对学业没多大兴趣。\n2. That is manifest to all of us. 那对我们大家来说是显而易见的。"},{"id":"ca2a63af-9789-4b69-b1b0-88282839193f","english":"vision board","ipa":"","chinese":"愿景板","usage":"I created a vision board with images of my dream house, travel destinations, and career aspirations. 我制作了一个愿景板，上面贴着我梦想的房子、旅行目的地和职业抱负的图片。”"},{"id":"daf66295-3767-4746-b0b2-5f3b069b52ea","english":"lavender","ipa":"/ˈlævəndə(r)/","chinese":"1. n. 淡紫色；薰衣草\n2. adj. 淡紫色的\n3. vt. 用熏衣草熏","usage":"The air was fragrant with lavender空气中弥漫 薰衣草香。"},{"id":"c7256031-4c46-4fa8-8a6d-7b5263b81949","english":"mist","ipa":"/mɪst/","chinese":"1. n. 薄雾\n2. 视线模糊不清\n3. vt. & vi. (使)蒙上薄雾, (使)模糊","usage":"at that moment the mist parted. 那时薄雾散开了。\nthe mists of the past. 模糊往事"},{"id":"76d39cd3-7ee0-4460-a405-47f93ac3f3d9","english":"spray","ipa":"/spreɪ/","chinese":"1. n. 水沫；喷雾；喷雾器\n2. vt. 喷射\n3. vi. 喷","usage":"1. spray drying 喷雾干燥\n2. water spray 喷雾，喷水；水喷雾\n3. He sprayed water over the flowers. 他把水喷在花上。"},{"id":"6e2c27cc-3def-4664-8322-30c60135b8c5","english":"set the mood for","ipa":"","chinese":"创造或塑造特定情绪或氛围","usage":"I lit some scented candles to set the mood for a relaxing evening at home. 我点燃了一些香薰蜡烛，营造出家中放松的氛围。"}]},{"day":22,"title":"英语积累Day 22","topic":"情感成长","author":"Sydney Serena","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/556215e3dcdf40488fd3f3f585cb10c4","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/Qk0uFJ-hvP0?si=O9fo1-a6HnBG3ZLY","audioSize":"349.2KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-022.m4a","youtubeId":"Qk0uFJ-hvP0","chinese":"坐在房间里，闭上眼睛，设想一下理想中的自己。对事物进行想象确实可以成为显化自我的一种方式。我甚至为自己制作了一个实体愿景板。也许你正面临紧迫的情况，或是和某人起争执，或是经历分手，你的情绪占了上风，特别想以某种不妥当的方式处理问题。退一步，深呼吸，思考一下内心高阶版本的自我会如何处理这种情况。","english":"Sit down in a room, close your eyes, and envision the ideal version of yourself. Visualizing things really can be a form of manifesting for yourself. I even made a physical vision board for myself. Maybe you're in a pressing situation or like an argument with somebody, a breakup, and your emotions to take over and you really want to handle something a certain way that might not be the best. Taking a step back, taking a deep breath, and thinking about how the highest version of yourself would handle the situation.","sentences":["Sit down in a room, close your eyes, and envision the ideal version of yourself.","Visualizing things really can be a form of manifesting for yourself.","I even made a physical vision board for myself.","Maybe you're in a pressing situation or like an argument with somebody, a breakup, and your emotions to take over and you really want to handle something a certain way that might not be the best.","Taking a step back, taking a deep breath, and thinking about how the highest version of yourself would handle the situation."],"exercise":"Sit down in a room, close your eyes, and 设想 the 理想中的自己. 想象 things really can be a form of manifesting for yourself. I even made a 实体 vision board for myself. Maybe you're in a 紧迫的 situation or like an argument with somebody, a breakup, and your emotions to 占了上风 and you really want to 处理 something a 某种 way that might not be the best. Taking a step back, taking a deep breath, and thinking about how the highest version of yourself would handle the situation.","vocabulary":[{"id":"200f8254-55be-4889-9224-4c1510347d77","english":"envision","ipa":"/ɪnˈvɪʒn/","chinese":"vt. 想像,展望","usage":"And though I had very high expectations, and though I envisioned success. 尽管我期望很高，尽管我预想我能成功。"},{"id":"41a2cc78-1292-408d-85bf-1f87b09aff73","english":"ideal version of oneself","ipa":"","chinese":"描述一个人在自我想象或期望中的最理想状态","usage":"Everyone should strive to become the ideal version of themselves. 每个人都应该努力成为他们心中的理想自己。"},{"id":"e6a9b044-9a08-42ab-aa35-219db2ff4b1c","english":"Visualize","ipa":"/ˈviʒuəlaiz/","chinese":"vt. 在脑中使(某人或某物)形象化, 设想, 想像","usage":"it is not easy to visualize the future.想像未来并非易事。"},{"id":"62531c28-6933-4c5c-929e-75bff65a93c0","english":"physical","ipa":"/ˈfɪzɪkl/","chinese":"adj. 实体的，物质的；物理的；身体的；","usage":"她在墙上挂了一张实体的愿景板，上面贴满了她想要实现的目标和梦想。She hung a physical vision board on the wall, filled with her goals and dreams she wants to achieve."},{"id":"5ee7248f-ae3d-407d-99ed-d3cec7c696cf","english":"pressing","ipa":"/ˈpresɪŋ/","chinese":"adj. 紧迫的；迫切的；恳切的","usage":"1. problems pressing for solution 急待解决的问题\n2. a pressing invitation. 恳切的邀请"},{"id":"3b8155bd-e7d3-4a03-8f78-0d26c7995baf","english":"take over","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 接手；接管\n2. 控制；主导","usage":"1. When you feel angry or upset, it's best not to let your emotions take over your decisions. 当你感到愤怒或沮丧时，最好不要让情绪控制你的决定。\n2. He's kind of grooming me to take over. 他打算栽培我日后接手公司。"},{"id":"4cb7677f-193e-41c9-abd5-08d1a35f3129","english":"handle","ipa":"/ˈhændl/","chinese":"1. n. 柄；把手；手感；口实\n2. vt. 买卖；处理；操作；触摸；运用\n3. vi. 易于操纵；搬运","usage":"1. handle with 处理\n2. door handle 门把手\n3. get a handle on [口语]控制，掌握"},{"id":"f6ec55ad-a137-477d-a70a-1b6baf473191","english":"certain","ipa":"/ˈsɜːtn/","chinese":"1. adj. 肯定的，无疑的；有把握的；确定的\n2.（不提及细节时用）某事，某人，某种\n3. pron. （不提及人或事物的名称时用）某些，一些，若干","usage":"1. a certain extent 一定程度上\n2. a certain degree 到某种程度\n3. for certain 肯定地；确凿地\n4. certain level 某一水平"}]},{"day":23,"title":"英语积累Day 23","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Amanda Ekstrand","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/02101b19a8ac4cdbbe5a70a06db5d525","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/XWXBsfSW5MU?si=PDjoknlvzTr6j7nJ","audioSize":"744.4KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-023.m4a","youtubeId":"XWXBsfSW5MU","chinese":"我需要重新做一下指甲，这只手看起来保持的还不错，只在这个位置有一点剥落。这根手指的整个美甲都脱落了。我打算做粉色镀铬美甲，感觉会很可爱，比做法式美甲要有意思，而且耗时也少一些。我一会儿还想敷个面膜，但这件事不是非做不可，如果我晚上有时间的话再做吧。我还想清理一下化妆刷和化妆包，可能会把它们和衣服一起丢进洗衣机。今天的首饰是可爱的珍珠蝴蝶结项链和耳环。现在我的首饰都戴好了，让我们把头发扎起来，这样就不会碍事了。","english":"I need to redo my nails, this hand still looks pretty good, we got a little chip in here. This hand, this whole nail peeled off. I'm thinking we'll do pink chrome, I feel like that could be cute, something a little fun and a little less time-consuming than doing French tips. And also I want to do a face mask later but that is low on the to-do list like I'll just do it tonight if I have time. And I also want to clean my makeup brushes and clean out my makeup bag like I'll probably just throw it in with my laundry. Here is the jewelry for today, this adorable Pearl bow necklace and these earrings. Now that my jewelry is all on let's put my hair up so it's out of the way.","sentences":["I need to redo my nails, this hand still looks pretty good, we got a little chip in here.","This hand, this whole nail peeled off.","I'm thinking we'll do pink chrome, I feel like that could be cute, something a little fun and a little less time-consuming than doing French tips.","And also I want to do a face mask later but that is low on the to-do list like I'll just do it tonight if I have time.","And I also want to clean my makeup brushes and clean out my makeup bag like I'll probably just throw it in with my laundry.","Here is the jewelry for today, this adorable Pearl bow necklace and these earrings.","Now that my jewelry is all on let's put my hair up so it's out of the way."],"exercise":"I need to redo my nails, this hand still looks pretty good, we got a little 剥落 here. This hand, this whole nail 脱落 . I'm thinking we'll do pink 镀铬, I feel like that could be cute, something a little fun and a little less 耗时 than doing 法式美甲. And also I want to do a 面膜 later but that 但这件事不是非做不可 like I'll just do it tonight if I have time. And I also want to clean my makeup brushes and clean out my makeup bag like I'll probably just throw it in with my laundry. Here is the jewelry for today, this adorable 珍珠蝴蝶结项链 and these earrings. Now that my jewelry is all on let's 把头发扎起来 so 不会碍事.","vocabulary":[{"id":"060fcb3c-cf9a-4d43-9ada-89efaf0652f2","english":"chip","ipa":"/tʃɪp/","chinese":"1. n. 缺口，缺损处\n2. v. 打破；弄缺；被损坏\n3. v. 切下，削下，凿下（碎片、屑片）","usage":"1. This mug has a chip in it. 这缸子有个豁口。\n2. She chipped one of her front teeth. 她锛了一颗门牙。\n3. Chip away the damaged area. 把损坏的部分凿掉。"},{"id":"164bb91e-a85f-47e8-8027-aeb1801a495e","english":"peel off","ipa":"","chinese":"剥掉","usage":"I like to peel off the first layer of my leek. 把大葱最外面的皮剥掉。"},{"id":"a6ccee4a-5b54-4b49-b377-6f7770530216","english":"chrome","ipa":"/krəʊm/","chinese":"铬；铬合金","usage":"chrome plating 镀铬"},{"id":"123e6534-8880-478f-b429-8fac6b625a8f","english":"time-consuming","ipa":"/ˈtaɪm kənsjuːmɪŋ/","chinese":"费时的；耗时间的","usage":"a difficult and time-consuming process 困难而又费时的过程"},{"id":"b5747b6a-d8c2-4675-877c-7b7c8ae915ce","english":"tips","ipa":"/tɪps/","chinese":"尖端；尖儿；端","usage":"1. the tips of your fingers 手指尖\n2. French tips 法式尖美甲"},{"id":"56f4656f-f1f9-4b75-9307-900c8d9da7a9","english":"face mask","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 面膜\n2. 面罩；面具","usage":"1. Face Mask Powder 粉体面膜\n2. Then he realized that their heads were hooded and their faces masked. 接着他才反应过来，他们的脑袋上戴着兜帽，脸上蒙着面罩。"},{"id":"70372913-a437-43a1-9c07-651e28b2134b","english":"necklace","ipa":"/ˈnekləs/","chinese":"项链","usage":"1. diamond necklace 钻石项链\n2. Pearl bow necklace 珍珠蝴蝶结项链"},{"id":"1cffde57-c71a-4b9d-97c7-f77367ff0d21","english":"put one’s hair up","ipa":"","chinese":"把头发扎起来","usage":"She put up your hair: 她把头发扎起来"},{"id":"a37fa7c1-1e71-4ff3-aa87-3b675cc84fef","english":"be out of the way","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 某人已经远离某个位置\n2. 不会妨碍或影响到其他事情或人","usage":"Her car was parked awkwardly, causing it to be out of the way for other vehicles. 她的车停得不太合适，导致其他车辆受到妨碍。"}]},{"day":24,"title":"英语积累Day 24","topic":"生活方式","author":"Anna Neubert","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/ad82415e1f494a55858e009bcd5d82c4","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?si=foQrlDh6su_J6vTA&v=20efEGXwE5I&feature=youtu.be","audioSize":"486.4KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-024.m4a","youtubeId":"20efEGXwE5I","chinese":"我会用清水洗脸，抹上一点保湿霜，让皮肤更加舒适水润，但完整的护肤流程要等到我锻炼结束后再开始。然后就是选出今天的健身装备了。我觉得漂亮的运动装会显著激发健身的动力。我每周大约去健身房四次，我绝对更喜欢早上锻炼而不是晚上。从科学角度来说，举重并不是一项放松的运动，因为它会刺激肾上腺素的分泌。但运动确实能让我内心感到平静。","english":"I splash my face with water, I put on a little bit of moisturizer just so that my skin feels nice and hydrated, but my actual skincare routine does not take place, up until I'm done with my workout. And then it's time to pick out my gym fit of the day. I think a cute outfit for the gym is so essential to boost your motivation. I go to the gym about four times a week, and I 100% prefer an early morning workout over an evening or nighttime workout. Scientifically, weightlifting is not relaxing as it does spike your adrenaline production. But incorporating physical movement is something that brings me inner peace.","sentences":["I splash my face with water, I put on a little bit of moisturizer just so that my skin feels nice and hydrated, but my actual skincare routine does not take place, up until I'm done with my workout.","And then it's time to pick out my gym fit of the day.","I think a cute outfit for the gym is so essential to boost your motivation.","I go to the gym about four times a week, and I 100% prefer an early morning workout over an evening or nighttime workout.","Scientifically, weightlifting is not relaxing as it does spike your adrenaline production.","But incorporating physical movement is something that brings me inner peace."],"exercise":"I 洗 my face with water, I put on a little bit of 保湿霜 just so that my skin feels nice and 水润, but my actual skincare routine does not take place, up until I'm done with my 锻炼. And then it's time to 选出 my gym fit of the day. I think a cute outfit for the gym is so essential to boost your motivation. I go to the gym about four times a week, and I 绝对 prefer an early morning workout over an evening or nighttime workout. Scientifically, 举重 is not relaxing as it does 刺激 your 肾上腺素 production. But incorporating 运动 is something that brings me 内心 peace.","vocabulary":[{"id":"7575d9c8-21d3-4210-a9db-13e9ca378fec","english":"splash","ipa":"/splæʃ/","chinese":"1. vi. 泼洒\n2. vt.把（水、泥等）泼在 … 上\n3. n. 落水声；\n4. We heard the splash when she fell into the pool. 她掉进游泳池时我们听见扑通的一声。","usage":"1. Water splashed onto the floor.\n水哗的一声泼洒在地板上。\n2. He splashed cold water on his face. 他把冷水往脸上泼。"},{"id":"3a64b2a2-7df9-403e-976e-6e6f6972ce2d","english":"moisturizer","ipa":"/ˈmɔɪstʃəraɪze(r)/","chinese":"润肤霜；润肤膏","usage":"After Lucy puts this toner on her face, then she puts on \" some moisturizer. 在露西把这种润肤水涂在脸上之后，她又抹了一层“保湿霜”。"},{"id":"f58e97a9-60f2-4b71-b47b-11d47a0cf195","english":"hydrated","ipa":"/'haɪdreɪtɪd/","chinese":"adj. 含水的,与水结合的","usage":"So, the best thing you can do is keep yourself hydrated and keep yourself rested. 所以，你能做的最好的事情就是让自己保持水分，让自己保持休息。"},{"id":"47fc3344-0d46-45dc-8039-1387409db2dc","english":"workout","ipa":"/ˈwɜːkaʊt/","chinese":"n. 锻炼","usage":"She does a 20-minute workout every morning. 她每天早晨做运动 20 分钟。"},{"id":"886ccf33-91b4-4741-acb8-80bdb99f5dc8","english":"pick out","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 精心挑选\n2. 认出来；辨别出","usage":"1. He picked out the ripest peach for me. 他给我挑了个熟透了的桃子。\n2. See if you can pick me out in this photo. 看你能不能把我从这张照片上认出来。"},{"id":"4d0a398b-6154-4174-8e01-8666d8d8b035","english":"essential","ipa":"/ɪˈsenʃl/","chinese":"完全必要的；必不可少的；极其重要的","usage":"an essential part/ingredient/component of sth\n某事物必不可少的一部分/成分/组成部分"},{"id":"012cd043-13c8-44d8-8e90-73d66ecefa68","english":"100 percent","ipa":"","chinese":"","usage":"表强调，表明说话者没有任何犹豫，百分之百确定"},{"id":"2b5f2024-a52f-4c00-95dd-e32f5a3dfcab","english":"weightlifting","ipa":"/ˈweɪtlɪftɪŋ/","chinese":"n. 举重","usage":"I think in the US, weightlifting has actually really hit the ground running. 我认为在美国，举重实际上已经很有名气了。"},{"id":"bc79b0eb-5076-458f-9750-fc950c332eaf","english":"spike","ipa":"/spaɪk/","chinese":"1. 指突然激增或激发某种感觉或情绪\n2. vi. 迅速升值；急剧增值\n3. n. 猛增；急升\n4. n. 尖状物；尖头；尖刺\n5. vt. 用尖物刺入（或扎破）","usage":"1. The sudden news of her promotion spiked her excitement 她突然得知晋升消息，激起了她的兴奋情绪。\n2. The US dollar spiked to a three-month high. 美元猛然升值到三个月来的最高价。\n3. a spike in oil prices 油价的急剧上涨\n4. a row of iron spikes on a wall 墙头的一排尖铁"},{"id":"5be1ae72-080c-4fba-8e00-31beac376a1e","english":"adrenaline","ipa":"/ə'drenəlin,-li:n/","chinese":"n. 肾上腺素（激动、害怕或愤怒时产生的体内分泌，使心跳加快，提升活动能力）","usage":"The excitement at the start of a race can really get the adrenaline flowing. 比赛起点的兴奋确实能使人热血沸腾。"},{"id":"1663cc0c-4dc3-4445-a3f1-435621c38237","english":"incorporate","ipa":"/ɪnˈkɔːpəreɪt/","chinese":"v. 将 … 包括在内；包含；吸收；使并入","usage":"1. incorporating physical movement 意思是将运动融入到生活中，成为生活方式的一部分。\n2. Many of your suggestions have been incorporated in the plan.\n你的很多建议已纳入计划中。"},{"id":"5f69d3d4-2798-4e70-8aa8-b8b0720334d0","english":"physical movement","ipa":"","chinese":"运动，肢体运动","usage":"Physical movements have no intrinsic emotional meaning. 肢体动作没有内在的情感意义。"},{"id":"231ee26a-0959-432e-95b7-3cceb804cc70","english":"inner","ipa":"/ˈɪnə(r)/","chinese":"1. 里面的；向内的；内部的\n2.  内心的；未表达出来的；隐藏的","usage":"1. inner London 伦敦市中心区\n2. She doesn't reveal much of her inner self. 她不大流露她的内心自我。"}]},{"day":25,"title":"英语积累Day 25","topic":"旅行","author":"Morgan Venn","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/3012093e2bd443979d6b4104a99d4b62","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/uYFtWVv5F3E?si=uD9bOLONtfSH8khd","audioSize":"501.0KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-025.m4a","youtubeId":"uYFtWVv5F3E","chinese":"我们先从马德里飞往米兰，再换乘火车去威尼斯。实际上，飞到米兰比直飞威尼斯要划算得多，所以我们就从米兰搭火车去威尼斯，交通相当方便。我们订了火车商务舱的票，我觉得这钱花的很值。我记得只多花了10或15欧元，但空间非常宽敞，让旅行更加舒适。在寻觅咖啡店的过程中，我们偶然发现了这家酒吧咖啡馆，他们刚把烤好的披萨从烤箱拿出来，看起来太美味了。","english":"We took a flight from Madrid to Milan, and then hopped on a train to Venice. It was actually much more affordable to fly into Milan versus flying into Venice directly. So we just took a train from Milan, which was fairly easy to navigate. We booked business class tickets for the train, which in my opinion were worth it. I think it was only an additional 10 or 15 Euro, but it was so spacious and made the trip so much more comfortable. On my hunt to find coffee we stumbled across this bar cafe and they had just taken this right out of the oven and it looked so good.","sentences":["We took a flight from Madrid to Milan, and then hopped on a train to Venice.","It was actually much more affordable to fly into Milan versus flying into Venice directly.","So we just took a train from Milan, which was fairly easy to navigate.","We booked business class tickets for the train, which in my opinion were worth it.","I think it was only an additional 10 or 15 Euro, but it was so spacious and made the trip so much more comfortable.","On my hunt to find coffee we stumbled across this bar cafe and they had just taken this right out of the oven and it looked so good."],"exercise":"We took a flight from Madrid to Milan, and then 换乘 a train to Venice. It was actually much more 划算 to fly into Milan 比 flying into Venice directly. So we just took a train from Milan, which was fairly easy to 找到车站、乘车方式 . We booked 商务舱的票 for the train, which in my opinion were worth it. I think it was only 多花 10 or 15 Euro, but it was so 宽敞 and made the trip so much more comfortable. 寻觅 find coffee we 偶然发现 this 酒吧咖啡馆 and they had just taken this right out of the oven and it looked so good.","vocabulary":[{"id":"8144763b-6190-4b50-9037-e84725855676","english":"hop on","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 加入某个活动、团体或者项目\n2. 搭载某种交通工具","usage":"The bus is here. Let's hop on! 公交车来了，赶快上车！"},{"id":"9c66e99b-bcdc-45c2-bd44-d7a165056426","english":"affordable","ipa":"/əˈfɔːdəbl/","chinese":"adj. 付得起的，买得起的，不太昂贵的","usage":"affordable prices/housing 付得起的价格；买得起的住宅"},{"id":"6fb19eef-1f28-4f2b-b743-5356c530bf0d","english":"versus","ipa":"/ˈvɜːsəs/","chinese":"比较两种不同想法、选择等）与 … 相对，与 … 相比","usage":"It was the promise of better job opportunities versus the inconvenience of moving away and leaving her friends. 那是较好的就业前景与搬走并远离朋友的不便之间的矛盾。"},{"id":"c010f6d5-cea3-4e44-90b2-244e6f70a6ab","english":"navigate","ipa":"/ˈnævɪɡeɪt/","chinese":"1. v. 导航；确定（船、飞机、汽车等）的位置和方向\n2. vt. 航行；航海；横渡\n3. vt. 找到正确方法（对付困难复杂的情况）\n句中指的是从米兰搭乘火车的过程中，容易找到车站、乘车方式等","usage":"1. How do you navigate your way through a forest? 你怎么才能设法走出森林？\n2. The river became too narrow and shallow to navigate. 河道变得又窄又浅，无法航行。\n3. We next had to navigate a complex network of committees. 我们下一步必须设法使各级委员会予以通过。"},{"id":"3ebeb4f8-c389-4a96-bdda-7ec9a8c6e461","english":"business class tickets","ipa":"","chinese":"商务舱票","usage":"economy class 经济舱\nfirst-class 头等舱"},{"id":"5c35ccc5-504d-4bea-b8ae-0629bf5c5240","english":"additional","ipa":"/əˈdɪʃənl/","chinese":"a. 附加的；额外的；外加的","usage":"1. “an additional 10 or 15 Euro”句中形容词动词化，additional直接用作动词“多花了…”\n2. The government provided an additional £25 million to expand the service. 政府另拨了 2 500 万英镑用于扩展该服务。"},{"id":"69b0485b-2d2e-40ea-bd43-702333b927a5","english":"spacious","ipa":"/ˈspeɪʃəs/","chinese":"a. 宽敞的","usage":"1. a spacious view. 开阔的视野\n2. a spacious apartment; 宽阔的公寓；"},{"id":"e322d7c1-c06a-4069-8452-8e66c5ed351b","english":"On one’s hunt to","ipa":"","chinese":"某人在寻找或追求某物或某种目标","usage":"On his hunt to find the perfect job, he applied to over fifty positions. 他为了找到一个称心如意的工作，投了超过20份简历。"},{"id":"ca2c8327-61f0-4456-bc24-5892716324b9","english":"stumble across","ipa":"","chinese":"偶然发现或碰到某事物或某人","usage":"I was cleaning out the attic and stumbled across some old photographs. 我清理阁楼的时候，偶然发现了一些老照片"},{"id":"c229fe5d-2180-4c0c-812a-c5f0b43835d9","english":"bar/cafe","ipa":"","chinese":"Bar/café：酒咖，是一个结合了酒吧和咖啡厅的概念的场所。在这样的地方，顾客可以享用咖啡、茶、饮料以及酒类饮品，同时也可以点一些小吃或者简餐。这种场所通常提供了一个休闲的环境，让人们可以在不同的时间段里享受不同的氛围和服务","usage":"I met my friends at the bar café last night for some drinks and lively conversation. 昨晚我在酒吧咖啡厅和朋友们碰面，喝了点酒，聊了会天"}]},{"day":26,"title":"英语积累Day 26","topic":"情感成长","author":"Leyla Tavas","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/bea46a5a84b1487981c8a02c8542a7e8","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/nB6X9quQS0Q?si=wGp8fLHFro8sV90r","audioSize":"378.7KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-026.m4a","youtubeId":"nB6X9quQS0Q","chinese":"你不需要取悦任何人，除了你自己。如果有人不喜欢你，没关系。如果有人不回你消息 ，也没关系。你不需要他们的认可，因为你自己就能认可自己。你爱自己的每一个部分，包括你的缺点和优点。在那种状态下，你自然而然地吸引事物来到你身边。人们会被你的正能量所吸引。如果有人不尊重你，那是因为他们自己有问题。这只是他们内心不安全感的投射而已。","english":"You have nobody to impress but yourself. If a certain person doesn't like you, okay. And if a guy didn't text you back, okay. You don't need their validation because you validate yourself. You love every part of you, your flaws, your strengths. And in that state, you attract things naturally to you. People will be drawn to that positive energy. And if someone disrespects you, it's because they have problems themselves. It's merely a projection of their own insecurities.","sentences":["You have nobody to impress but yourself.","If a certain person doesn't like you, okay.","And if a guy didn't text you back, okay.","You don't need their validation because you validate yourself.","You love every part of you, your flaws, your strengths.","And in that state, you attract things naturally to you.","People will be drawn to that positive energy.","And if someone disrespects you, it's because they have problems themselves.","It's merely a projection of their own insecurities."],"exercise":"You have nobody to 取悦 but yourself. If a certain person doesn't like you, okay. And if a guy didn't 回你消息, okay. You don't need their 认可 because you 认可 yourself. You love every part of you, your 缺点, your strengths. And in that state, you attract things naturally to you. People will 被…所吸引 that 正能量. And if someone 不尊重 you, it's because they have problems themselves. It's merely a 投射 of their own 不安全感.","vocabulary":[{"id":"148ae37e-9142-46da-af09-9a23164c6bd3","english":"impress","ipa":"/ɪmˈpres/","chinese":"v.  使钦佩；使敬仰；给 … 留下深刻的好印象","usage":"He impressed her with his sincerity. 他的真诚打动了她。"},{"id":"0cac71bd-4805-4d81-bed5-595ae1a7b578","english":"text sb. back","ipa":"","chinese":"回消息","usage":"Look, I'm sorry I didn't text you back. I just needed some time to think. 听着，抱歉没给你回短信，我只是需要好好想想。"},{"id":"79628949-dcc3-4c98-ab26-3b1799859558","english":"validate","ipa":"/ˈvælɪdeɪt/","chinese":"1. vt. 证实；确认；确证\n2. 使生效；使有法律效力\n3. 批准；确认 … 有效；认可","usage":"1. Time validated our suspicion. 时间证实了我们的怀疑。\n2. Check that their courses have been validated by a reputable organization. 要确保他们的课程获得有声望机构的承认。"},{"id":"56cd4d35-065a-4f40-8fd6-11b628780c8c","english":"flaws","ipa":"/flɔ:/","chinese":"1. n. 错误；缺点\n2. 裂痕；裂隙；瑕疵\n3. （性格上的）弱点，缺点","usage":"1. The argument is full of fundamental flaws. 这段论述充满根本性的错误。\n2. There is always a flaw in the character of a tragic hero. 悲剧主角总有性格上的缺点。"},{"id":"c13409fa-28c2-46fe-994f-20bf2f300c3a","english":"be drawn to","ipa":"","chinese":"被…吸引","usage":"We are drawn to our pets because pets do not lie. 我们被宠物吸引，是因为宠物不会撒谎。"},{"id":"df199f5a-8212-4ff6-9ec3-0c616a696206","english":"positive energy","ipa":"","chinese":"正能量","usage":"They have to learn to accept it and gradually turn this into positive energy. 他们必须学会接受这一切并且逐渐把这转化成正能量。"},{"id":"24482b96-4cd6-4b17-b1d4-cda1dd13be13","english":"disrespect","ipa":"/dɪsrɪ'spekt/","chinese":"1. n. 不尊敬；无礼；轻蔑\n2. vt. 不尊敬；对 … 无礼","usage":"1. No disrespect intended sir. It was just a joke. 先生，绝无不敬之意。这不过是个玩笑而已。\n2.  They were accused of disrespecting the country's flag. 他们被控亵渎国旗。"},{"id":"42e993cc-badd-4ee9-8449-16868e754a4e","english":"projection","ipa":"/prəˈdʒekʃn/","chinese":"1. n. 预测；推断；设想\n2. 投射；放映；投影；放映的影像\n3. 投射（不自觉地把自己的思想等加诸他人）\n4. (思想感情的）体现，形象化","usage":"1. Sales have exceeded our projections. 销售量超过了我们的预测。\n2. the projection of three-dimensional images on a computer screen 在电脑屏幕上显示的立体影像\n3. Sometimes our judgments about others are simply projections of our own fears and anxieties. 有时候我们对别人的判断只是我们自己恐惧和焦虑的一种投射。"},{"id":"c8380c1c-f83f-49aa-8615-7d865223b2e2","english":"insecurity","ipa":"/ˌɪnsɪˈkjʊərɪtɪ/","chinese":"1. n. 不安全；危险\n2. 不牢靠；不稳定\n3. 无把握\n4. 局促不安，心神不定","usage":"1. We all have our fears and insecurities. 我们大家都有各自的恐惧和不安全感。\n2. job insecurity 工作无保障"}]},{"day":27,"title":"英语积累Day 27","topic":"情感成长,旅行","author":"Eva Meloche","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/a889497bc86a475fa7026f2f25efacf8","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/5Iv7hgvaOWs?si=sFf7eYeYEVLC2Nsi","audioSize":"337.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-027.m4a","youtubeId":"5Iv7hgvaOWs","chinese":"我一直在咳嗽。气温变化很大的时候，我就很容易生病。昨天的旅行让我筋疲力尽。我哭得很厉害，所以现在鼻塞得很厉害。我需要恢复精力。一个月来，我不停地奔波，不停地参加各种聚会，不停地奔赴下一个目的地，这让我略微有些倦怠。所以，我发现自己很渴望休息。","english":"I've been coughing a bunch. I get sick really easily when submitted to intense temperature changes. And then yesterday's travel day stressed me out so much. I cried so much, so I have a really stuffy nose. I really need to like rejuvenate. I was experiencing a micro-burnout from being on the go non-stop for a month, partying and always running to the next destination. So, I found myself craving downtime.","sentences":["I've been coughing a bunch.","I get sick really easily when submitted to intense temperature changes.","And then yesterday's travel day stressed me out so much.","I cried so much, so I have a really stuffy nose.","I really need to like rejuvenate.","I was experiencing a micro-burnout from being on the go non-stop for a month, partying and always running to the next destination.","So, I found myself craving downtime."],"exercise":"I've been 一直在咳嗽. I get sick really easily 气温变化很大的时候. And then yesterday's travel day 让我筋疲力尽 so much. I cried so much, so I really 鼻塞. We need to like 恢复精力. I was experiencing a 略微有些倦怠 from being on the 不停地奔波 for a month, partying and always running to the next destination. So, I found myself 很渴望休息.","vocabulary":[{"id":"b204f6ba-9bbe-4920-b815-aebe1a3f8d28","english":"bunch","ipa":"/bʌntʃ/","chinese":"n. 大量；大批","usage":"a bunch of 表示“一捆、一串、一批、一群”"},{"id":"d4b45156-b7ca-4429-968e-ab76648f03cc","english":"submit","ipa":"/səbˈmɪt/","chinese":"1. 句中表示：暴露于；经历\n2. 顺从；屈服；\n3. 提交，（文件、建议等）\n4. 表示；认为；","usage":"1. . She refused to submit to threats. 面对威胁，她拒不低头。\n3. to submit an application/a claim/a complaint 呈递申请书/书面要求；提交控诉书\n4. Counsel for the defence submitted that the evidence was inadmissible. 被告律师认为这一证据不可采纳。"},{"id":"a671ac63-4346-4b73-acd1-b42591cfbe5c","english":"intense","ipa":"/ɪnˈtens/","chinese":"1. a. 很大的；十分强烈的\n2. 严肃紧张的；激烈的\n3. 有强烈感情（或意见、想法）的；尖锐的；热切的","usage":"1. intense heat/cold/pain 酷热；严寒；剧痛\n2. intense competition 激烈的竞争\n3. He's very intense about everything. 他对一切都很热心。"},{"id":"a98597e0-9324-4955-999e-c9761170f1a2","english":"stress out","ipa":"","chinese":"压力过大，紧张","usage":"I try not to stress out when things go wrong. 出问题时，我尽量不紧张。"},{"id":"2ef4bcea-d51f-4724-82c2-a5e7b4181874","english":"stuffy","ipa":"/ˈstʌfi/","chinese":"1. （鼻子）不通的，堵住的；鼻塞的\n2. 闷热的；闷人的；通风不畅的\n3. 一本正经的；古板的；无聊的；保守的","usage":"1. a stuffy nose. 堵住的鼻子\n2. a stuffy lecture. 枯燥无味的演讲\n3. she's stuffy and old-fashioned. 她古板又守旧。"},{"id":"57b5c88b-278c-4cb7-bb65-11e05cedbf4e","english":"rejuvenate","ipa":"/rɪˈdʒuːvəneɪt/","chinese":"vt. 使年轻；使更有活力","usage":"The mountain air will rejuvenate you. 山里的空气会使你恢复活力。"},{"id":"6884d172-785c-417f-836c-91268d59033a","english":"burnout","ipa":"/'bɜːnaʊt/","chinese":"精疲力竭；过度劳累","usage":"Many students have burnout after taking exams. 考试过后许多学生筋疲力尽。"},{"id":"bbe48c9c-7dfc-48d1-b074-846b4b8369e7","english":"non-stop","ipa":"/'nɔn'stɔp/","chinese":"1. 不间断的；不停的\n2. 直达的；不在途中停留的","usage":"1. non-stop entertainment/work 连续不断的娱乐/工作\n2. a non-stop flight to Tokyo 到东京的直达航班"},{"id":"c71f0616-07f6-470c-9e7f-4c41c72a3ef0","english":"crave","ipa":"/kreɪv/","chinese":"1. v. 渴望；热望\n2.  恳求；请求","usage":"1. She has always craved excitement. 她总盼望得到刺激。\n2. I must crave your pardon. 我必须恳求您原谅。"},{"id":"66b5f7c0-1885-4a1c-88f3-65d7f5c2b0eb","english":"downtime","ipa":"/'daʊntaɪm/","chinese":"1. n. （尤指计算机的）停机时间，停止运行时间\n2. 停工；休息","usage":"Everyone needs a little downtime. 大家都需要休息一下。"}]},{"day":28,"title":"英语积累Day 28","topic":"生活方式","author":"Anna Neubert","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/f38437995f4042d5ae38139d5256e743","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PLo0x7dFHc&list=WL&index=5","audioSize":"469.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-028.m4a","youtubeId":"4PLo0x7dFHc","chinese":"我花了两年的时间才弄清楚自己喜欢什么运动，以及哪种运动能让身体感觉舒适。比如说，我发现自己并不是跑步爱好者，更喜欢散步、远足。因此，与其强迫自己去做跑步那种剧烈、高强度的有氧运动，我觉得每天进行较长时间的散步更容易坚持。我并不是说，因为觉得改变运动习惯很有趣，所以有一天我可能会开始跑步；我想说的是，究竟选择哪种运动方式，完全取决于你觉得哪种运动让你感觉有活力。","english":"It took me a good 2 years to figure out what exercises I enjoyed doing and what made my body feel good. For example, I know that I'm not a runner, I'm more of a walker. So instead of forcing myself to do that intense, high-level cardio of running, I find it a lot more maintainable to go on longer walks every day. That's not to say that one day I might get into running because I think it's so fun to switch up your workout routine. But the point I'm trying to make is it's up to you on what kind of exercises you do to feel active.","sentences":["It took me a good 2 years to figure out what exercises I enjoyed doing and what made my body feel good.","For example, I know that I'm not a runner, I'm more of a walker.","So instead of forcing myself to do that intense, high-level cardio of running, I find it a lot more maintainable to go on longer walks every day.","That's not to say that one day I might get into running because I think it's so fun to switch up your workout routine.","But the point I'm trying to make is it's up to you on what kind of exercises you do to feel active."],"exercise":"It took me a good 2 years to 弄清楚 what exercises I enjoyed doing and what made my body feel good. For example, I know that I'm not a runner, I'm 更喜欢 walker. So instead of forcing myself to do that 剧烈, 高强度的有氧运动 of running, I find it a lot more 容易坚持 to go on longer walks every day. 我并不是说 one day I might 开始 running, because I think it's so fun to 改变 your workout routine. 我想说的是 it's 取决于你 on what kind of exercises you do to feel active.","vocabulary":[{"id":"524f7aa7-130a-4e23-b287-cc5dbf6f5bf6","english":"figure out","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 弄懂；弄明白；\n2. 计算（数量或成本）","usage":"1. I can't figure out how to do this. 我弄不懂怎样做这件事。\n2. Have you figured out how much the trip will cost? 旅行要花多少费用你算出来没有？"},{"id":"32ed2598-23ce-499f-9c67-6b441ec67cda","english":"more of a/an + n….","ipa":"","chinese":"数量或程度上“更（像/是）……”","usage":"The big surf proved even more of a challenge for Bali. 大浪对巴利更有挑战性"},{"id":"37b81a90-256f-4e1d-b104-db054d8063ac","english":"intense","ipa":"/ɪnˈtens/","chinese":"a. 十分强烈的；剧烈的","usage":"A serious toothache is an intense pain. 严重的牙痛是一种剧烈的疼痛。"},{"id":"2f2e645f-4638-400a-8eb9-b5c405e7814b","english":"cardio","ipa":"/kɑːdiəʊ/","chinese":"n. 健心运动/有氧运动","usage":"Cardio is the answer if you want to lose weight. 想减肥就得做有氧运动。"},{"id":"9d89c3d5-6d37-4549-b5a3-e644444439b6","english":"maintainable","ipa":"/mein'teinəbl/","chinese":"a. 可维持的","usage":""},{"id":"80793f85-c08c-44c6-b746-8bdc21b37a94","english":"That's not to say that…But the point I'm trying to make is","ipa":"","chinese":"我并不是说...而是想说...","usage":""},{"id":"1f10623a-4a5b-454f-8a35-53a3e782c91a","english":"get into","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 对 … 产生兴趣；\n2. 开始（某事）","usage":"1. I'm really getting into jazz these days. 我最近真的开始喜欢爵士乐了。\n2. I got into conversation with an Italian student. 我与一位意大利学生谈了起来。"},{"id":"401ca919-7f03-4587-b617-c863fe4870b6","english":"switch up","ipa":"","chinese":"切换","usage":"Had to switch up look at things different, see the bigger picture. 换一个不同的角度，看看更广阔的世界。"},{"id":"8cf5754a-2ca3-47dc-8af2-feb8c15e1a74","english":"be up to sb.","ipa":"","chinese":"由 … 决定","usage":"Shall we eat out or stay in? It's up to you. 咱们是到外面吃饭还是待在家里？你决定吧。"}]},{"day":29,"title":"英语积累Day 29","topic":"生活方式","author":"Anna Neubert","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/3edf9d6bc5b44139a98d3557176c3bad","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PLo0x7dFHc&list=WL&index=5","audioSize":"384.8KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-029.m4a","youtubeId":"4PLo0x7dFHc","chinese":"如何判断一天当中应该什么时候健身？这主要取决于个人偏好，但从科学角度来看，一个重要因素是自然昼夜节律。每个人都有自己的一套生物钟，以及一天中精力更充沛或精力稍显不足的时候。这被称作“时间类型”，也就是身体对睡眠时间和清醒时间的自然偏好。有四种类型，但我记住的最容易的区分方法是：判断自己到底是“早起的鸟儿”还是“夜猫子”。","english":"How do you figure out what time of day you should work out? It all comes down to personal preference, but scientifically, a big factor is your natural circadian rhythm, and everyone has a different set body clock and a time of day where they have more energy or less energy. This is called your “chronotype”, which is your body's natural preference for sleep and alertness. There are four categories, and the easiest way I remember it is whether or not you are an early bird or a night owl.","sentences":["How do you figure out what time of day you should work out?","It all comes down to personal preference, but scientifically, a big factor is your natural circadian rhythm, and everyone has a different set body clock and a time of day where they have more energy or less energy.","This is called your “chronotype”, which is your body's natural preference for sleep and alertness.","There are four categories, and the easiest way I remember it is whether or not you are an early bird or a night owl."],"exercise":"How do you 判断 what time of day you should 健身? It all 取决于 个人偏好, but scientifically, a big factor is your natural 昼夜节律, and everyone has a different set 生物钟 and a time of day where they have more energy or less energy. This is called your “时间类型”, which is your body's natural preference for sleep and 清醒时间. There are four categories, and the easiest way I remember it is whether or not you are “早起的鸟儿”还是“夜猫子”.","vocabulary":[{"id":"518f1d81-5c36-4edf-91bb-700cb4021fc3","english":"work out","ipa":"","chinese":"锻炼身体；做运动","usage":"I work out regularly to keep fit. 我经常做运动以保持健康。"},{"id":"6109b7ab-755f-4297-b7b9-fdba58395bf2","english":"come down to","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 可归结为；\n2. 取决于","usage":"1. What it comes down to is, either I get more money or I leave. 归结起来就是：不给我加薪，我就辞职。\n2. And again, this comes down to culture. 再次强调，这取决于文化。"},{"id":"40fbd267-e0a2-4ff1-86cc-93e5eeb29162","english":"preference","ipa":"/ˈprefrəns/","chinese":"n. 偏爱；爱好；喜爱","usage":"It's a matter of personal preference. 那是个人的爱好问题。"},{"id":"bd61002a-aaf5-4749-8bf5-6f39d5f15375","english":"circadian","ipa":"/sɜː'keɪdɪən/","chinese":"a.（每 24 小时人或动物体内变化）昼夜节律的，生理节奏的","usage":"upset sb.’s circadian clock 扰乱某人的生物钟"},{"id":"85f48195-343c-48d7-9e02-40140a8a055c","english":"rhythm","ipa":"/ˈrɪðəm/","chinese":"1. n. 节奏；韵律；\n2. 规律；节律","usage":"1. to dance to the rhythm of the music 随着音乐的节奏跳舞\n2. biological/body rhythms 生物/人体节律\n3. a circadian rhythm. 昼夜节律"},{"id":"f81d7737-4f9a-4c41-816b-6686ba6ed24e","english":"body clock","ipa":"","chinese":"（人体）生物钟","usage":"Sleep is regulated by your circadian rhythm, or body clock, located in the brain. 睡眠由脑内的昼夜节律或生理时钟所管理。"},{"id":"426873ee-2aca-4002-8432-9c1335fd6f47","english":"chronotype","ipa":"","chinese":"时间类型","usage":"chrono-词缀：时间+type类型\n所谓“时间类型”（chronotype），指的不仅仅是你的作息时间，还是你的各种原始的活动，如吃饭、睡的“时间表”。它可以用来解释为什么有的人深夜的工作效率就是特别高。"},{"id":"204b05dd-5406-46ff-b1c1-9050f3abb20c","english":"alertness","ipa":"/ə'lə:tnis/","chinese":"n. 警觉性；清醒","usage":"Alcohol causes a loss of judgment and alertness. 酒精使人失去判断力和警觉性。"},{"id":"a65fff19-b766-43a9-b0da-84816322eba5","english":"an early bird  or a night owl","ipa":"","chinese":"“早起的鸟儿”还是“夜猫子”","usage":""}]},{"day":30,"title":"英语积累Day 30","topic":"生活方式","author":"Anna Neubert","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/3a2e913f448b4f71afc47d66c13b0b56","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PLo0x7dFHc&list=WL&index=5","audioSize":"679.2KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-030.m4a","youtubeId":"4PLo0x7dFHc","chinese":"过去我只把运动看作是改变体型的一种方式。但当我单纯为了外貌而锻炼时，往往无法坚持下去。你会失去动力，不断拿自己的身体做比较，对自己评价不高，而这仅仅源于体重就是会日复一日、月复一月地波动，这是很正常的。所以，如果一直只追求外在的改变，最终多少会觉得还是不满意。就我个人而言，每当我感到焦虑或心情有点糟糕时，哪怕只是在外面散个步，都会感觉好多了。在阳光下锻炼会自然提高体内的血清素，这是一种能影响心情的激素。运动本身也会产生内啡肽，从整体上改善心情，减轻压力。","english":"I used to only see exercise as being something about physically changing the look of my body. When I say exercise for appearance purposes never lasts. You'll lose motivation, you'll constantly be comparing your body, and thinking poorly of yourself because it's normal for your body to fluctuate in weight day to day, month to month. So if you're constantly looking for physical change, you end up feeling kind of unfulfilled. I know personally, whenever I'm feeling anxious or a little moody, going for even just a light walk outside helps me feel so much better. Working out in the sunshine naturally increases your serotonin, which is a hormone that affects your mood. Exercise itself also produces endorphins, which overall boosts your mood and reduces stress.","sentences":["I used to only see exercise as being something about physically changing the look of my body.","When I say exercise for appearance purposes never lasts.","You'll lose motivation, you'll constantly be comparing your body, and thinking poorly of yourself because it's normal for your body to fluctuate in weight day to day, month to month.","So if you're constantly looking for physical change, you end up feeling kind of unfulfilled.","I know personally, whenever I'm feeling anxious or a little moody, going for even just a light walk outside helps me feel so much better.","Working out in the sunshine naturally increases your serotonin, which is a hormone that affects your mood.","Exercise itself also produces endorphins, which overall boosts your mood and reduces stress."],"exercise":"I used to only see exercise as being something about physically changing the look of my body. When I say exercise for 外貌 purposes never lasts. You'll lose motivation, you'll constantly be comparing your body, and 对…评价不高 yourself because it's normal for your body to 波动 in weight day to day, month to month. So if you're constantly looking for physical change, you 最终 feeling kind of 不满意.  I know personally, whenever I'm feeling anxious or a little 心情有点糟糕, going for even just a 哪怕只是在外面散个步 outside helps me feel so much better. Working out in the sunshine naturally increases your 血清素, which is a 激素 that affects your mood. Exercise itself also produces 内啡肽, which overall boosts your mood and reduces stress.","vocabulary":[{"id":"6cb6f7a4-3a7e-488a-88ae-d9dd37baa625","english":"appearance","ipa":"/əˈpɪərəns/","chinese":"n.  外貌；外观;","usage":"She had never been greatly concerned about her appearance. 她从来不怎么注重外貌。"},{"id":"6bb1e729-c8e2-4e6c-9336-f57e1c78dc75","english":"thinking poorly of","ipa":"","chinese":"贬低…","usage":""},{"id":"04494ab8-c591-4e23-8176-96de1038671f","english":"fluctuate","ipa":"/ˈflʌktʃueɪt/","chinese":"vi. （大小、数量、质量等）波动；（在 … 之间）起伏不定","usage":"My mood seems to fluctuate from day to day. 我的情绪似乎天天在变。"},{"id":"5ffa6a4f-a434-4cbe-949e-0d742ebd7771","english":"end up","ipa":"","chinese":"最终成为；最后处于","usage":"I ended up doing all the work myself. 结果所有的活儿都是我一个人干了。"},{"id":"5d94d5d7-016f-44f7-8612-0ba958686068","english":"unfulfilled","ipa":"/ʌnfʊl'fɪld/","chinese":"a. 未满足的；未实现的；","usage":"unfulfilled ambitions/hopes/promises, etc. 未实现的抱负、希望、诺言等"},{"id":"939a1742-ae01-4cc6-bf6b-87c8c7f7b3be","english":"moody","ipa":"/ˈmuːdi/","chinese":"1. a. 情绪多变的；喜怒无常的\n2. 脾气坏的；郁郁寡欢的","usage":"1. Moody people are very difficult to deal with. 喜怒无常的人很难打交道。\n2. Why are you so moody today? 你今天怎么这么闷闷不乐啊？"},{"id":"45fe63a2-e5a2-4ed1-9ca6-e777753cc7ab","english":"light","ipa":"/laɪt/","chinese":"1. a. 轻松的；容易做的\n2. 轻的","usage":"some light housework 一些轻松的家务活"},{"id":"f61df74d-4b2c-466c-9258-78c3e16654b1","english":"serotonin","ipa":"/ˌserə'təʊnɪn/","chinese":"血清素（神经递质，亦影响情绪等）","usage":"One widespread impression among the public is that depression is caused by having too little serotonin. 公众普遍认为抑郁症是由血清素过少而引起的。"},{"id":"10d6f091-e579-40ef-9333-9f75165f3a21","english":"hormone","ipa":"/ˈhɔːməʊn/","chinese":"激素；荷尔蒙","usage":"growth hormones 生长激素"},{"id":"e392c3ee-e40b-420b-82d9-5ce67108229c","english":"endorphin","ipa":"/en'dɔːfɪn/","chinese":"内啡肽（内分泌激素，有镇痛作用）","usage":"Endorphins are good. Endorphins are mood elevators. This supposed to make us feel better. 内啡肽是个好东西。内啡肽是情绪升降机。这应该会让我们感觉好一点。"}]},{"day":31,"title":"英语积累Day 31","topic":"情感成长","author":"Eva Meloche","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/443189ce77c14b5392f98f74444d1b39","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/5Iv7hgvaOWs?si=kzECJovJIjIl3-yS","audioSize":"355.9KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-031.m4a","youtubeId":"5Iv7hgvaOWs","chinese":"我是一个需要经常分享和倾诉自己感受的人，这样才能每天感觉良好。毫不夸张地说，即使周围没有人，我也会大声讲话。我觉得这样很自在。我问自己，在暑期剩下的时间里，想优先做什么，得出的结论是，我的幸福由我做主，虽然听起来有点老套。这次旅行让我学会了要优先考虑个人幸福，而不是取悦别人。","english":"I'm someone who needs to share a lot and talk about my feelings in order to feel good on a daily basis. Literally, even if there's nobody around, I will talk out loud. I just find it so liberating. I asked myself what I wanted to prioritize during the rest of the summer, coming to the conclusion that I am in charge of my own happiness, as cheesy as that may sound. This trip helped me learn to prioritize my personal well-being over wanting to please others.","sentences":["I'm someone who needs to share a lot and talk about my feelings in order to feel good on a daily basis.","Literally, even if there's nobody around, I will talk out loud.","I just find it so liberating.","I asked myself what I wanted to prioritize during the rest of the summer, coming to the conclusion that I am in charge of my own happiness, as cheesy as that may sound.","This trip helped me learn to prioritize my personal well-being over wanting to please others."],"exercise":"I'm someone who needs to share a lot and talk about my feelings in order to feel good 每天. 毫不夸张地说, even if there's nobody around, I will talk out loud. I just find it so 自在. I asked myself what I wanted to 优先 during the rest of the summer, 得出的结论是 I am 由我做主 my own happiness, as 老套 as that may sound. This trip helped me learn to prioritize my personal well-being over wanting to 取悦 others.","vocabulary":[{"id":"ae0a0a3e-5574-4f64-97ec-73de8b5839ba","english":"on a daily basis","ipa":"","chinese":"每天","usage":"Occur on a daily basis 每天发生"},{"id":"c045849c-7a69-42e8-a706-6d6205c9f081","english":"literally","ipa":"/ˈlɪtərəli/","chinese":"1. adv. 按字面；字面上\n2. 强调事实可能令人惊讶）真正地，确实地","usage":"1. When I told you to ‘get lost’ I didn't expect to be taken literally. 我叫你“滚开”，并没让你按字面意思来理解呀。\n2. There are literally hundreds of prizes to win. 可赢取的奖品真的有好几百份。"},{"id":"d3295a07-db6f-45c4-9421-eecaae133ac0","english":"liberating","ipa":"/ˈlɪb.ə.reɪ.t̬ɪŋ/","chinese":"a. 令人感到自由的；令人畅快的；","usage":"Taking all your clothes off can be a very liberating experience. 脱掉所有衣服能让你感到非常自由自在。"},{"id":"ae37a767-41be-4163-8fa7-0e56bdc49edf","english":"prioritize","ipa":"/praiˈɔritaiz/","chinese":"1. 按重要性排列；划分优先顺序\n2. 优先处理","usage":"1. You should make a list of all the jobs you have to do and prioritize them. 你应该把所有要做的事都列出来，并按轻重缓急排个顺序。\n2. The organization was formed to prioritize the needs of older people. 这个机构是为优先满足老年人的需要而成立的。"},{"id":"5273af18-d52f-43da-b747-a34422c101b6","english":"coming to the conclusion that","ipa":"","chinese":"得出的结论是","usage":"A growing number of people are coming to the conclusion that the civilization in the West is more materially rich but, paradoxically, less and less happy.  越来越多的人开始发现西方文明更多的是物质的丰富，相反，人却变得越来越不快乐。"},{"id":"23c5d015-9cea-4f9a-a31a-0031f4b1d331","english":"be in charge of sth","ipa":"","chinese":"负责某事；负责","usage":"They left the au pair in charge of the children for a week. 他们把孩子留给做换工的照料一周。"},{"id":"cbd9aa8f-50ca-4811-bf15-1577e0bc104f","english":"cheesy","ipa":"/'tʃiːzɪ/","chinese":"1. a. 庸俗的\n2. 虚假的，做作的","usage":"1. cheesy hotel music 庸俗的酒店音乐\n2. She gave a cheesy grin to the cameras. 她冲着镜头做作地一笑。"},{"id":"f6d027e5-8b1b-462d-8ae4-cdf90f9e6158","english":"please","ipa":"/pliːz/","chinese":"使满意；使愉快","usage":"He's a difficult man to please. 他是个难以取悦的人。"}]},{"day":32,"title":"英语积累Day 32","topic":"情感成长,生活方式","author":"Dr Izzy Sealey 凯琦","accent":"英音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/4eebb856741f426cb4fa28d4b0beb49a","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O96AVWwiUbs&t=100s","audioSize":"334.4KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-032.m4a","youtubeId":"O96AVWwiUbs","chinese":"我们都有过这种感觉：在一天中空闲的时候，发现自己会不由自主、漫无目的地拿起手机。社交媒体主宰着我们的生活，而这也绝非巧合。各种帖子层出不穷，我们的大脑接触到大量的信息和歪曲的事实，这不仅使我们的自尊心受挫，还放大了不切实际的攀比，也让我们无法长时间专注。","english":"You know the feeling: you have a free moment in your day and as if on autopilot, you find yourself aimlessly reaching for your phone. Social media dominates our lives, and it's no coincidence. Post after post, our brain is exposed to so much information and a skewed view of reality, reducing our self-esteem, magnifying unrealistic comparisons, stealing our attention spans.","sentences":["You know the feeling: you have a free moment in your day and as if on autopilot, you find yourself aimlessly reaching for your phone.","Social media dominates our lives, and it's no coincidence.","Post after post, our brain is exposed to so much information and a skewed view of reality, reducing our self-esteem, magnifying unrealistic comparisons, stealing our attention spans."],"exercise":"You know the feeling: you have a 空闲的时候 in your day and 不由自主, you find yourself aimlessly拿起手机. Social media 主宰 our lives, and it's no 巧合.  各种帖子层出不穷, our brain 接触到 so much information and a 歪曲的 view of reality, reducing our 自尊心, 放大 unrealistic comparisons, 让我们无法长时间专注.","vocabulary":[{"id":"62d06747-0c64-4da3-a56a-87b94fbc7d4c","english":"on autopilot","ipa":"/'ɔːtəʊ,paɪlət/","chinese":"自动驾驶模式：指在完成某项任务时，不需要过多思考，凭借习惯或经验自动完成。","usage":"You see, for some of you, all of the steps and the skills that go into care tasks run on autopilot. 对一些人来说，这些家务的流程和技能都能自然而然地完成。"},{"id":"cac3c321-a27c-4b5e-9803-738f586396af","english":"aimlessly","ipa":"/'eimlisli/","chinese":"adv. 漫无目的地","usage":"He drifted aimlessly from one job to another. 他漫无目的地换了一份又一份工作。"},{"id":"50fb2636-51ae-4ec6-bbfe-af20b07fc258","english":"reach for phone","ipa":"","chinese":"拿手机","usage":"As I take my gloves off and reach for my phone, I think, \"It can't be that tough to make headphones with two plugs, one for music and one for your cell phone.  当我脱下手套并拿起我的手机时，我想，“做一个有两个插头的耳机，一个用于音乐，一个用于手机，不会那么难吧。”"},{"id":"2146140b-c595-48a4-9cdb-86e3a5e51619","english":"dominate","ipa":"/ˈdɒmɪneɪt/","chinese":"1. v. 支配；控制；\n2. 在 … 中具有最重要（或明显）的特色","usage":"1. As a child he was dominated by his father. 他小时候由父亲主宰一切。\n2. The train crash dominated the news. 火车相撞事故成了最重要的新闻。"},{"id":"46ee13b3-6a08-4f9b-8f49-065a7bcfeda6","english":"coincidence","ipa":"/kəʊˈɪnsɪdəns/","chinese":"n.（令人吃惊的）巧合，巧事","usage":"1. What a coincidence! I wasn't expecting to see you here. 真巧！我没料到会在这里见到你\n2. It's not a coincidence that none of the directors are women. 没有一位董事是女性，这并非偶然。"},{"id":"60239828-23f3-42a4-8651-37de3cac182b","english":"be exposed to","ipa":"","chinese":"暴露于；接触到","usage":"The doctor says your eyes can't be exposed to any light. 医生说你的眼睛不能暴露在光线下。"},{"id":"057e297f-02cd-4064-920b-213c2620e280","english":"skewed","ipa":"/skjuːd/","chinese":"a. 歪曲的；不准确的","usage":"Maybe your world view is a little skewed. 也许你对世界的认知有点不准确。"},{"id":"7cf55a23-4d7f-409c-9fd7-2fd1837a43b1","english":"self-esteem","ipa":"/'selfis'ti:m/","chinese":"n. 自尊（心）","usage":"to have high/low self-esteem 自尊心强/弱"},{"id":"ad6c9099-266f-4eaf-991e-794b1e6dfca3","english":"magnify","ipa":"/ˈmæɡnɪfaɪ/","chinese":"1. v. 放大\n2. 夸大（重要性或严重性）；夸张","usage":"1. an image magnified by a factor of 4 放大了 4 倍的图像\n2. He always magnifies the problems and inconveniences of travel. 他总是夸大旅游的问题和不便。"},{"id":"0df778de-1640-431c-b7fc-1c2a2e1eccd6","english":"span","ipa":"/spæn/","chinese":"n. 持续时间","usage":"I worked with him over a span of six years. 我和他共事达六年之久。"}]},{"day":33,"title":"英语积累Day 33","topic":"情感成长","author":"TheCottageFairy","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/60ad16cc1ef64f5f93ce4ca5423729d4","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7H3D-6nj_dY&list=WL&index=7","audioSize":"377.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-033.m4a","youtubeId":"7H3D-6nj_dY","chinese":"我可以肯定地说，你们分享的故事和信息丰富了我的生活。我非常喜欢社交媒体，但也注意到社交媒体很容易助长匮乏感和攀比心理。我还发现，在社交媒体上很容易将自己的不满或不安全感投射到其他人身上，而不是赋予自己力量来接纳自己，以及明白每个人的成长轨迹都是不同的。","english":"I can say for certain that the stories and messages you’ve shared have enriched my life. I have enjoyed it very much, but have also observed how easy it is for social media to fuel a sense of inadequacy and comparison. I also found that with social media it is easy to project your own dissatisfaction or insecurity onto other people, instead of empowering yourself to embrace who you are and that everyone’s timeline is different.","sentences":["I can say for certain that the stories and messages you’ve shared have enriched my life.","I have enjoyed it very much, but have also observed how easy it is for social media to fuel a sense of inadequacy and comparison.","I also found that with social media it is easy to project your own dissatisfaction or insecurity onto other people, instead of empowering yourself to embrace who you are and that everyone’s timeline is different."],"exercise":"我可以肯定地说 that the stories and messages you’ve shared have 丰富了 my life. I have enjoyed it very much, but have also observed how easy it is for social media to 助长 匮乏感 and comparison. I also found that with social media it is easy to 投射 your own dissatisfaction or 不安全感 onto other people, instead of 赋予自己力量 yourself to 接纳 who you are and that everyone’s 成长轨迹 is different.","vocabulary":[{"id":"8a7e4ee7-7bba-427b-b8c3-ded630ca5bd1","english":"can say for certain","ipa":"","chinese":"可以肯定地说；可以确定的是","usage":"But what I can say for certain is how to get a free audiobook. 但我能确定的是如何获得免费的有声书。"},{"id":"aa8072ff-8865-42ed-b2e2-fce95e9394c6","english":"enrich","ipa":"/ɪnˈrɪtʃ/","chinese":"vt. 充实；使丰富；使饱含（某物）","usage":"The study of science has enriched all our lives. 科学研究丰富了我们的整个生活。"},{"id":"b0ad8f05-57b0-402b-a106-f495323f4ea0","english":"fuel","ipa":"/ˈfjuːəl/","chinese":"vt. 增加；加强；刺激","usage":"Higher salaries helped to fuel inflation. 工资提高刺激通货膨胀"},{"id":"0f376761-0041-4854-816f-1c243535693b","english":"inadequacy","ipa":"/ɪn'ædɪkwəsɪ/","chinese":"n. 不充分；不足；不够","usage":"the inadequacy of our resources 我们的资源的贫乏"},{"id":"e58fb88d-8392-47e6-97c6-af3c2c24944e","english":"project sth onto sb","ipa":"","chinese":"（不自觉地）把（自己的感觉或问题等）投射到别人身上","usage":""},{"id":"8070f057-e96b-4337-bf81-a51920df7c17","english":"insecurity","ipa":"/ˌɪnsɪˈkjʊərɪtɪ/","chinese":"n. 不安全；局促不安","usage":"feelings of insecurity\n不安全感"},{"id":"e5910e2a-9edd-4a7a-b2a2-61ccafd9e417","english":"empower","ipa":"/ɪmˈpaʊə(r)/","chinese":"v. 授权；赋予；增加（某人的）自主权；","usage":"The movement actively empowered women and gave them confidence in themselves. 这场运动使女性更能主动掌握自己的命运，对自己充满信心。"},{"id":"e3cdb76c-41ae-4725-b783-67650bc21c5d","english":"embrace","ipa":"/ɪmˈbreɪs/","chinese":"v. 欣然接受","usage":"embrace a good chance 抓住好时机"},{"id":"d2f2a9b8-169b-4914-a701-8ac554838499","english":"timeline","ipa":"/ˈtaɪmlaɪn/","chinese":"n. 时间线","usage":"Don't give yourself a timeline on when to achieve a dream. 不要给自己一个何时实现梦想的时间表。"}]},{"day":34,"title":"英语积累Day 34","topic":"生活方式","author":"Eva Meloche","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/846977b68e5d46a5aa362a900ec8d2b1","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vesxo3zHUNs&t=603s","audioSize":"400.9KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-034.m4a","youtubeId":"vesxo3zHUNs","chinese":"2 月 16 日早上，我失眠了，这是我从未面临过的情况。我在4 点钟醒来，但无论如何都无法再次入睡。我被论文压得喘不过气来。每次一写作业，我就文思枯竭，这简直令人抓狂。不过幸运的是，当我失眠坐在客厅的时候，目睹了最迷人的日出景色。","english":"On the morning of February 16th, I experienced insomnia, which is not something I've ever really had to deal with. I was up at 4:00 and could not fall back asleep for the life of me. I was consumed with stress about my essays. The writer's block for my assignments was real and freaking dazing confused. The silver lining was I got to witness the most mesmerizing sunrise as I sat unable to shut my eyes in the living room.","sentences":["On the morning of February 16th, I experienced insomnia, which is not something I've ever really had to deal with.","I was up at 4:00 and could not fall back asleep for the life of me.","I was consumed with stress about my essays.","The writer's block for my assignments was real and freaking dazing confused.","The silver lining was I got to witness the most mesmerizing sunrise as I sat unable to shut my eyes in the living room."],"exercise":"On the morning of February 16th, I 失眠了, which is not something I've ever really had to 面临. I was up at 4:00 and could not 再次入睡 无论如何都. I 被压得喘不过气来 about my essays. The 文思枯竭 for my assignments was real and 抓狂. 不过幸运的是 was I got to witness the 最迷人的 sunrise as I sat unable to shut my eyes in the living room.","vocabulary":[{"id":"5536ea82-94a1-4f05-87ad-7bec758d3de3","english":"insomnia","ipa":"/ɪn'sɒmnɪə/","chinese":"n. 失眠（症）","usage":"to suffer from insomnia 失眠"},{"id":"c619268e-f385-4a4f-8c93-36fe0ab66c89","english":"deal with","ipa":"","chinese":"解决；处理；","usage":"to deal with enquiries/issues/complaints 处理各种询问/问题/投诉"},{"id":"a934504b-abbe-418c-b176-f277999e8214","english":"asleep","ipa":"/ə'sliːp/","chinese":"adj. 睡着","usage":"1. fall back asleep 再次入睡\n2. sound asleep 睡得香\n3. fall asleep 入睡\n4. half asleep睡眼惺忪"},{"id":"d7b4421d-e7ca-4426-8d9e-427890a4f01f","english":"for the life of me","ipa":"","chinese":"无论如何","usage":"I couldn’t for the life of me remember his name. 我怎么也想不起他的名字。"},{"id":"4d1dbd6d-afb4-4ea3-810d-afd5f78f5011","english":"consume","ipa":"/kənˈsjuːm/","chinese":"1. vt. 消耗\n2. 吞噬","usage":"1. be consumed by fear 被恐惧吞噬； \n2. be consumed with stress 被压力吞噬；压得喘不过气来"},{"id":"9733127c-eae9-4566-86b1-2396919ebb0e","english":"writer's block","ipa":"","chinese":"文思枯竭","usage":"Gerwig likes to walk, often as a remedy for writer's block. 葛韦格喜欢步行，写作没有思路的时候她就会出去走一走。"},{"id":"b6cfc6dc-023e-4810-ac37-717f29f435b7","english":"block","ipa":"/blɒk/","chinese":"1. n. 块；街区；障碍物；大厦\n2. vt. 阻塞；阻止；限制","usage":"1. After today's heavy snow, many roads are still blocked. 今天下过大雪，很多道路仍然堵塞。\n2. Lack of training acts as a block to progress in a career. 缺乏训练会妨碍事业的发展。"},{"id":"c3f1d2c1-f438-4c0c-a9fd-f2998c4630fe","english":"freaking","ipa":"","chinese":"用以加强语气或表示愤怒","usage":"We got big freaking spiders here! 我们这里有大死人的蜘蛛！"},{"id":"77d97352-cf95-49a4-abc6-c82a74d8ab00","english":"dazing confused","ipa":"","chinese":"使茫然困惑","usage":""},{"id":"f671b130-1c71-45fd-abde-a66dbeb4accd","english":"The silver lining","ipa":"","chinese":"一线希望。\"the silver lining\" 是一个习语，指的是困境或不利情况中的一点积极的或令人鼓舞的方面。它来自于英语习语\"Every cloud has a silver lining\"，意为每朵乌云都有一丝银边。","usage":"The silver lining is this system is not as strong as Hurricane Maria. 不幸中的万幸是这个袭击没有Maria飓风那么强大。"},{"id":"19fc680d-1fdf-4d84-b25b-944c6309340f","english":"mesmerizing","ipa":"/ˈmezməraɪzɪŋ/","chinese":"a. 令人着迷的","usage":"Her performance was mesmerizing.她的表演让人入迷。"},{"id":"fc6e746e-a117-4a93-b6a6-d0a06cf913ed","english":"shut one’s eyes","ipa":"","chinese":"闭眼","usage":"I will be going too fast to look at things, so I'll do shut my eyes. 我会走得太快而看不见的，所以我闭上眼睛"}]},{"day":35,"title":"英语积累Day 35","topic":"情感成长","author":"TheCottageFairy","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/da2d19a6462a478cb2260b62036b625f","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jZB08H8ND8o","audioSize":"624.9KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-035.m4a","youtubeId":"jZB08H8ND8o","chinese":"从那时起，我学到了不少如何在简单生活的同时滋养富足感的经验。当我搬到这里时，没有任何计划在未来再次搬家或旅行，这是一次净化心灵的体验，让我重新定义何为有意义的生活。真正的满足感并不来自物质的获取。悲伤是不容易被治愈的。相反，我发现，要培养快乐的情绪，你必须像对待一颗种子那样对待它。必须细心呵护它，让它生长，并时刻关注它的成长。","english":"Since then I've learned quite a few lessons on how to cultivate a feeling of abundance while living simply. When I moved here without any plans to move or travel again in the future, it was a cathartic experience in which I had to redefine what it was to live a meaningful life. True fulfillment doesn't come from the acquisition of material things. There is no easy cure for sadness. Instead, I find that to cultivate joy, you must treat it like a seed. You must take care of it and let it grow and watch over it.","sentences":["Since then I've learned quite a few lessons on how to cultivate a feeling of abundance while living simply.","When I moved here without any plans to move or travel again in the future, it was a cathartic experience in which I had to redefine what it was to live a meaningful life.","True fulfillment doesn't come from the acquisition of material things.","There is no easy cure for sadness.","Instead, I find that to cultivate joy, you must treat it like a seed.","You must take care of it and let it grow and watch over it."],"exercise":"Since then I've learned quite a few lessons on how to 滋养 富足感 while living simply. When I moved here without any plans to move or travel again in the future, it was a 净化心灵的体验 in which I had to 重新定义 what it was to live a meaningful life. True fulfillment doesn't come from the 获取 of material things. 不容易被治愈 for sadness. Instead, I find that to 培养 joy, you must treat it like a seed. You must take care of it and let it grow and 时刻关注 it.","vocabulary":[{"id":"1831ca81-d23e-4666-9ca9-af728e6ab4e3","english":"cultivate","ipa":"/ˈkʌltɪveɪt/","chinese":"1. vt. 陶冶思想[感情]\n2. 培育，培养","usage":"cultivate a love of art 培养对艺术的热爱"},{"id":"79feaccc-2774-4655-896e-235c1ddb4532","english":"abundance","ipa":"/əˈbʌndəns/","chinese":"n. 大量；富足；充裕","usage":"in abundance 大量；丰盛；充裕"},{"id":"a3f70bb8-875d-4eb9-834e-a54eca5b3045","english":"cathartic-catharsis","ipa":"/kə'θɑːtɪk/","chinese":"a. （情感）宣泄的\n精神净化","usage":"crying is a cathartic release. 哭泣是一种宣泄。"},{"id":"ca635c26-e352-4450-b9a8-72a75957262a","english":"redefine","ipa":"/ˌridɪ'faɪn/","chinese":"vt. 重新定义；使重新考虑","usage":"We need to redefine what we mean by democracy. 我们需要重新考虑我们对民主的理解。"},{"id":"6acf29a0-dd50-469f-b231-cbb676821198","english":"acquisition","ipa":"/ˌækwɪˈzɪʃn/","chinese":"n. 知识、技能等的）获得","usage":"the acquisition of management skills. 管理技能的习得。"},{"id":"bb0811fe-7def-4ded-baf5-e701ca4042b9","english":"watch over","ipa":"","chinese":"照管；监督；","usage":"The soldiers were close watch over the enemies. 士兵们严密注意著敌人的行动."}]},{"day":36,"title":"英语积累Day 36","topic":"旅行","author":"Hannah Elise","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/2a6554bed4d24ed2b6cfad843e21ac3c","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cDhp3escMg8&t=396s","audioSize":"483.5KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-036.m4a","youtubeId":"cDhp3escMg8","chinese":"我真的第一次这么想打开行李箱，把东西放进衣柜，挂起来。因为我会在这里住四个晚上。所以，我真的不想一直从随身行李箱里翻找东西。但首先，让我们来参观一下酒店房间。首先，这是一走进来时的门。然后是一个滤水器。还有一个全身镜。然后，还有这个推拉门，这是浴室，这个超大的花洒。","english":"I actually want to unpack my suitcase for, like, the first time ever and put my stuff in the wardrobe and hang some stuff up. Because I'll be here for four nights. So, I just don't really feel like living out of my carry-on suitcase. But first, let's do a hotel room tour. Starting off here is the door when you first walk in. And then this is a water filter. We've got this full-body mirror. Then, we have this sliding door and this is the bathroom. This massive freaking shower.","sentences":["I actually want to unpack my suitcase for, like, the first time ever and put my stuff in the wardrobe and hang some stuff up.","Because I'll be here for four nights.","So, I just don't really feel like living out of my carry-on suitcase.","But first, let's do a hotel room tour.","Starting off here is the door when you first walk in.","And then this is a water filter.","We've got this full-body mirror.","Then, we have this sliding door and this is the bathroom.","This massive freaking shower."],"exercise":"I actually want to 打开 my suitcase for, like, the first time ever and put my stuff in the 衣柜 and hang some stuff up. Because I'll be here for four nights. So, I just don't really feel like 一直从随身行李箱里翻找东西. But first, let's do 参观一下酒店房间. Starting off here is the door when you first walk in. And then this is a 滤水器. We've got this 全身镜. Then, we have this 推拉门 and this is the bathroom. This 超大的花洒.","vocabulary":[{"id":"83b311d7-237e-4407-aba2-67fe2ff4eaa0","english":"unpack","ipa":"/ˌʌnˈpæk/","chinese":"v. 打开（箱、包等）取；从（箱、包等中）取出","usage":"She unpacked all the clothes she needed and left the rest in the case.她取出所有要穿的衣服，其余的都留在箱子里。"},{"id":"7826950a-381e-4633-9d7d-a2b3f9aa008e","english":"wardrobe","ipa":"/ˈwɔːdrəʊb/","chinese":"n. 衣柜","usage":"a fitted wardrobe 入墙衣柜"},{"id":"97d6be42-04db-4c2e-9e04-66e45c9c8460","english":"live out of","ipa":"","chinese":"靠……生活：依赖某种资源或手段来维持生活。","usage":"1. Live out of a suitcase: 携带简便行李；成天在外奔波\n2. live out of can: 靠罐头食品过日子\n折叠"},{"id":"070a35e8-cc91-46e9-ba42-f2de870a290b","english":"carry-on suitcase","ipa":"","chinese":"随身手提箱","usage":"I have some personal effects in my carry-on suitcase. A wrist watch, a digital camera. This is a laptop computer.  我有一些个人物品在手提箱里，一支手表，一台数码相机。这是一台手提电脑。"},{"id":"6b627f91-18b1-4d74-a864-ffaef7d9f2ad","english":"room tour","ipa":"","chinese":"房间参观","usage":""},{"id":"5c46d4ed-fcda-40fa-b145-0fce6b083b2d","english":"filter","ipa":"/ˈfɪltə(r)/","chinese":"1. n. 滤器；过滤器\n2. v. 过滤","usage":"1. a coffee/water filter 咖啡过滤器；滤水器\n2. My secretary is very good at filtering my calls 我的秘书很会替我过滤电话。"},{"id":"6ccbd6d1-5aff-40a9-b2d5-d95641a371a0","english":"full-body mirror","ipa":"","chinese":"全身镜","usage":""},{"id":"034006e6-af8f-402e-af45-fa27bdca2842","english":"sliding door","ipa":"","chinese":"滑门；推拉门","usage":"People living near Cape Canaveral said their homes shook and sliding doors fell to the ground. 卡纳维拉尔角附近居民表示，当时房屋有震感，推拉门被震倒。"},{"id":"af98690f-590b-4d85-9526-6b1575e1fc69","english":"massive","ipa":"/ˈmæsɪv/","chinese":"1. a. 巨大的\n2. 严重的","usage":"1. a massive rock 一块巨大的岩石\n2. He suffered a massive heart attack. 他的心脏病严重发作了。"},{"id":"592bcdf9-1a8e-47db-af6b-3e2f27001122","english":"freaking","ipa":"","chinese":"用以加强语气或表示愤怒","usage":"We got big freaking spiders here! 我们这里有大死人的蜘蛛！"},{"id":"632467b1-372b-4be6-8644-9e1b7a4ff4f1","english":"shower","ipa":"/'ʃaʊə/","chinese":"n. 淋浴器","usage":"The shower is broken - you'll have to have a bath. 淋浴器坏了——你得用浴缸洗澡了。"}]},{"day":37,"title":"英语积累Day 37","topic":"旅行","author":"Hannah Elise","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/14a5682e08dc4af0ba6800d5443afb05","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eWcg3ncPrAU","audioSize":"377.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-037.m4a","youtubeId":"eWcg3ncPrAU","chinese":"这个房间太舒适了。以至于我们一直睡不醒。房间里有遮光窗帘，让人感觉非常宁静，简直像是个地牢一样。实际上，考虑到时差和昨天漫长的旅行，我现在感觉还不错。我觉得我从上次的错误中吸取了教训。上次因为感觉不饿，我到这儿的第一天就没怎么吃东西。我们得去找点吃的，因为我现在饿得要命。","english":"This room is so cozy. That's why we couldn't wake up. When we have blackout curtains, it just feels so serene. It's literally a dungeon. Actually, considering jet lag and everything, and the long-ass travel day we had yesterday, I feel pretty good right now. And I think I learned from my mistakes last time. Last time I like didn't really eat much the first day I got here because I wasn't hungry. We need to get food, cause I'm freaking starving now.","sentences":["This room is so cozy.","That's why we couldn't wake up.","When we have blackout curtains, it just feels so serene.","It's literally a dungeon.","Actually, considering jet lag and everything, and the long-ass travel day we had yesterday, I feel pretty good right now.","And I think I learned from my mistakes last time.","Last time I like didn't really eat much the first day I got here because I wasn't hungry.","We need to get food, cause I'm freaking starving now."],"exercise":"This room is so 舒适. That's why we couldn't wake up. When we have 遮光窗帘, it just feels so 宁静. It's literally a 地牢. Actually, considering 时差 and everything, and the 漫长的旅行 day we had yesterday, I feel pretty good right now. And I think I 从上次的错误中吸取了教训. Last time I like didn't really eat much the first day I got here because I wasn't hungry. We need to get food, 'cause I'm 饿得要命 now.","vocabulary":[{"id":"cb313ee1-cfd6-477e-b713-4e13a8ea6199","english":"cozy","ipa":"/ˈkəʊzi/","chinese":"a. 温暖舒适的（尤指细小的室内地方）","usage":"1. a cozy little room 温暖舒适的小房间\n2. a cozy feeling 惬意的感觉"},{"id":"1ca51377-b25c-480e-8cf1-bc5c1c2f6d2a","english":"blackout","ipa":"/'blækaʊt/","chinese":"1. n. 透光窗罩（或窗帘\n2. n. 眼前昏黑","usage":"She had a blackout and couldn't remember anything about the accident. 她眼前一黑，那场事故就怎么也想不起来了"},{"id":"58c5dacf-06db-4aa8-847a-2de3d5a0356b","english":"serene","ipa":"/səˈriːn/","chinese":"a. 平静的；宁静的；","usage":"a lake, still and serene in the sunlight 阳光下宁静安谧的湖水"},{"id":"bd107237-a5e7-415a-beeb-419e1c3057fc","english":"dungeon","ipa":"/'dʌn(d)ʒ(ə)n/","chinese":"n. 地牢","usage":"a weird atmosphere in the dungeon 地牢里怪异的气氛"},{"id":"08df7ba1-dd1e-4897-a14b-e62e2d458a81","english":"jet lag","ipa":"","chinese":"n. 时差反应","usage":"I'm just a little tired.It's probably just jet lag. 我有点累 估计是时差还没倒过来吧。"},{"id":"c4fec738-544f-4096-9473-a4658e755a1f","english":"long-ass travel","ipa":"","chinese":"n. 长途旅行","usage":""},{"id":"59c94c5f-8175-4e12-886f-da35c5c42e0c","english":"be starving (for sth)","ipa":"","chinese":"饿得很","usage":"When's the food coming? I'm starving! 食物什么时候上来？我快饿死了！"}]},{"day":38,"title":"英语积累Day 38","topic":"工作职场","author":"Chole Shih","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/2df1122226704e199b36c014eb44b3b2","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/eK9CSHNbZ5Q?si=lXCp_rRWLTPWDUZg","audioSize":"365.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-038.m4a","youtubeId":"eK9CSHNbZ5Q","chinese":"我首先尝试在公司内部转岗。这个过程非常繁琐，要应对各种政策。公司CEO支持我转岗，但他把这件事推给了人力资源部门。然后人力资源主管说：“我支持你，但目前没有岗位空缺”。而当时我的经理甚至因为我提出了这个想法而大声斥责我，说我自私、不专业、不为团队着想。她还说：“你现在想离开就等于是自绝后路\"。所以那个时候我想转岗是不可能的。","english":"I first tried transitioning within the company. It's very bureaucratic and a lot of politics to navigate. My CEO was supportive of the move, but he deferred to HR. Then the HR exec was like, \"I'm supportive, but there isn't any headcount.\" And my manager at the time yelled at me for even bringing this up. She said I was selfish, I was unprofessional, I don't think of the team. She was like, \"You're burning this bridge by trying to leave.\" So then transferring for me was a no-go.","sentences":["I first tried transitioning within the company.","It's very bureaucratic and a lot of politics to navigate.","My CEO was supportive of the move, but he deferred to HR.","Then the HR exec was like, \"I'm supportive, but there isn't any headcount.\"","And my manager at the time yelled at me for even bringing this up.","She said I was selfish, I was unprofessional, I don't think of the team.","She was like, \"You're burning this bridge by trying to leave.\"","So then transferring for me was a no-go."],"exercise":"I first tried 转岗 within the company. It's very 繁琐 and a lot of politics to 应对. My CEO was supportive of the move, but he 推给 HR. Then the 人力资源主管 was like, \"I'm supportive, but there isn't any 岗位（空缺）.\" And my manager at the time yelled at me for even 提出. She said I was selfish, I was unprofessional, I don't think of the team. She was like, \"You're 自绝后路 by trying to leave.\" So then 转岗 for me was a 不可能的.","vocabulary":[{"id":"70802ca9-06f1-4032-b09c-2996abe20970","english":"transition","ipa":"/trænˈzɪʃn/","chinese":"1. n. 过渡；转变；\n2. v. (从某一状态或活动)转变，过渡(到另一状态或活动)","usage":"1. transition period 过渡时期\n2. smooth transition 顺利过渡，平稳过渡\n3. There was a significant decline in the size of the business as the company transitioned to an intellectual property company. 随着公司向知识产权公司转型，其业务规模显著下降。"},{"id":"c44e9125-c41a-4267-a672-d169023ea12f","english":"bureaucratic","ipa":"/ˌbjʊrə'krætɪk/","chinese":"1. a.  官僚的；\n2. 繁文缛节的","usage":"I had a lot of bureaucratic hassle trying to get the information I needed. 为了得到我所需要的信息，我费尽周折应对繁文缛节。"},{"id":"65011e38-0ed9-436f-bff4-0d873359dc38","english":"navigate","ipa":"/ˈnævɪɡeɪt/","chinese":"v.  找到正确方法（对付困难复杂的情况）","usage":"I wanted to know how they personally navigated this dichotomy. 我想知道他们从个人角度是如何处理这种分歧的。"},{"id":"a15d806e-de91-43b8-ab4e-056e8047c98e","english":"defer","ipa":"/dɪˈfɜː(r)/","chinese":"1. v. 推迟；延缓；\n2. 服从某人的意愿, 遵从","usage":"We will defer to whatever the committee decides. 我们遵从委员会的任何决定。"},{"id":"3bc8577f-ee0b-46ce-9eaf-16322055ac53","english":"exec","ipa":"/ɪg'zek/","chinese":"n. 公司的）经理，管理人员","usage":"All the execs are flying coach. 所有主管乘机都只能坐经济舱。"},{"id":"507cd546-d21c-49d7-bf32-cfabb801c965","english":"headcount","ipa":"/'hedkaunt/","chinese":"n. 某一处（或某公司）的人数","usage":"Times were hard, and the company was unwilling to increase the headcount. 艰难时期，公司不愿意增加雇员。"},{"id":"4b048f8a-cc32-462c-a018-536e900b87c8","english":"bring sth up","ipa":"","chinese":"提出（讨论等）","usage":"Bring it up at the meeting. 请将此事在会议上提出。"},{"id":"cb18c9b1-448f-48ec-9f2a-6a04a12be9df","english":"burn your bridges","ipa":"","chinese":"自毁前程，自绝后路","usage":"Think carefully before you resign—you don't want to burn your bridges. 辞职前要三思，你得给自己留条退路。"},{"id":"cfeab494-8b3f-47ef-a3e3-75aaba81fdd3","english":"transfer","ipa":"/trænsˈfɜː(r)/","chinese":"v. （使）调动；~ sb (from … ) (to … )","usage":"Ten employees are being transferred from the sales department. 十名雇员已调离销售部。"},{"id":"5a2eab2b-abdb-479e-a77b-b62eaaba4d93","english":"no-go","ipa":"/'nəu'ɡəu/","chinese":"a. 不可能；不行；","usage":"If the bank won't lend us the money it's no go, I'm afraid. 如果银行不愿贷款给我们，这恐怕就行不通了。"}]},{"day":39,"title":"英语积累Day 39","topic":"工作职场","author":"Chole Shih","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/4130d4cb6b5c4c9395886a4814c415cb","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/sJ5Shzq68Ac?si=EsBZUJiyCvZwmzAO","audioSize":"301.7KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-039.m4a","youtubeId":"sJ5Shzq68Ac","chinese":"但关键在于尽可能多地收集公司信息，了解公司的层级结构和薪酬理念。要了解他们将你安排到哪一层级的岗位。可以询问：“您能解释一下公司各个层级是如何运作的吗？这个职位属于哪一层级？层级是流动变化的吗？团队是如何区分上下级的？”还可以问：“您能展开讲讲薪酬包的构成吗？”","english":"But the key thing here is to gather information the heck out of the company and learn what their level structure and their compensation stance are. Try to see what level they're slating you for. Ask, \"Can you walk through how levels work at the company? What level is this for? Is level flexible? How does the team differentiate this level from the next level?\" Then ask, \"Can you break down how the compensation package is structured?\"","sentences":["But the key thing here is to gather information the heck out of the company and learn what their level structure and their compensation stance are.","Try to see what level they're slating you for.","Ask, \"Can you walk through how levels work at the company?","What level is this for?","Is level flexible?","How does the team differentiate this level from the next level?\"","Then ask, \"Can you break down how the compensation package is structured?\""],"exercise":"But the key thing here is to gather information 尽可能多地 the company and learn what their 层级结构 and their 薪酬理念 are. Try to see what level they're 安排到. Ask, \"Can you 介绍一下 how levels work at the company? What level is this for? Is level 流动变化? How does the team 区分 this level from the next level?\" Then ask, \"Can you 展开讲讲 how the 薪酬包 is structured?\"","vocabulary":[{"id":"618e78fb-d567-481f-8bf7-a19884aff39f","english":"heck","ipa":"/hek/","chinese":"表示略微烦恼或吃惊","usage":"We had to wait a heck of a long time! 我们只好等了很长时间！"},{"id":"a7082ae0-8360-4744-ba98-b95662d5ad5b","english":"level structure","ipa":"","chinese":"层次结构","usage":"the top-level structure for a typical enterprise architecture. 典型的企业架构的顶层结构。"},{"id":"2dcac385-dcdf-43f0-a850-2f29e76e157e","english":"stance","ipa":"/stæns/","chinese":"n. （公开表明的）观点，态度，立场","usage":"1. compensation stance 薪酬理念：表达公司对员工薪酬的立场和政策的正式声明\n2. What is the newspaper's stance on the war? 那家报纸对这场战争持什么立场？"},{"id":"df5f320d-cc5f-45b1-8790-9db8c36ad9e8","english":"slate","ipa":"/sleɪt/","chinese":"v. 计划；安排","usage":"The houses were first slated for demolition five years ago. 这些房子在五年前就确定要拆除了。"},{"id":"bfc1f4a0-9b0b-4ed9-a9da-de6aece0d573","english":"walk sb ˈthrough sth","ipa":"","chinese":"（循序渐进地）教；逐步引导","usage":"She walked me through a demonstration of the software. 她一步步地给我演示软件。"},{"id":"df45b79e-29ba-4857-a2cd-941b9c381483","english":"flexible","ipa":"/ˈfleksəbl/","chinese":"a. 灵活的；可变动的","usage":"1. a more flexible approach 更灵活的方法\n2. flexible working hours 弹性工作时间"},{"id":"f5c6571f-ba9f-4a22-ae4f-167baa06be2b","english":"differentiate","ipa":"/ˌdɪfəˈrenʃieɪt/","chinese":"v. 区分；区别；","usage":"It's difficult to differentiate between the two varieties. 这两个品种很难辨别。"},{"id":"39e49251-42db-44c1-a862-da1bbc6a90b5","english":"break down","ipa":"","chinese":"v. 分解","usage":"Break Things Down 把事情分解"},{"id":"df7bef93-b036-4018-88a6-d36394b15ce3","english":"compensation package","ipa":"","chinese":"薪酬包","usage":"指雇主向员工提供的全面的薪酬和福利待遇，以回报员工的工作和贡献。薪酬包通常由多个组成部分构成：\n1. 基本工资 \n2. 奖金和绩效奖励  \n3. 福利待遇 \n4. 股权或股票期权 \n5. 健康和福利计划\n6. 弹性工作安排\n7. 职业发展和培训计划"}]},{"day":40,"title":"英语积累Day 40","topic":"工作职场","author":"Ellen Miller","accent":"英音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/6b7a24ca24ce47f394b500b9a7953409","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NTe5grrbGMM","audioSize":"361.5KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-040.m4a","youtubeId":"NTe5grrbGMM","chinese":"我开了好几个会，让我感觉有点精神涣散。所以我决定来一次稍长点的午休，这样就可以起身离开办公桌，去商场逛逛。于是，我来到了John Lewis，因为在每年的这个时候，没有比John Lewis更有圣诞气氛的地方了。我开始选购他们的圣诞马克杯。你们知道，我一直都想买一个圣诞马克杯。","english":"I had a couple of meetings that felt like they slightly derailed me mentally. So I decided to fracture in a slightly longer lunch break so that I could get up, get away from my desk, and head into the shopping center. So, I popped to John Lewis because there is nowhere more Christmasy than John Lewis at this time of year. And I started to do a bit of a shop of their Christmasy mugs. You know that I have been on the hunt for a Christmas mug.","sentences":["I had a couple of meetings that felt like they slightly derailed me mentally.","So I decided to fracture in a slightly longer lunch break so that I could get up, get away from my desk, and head into the shopping center.","So, I popped to John Lewis because there is nowhere more Christmasy than John Lewis at this time of year.","And I started to do a bit of a shop of their Christmasy mugs.","You know that I have been on the hunt for a Christmas mug."],"exercise":"I had a couple of meetings that felt like they slightly 精神涣散 me mentally. So I decided to 来一次 in a slightly longer lunch break so that I could get up, get away from my desk, and 去 the shopping center. So, I 来到了 John Lewis because there is nowhere more 圣诞气氛的 than John Lewis at this time of year. And I started to do a bit of a shop of their 圣诞马克杯. You know that I have been 想买 a Christmas mug.","vocabulary":[{"id":"cdd2448e-0c11-4f5f-bff8-08bb9981f413","english":"derail","ipa":"/dɪˈreɪl/","chinese":"v. （使）脱轨，出轨","usage":"This latest incident could derail the peace process. 最近这个事件可能会扰乱和平进程。"},{"id":"d5a4067d-8b2c-4016-ad29-bf4937f35f1d","english":"fracture","ipa":"/ˈfræktʃə(r)/","chinese":"v. （使）断裂，折断\n语境中类似于break的用法：稍停；休息","usage":"His leg fractured in two places. 他的一条腿有两处骨折。"},{"id":"f994b0ec-7c35-4e61-9c8c-c0eb22383e7f","english":"head into","ipa":"","chinese":"走向；进入","usage":"1. head into a crisis 陷入危机\n2. So right now, we're heading into the channel. 所以现在，我们正驶向海峡。"},{"id":"03ec48b6-4d13-41df-87f2-5a87bac48a09","english":"pop to","ipa":"","chinese":"去…","usage":"I'm just popping to the shops for a sec 我去一下商店。"},{"id":"1233f862-4723-4f02-b8e0-f4fd4cebc2a5","english":"Christmassy","ipa":"/'krisməsi/","chinese":"a. 具有圣诞节特征的","usage":"We put up the decorations and the tree and started to feel Christmassy at last. 我们布置好了装饰品和圣诞树，这才开始感受到圣诞节的气氛。"},{"id":"7db899d6-e697-44de-a0bf-d498e2dd3ed9","english":"mug","ipa":"/mʌɡ/","chinese":"n. （不用茶碟的有柄的）大杯，缸子，（台）马克杯","usage":"a coffee mug 咖啡缸子\na beer mug 大啤酒杯"},{"id":"c1b3ee6b-a440-4938-b386-ec7ac54122fe","english":"on the hunt for","ipa":"","chinese":"正在寻找(或搜索)","usage":"Researchers there are on the hunt for a burial site in Germany. 该国研究人员正在德国境内寻找掩埋地点。"}]},{"day":41,"title":"英语积累Day 41","topic":"生活方式","author":"Annika","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/80a763635f46431d851359396e6cbce0","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ADXwswTjFSc","audioSize":"511.5KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-041.m4a","youtubeId":"ADXwswTjFSc","chinese":"妈呀，跑得我人快没了！而且天气热得要命，我简直无法停止对高温的抱怨，因为这个夏天已经是酷暑难耐了。我喜欢重量训练，喜欢去健身房，喜欢做各种力量训练。小时候，我一直被教导：这种训练和芭蕾并不互补，两者很难共存。说实话，这就是我迟迟拖延不来健身的原因，我需要摆正心态回到这里。","english":"Whoa, that run took me out! It's also so freaking hot; I never gonna shut up about the heat because this summer is already a scorcher. I love weight training, and I love going to the gym, and I love doing all types of strength training. And as a kid, I was always taught that that type of training and ballet are not very complementary, and it's really hard for them to coexist. And honestly, that's all I can say for why I procrastinated it for so long, and I need to be in the right headspace of coming in here.","sentences":["Whoa, that run took me out!","It's also so freaking hot; I never gonna shut up about the heat because this summer is already a scorcher.","I love weight training, and I love going to the gym, and I love doing all types of strength training.","And as a kid, I was always taught that that type of training and ballet are not very complementary, and it's really hard for them to coexist.","And honestly, that's all I can say for why I procrastinated it for so long, and I need to be in the right headspace of coming in here."],"exercise":"Whoa, that run 人快没了! It's also so freaking hot; I never gonna 无法停止对…的抱怨 the heat because this summer is already a 酷暑难耐. I love 重量训练, and I love going to the gym, and I love doing all types of 力量训练. And as a kid, I was always taught that that type of training and ballet are not very 互补, and it's really hard for them to 共存. And honestly, that's all I can say 这就是…的原因 I 迟迟拖延 it for so long, and I need to be 摆正心态 of coming in here.","vocabulary":[{"id":"06fca224-dfbe-40da-8476-132821abbcb8","english":"take someone/something out","ipa":"","chinese":"杀死（某人）；摧毁（某物）","usage":"The soldiers said that they were trying to take out the snipers. 战士们说他们正设法除掉那些狙击手。"},{"id":"8358cf32-d9b4-4e4a-bfa4-8c69c2436f08","english":"scorcher","ipa":"/'skɔːtʃə/","chinese":"n. 大热天","usage":"We had a week of scorchers in August. 八月份我们过了一星期酷热的日子。"},{"id":"257c8fb0-4164-471b-a600-d89e9d5c5702","english":"weight training","ipa":"","chinese":"重量训练; 负荷训练;","usage":"That's why I go swimming and do some weight training regularly. 那也是为什么我会经常去游泳，以及做一些重量训练的原因。"},{"id":"0b347dd8-e6b6-47c1-8bfe-632bde65b173","english":"strength training","ipa":"","chinese":"力量训练","usage":"Circuits combine strength training and cardio. 循环结合了力量训练和有氧运动。"},{"id":"d063df15-abdb-46f3-b94d-763ae808854c","english":"complementary","ipa":"/ˌkɒmplɪˈmentri/","chinese":"a.  互补的；补充的；","usage":"The school's approach must be complementary to that of the parents. 学校与家长的教育方法必须相辅相成。"},{"id":"934836a5-f918-450d-953f-886121e31d54","english":"coexist","ipa":"/ˌkəʊɪɡˈzɪst/","chinese":"a.  共存；（尤指）和平共处","usage":"English speakers now coexist peacefully with their Spanish-speaking neighbours. 讲英语的人现在与他们讲西班牙语的邻居和睦相处"},{"id":"15ec84fd-faa9-4edb-829b-9df7878532ac","english":"that's all I can say","ipa":"","chinese":"我能说的就这些","usage":"I'm just so chuffed - that's all I can say.  我只是感觉到太高兴了，这就是我现在所能说的。"},{"id":"c5f6cd76-47c2-4ee2-8f28-f91d944aa03b","english":"for why","ipa":"","chinese":"…的原因","usage":"Scientists have proposed many theories for why we catch yawns. 科学家们提出了许多理论来解释为什么我们会打哈欠。"},{"id":"2bd45c6a-66d8-4bb7-9cb4-4cf5a81b83bf","english":"procrastinate","ipa":"/prəʊˈkræstɪneɪt/","chinese":"v. 拖延；耽搁","usage":"He procrastinate until it is too late to do anything at all. 他因循坐误,一事无成。"},{"id":"ff7e84e1-d3bd-4c0a-955b-d0eeb26578e8","english":"headspace","ipa":"/'hedspeis/","chinese":"n. 顶部空间；状态","usage":"But I promise, being in a good headspace before returning makes the transition far easier.\n但我保证，回学校之前保持良好的心态会使过渡变得更容易。"}]},{"day":42,"title":"英语积累Day 42","topic":"食物","author":"Rebekah Joy","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/4795c2f0ad2c4f8db3e5fc372b683b8f","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FF79H0yQtMc","audioSize":"589.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-042.m4a","youtubeId":"FF79H0yQtMc","chinese":"首先从鸡胸肉开始，我把它们放进平底锅，倒入橄榄油稍微煎一下。我还撒了一些调料。等鸡胸肉煎熟后，我把它们盛到了这个可以放进空气炸锅的类似小硅胶托盘的容器里。我强烈推荐这种做法，因为这样你就不必清洗空气炸锅的机身，只需清理这个硅胶托盘。我在鸡肉上倒了一点意大利面酱，再撒上马苏里拉奶酪。然后我把它放进空气炸锅，以340度烹饪八分钟。","english":"Starting off with the chicken breast, I first put them in a skillet and cooked them a little bit with some olive oil. I also put some seasoning on them. After it was cooked, I put them in this little silicone tray holder type thing that we put in our air fryer. I 10 out of 10 recommend this because then you don't have to clean the actual air fryer, you just have to clean this silicone tray. I put some marinara pasta sauce on top of the chicken and then sprinkled mozzarella cheese on top of that. Then I put it in the air fryer and cooked it at 340 degrees for eight minutes.","sentences":["Starting off with the chicken breast, I first put them in a skillet and cooked them a little bit with some olive oil.","I also put some seasoning on them.","After it was cooked, I put them in this little silicone tray holder type thing that we put in our air fryer.","I 10 out of 10 recommend this because then you don't have to clean the actual air fryer, you just have to clean this silicone tray.","I put some marinara pasta sauce on top of the chicken and then sprinkled mozzarella cheese on top of that.","Then I put it in the air fryer and cooked it at 340 degrees for eight minutes."],"exercise":"从…开始 with the chicken breast, I first put them in a 平底锅 and cooked them a little bit with some olive oil. I also put some 调料 on them. After they were cooked, I put them in this little 硅胶托盘 type thing that we put in our 空气炸. I 强烈推荐 this because then you don't have to clean the actual air fryer, you just have to clean this silicone tray. I put some marinara pasta sauce on top of the chicken and then 撒上 mozzarella cheese on top of that. Then I put it in the air fryer and cooked it at 340 度 for eight minutes.","vocabulary":[{"id":"f57927b4-dfa7-4cc8-adb4-8117ea4b6f8c","english":"start (something) off","ipa":"","chinese":"（使）（以…）开始","usage":"She started off the meeting with the monthly sales report. 她在会议开始时首先做了月度销售报告。"},{"id":"c43d983e-f2e3-46b4-98a3-89e062119e50","english":"skillet","ipa":"/'skɪlɪt/","chinese":"n. 煎锅","usage":"\" To saute\" means in a skillet or in a pan, to cook lightly. “煎”是指在一个煎锅或炒锅里慢慢烹饪。"},{"id":"d0f14783-d567-4c09-a245-5f7d41628ffb","english":"seasoning","ipa":"/'siːz(ə)nɪŋ/","chinese":"n. 调味品；作料","usage":"The food is served cold, without much meat and just simple seasoning. 食物是冷的，没有太多的肉，只有简单的调味料。"},{"id":"a4eed743-2725-4c53-8842-3bd852e72cd6","english":"air fryer","ipa":"","chinese":"空气炸锅","usage":"An air fryer avoids the need to deep-fry food in hot and often unhealthy oil. 有了空气炸锅，你就不需要在热油中油炸食物了，这样通常是不健康的。"},{"id":"277621ec-5eab-4b8c-b610-014e7fe40243","english":"silicone","ipa":"/'sɪlɪkəʊn/","chinese":"n. 硅酮；硅胶","usage":"silicone rubber 硅橡胶"},{"id":"ba407807-9b27-45b9-a860-ef2f25b836c4","english":"tray","ipa":"/treɪ/","chinese":"n. 盘；托盘","usage":"He brought her breakfast in bed on a tray. 他把早餐用托盘给她送到床上。"},{"id":"3d195c8e-ae24-437c-aa0f-775e649d1d4a","english":"10 out of 10","ipa":"","chinese":"赞扬工作做得出色，可以打满分；出色","usage":"I give this movie ten out of ten for special effects. 我给这部电影的特技效果打满分。"},{"id":"bb8b4bb8-ac72-4305-9318-8a4f01cf250c","english":"holder","ipa":"/ˈhəʊldə(r)/","chinese":"n. 支托（或握持）… 之物","usage":"a pen holder 笔筒"},{"id":"de5d9ed8-c497-4622-9ce4-926c0923a8ab","english":"sprinkle","ipa":"/ˈsprɪŋkl/","chinese":"v. 把 … 撒（或洒）在 … 上","usage":"She sprinkled sugar over the strawberries. 她在草莓上撒了点糖。"},{"id":"18de1493-fdf8-4a13-8027-56033e6308e4","english":"degree","ipa":"/di'ɡri:/","chinese":"n. 度，度数（温度单位）","usage":"Water freezes at 32 degrees Fahrenheit (32°F) or zero/nought degrees Celsius (0°C). 水在 32 华氏度或零摄氏度结冰。"}]},{"day":43,"title":"英语积累Day 43","topic":"生活方式","author":"Ellen Miller","accent":"英音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/6fd60a8227de46d389918f17c52757b2","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NTe5grrbGMM","audioSize":"526.2KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-043.m4a","youtubeId":"NTe5grrbGMM","chinese":"今晚回家真是让我感到如释重负。回到家，看到这扇门，我的脸上露出了最灿烂的笑容。真的，真的，没有什么地方能比得上家。如果说有什么能让我在辛苦工作一天后感觉好些的话，那就是在进门 30 秒钟后，有人递给我一块热乎乎的蒜香面包。我不知道怎么才能确保每次回家都有热乎的蒜香面包，但我确实觉得我掌握了幸福的秘诀。我坐在沙发上，拿出笔记本电脑，决定再接着工作几个小时。","english":"I was so relieved to be heading home this evening. Arriving home to this front door just put the biggest smile on my face. Truly, truly, there is no place like home. And truly, if anything was going to make me feel better after a tough day in the office, it is being handed a piece of warm garlic bread about 30 seconds after I walk in the door. I don't know how to make sure that I always have warm garlic bread on tap when I get home, but I honestly think I found the new key to my happiness. I sat myself on the sofa, got my laptop out, and decided to plow on with work for another couple of hours.","sentences":["I was so relieved to be heading home this evening.","Arriving home to this front door just put the biggest smile on my face.","Truly, truly, there is no place like home.","And truly, if anything was going to make me feel better after a tough day in the office, it is being handed a piece of warm garlic bread about 30 seconds after I walk in the door.","I don't know how to make sure that I always have warm garlic bread on tap when I get home, but I honestly think I found the new key to my happiness.","I sat myself on the sofa, got my laptop out, and decided to plow on with work for another couple of hours."],"exercise":"I was so 如释重负 to be 回到 home this evening. 看到这扇门，我的脸上露出了最灿烂的笑容。Truly, truly, 没有什么地方能比得上家. And truly, if anything was going to make me feel better after a tough day in the office, it is being handed a piece of warm 蒜香面包 about 30 seconds after I walk in the door. I don't know how to make sure that I always have warm garlic bread 每次都有 when I get home, but I honestly think I 掌握了幸福的秘诀. I sat myself on the sofa, got my laptop out, and decided to 再接着工作 for another couple of hours.","vocabulary":[{"id":"2bed5055-52cb-40d4-aa58-4cd1caea5113","english":"relieved","ipa":"/rɪˈliːvd/","chinese":"a. 感到宽慰的；放心的；","usage":"They exchanged relieved glances. 他们如释重负地彼此看了看。"},{"id":"243ae413-0864-4dff-b678-45f28ae1917b","english":"head","ipa":"","chinese":"vi. 朝（某方向）行进","usage":"She headed for the door.\n她朝着门走去。"},{"id":"98de7293-a256-498e-b908-0482cbf7e669","english":"garlic bread","ipa":"","chinese":"蒜香面包","usage":"1. Garlic bread crust 蒜味面包碎\n2. Finger Garlic bread 蒜蓉手指面包"},{"id":"682dbd91-4ae4-4d3c-98b9-f92593004705","english":"on tap","ipa":"","chinese":"可随时使用的","usage":"We have this sort of information on tap. 我们可随时向您提供这种资料。"},{"id":"a60f6f23-a1dd-454a-9fa3-e4fb8acc87f1","english":"found the new key to","ipa":"","chinese":"…的真谛","usage":"Having extremely high expectations for yourself or others may not be such a good thing after all, for a new study has found that the real key to happiness lies in not expecting too much.  一项最新研究发现，快乐的真谛在于“知足”，对自己和他人抱有过高期望其实不是件好事。"},{"id":"44984e91-de55-496f-8ffd-e41713751593","english":"premature","ipa":"/ˈpremətʃə(r)/","chinese":"a. 未成熟的；过早的；","usage":"It is yet premature to predict the possible outcome of the dialogue. 预言这次对话可能有什么结果为时尚早。"},{"id":"5fa233f9-c9a6-41b0-a789-4381a1cd779c","english":"plow on with","ipa":"","chinese":"继续干下去","usage":""}]},{"day":44,"title":"英语积累Day 44","topic":"工作职场","author":"Jenn Cho","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/ace837b53c664b819fa467c1e6c11fe0","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uS91GRgKfv4","audioSize":"501.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-044.m4a","youtubeId":"uS91GRgKfv4","chinese":"今天早上，我使出了全身的力气才醒过来。周一，我通常在家工作。所以，在去参加第一个会议，也就是我们的“站立会议”之前，我要先吃顿酸奶碗早餐，再喝杯急需的咖啡帮我清醒一下。我不了解你们的情况，但就我个人而言，连续两天以上待在办公室真的太难了。但这主要是因为我是个内向的人，任何办公室里的社交互动都会耗尽我的精力，之后我会变得非常疲惫。","english":"It took every effort in my body to wake up this morning. On Mondays, I typically work from home. So, before I hop on to my very first meeting, which is our stand-up, I'm just gonna have my yogurt bowl for breakfast and much-needed coffee to help me wake up. I don't know about you guys, but for me personally, it's so hard to go into the office for more than two days consecutively. But that's mainly because I'm an introvert, so all the social interaction I have in the office really does drain all my energy, and I get so exhausted afterwards.","sentences":["It took every effort in my body to wake up this morning.","On Mondays, I typically work from home.","So, before I hop on to my very first meeting, which is our stand-up, I'm just gonna have my yogurt bowl for breakfast and much-needed coffee to help me wake up.","I don't know about you guys, but for me personally, it's so hard to go into the office for more than two days consecutively.","But that's mainly because I'm an introvert, so all the social interaction I have in the office really does drain all my energy, and I get so exhausted afterwards."],"exercise":"It 使出了全身的力气 to wake up this morning. On Mondays, I typically work from home. So, before I 参加 to my very first meeting, which is our 站立会议, I'm just gonna have my yogurt bowl for breakfast and 急需的 coffee to help me wake up. I don't know about you guys, but for me personally, it's so hard to go into the office for more than two days 连续. But that's mainly because I'm 内向的人, so all the social interaction I have in the office really does 耗尽我的精力, and I get so exhausted afterwards.","vocabulary":[{"id":"113e5ba9-55f9-4d73-bd20-0bf29f6efe95","english":"take every effort","ipa":"","chinese":"尽一切努力","usage":"Now, the pollution slick is still floating within Chinese territory, and China will take every effort to remove pollution as much as possible.  目前污染带还在中国境内，中国将努力采取各项措施，争取在中国境内最大限度地消除污染。"},{"id":"a6f3c35a-8da4-44ed-b486-1216cf61f1b9","english":"hop on","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 快速移动到某位置或某地;\n2. 加入电话或视频通话","usage":"1. We'll hop on our bikes and go down there. 我们骑上自行车过去。\n2. Hopping on calls responding to texts or emails, chilling outside. 接电话，回复短信或邮件，在外面放松。"},{"id":"d8d3dc03-dee4-4ded-84d0-3ea7366f08d6","english":"stand-up","ipa":"","chinese":"站立会议","usage":"每天的同一时间，一个敏捷开发团队的所有成员面对面站在一起，进行一个为期15~20分钟的短会。每日站立会议的主要目的是让团队成员互相交流所承担任务的进度以及碰到的问题难点。"},{"id":"6bacaa1b-108b-47fd-8166-db08147d3e67","english":"much-needed","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 急需的","usage":"They are taking a much needed breather between dives. 它们现在正处于最需要的潜水间歇。"},{"id":"b9e027ea-8382-4075-88ea-743b7519de99","english":"consecutively","ipa":"/kən'sekjutivli/","chinese":"adv. 连续地","usage":"He applied himself readily and zealously, but did not work consecutively. 他从容而热心地投入工作， 但并没有连续工作。"},{"id":"f97789d4-2a98-4049-84fd-d429e1b7b500","english":"introvert","ipa":"/ˈɪntrəvɜːt/","chinese":"n. 内向的人；","usage":"But few things are worse than networking if you are an introvert. 但如果你是一个性格内向的人，那就没有什么比社交更糟糕的了。"},{"id":"82b89529-89b1-44d5-8c42-f2b4796c930b","english":"drain","ipa":"/dreɪn/","chinese":"vt. 使（精力、金钱等）耗尽","usage":"an exhausting and draining experience 令人精疲力竭的一段经历"}]},{"day":45,"title":"英语积累Day 45","topic":"书籍电影","author":"Jenn Im","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/f99566afd2f646838e58a57451450b64","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M82GvA_7I9I","audioSize":"418.7KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-045.m4a","youtubeId":"M82GvA_7I9I","chinese":"阅读绝对是我最喜欢的高质量休闲活动。因为在书的方寸之间，我可以游遍全国各地，甚至像穿越时空一样，去到不同的时代。我能够探索最出色、最幽默的人的思想世界。我觉得我对阅读的热爱始于大学毕业的那一刻。当时我意识到，\"哦，等等，我不需要读任何人指定的书了？我可以自己选择我想读的书？\" 这个想法令我兴奋不已。","english":"Reading is hands down my most favorite high quality leisure activity. And it's because in one spot, I can travel to all parts of the country. I can even like time travel to different time periods. I can enter the minds of the most brilliant and most hilarious people. And I feel like my love for reading really started the second I graduated from college. I was like, \"Oh wait, I don't need to read anything that anyone assigned me? Like I get to choose what books I wanna read?\" And that just blew my mind.","sentences":["Reading is hands down my most favorite high quality leisure activity.","And it's because in one spot, I can travel to all parts of the country.","I can even like time travel to different time periods.","I can enter the minds of the most brilliant and most hilarious people.","And I feel like my love for reading really started the second I graduated from college.","I was like, \"Oh wait, I don't need to read anything that anyone assigned me?","Like I get to choose what books I wanna read?\"","And that just blew my mind."],"exercise":"Reading is 绝对 my most favorite high quality 休闲活动. And it's because 在书的方寸之间, I can travel to all parts of the country. I can even like 穿越时空 to different time periods. I can 探索…的思想世界 the most brilliant and most 幽默的 people. And I feel like my love for reading really started the second I graduated from college. I was like, \"Oh wait, I don't need to read anything that anyone 指定 me? Like I get to choose what books I wanna read?\" And that just 令我兴奋不已.","vocabulary":[{"id":"941fcea0-ac2e-49bf-95f4-a707851ca0b8","english":"hands down","ipa":"","chinese":"1. a. 轻易取胜的；首选无疑的\n2. 容易地；毋庸置疑地","usage":"It is hands down the best movie this year. 这无疑是今年最好的电影。"},{"id":"49b458db-b486-43f3-a2a1-34055a63582f","english":"leisure","ipa":"/ˈliːʒər/ [美音]","chinese":"n. 闲暇；空闲；","usage":"leisure activities/interests/pursuits 业余活动/爱好/嗜好"},{"id":"00b32d55-eda5-4c24-ae2c-dd4e24e3eb35","english":"in one spot","ipa":"","chinese":"在一个地方","usage":"But most people spend over half the day sitting in one spot. 但大多数人花大半天的时间坐在一个地方。"},{"id":"5b103fb0-6fad-48c6-a7f2-adef9d10ddfe","english":"time travel","ipa":"","chinese":"时间旅行，时空之旅","usage":"It's a science fiction novel about time travel. 一部关于时空穿越的科幻小说。"},{"id":"dce9faf8-8274-41ad-9cf1-e1e96b0c791e","english":"enter the minds of","ipa":"","chinese":"进入…的思想世界","usage":"Leading brands are almost always the first to enter the minds of consumers in the brand.  领先的品牌几乎总是那些最先进入消费者心智中的品牌。"},{"id":"d2ad3c0a-5de6-4975-9400-eedaced68904","english":"hilarious","ipa":"/hɪˈleəriəs/","chinese":"a. 极其滑稽的","usage":"a hilarious joke/story 令人捧腹的笑话/故事"},{"id":"98b08a8d-7ed7-450c-b05f-caf9769c4f11","english":"assign","ipa":"/əˈsaɪn/","chinese":"1. vt. 分配;分派;指派\n2. 定出，确定（时间或期限）","usage":"1. UN troops were assigned the task of rebuilding the hospital. 重建这所医院的任务被指派给了联合国部队。\n2. Have you assigned a day for the interviews yet? 你们定下哪一天进行面试了吗？"},{"id":"ba2f1611-0a5f-4ced-bd37-5b3db10866bc","english":"blow one's mind","ipa":"","chinese":"使感到极度兴奋（或激动）","usage":"There was one scene in the film that really blew my mind. 电影中有个场面的确让我很震撼。"}]},{"day":46,"title":"英语积累Day 46","topic":"书籍电影","author":"moya mawhinney","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/1be5b0841428401d89e60897c30878eb","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NDObM4SSees","audioSize":"443.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-046.m4a","youtubeId":"NDObM4SSees","chinese":"我喜欢散文集，因为它们很容易随手翻阅，几乎不费吹灰之力就能让你感到满足。因此，伴着清晨的阳光，它们是最完美的晨读读物。我很庆幸在人生的这个阶段发现了这本书，因为它真的深入探讨了在“奔三”这个年龄段会有的矛盾和种种感受。这些散文主要围绕独居、爱情、亲密关系、孤独等话题展开，其中有几篇散文对我很有启发，因为探讨了遗产和文化的概念。","english":"I love essay collections because they're kind of easy to pick up; you feel satisfied with almost minimal effort. I'm kind of happy that I discovered it at this stage of my life because it really goes into the contradictions and all the feelings of being in your mid-late 20s. The essays kind of center around living alone, love, intimacy, loneliness, and there's a couple of essays that really spoke to me because they go into ideas of heritage and culture.","sentences":["I love essay collections because they're kind of easy to pick up; you feel satisfied with almost minimal effort.","I'm kind of happy that I discovered it at this stage of my life because it really goes into the contradictions and all the feelings of being in your mid-late 20s.","The essays kind of center around living alone, love, intimacy, loneliness, and there's a couple of essays that really spoke to me because they go into ideas of heritage and culture."],"exercise":"I love 散文集 because they're kind of easy to 随手翻阅; you feel satisfied with almost 不费吹灰之力. Thus, they 最完美的晨读读物 in the sun. I'm kind of happy that I discovered it 在人生的这个阶段 because it really 深入探讨 the contradictions and all the feelings of being “奔三”. The essays kind of 围绕 living alone, love, intimacy, loneliness, and there's a couple of essays that really 启发 me because they 探讨了 ideas of heritage and culture.","vocabulary":[{"id":"91de14a3-bbc5-43b8-bb9c-9e23a56e091d","english":"collection","ipa":"/kəˈlekʃn/","chinese":"(故事、诗歌或文章的)集子，作品集","usage":"The Brookings Institution has assembled a collection of essays from foreign affairs experts.\n布鲁金斯研究所将一批外交专家撰写的文章结集出版。"},{"id":"9a0cfd44-ee0e-486f-97c1-f2a1de6d951e","english":"pick up","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 重新开始，继续\n2. 拿起；","usage":"1. Let's pick up where we left off yesterday. 我们接着昨天的话题谈下去吧。\n2. I put down the remote, and pick up a magazine. 放下遥控器，我拿起一本杂志。"},{"id":"2b859ac3-8a75-4791-add2-a8ad5838e86b","english":"minimal","ipa":"/ˈmɪnɪməl/","chinese":"a. 最小的;极少的;最低限度的","usage":"The storm did only minimal damage.暴风雨只造成极轻微的损失。"},{"id":"fc66aa41-b68b-4bc9-8c91-41fc86d02da8","english":"with minimal effort","ipa":"","chinese":"不费吹灰之力","usage":"It's such a sophisticated skill and yet children learn it so easily with minimal effort at all. 这是一项精妙复杂的技能，而孩子们却能够轻而易举地掌握。"},{"id":"73f43e42-c063-4cf2-94e4-bda1be287731","english":"at this stage of…","ipa":"","chinese":"在…阶段","usage":"I never thought I'd be poor at this stage of my life. 我从没想过会在人生的这个阶段变成穷人。"},{"id":"7412283a-8af6-441b-97af-bcc8f1490e2d","english":"go into","ipa":"","chinese":"详细调查（或研究）某事","usage":"We need to go into the question of costs. 我们需要研究一下费用问题。"},{"id":"2bbddcc8-c30a-4fe8-b028-4b6e69c565e5","english":"in one’s mid-late 20s","ipa":"","chinese":"“奔三”的年龄段，20岁的中后期","usage":""},{"id":"58b927f0-d232-4b22-bb05-cbfa98041de1","english":"center around","ipa":"","chinese":"vt. 围绕(以 ... 为中心)","usage":"Organizers say the events will center around the subject. 组织者表示，活动将会围绕主题展开。"},{"id":"e6434c94-c962-4294-9c1d-ac445240af1f","english":"intimacy","ipa":"/'ɪntɪməsɪ/","chinese":"n. 亲密；密切；","usage":"His claims to an intimacy with the President are somewhat exaggerated. 他声称自己与总统关系密切, 这有点言过其实。"},{"id":"bd8d1465-6057-41a7-95fd-7197c737310f","english":"speak to","ipa":"","chinese":"对……说话：指与某人交谈或与某人沟通。","usage":"speak to oneself 自言自语"}]},{"day":47,"title":"英语积累Day 47","topic":"书籍电影","author":"moya mawhinney","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/f6896fc5c795424490762e06988504e2","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NDObM4SSees","audioSize":"299.0KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-047.m4a","youtubeId":"NDObM4SSees","chinese":"几年前，我读过这本书，确切地说是四年前，当时正值第一次居家隔离期间。那时我住在父母家，他们都很喜欢阅读，所以每当我没有灵感时，就会翻找他们的书架，偷偷摸摸地选一本书看。这本书就是其中之一。它是一本很好的夏日读物，因为一翻开就仿佛置身于地中海炽热的骄阳下和分布着水母的海水中。","english":"I read this a few years ago, four years ago actually, during the first lockdown. I was at my parents' house, and they're big readers, so whenever I'm out of inspiration, I usually flick through the shelves to steal something, and this was one of them. It is such a good summer read because you're immediately transported to the Mediterranean in the blazing sun and the jellyfish-littered waters.","sentences":["I read this a few years ago, four years ago actually, during the first lockdown.","I was at my parents' house, and they're big readers, so whenever I'm out of inspiration, I usually flick through the shelves to steal something, and this was one of them.","It is such a good summer read because you're immediately transported to the Mediterranean in the blazing sun and the jellyfish-littered waters."],"exercise":"I read this a few years ago, four years ago actually, during the first 封锁期间. I was at my parents' house, and they're 很喜欢阅读, so whenever I'm 没有灵感时, I usually 翻找 the shelves to steal something, and this was one of them. It is such a good 夏日读物 because you're immediately 置身于 to the Mediterranean in the 炽热 sun and the 分布着水母的 waters.","vocabulary":[{"id":"2f818c81-9458-4004-92ea-0cc07492e682","english":"lockdown","ipa":"/'lɔkdaun/","chinese":"n.（建筑或地区）因紧急情况而被封锁","usage":"The Secret Service is imposing a virtual lockdown on the city. 特勤局实质上把整个城市都封锁了。"},{"id":"d6c1e1b7-81b4-48fa-be95-bbaab6170224","english":"big reader","ipa":"","chinese":"v. 很喜欢阅读\nn. 爱读书的人","usage":"Many travel and play sports. They are often big readers. 爱好旅行和运动。他们经常进行大量的阅读。"},{"id":"3a7b5669-1baa-44e7-8080-5cc5cc494bad","english":"out of inspiration","ipa":"","chinese":"缺乏灵感","usage":"Jackson succeeded in prolonging his brilliant boyhood into his thirties, but eventually he ran out of inspiration.  杰克逊成功地把其才华横溢的少年时代延伸到30多岁，但是最终还是耗尽了他的灵感。"},{"id":"004904ac-dab6-479d-a00b-8cad94b82ff5","english":"flick through","ipa":"","chinese":"浏览；草草翻阅","usage":"I've only had time to flick through your report but it seems to be fine. 我的时间不多，只是草草翻阅了一下你的报告，但似乎还不错。"},{"id":"48b34098-f264-42f3-b88b-e0cbe1d4f586","english":"transport","ipa":"/træns'pɔ:t/","chinese":"vt. 使产生身临其境的感觉","usage":"The book transports you to another world. 这本书会把你带到另一个世界。"},{"id":"8d362ee6-750b-4867-b9a4-65b5289b1b93","english":"blazing","ipa":"/ˈbleɪzɪŋ/","chinese":"a.  酷热的；炽热的","usage":"1. blazing heat 十分炎热\n2. a blazing hot day 大热天"},{"id":"36feed46-7da5-4026-b1f2-47adcb0f3169","english":"litter","ipa":"/'lɪtə/","chinese":"v.  使饱含，使遍布（一般指不好的东西）","usage":"Your essay is littered with spelling mistakes. 你的文章里到处是拼写错误。"}]},{"day":48,"title":"英语积累Day 48","topic":"书籍电影","author":"Movie Lines","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/7e78fa2f0dd34c9fa1c538eea1613ced","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/eYxf9YcoyDY?si=GrOLc_SddcSLa48X","audioSize":"402.3KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-048.m4a","youtubeId":"eYxf9YcoyDY","chinese":"继《唐人街探案》第一部大获成功后，电影续集也没有让观众失望，《唐人街探案 2》成为中国有史以来票房最高的电影之一。该片讲述了两名侦探联手调查一起由失踪案演变为谋杀案的故事。这对 \"老铁\"将带我们开启一场愉快的旅程，在揭开谜团的同时为我们带来欢声笑语。","english":"Following the hit of its first movie \"Detective Chinatown\", the movie sequel did not disappoint viewers, as \"Detective Chinatown 2\" became one of the highest-grossing films of all time in China. This movie is about two detectives teaming up for a case of a missing person that turned out into a murder investigation. These buddies that will fill up our screens will put us on an enjoyable ride as they try to uncover the mystery while bringing out the laughter in us all.","sentences":["Following the hit of its first movie \"Detective Chinatown\", the movie sequel did not disappoint viewers, as \"Detective Chinatown 2\" became one of the highest-grossing films of all time in China.","This movie is about two detectives teaming up for a case of a missing person that turned out into a murder investigation.","These buddies that will fill up our screens will put us on an enjoyable ride as they try to uncover the mystery while bringing out the laughter in us all."],"exercise":"Following the 大获成功 of its first movie \"Detective Chinatown\", the movie 续集 did not disappoint viewers, as \"Detective Chinatown 2\" became one of the 票房最高的 films of all time in China. This movie is about two detectives 联手 for a case of a missing person that 演变为 a murder investigation. These buddies that will fill up our screens will 开启一场愉快的旅程 as they try to 揭开 the mystery while bringing out the laughter in us all.","vocabulary":[{"id":"3c7089f9-264c-4917-b751-3fbd5497988a","english":"hit","ipa":"/hɪt/","chinese":"n. 很受欢迎的人（或事物）","usage":"Her new series is a smash hit.\n她的新系列节目极为成功，引起轰动。"},{"id":"54d52665-7dd4-45d0-9028-364ee6229b59","english":"sequel","ipa":"/'siːkw(ə)l/","chinese":"n. 书、电影、戏剧等的）续篇，续集","usage":"a sequel to the hit movie ‘Madagascar’\n热门影片《马达加斯加》的续集"},{"id":"0902d676-6752-48c1-9bfc-27f410cd9899","english":"highest-grossing","ipa":"","chinese":"最高票房","usage":"This movie, thought of as a prequel, actually became the second highest grossing cartoon movie, only behind Frozen.\n这部被认为是前传的电影，成为了票房第二高的卡通电影，仅次于《冰雪奇缘》。"},{"id":"ca1d3948-09e9-46ea-8796-3907a1275153","english":"gross","ipa":"/ɡrəʊs/","chinese":"a. 总的；毛的","usage":"1. gross weight 毛重\n2. gross income/wage（税前）总收益/工资"},{"id":"ca007e5b-fadc-4bcf-9bba-8521c5c195d2","english":"team sb/sth up (with sb)","ipa":"","chinese":"使互相配合；使协作","usage":"That sounds like the bad guys teaming up.\n听起来好像坏人们都搭伙了。"},{"id":"fe53bf0e-2006-465e-a6e9-66a5c9e10a37","english":"turn out into","ipa":"","chinese":"变成","usage":"The coal-fire smelt homelike; the fog had a fruity taste of youth; anything was better than being turned out into the wastes of Wigmore Street.\n煤火闻起来像家一样。雾有一种青春的果味；任何事情都比变成威格莫尔街的废墟要好。"},{"id":"49f83052-62ab-4a5b-9b65-53d940473dea","english":"put sb on an enjoyable ride","ipa":"","chinese":"让某人享受愉快的旅程；\n句中表示：《唐人街探案》将带大家开启一场愉快的电影之旅","usage":""},{"id":"c4a4de90-147d-415e-9156-894df408c3d3","english":"uncover","ipa":"/ʌnˈkʌvə(r)/","chinese":"v. 发现；揭露；","usage":"Police have uncovered a plot to kidnap the President's son.\n警方发现了一起绑架总统之子的阴谋"}]},{"day":49,"title":"英语积累Day 49","topic":"生活方式","author":"Eva Meloche","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/853ffd05989e4c4989c2f46f1eb63174","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/c7U0xeiifKs?si=fH9XlRjOqCoEB8zk","audioSize":"248.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-049.m4a","youtubeId":"c7U0xeiifKs","chinese":"我们去见朋友吧。那个地方氛围很不错。如果你喜欢天然葡萄酒，这应该是你的不二之选。我很享受能有时间休息，没有紧迫的任务截止日期，可以放松一下。但我可能有点过于沉溺其中，真的什么事情都没做，这让我有些不安。","english":"Let's go meet up with some friends. And the ambiance is wonderful. If you're into natural wines, this should be right up your alley. I'm enjoying having time off, and not having all these pressing deadlines, and being able to relax. But I'm kind of leaning too deeply into that and really not doing anything else, and it's catching up to me.","sentences":["Let's go meet up with some friends.","And the ambiance is wonderful.","If you're into natural wines, this should be right up your alley.","I'm enjoying having time off, and not having all these pressing deadlines, and being able to relax.","But I'm kind of leaning too deeply into that and really not doing anything else, and it's catching up to me."],"exercise":"Let's go 见 some friends. And the 氛围 is wonderful. If you'喜欢 natural wines, this should be 不二之选. I'm enjoying 有时间休息, and not having all these 紧迫的 deadlines, and being able to relax. But I'm kind of 过于沉溺其 that and really not doing anything else, and it's 让我有些不安.","vocabulary":[{"id":"a6c85518-5f2a-4a39-83ec-0bdd168a9a36","english":"meet up with","ipa":"","chinese":"碰面","usage":"On Fridays, I usually meet up with my friends and hang out.\n星期五，我通常和我的朋友见面，出去玩。"},{"id":"7df084fc-2d11-4f44-ae5c-929896355f63","english":"ambiance","ipa":"/'æmbɪəns/","chinese":"n. 环境；气氛；","usage":"the relaxed ambience of the city\n这座城市轻松的氛围"},{"id":"69454c3e-ef6e-48d3-82d8-09dba4d85841","english":"be into","ipa":"","chinese":"喜欢；对……有兴趣；","usage":"1. be into sb: 喜欢上某人；喜欢某人\n2. be into sth: 喜欢；表喜欢；对…感兴趣；深深迷上\n3. Your parents possibly think that because your brother is into guitar, you must be into it too. \n你的父母可能以为，因为你哥哥喜欢弹吉他，所以你一定也喜欢。"},{"id":"776f3c09-7bc3-4434-b03f-b91b880c20d6","english":"right up your alley","ipa":"","chinese":"正合口味；非常适合你的兴趣或技能","usage":"I've got a job for you which is right up your alley.  \n我已为你找到一个适合你兴趣的工作。"},{"id":"3937ffda-eb0a-45ea-9b6f-2571c12052c5","english":"have time off","ipa":"","chinese":"放假，休息；有空","usage":"First thing I do when I have time off is sleep.\n当我有时间休息时， 我做的第一件事就是睡觉。"},{"id":"23f21606-29aa-4dd8-93f4-ce6ff183245b","english":"pressing","ipa":"/ˈpresɪŋ/","chinese":"a.  紧急的；急迫的","usage":"I'm afraid I have some pressing business to attend to.\n很抱歉，我有些急事需要处理。"},{"id":"1f3d9ab9-42b5-4799-89d7-a51b4f77b2d9","english":"lean into","ipa":"","chinese":"全力投入；沉浸于","usage":"leaning into my mortal anguish.\n沉浸于致命的痛苦中。"},{"id":"3f9f88b1-9add-46ea-b0a4-3cb9678ee464","english":"catch up with someone","ipa":"","chinese":"（坏事）纠缠住…，给…带来麻烦","usage":"His lies will catch up with him one day.\n他总有一天会尝到撒谎的苦头。"}]},{"day":50,"title":"英语积累Day 50","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Daiz","accent":"美音","period":"1-50期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/e73494f2ce0e479887426784853d4aa3","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/DDVs9mpECWw?si=Z6CRDadwDZfqImqM","audioSize":"480.4KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-050.m4a","youtubeId":"DDVs9mpECWw","chinese":"我买了之前视频中出现过的这台 iMac，可谓是我今年迄今为止最成功的一次购物。我觉得它太方便了。比如说，我的坐姿得到了改善，因为它刚好和我的视线平齐。最近，我的皮肤状态有些恶化。这可能属于异常状况。我也不知道是怎么回事。可能是季节性过敏。这很奇怪，因为我的痘痘总是时好时坏，不过没关系。毕竟这是皮肤的常态。我都有长痘痘的时候。","english":"I just purchased this iMac in my previous video, and it's by far the best purchase of this year. I think it's so convenient. Like, my posture is so much better because it's positioned right at my eye level. Recently, my skin has been purging. It might be a deviating symptom. Like, I don't know what's going on. It might be seasonal allergies. It's strange because my acne has always been very on and off, but it's okay. Skin is skin. We all get acne at times.","sentences":["I just purchased this iMac in my previous video, and it's by far the best purchase of this year.","I think it's so convenient.","Like, my posture is so much better because it's positioned right at my eye level.","Recently, my skin has been purging.","It might be a deviating symptom.","Like, I don't know what's going on.","It might be seasonal allergies.","It's strange because my acne has always been very on and off, but it's okay.","Skin is skin.","We all get acne at times."],"exercise":"I just purchased this iMac in my previous video, and it's by far the 最成功的一次购物. I think it's so convenient. Like, my posture is so much better because it's 刚好和我的视线平齐. Recently, my skin has been 恶化. It might be a 异常状况. Like, I don't know what's going on. It might be 季节性过敏. It's strange because my acne has always 时好时坏, but it's okay. 毕竟这是皮肤的常态. We all get acne at times.","vocabulary":[{"id":"794a4b9a-4516-4503-b5e9-86a71afa0712","english":"position","ipa":"/pəˈzɪʃn/","chinese":"v. 使处于","usage":"She quickly positioned herself behind the desk.\n她迅速在桌子后面她的位置上坐好。"},{"id":"e8bc4c58-a96f-4a53-85ec-62971f6c8f21","english":"purge","ipa":"/pɜːdʒ/","chinese":"v. 使洁净","usage":"a cold air blower purges residual solvents from the body.\n冷风机把身上残留的溶剂吹净了。"},{"id":"2c465564-a697-4c4d-8e98-40728df12b85","english":"skin purging","ipa":"","chinese":"皮肤净化：是指在开始使用某些新的皮肤护理产品（例如化妆品、护肤品）后，皮肤可能出现暂时性的恶化或加速排毒的过程。这通常表现为暂时性的痘痘、粉刺或皮肤不适，但随着时间的推移，皮肤会逐渐改善。","usage":""},{"id":"974af82e-dc9b-4fa5-8556-e426a7139fc2","english":"deviate","ipa":"/ˈdiːvieɪt/","chinese":"v. 背离；偏离；","usage":"those who deviate from society's values.\n背离社会价值观念的人。"},{"id":"cc66f85d-bd7e-4bdf-8e33-9232925c5ed3","english":"deviating symptom","ipa":"","chinese":"异常状况","usage":""},{"id":"fe250841-3b3f-46ea-a5f9-10e45f24193c","english":"seasonal allergies","ipa":"","chinese":"季节性过敏","usage":"it's not really fair to blame flowers for most seasonal allergies.\n当然，把大多数季节性过敏归咎于鲜花是不公平的。"},{"id":"f05dcbae-783d-47e8-9f67-b0bb44e1b9ee","english":"be on and off","ipa":"","chinese":"时断时续；时好时坏","usage":""}]},{"day":51,"title":"英语积累Day 51","topic":"生活方式","author":"Eva Meloche","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/1550a589a930409891302320a6f94571","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/jAZXy1jwT0I?si=bbMstoDViijodZXv","audioSize":"182.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-051.m4a","youtubeId":"jAZXy1jwT0I","chinese":"我找到了一款质地柔软的磨砂膏。我在回家路上买了寿司，因为逛得太累了。我发誓，逛街绝对也算一项运动。我昨晚没怎么上网冲浪。一天快结束的时候我和Olivia的几个朋友一起去看了超级碗。中场表演结束后，我累得要命，很想直接上床睡觉，但我还是坚持了下来。和不认识的人一起玩真的很开心。一想到除此之外还有很多素未谋面但可能合得来的人，我就对生活感到兴奋。","english":"I found a scrub that is so soft. I got sushi on my way home because all that browsing exhausted me. I swear, shopping is a sport. Kind of fell off the grid last night. I ended up going to watch the Super Bowl with some of Olivia's friends. I was so shattered after the halftime show, I was ready for bed, but I pushed through. It was really nice to be around people that I didn't know. It just excites me about life to realize that there's so many people out there that I haven't met yet but that I could potentially get along with.","sentences":["I found a scrub that is so soft.","I got sushi on my way home because all that browsing exhausted me.","I swear, shopping is a sport.","Kind of fell off the grid last night.","I ended up going to watch the Super Bowl with some of Olivia's friends.","I was so shattered after the halftime show, I was ready for bed, but I pushed through.","It was really nice to be around people that I didn't know.","It just excites me about life to realize that there's so many people out there that I haven't met yet but that I could potentially get along with."],"exercise":"I found a 磨砂膏 that is so soft. I got sushi on my way home because all that 逛得 exhausted me. I swear, shopping is a sport. Kind of 没怎么上网冲浪 last night. I ended up going to watch the Super Bowl with some of Olivia's friends. I was so 累得要命 after the 中场表演, I was ready for bed, but I 坚持了下来. It was really nice to be around people that I didn't know. It just excites me about life to realize that there's so many people out there that I haven't met yet but that I could 可能 get along with.","vocabulary":[{"id":"75fa0ef1-1b7b-42d5-952e-7958515ae39c","english":"scrub","ipa":"/skrʌb/","chinese":"n. （用来清洁皮肤的）磨砂","usage":"exfoliating facial scrubs\n去除面部死皮的磨砂膏"},{"id":"1e50ecc1-ead8-419f-8966-2b4363c86038","english":"browse","ipa":"/'brauz/","chinese":"v. （在商店里）随便看看","usage":"You can see shoppers browsing, even pictures of her coworkers hunting for directions and pumping gas.\n您可以看到购物者在闲逛，甚至可以看到她的同事们在找路和加油的照片。"},{"id":"32c52a8e-4a7d-478d-8147-09495a561659","english":"fall off the grid","ipa":"","chinese":"断网；不见踪影","usage":"This guy fell off the grid six years ago.\n这家伙在六年前就消失了。"},{"id":"ee55bb6b-b641-48e3-bc7c-589718aa7b98","english":"shattered","ipa":"/ˈʃætəd/","chinese":"a. 筋疲力尽的","usage":"By the time I got home, I was shattered.\n我到家的时候，已经筋疲力尽了。"},{"id":"623064fa-3a4c-47d7-8497-1de9c0ac1ae8","english":"halftime show","ipa":"","chinese":"中场秀; 中场表演;","usage":"Others watch for the halftime show, which this year will be headlined by none other than Rihanna.\n其他人则是为了看中场秀，今年的主角不是别人，正是蕾哈娜。"},{"id":"fb6d1bd8-de43-4469-b3f6-f45e6aa1bd20","english":"push through","ipa":"","chinese":"穿过; 努力完成","usage":"Despite all this, I've managed to push through as best I can.  \n尽管如此，我已经竭尽所能的去做。"},{"id":"9b596e21-688f-4211-882f-799d31c0c0e7","english":"potentially","ipa":"/pəˈtenʃəlɪ/","chinese":"adv. 潜在地","usage":"a potentially dangerous situation\n有潜在危险的局势"}]},{"day":52,"title":"英语积累Day 52","topic":"生活方式","author":"Leah's Fieldnotes","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/707b38c2cc984c299837affda9590550","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2Sdq5fw5Dew","audioSize":"500.2KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-052.m4a","youtubeId":"2Sdq5fw5Dew","chinese":"我最近早上的护肤流程超级简单。我经常什么都不做，或者最多就是用冷水洗一下脸。这些天，我还开始在早上挤时间学音乐，因为和一个人人都喜欢唱歌和演奏乐器的家庭一起生活，让我燃起了对音乐的热爱。我小时候上过钢琴课，但那时感觉更像是一种苦差事，而不是一种享受。吃完早餐，享受了一段纯粹的时光后，我开始工作。","english":"My skincare routine these mornings have been ultra-simple. I usually just don't do anything, or the most I'll do is splash my face with some cold water. These days, I've also started carving out time in the morning to practice music because living with a family where everyone loves to sing and plays an instrument has really reignited my appreciation for music. I used to take piano lessons as a kid, but it felt way more like a chore than enjoyment. After having breakfast and those hours of pure enjoyment, I hop into work.","sentences":["My skincare routine these mornings have been ultra-simple.","I usually just don't do anything, or the most I'll do is splash my face with some cold water.","These days, I've also started carving out time in the morning to practice music because living with a family where everyone loves to sing and plays an instrument has really reignited my appreciation for music.","I used to take piano lessons as a kid, but it felt way more like a chore than enjoyment.","After having breakfast and those hours of pure enjoyment, I hop into work."],"exercise":"My skincare routine these mornings have been 超级简单. I usually just don't do anything, or the most I'll do is 洗 my face with some cold water. These days, I've also started 挤时间 in the morning to practice music because living with a family where everyone loves to sing and plays an instrument has really 燃起了对音乐的热爱. I used to take piano lessons as a kid, but it felt way more like a 苦差事 than enjoyment. After having breakfast and those hours of 纯粹 enjoyment, I 开始 work.","vocabulary":[{"id":"8bc02188-a88a-43b4-b03d-f197531cb264","english":"ultra-simple","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 极简的，非常简单的","usage":"You won't get to ultra-simple if your life includes children... but you can find ways to simplify, no matter how many kids you have.    如果生活中有孩子，生活不可能会变得很简单…但是总能找到一些方法去简化它，无论你有多少个孩子。"},{"id":"37675c5f-ff7c-442f-8fc1-54266c466e87","english":"splash","ipa":"/splæʃ/","chinese":"v. 使溅泼;使飞溅;使洒落；","usage":"He closed his eyes tight, and splashed the water on his face...\n他紧闭双眼，将水泼在自己脸上。"},{"id":"b0d35686-10e0-42a1-870d-f98e089a1ff9","english":"carve out time","ipa":"","chinese":"挤出时间","usage":"It all starts with carving out time for one-on-one discussions.   \n这一切都始于腾出空来进行一对一的讨论。"},{"id":"7091cacf-1c11-48ed-92a8-d6252fe1f9bf","english":"reignite","ipa":"/ˌri:iɡ'nait/","chinese":"v. 再点燃,重新激起","usage":"The pandemic has reignited those longstanding concerns.\n这次的新冠肺炎疫情再次点燃了这一由来已久的担忧。"},{"id":"43c37323-0425-4e41-8f7e-d410630bf87c","english":"chore","ipa":"/tʃɔː(r)/","chinese":"n. 杂务;琐事；","usage":"Making pasta by hand with a rolling pin can be a real chore.\n用擀面杖擀意大利面会是个非常枯燥乏味的活儿。"},{"id":"b3b9eb3c-6c8d-4e4c-b275-e5174d471d83","english":"pure","ipa":"/pjʊə(r)/","chinese":"a. 完全的；纯粹的；","usage":"It's blackmail, pure and simple.\n这纯粹是敲诈。"},{"id":"21d73734-2b5d-41e8-be24-14ddac6b4037","english":"hop into","ipa":"","chinese":"跳进；进入","usage":"So yeah let's just hop right into the video.\n那我们赶紧进入视频吧。"}]},{"day":53,"title":"英语积累Day 53","topic":"购物时尚,情感成长","author":"Annika","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/9e5b961be59a4e5990f616eb5a2ba09d","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K8wG-ql0qJA","audioSize":"582.8KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-053.m4a","youtubeId":"K8wG-ql0qJA","chinese":"上周我真的是病倒了，得了流感，什么都做不了，这种感觉太难受了。我陷入了另一种糟糕的状态，现在还在努力摆脱。所以这周得多关注这点，让自己恢复到最佳状态。首先，我们今天预约了去做头发，来开个好头。我觉得我的发型显得很单调，有时想让它靓丽一些。上次染发的经历给我留下了心理阴影，那是我15岁的时候，染了一个非常糟糕的渐变色。","english":"I was literally taken out, sat on my butt last week with the flu, and it was so awful. I entered into another state of crustiness, and I'm still trying to redeem myself from that. So we're going to focus on that this week, getting myself back to feeling 100%. First things first, we have a hair appointment for today, which kicking it off strong. I feel like my hair just gets, like, it gets very one-dimensional. Sometimes I want like some oomph to it. The last time I did color, it traumatized me a little bit. It was when I was 15, and I had a really awful ombre.","sentences":["I was literally taken out, sat on my butt last week with the flu, and it was so awful.","I entered into another state of crustiness, and I'm still trying to redeem myself from that.","So we're going to focus on that this week, getting myself back to feeling 100%.","First things first, we have a hair appointment for today, which kicking it off strong.","I feel like my hair just gets, like, it gets very one-dimensional.","Sometimes I want like some oomph to it.","The last time I did color, it traumatized me a little bit.","It was when I was 15, and I had a really awful ombre."],"exercise":"I was literally 病倒了, 什么都做不了 last week with the flu, and it was so awful. I entered into another 糟糕的状态, and I'm still trying to 努力摆脱 that. So we're going to focus on that this week, 恢复到最佳状态. First things first, we 预约了去做头发 for today, which 开个好头. I feel like my hair just gets, like, it gets very 单调. Sometimes I want like some 靓丽 to it. The last time I 染发, it 留下了心理阴影 me a little bit. It was when I was 15, and I had a really awful 渐变色.","vocabulary":[{"id":"99d299ff-9814-4049-a148-22daf42ca13d","english":"take sb/sth out","ipa":"","chinese":"杀死；毁灭","usage":"They took out two enemy bombers.\n他们摧毁了敌人的两架轰炸机。"},{"id":"704517ff-f785-473e-9f1a-2c11b8ce58de","english":"sit on your butt/ass","ipa":"","chinese":"什么都不做","usage":"She just sits on her ass all day, while I do all the work.\n我工作的时候，她一天什么都不干"},{"id":"606bc540-a172-4573-b2d9-5d07156a1e19","english":"crusty","ipa":"/'krʌstɪ/","chinese":"a.  脾气坏的；易发怒的","usage":"a crusty old Scots judge.\n易怒的老苏格兰法官。"},{"id":"52cb413e-aef0-4166-bb74-63c918294fef","english":"redeem sb from..","ipa":"/rɪˈdiːm/","chinese":"v. 拯救；救赎","usage":"Jesus Christ came to redeem us from sin.\n耶稣基督来将我们从罪恶中拯救出来。"},{"id":"d63b278b-89c2-4a34-a664-99fafd8f82bf","english":"appointment","ipa":"/əˈpɔɪntmənt/","chinese":"n.  约会；预约；","usage":"I've got a dental appointment at 3 o'clock.\n我约了下午 3 点看牙医。"},{"id":"ac0334e8-fe0d-401a-960c-84c59593a452","english":"kick it off","ipa":"","chinese":"开始，启动某事物","usage":"When do we kick it off and begin?  什么时候我们开始呢？"},{"id":"50fc42ef-0f03-4b85-b5b6-fce5a314a404","english":"strong","ipa":"/strɒŋ/","chinese":"a. 状况良好的；景气的","usage":"Their catering business remained strong despite the recession.\n尽管出现经济衰退，他们的酒席承办生意仍然景气。"},{"id":"c9e372c1-edaf-4923-ac56-d731211cc9c2","english":"one-dimensional","ipa":"/daɪ'menʃənəl/","chinese":"a. 单一的","usage":"That is gonna give us a wonderful golden crunch on top of our pasta dish just so it's not too one dimensional.\n这样意面上就会有一种美妙的金色嘎吱嘎吱的口感，这样就不会太单一了。"},{"id":"ee399b8a-392b-4811-aa3d-20c8a064276b","english":"oomph","ipa":"/ʊmf/","chinese":"1. n. 活力，魅力\n2. n. 精力；特质；","usage":"1. There's no buzz, there's no oomph about the place,\" he complained.  这地方没有人气，没有活力，”他抱怨道。\n2. a styling product to give your hair more oomph\n使头发更靓丽的一种定型剂"},{"id":"2ea565a9-d80e-4eb2-afdb-6c0d30180d2a","english":"color","ipa":"","chinese":"vt. 给...上色；","usage":"Olivia is coloring the picture in her book.\n奥莉维亚在给书上的画涂颜色。"},{"id":"05038baa-1308-4ac8-b767-a621f85d610d","english":"traumatize","ipa":"/ˈtrɔ:mətaiz/","chinese":"v. 使受精神创伤","usage":"But in the meantime, caretakers said many of the children here were severely traumatized.\n与此同时，看护人员称许多儿童的心灵遭到了重创。"},{"id":"33af7ceb-ae8c-4943-a631-512c1a4925e3","english":"ombre","ipa":"/'ɑmbɚ/","chinese":"a. 颜色深浅渐进的","usage":"When your hair has been dyed in the style of ombre, it means that your hair fades from one colour to another.\n当你的头发被染成深浅不一的风格时，就表示你的头发从一个颜色褪色到另一种颜色。"}]},{"day":54,"title":"英语积累Day 54","topic":"生活方式","author":"Kate Brock","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/0318f95447ec41f8bc8c97ba968af993","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/nzfP5Glm-JA?si=TEyA4Xd0BkzacC3v","audioSize":"647.7KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-054.m4a","youtubeId":"nzfP5Glm-JA","chinese":"首先，我要吃早餐，然后开始日常工作。在今天的视频中，我想尝试克服对尴尬的恐惧。因为虽然我是一个视频博主和内容创作者，必须在外面拍视频，但这也让我感到非常恐惧。但今天我要主动做一些让我感到害怕的事，就是那些让我怕得缩成一团、闭门不出的事，其实也并没有那么夸张。我还决定或许要带一个自拍杆。","english":"First, I will be eating breakfast, and then I will head out on my daily mission. In today's video, I thought that I would attempt to get over my fear of embarrassment. Because although I am a vlogger, a YouTuber, a content creator, it's kind of something you have to do, you know, vlog outside. But that also brings me immense fear. But I thought today I would do things that really horrify me and you know, make me want to curl into a ball and never leave my house, which aren't really things that are that crazy. I also decided that maybe I'll bring a selfie stick.","sentences":["First, I will be eating breakfast, and then I will head out on my daily mission.","In today's video, I thought that I would attempt to get over my fear of embarrassment.","Because although I am a vlogger, a YouTuber, a content creator, it's kind of something you have to do, you know, vlog outside.","But that also brings me immense fear.","But I thought today I would do things that really horrify me and you know, make me want to curl into a ball and never leave my house, which aren't really things that are that crazy.","I also decided that maybe I'll bring a selfie stick."],"exercise":"First, I will be eating breakfast, and then I will 开始 on my daily mission. In today's video, I thought that I would 尝试 克服 my fear of embarrassment. Because although I am a vlogger, a YouTuber, a 内容创作者, it's kind of something you have to do, you know, vlog outside. But that also 让我感到非常恐惧. But I thought today I would do things that really 让（我）感到害怕 me and you know, make me want to 缩成一团 and never leave my house, which 其实也并没有那么夸张. I also decided that maybe I'll bring a 自拍杆.","vocabulary":[{"id":"03f8b625-3eb9-4da8-8aff-7c06f50aa82f","english":"head out","ipa":"","chinese":"出发；开始做","usage":"Head out to the mall, or Main Street, look and shop, and buy.  \n去购物中心或者主街看一看，买一买。"},{"id":"fd88039c-906b-4fb4-9685-7b566971ded0","english":"attempt","ipa":"/əˈtempt/","chinese":"v. 尝试；试图","usage":"I will attempt to answer all your questions.\n我将努力回答你的全部问题。"},{"id":"caee0110-9178-438d-821c-60e9756e8dc5","english":"get over","ipa":"","chinese":"克服;","usage":"She can't get over her shyness.  \n她无法克服羞怯心理。"},{"id":"32dfeab7-c2d5-4c25-94fd-47029ca61741","english":"content creator","ipa":"","chinese":"内容创作者","usage":"Being a content creator is now a career.\n成为一名内容创作者现在是一种职业。"},{"id":"8c6b5744-61ce-4961-b619-1de5aad415ca","english":"horrify","ipa":"/'hɒrɪfaɪ/","chinese":"v. 惊吓；恐吓","usage":"The whole country was horrified by the killings.\n全国都对这些凶杀案感到大为震惊。"},{"id":"a3a71ba6-55d1-4ceb-bcf0-c887cc7ca5ab","english":"curl into a ball","ipa":"","chinese":"蜷缩成一团","usage":"In colder weather, your cat will curl up into a tight, heat-conserving ball.  \n在更冷的天气里，你的猫会蜷缩成紧紧的一团来保暖。"},{"id":"d9b5fde2-c184-4b6f-99fb-8cb48a36ac7c","english":"selfie stick","ipa":"","chinese":"自拍杆","usage":""}]},{"day":55,"title":"英语积累Day 55","topic":"购物时尚","author":"emmaxolouise","accent":"英音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/8132e91380d84f1ab4bff13429930fc2","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9Ag8JDGayDs","audioSize":"433.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-055.m4a","youtubeId":"9Ag8JDGayDs","chinese":"我要去换衣服了。今天我必须穿那种“邋遢”一点的衣服，因为我要干的这活显然会很脏乱。所以，我穿了一件旧衬衫和一条旧牛仔裤。就这种感觉。我真的很爱买打折货。这件衣服从 6 英镑降到了 3 英镑。我还买了毛茸茸的手套，因为它们才 1 英镑。手套总是需要的，买来后我总是将其中一只到处乱丢，然后找不到另一只。这就是我买的东西。没什么特别的。","english":"So I'm going to get changed. I have to wear, like, kind of “scrappy” clothes today because apparently this thing I'm doing is quite messy. So, I'm wearing like an old shirt and old jeans. That's the vibe. I'm really just a sucker for buying things at a reduced price. This was down from £6 to £3. Some fluffy gloves because they were a pound. You always need gloves and I always end up having one scattering around the place and I can never find the other. That's what I bought. Nothing major.","sentences":["So I'm going to get changed.","I have to wear, like, kind of “scrappy” clothes today because apparently this thing I'm doing is quite messy.","So, I'm wearing like an old shirt and old jeans.","That's the vibe.","I'm really just a sucker for buying things at a reduced price.","This was down from £6 to £3.","Some fluffy gloves because they were a pound.","You always need gloves and I always end up having one scattering around the place and I can never find the other.","That's what I bought.","Nothing major."],"exercise":"So I'm going to 换衣服. I have to wear, like, kind of “邋遢” clothes today because apparently this thing I'm doing is 会很脏乱. So, I'm wearing like an old shirt and old jeans. 就这种感觉. I'm really just a 很爱买 things at a reduced price. This was 从 £6 降到了 £3. Some 毛茸茸的 gloves because they were a pound. You always need gloves and I always 买来后 having one 到处乱丢 the place and I can never find the other. That's what I bought. 没什么特别的.","vocabulary":[{"id":"19115875-0760-46c6-8fec-01da0015f631","english":"get changed","ipa":"","chinese":"换衣服；更衣","usage":"Get changed and go back to sleep.\n换好衣服后回去睡。"},{"id":"a5b7e13f-c24a-47bd-9e9b-9b1066a65b50","english":"scrappy","ipa":"/ˈskræpi/","chinese":"a. 不整洁的；糟糕的","usage":"The note was written on a scrappy bit of paper.\n便条写在一片破纸上。"},{"id":"7e104f0e-328c-472f-852f-d0d603e50937","english":"messy","ipa":"/ˈmesi/","chinese":"a. 使脏乱的；使不整洁的","usage":"a messy bedroom.\n一间脏乱的卧房"},{"id":"83e592f9-fb7f-4f28-accc-4bf9868c6c55","english":"vibe","ipa":"/vaib/","chinese":"n. 感觉；气氛；","usage":"The vibes weren't right.\n这气氛不对头。"},{"id":"2332beaa-9b6f-4b92-9602-1aa7dfeff937","english":"sucker  for sb/sth","ipa":"/'sʌkə/","chinese":"n. 酷爱 … 的人","usage":"I always was a sucker for a good fairy tale.\n我从前一直是一个对精彩的神话故事很着迷的人。"},{"id":"11477592-5718-476b-a860-1f15e0723651","english":"down","ipa":"/daʊn/","chinese":"a. 下跌；在较低的水平","usage":"Prices have gone down recently.\n最近物价下降了。"},{"id":"40f83b60-9cad-46c8-8364-159af87c588f","english":"fluffy","ipa":"/ˈflʌfi/","chinese":"a. 绒毛般的；覆有绒毛的","usage":"a little fluffy kitten\n毛茸茸的小猫"},{"id":"9fd7b95f-f6a7-4605-b8ad-124e1dfcd3ee","english":"end up","ipa":"","chinese":"最终成为；最后处于","usage":"I ended up doing all the work myself.\n结果所有的活儿都是我一个人干了。"},{"id":"f710fb55-f9fe-4035-94cc-5362e959a832","english":"scatter around","ipa":"/ˈskætə(r)/","chinese":"散落在","usage":"The files are scattered around the office.\n文件散落在办公室。"},{"id":"b9ba7d92-3e47-41c3-b7a4-b5dd2038bd8d","english":"nothing major","ipa":"","chinese":"没什么大不了的","usage":"Don't worry. Nothing major. You'll still be able to enjoy the party this evening.\n不用担心，没有大变动。你们今晚仍然能够参加聚会。"}]},{"day":56,"title":"英语积累Day 56","topic":"生活方式","author":"Jack Edwards","accent":"英音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/f9b3c2c5ea8a457db847c877ac7dab23","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/dkjFrkXBgIk?si=pslqME62MCmnrAaC","audioSize":"238.0KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-056.m4a","youtubeId":"dkjFrkXBgIk","chinese":"这是家庭图书馆的布置，地板上摆着张桌子——简直是我我梦想中的样子！这边是公共厨房，还有各式各样的杯子。环顾四周，会看到这个共享工作空间。看看这儿的风景！这些窗户真是太美了。光线打得恰到好处。我想我们会在这里产生很多想法灵感。","english":"This is the home library set up with a table on the floor—dreamy! over here, we have the communal kitchen and a very extensive selection of mugs. And as we pan around, we have this co-working space. And look at this view! These windows are just to die for. The light catches it perfectly. I think we're going to get a lot of thinking done here.","sentences":["This is the home library set up with a table on the floor—dreamy!","over here, we have the communal kitchen and a very extensive selection of mugs.","And as we pan around, we have this co-working space.","And look at this view!","These windows are just to die for.","The light catches it perfectly.","I think we're going to get a lot of thinking done here."],"exercise":"This is the home library 布置 with a table on the floor—简直是我我梦想中的样子!  over here, we have the 公共厨房 and a very 各式各样 of mugs. And as we 环顾四周, we have this 共享工作空间. And look at this view! These windows are just 太美了. 光线打得恰到好处. I think we're going to 产生很多想法灵感 here.","vocabulary":[{"id":"862e86c9-dd9d-41a9-97e9-d1ae591e9a14","english":"set up","ipa":"","chinese":"准备;（尤指）安装，装配","usage":"We only had a couple of hours to set up before the exhibition opened.\n展览开始前，我们只有几个小时来准备展台。"},{"id":"42304205-3d05-4273-a148-6170a57abb4e","english":"dreamy","ipa":"/'driːmɪ/","chinese":"a. 美妙的；极好的","usage":"a slow dreamy melody.\n令人心情宁静的舒缓音乐。"},{"id":"91244dba-e141-4f02-88be-f774ffc71739","english":"communal","ipa":"/kəˈmjuːnl/","chinese":"a. 共享的，共用的","usage":"a communal kitchen/garden, etc.\n共用的厨房、花园等"},{"id":"a403208b-9e00-44b1-a1ec-14e34e97055d","english":"extensive","ipa":"/ɪkˈstensɪv/","chinese":"a. 大量的","usage":"an extensive range of wines\n各种各样的葡萄酒"},{"id":"988b60eb-d6f2-4acd-a900-804b0cd163f3","english":"pan around","ipa":"","chinese":"转一圈；环顾四周","usage":"But if we slowly pan around, then we can see that this is a very different introduction.\n但如果我们慢慢地环顾四周，就会发现这是一个非常不同的介绍"},{"id":"21dbe052-1789-460b-81ee-11c50984b9bc","english":"co-working space","ipa":"","chinese":"共用工作空间","usage":""},{"id":"9f8995c7-2137-4297-a400-f93439b14ca8","english":"to die for","ipa":"","chinese":"特别棒的;非常诱人的","usage":"That chocolate cake is to die for.\n那个巧克力蛋糕非常诱人。"},{"id":"de15a546-191f-4caf-a4f2-9624022100de","english":"catch","ipa":"","chinese":"v. （光）照射；受到（光的）照射","usage":"The knife gleamed as it caught the light.\n刀在光照下闪闪发亮。"}]},{"day":57,"title":"英语积累Day 57","topic":"旅行,生活方式","author":"Elena Taber","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/3cdac9ffaa1a4766808d266ce7b1800f","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qpr25an1azc","audioSize":"511.9KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-057.m4a","youtubeId":"qpr25an1azc","chinese":"今年我很幸运能更加自由地辗转各地，在欧洲待了较长的一段时间。相较于纽约的生活方式，我更欣赏欧洲人的生活方式和对夏天态度。我真的受够了那种不断奔波、拼命工作的文化。我觉得今年很多时候都在发掘享受简单、慢节奏时刻的美好，无论是一顿悠长晚餐还是与朋友在大自然中漫步的，我珍视所有这些微小的瞬间。说到这里，我觉得可以喝杯咖啡了，我们喝咖啡去吧。","english":"I've been lucky enough to be able to be a bit more nomadic this year and been spending a lot more time in Europe. And I feel like I have such a great appreciation for the European way of living and viewing summer as opposed to the New York City way. I'm truly so over that hustle grind culture. I feel like a lot of this year has been uncovering the beauty of like enjoying the simple moments, the slow moments, the long dinners, the walks in nature with friends, which I appreciate all the little moments. On that note, I think I'm ready for some coffee. Let's go get some coffee.","sentences":["I've been lucky enough to be able to be a bit more nomadic this year and been spending a lot more time in Europe.","And I feel like I have such a great appreciation for the European way of living and viewing summer as opposed to the New York City way.","I'm truly so over that hustle grind culture.","I feel like a lot of this year has been uncovering the beauty of like enjoying the simple moments, the slow moments, the long dinners, the walks in nature with friends, which I appreciate all the little moments.","On that note, I think I'm ready for some coffee.","Let's go get some coffee."],"exercise":"I've been lucky enough to be able to be a bit more 自由地辗转各地 this year and been spending a lot more time in Europe. And I feel like I have such a great 欣赏 the European生活方式和对夏天态度 相较于 the 纽约的生活方式 我真的受够了 that 不断奔波、拼命工作culture. I feel like a lot of this year has been 发掘…的美好 of like enjoying the simple moments, the slow moments, the long dinners, the walks in nature with friends, which I appreciate all the little moments. 说到这里, I think I'm ready for some coffee. Let's 喝咖啡去吧.","vocabulary":[{"id":"6a9ac3e4-aac4-43f2-a6ec-d2cedfb680f0","english":"nomadic","ipa":"/nəʊˈmædɪk/","chinese":"a. 游牧的；流浪的；","usage":"the nomadic life of a foreign correspondent\n驻国外记者的流浪生活"},{"id":"175c53db-3f52-4e73-9c7c-f85f990e8720","english":"appreciation","ipa":"/əˌpriːʃiˈeɪʃn/","chinese":"n. 欣赏","usage":"She shows little appreciation of good music.\n她感受不到美好音乐的妙处。"},{"id":"40a6f0ab-af8a-4e08-88bf-37432e7f1229","english":"as opposed to","ipa":"","chinese":"（表示对比）而，相对于","usage":"This exercise develops suppleness as opposed to strength.\n这项锻炼不是增强力量，而是增强柔韧性的。"},{"id":"5d5b6659-f22b-4193-967d-78e0bb767ac4","english":"I'm so over it","ipa":"","chinese":"我受够了","usage":""},{"id":"9c65bcb0-d737-46f3-858c-328c423daf66","english":"hustle","ipa":"/ˈhʌsl/","chinese":"n. 忙碌喧嚣","usage":"We escaped from the hustle and bustle of the city for the weekend.\n我们周末时躲开了城市的拥挤喧嚣。"},{"id":"93ce0df5-fdbc-4498-8011-0d5927a93174","english":"grind","ipa":"/ɡraɪnd/","chinese":"n. 令人疲劳（或厌倦）的工作；苦差事","usage":"It's a long grind to the top of that particular profession.\n爬到那种行业的最高位置要经过漫长的艰苦奋斗。"},{"id":"e437931f-a08d-4cca-a070-93c8843aad2a","english":"uncover","ipa":"/ʌnˈkʌvə(r)/","chinese":"v.  发现","usage":"We ought to look below the surface of things and then uncover the essence of them.\n我们应该透过事物的表面进行观察, 然后揭示其本质。"},{"id":"d66b04db-d01b-4c0b-a676-e426739ab4a2","english":"on that note","ipa":"","chinese":"说到这里","usage":"On that note, let's cross now to some more economic news.\n说到这里，我们再来看一些经济新闻。"},{"id":"16397bd7-dada-4a10-8923-790e87e9b2e2","english":"get some coffee","ipa":"","chinese":"喝点咖啡","usage":"I'm going to get some coffee in the dining hall.\n我要去餐厅喝点咖啡。"}]},{"day":58,"title":"英语积累Day 58","topic":"情感成长","author":"Pick Up Limes","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/7cb47405171b42349f15aa1ff8078dc9","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1-VFShuFJXQ","audioSize":"483.0KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-058.m4a","youtubeId":"1-VFShuFJXQ","chinese":"这样做会让我们更自信，对自己感觉更好，同时也会让对方感到被重视，这是双赢的局面。接受别人的夸赞也是如此。过去，我经常会淡化或推脱别人的夸奖，觉得自己是在谦虚。但其实，别人夸你的时候，是在赠予你他们的钦佩和赞赏。而推脱或不以为然是在轻视自己，也是在拒绝别人真心的馈赠。所以，下次有人夸你的时候，坦然接受并说声谢谢就好了。","english":"It's just so much more empowering, it makes us feel better about ourselves, and it also makes the other person feel valued too. It's a win-win. And the same thing goes when we're receiving compliments. In the past, I used to downplay or brush off compliments, thinking I was being modest. But when someone is offering praise, they're gifting you with their admiration. And to dismiss it is to downplay yourself and also to refuse someone's heartfelt gift. So the next time someone gives you a compliment, just accept it and say thank you.","sentences":["It's just so much more empowering, it makes us feel better about ourselves, and it also makes the other person feel valued too.","It's a win-win.","And the same thing goes when we're receiving compliments.","In the past, I used to downplay or brush off compliments, thinking I was being modest.","But when someone is offering praise, they're gifting you with their admiration.","And to dismiss it is to downplay yourself and also to refuse someone's heartfelt gift.","So the next time someone gives you a compliment, just accept it and say thank you."],"exercise":"It's just so 让我们更自信, it makes us feel better about ourselves, and it also makes the other person 感到被重视 too. It's a 双赢的局面. And 也是如此 when we're receiving compliments. In the past, I used to 淡化 or 推脱 compliments, thinking I was being modest. But 别人夸你的时候, they're 赠予 you with their admiration. And 推脱或不以为然 is to 轻视 yourself and also to refuse someone's 真心的 gift. So the next time someone gives you a compliment, just accept it and say thank you.","vocabulary":[{"id":"085e5ad2-4d85-49fd-915f-53b7b0cb2f43","english":"empowering","ipa":"/ɪmˈpaʊə.rɪŋ/","chinese":"a. 使有自主感的；增强自信的","usage":"For me, learning to drive was an empowering experience.\n对我来说，学习驾驶是一次让自己更自主自立的经历。"},{"id":"76ffba88-8387-46e5-9892-bf1468b14a81","english":"valued","ipa":"/'væljuːd/","chinese":"a. 重要的；有价值的","usage":"a valued member of staff\n受器重的职员"},{"id":"1cfb98e7-3476-4718-9b02-482a22be5389","english":"win-win","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 双赢的","usage":"This is a win-win situation all around.\n这是一个各得其所的局面。"},{"id":"913f82d1-62ea-4bf9-b0c7-f7da289c37f2","english":"the same thing goes","ipa":"","chinese":"…也是如此","usage":"And the same thing goes in reverse.\n同样的事情反过来也一样。"},{"id":"4a971e9b-2d26-45d2-971b-d5939c48d659","english":"downplay","ipa":"/ˌdaʊnˈpleɪ/","chinese":"v. 对 … 轻描淡写；使轻视；贬低","usage":"The coach is downplaying the team's poor performance.\n教练对这个队的拙劣表现不以为然。"},{"id":"db760f90-fe49-4d8f-aa96-cd8d6bd4ad8e","english":"brush off","ipa":"","chinese":"漠视；不理睬","usage":"Paul asked Tara out to dinner but she gave him the brush-off.\n保罗邀请塔拉外出吃饭，但遭到拒绝。"},{"id":"cec145fd-7008-40e1-8ccf-fdfa76ed13dd","english":"gift","ipa":"/ɡɪft/","chinese":"v. （正式）赠送","usage":"The child's grandmother had gifted her £10,000.\n孩子的祖母赠予她一万英镑。"},{"id":"e1313d84-17e4-4720-a7f2-8d9779d3f698","english":"dismiss","ipa":"/dɪsˈmɪs/","chinese":"v. 不予考虑；","usage":"I think we can safely dismiss their objections.\n我认为我们对他们的异议完全可以不予理会。"},{"id":"f1d7e85a-faf5-4721-a2fb-e68828f7f3bf","english":"heartfelt","ipa":"/ˈhɑːtfelt/","chinese":"a. 衷心的；真诚的","usage":"1. a heartfelt apology/plea/sigh\n真切的道歉/恳求/叹息\n2. heartfelt sympathy/thanks\n由衷的同情/感谢"}]},{"day":59,"title":"英语积累Day 59","topic":"生活方式,食物","author":"Lauren Snyder","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/2092139fb8e3476481337757ed6e69cf","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/N4om5YkLbQw?si=Ghp6dGLUgNpmab5B","audioSize":"410.4KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-059.m4a","youtubeId":"N4om5YkLbQw","chinese":"今早，我的手臂有一股灼烧感，几乎失去知觉了，我的肱二头肌还在抽动。那次手臂训练真是太有效果了。刚刚我做了一杯锻炼后喝的饮品。我真的很在意对于人工甜味剂的摄入量，尽量能少吃就少吃。我对自己喜欢的蛋白粉非常挑剔。我一直都不喜欢那种明显尝起来口感不顺滑或者蛋白质味道太冲的蛋白粉，我对蛋白粉的喜好非常明确。但我特别爱这款蛋白粉。","english":"This morning, my arms are on fire. I can hardly feel them right now. Like, my biceps are twitching still. That was such a good arm workout. But I just made my post-workout drink. And I really try to watch my artificial sweetener intake and cut it out where I can. I'm pretty picky about what protein powders I like. I never like things obviously that taste very chalky or have a very protein flavor to them, very specific. But I freaking love this protein powder.","sentences":["This morning, my arms are on fire.","I can hardly feel them right now.","Like, my biceps are twitching still.","That was such a good arm workout.","But I just made my post-workout drink.","And I really try to watch my artificial sweetener intake and cut it out where I can.","I'm pretty picky about what protein powders I like.","I never like things obviously that taste very chalky or have a very protein flavor to them, very specific.","But I freaking love this protein powder."],"exercise":"This morning, my arms 有一股灼烧感. I can hardly feel them right now. Like, my 肱二头肌 are 抽动 still. That was such a good arm workout. But I just made my 锻炼后喝的饮品. And I really try to watch my 人工甜味剂摄入量 and 尽量能少吃就少吃 where I can. I'm pretty 挑剔 about what protein powders I like. I never like things obviously that taste very 口感不顺滑 or have a 蛋白质味道太冲 to them, very specific. But I 特别 love this protein powder.","vocabulary":[{"id":"7af48927-2c29-4f4a-a8de-0e18d1d83f60","english":"on fire","ipa":"","chinese":"灼烧感","usage":"My legs are on fire after that workout!\n运动之后，我的腿有一种灼烧感。"},{"id":"7a031229-29bb-474a-a2d3-6656c041bc3c","english":"biceps","ipa":"/'baɪseps/","chinese":"n. 二头肌（上臂前侧的主要肌肉）","usage":"Tension on the biceps as the muscle lengthens.\n二头肌被拉伸时承受着拉力。"},{"id":"0721fc20-8c1b-4695-8d77-8c50c0b1d14a","english":"twitch","ipa":"/twɪtʃ/","chinese":"v. 痉挛；抽搐；","usage":"Her lips twitched with amusement.\n她忍俊不禁地颤动着嘴唇。"},{"id":"fe82b6e7-858f-4bb4-a29f-2f1f69f1b804","english":"post-workout","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 运动后的","usage":"post-workout shake: 运动后的饮料"},{"id":"e8a95432-02c4-4c83-ae41-6d634d07e1d9","english":"artificial","ipa":"/ˌɑːtɪˈfɪʃl/","chinese":"a. 人工的；","usage":"an artificial limb/flower/sweetener/fertilizer\n假肢；假花；人造甜味剂；化肥"},{"id":"d9be1bd4-9833-45fa-84c0-ef1dddf6d4b5","english":"sweetener","ipa":"/'swiːt(ə)nə/","chinese":"n.  甜味剂","usage":"artificial sweetener(s)\n人造甜味剂"},{"id":"6f094fee-3749-4f92-9ac2-4dd2d01abc25","english":"intake","ipa":"/ˈɪnteɪk/","chinese":"n. 食物、饮料等的）摄取量，吸入量","usage":"to reduce your daily intake of salt\n减少每天的食盐量"},{"id":"61c191c7-9c55-4d0e-abe1-0ab4d219dfe6","english":"cut out","ipa":"","chinese":"停止","usage":"We're just gonna cut one thing out of a diet, let's cut out soda.\n我们要从饮食中去掉一件事，让我们去掉苏打水。"},{"id":"90a860ec-6b14-463a-bab7-162818ebf0b2","english":"picky","ipa":"/ˈpɪki/","chinese":"a.  挑剔的","usage":"So they are really picky concerning their houses.\n所以它们对自己的房子真的很挑剔。"},{"id":"6c04696f-9f02-437f-90b6-795b5932300d","english":"chalky","ipa":"/'tʃɔːkɪ/","chinese":"a. (口感）粗糙、厚实","usage":""},{"id":"9e39a8a8-c5bb-4b17-881a-ad625413bba8","english":"protein","ipa":"/ˈprəʊtiːn/","chinese":"n. 蛋白质","usage":"essential proteins and vitamins\n必不可少的蛋白质和维生素"},{"id":"ba05115b-8b0a-47fe-91a5-56254199ff72","english":"freaking","ipa":"/ˈfriː.kɪŋ/","chinese":"用以加强语气或表示愤怒","usage":"We got big freaking spiders here!\n我们这里有大死人的蜘蛛！"}]},{"day":60,"title":"英语积累Day 60","topic":"生活方式","author":"Morgan Venn","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/821e4b82d17b4dadb719196c38184cfb","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/0mAGCXxnEP8?si=m2JgTQ8RGH0nlbMr","audioSize":"508.7KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-060.m4a","youtubeId":"0mAGCXxnEP8","chinese":"在月经期间，最重要的一件事是尽可能地多睡觉。每次睡觉起来，我的头发简直是不能再乱了。我觉得每次来姨妈的时候，都睡得很不安稳。洗个水温很烫的热水澡可以缓解痛经，但老实说，我之所以喜欢水温很烫的热水澡，是因为这让我感觉很舒服。我不再穿牛仔裤，而是穿健身裤和舒适的运动衫。最糟的是，来姨妈的同时还感冒了，我的喉咙疼得要命。简直是双重打击。","english":"The first most important thing when you're on your menstrual cycle is to get as much sleep as possible. I have the most crazy bedhead. I think I just sleep so restlessly whenever I'm on my period. Taking a really hot shower can help with your period cramps, but honestly, the reason I like taking scorching hot showers is because it's just really comforting to me. I forgo all my jeans and just wear leggings and a comfy sweatshirt. The worst thing is I have my period and I have a cold, and my throat is killing me. It's like a double whammy.","sentences":["The first most important thing when you're on your menstrual cycle is to get as much sleep as possible.","I have the most crazy bedhead.","I think I just sleep so restlessly whenever I'm on my period.","Taking a really hot shower can help with your period cramps, but honestly, the reason I like taking scorching hot showers is because it's just really comforting to me.","I forgo all my jeans and just wear leggings and a comfy sweatshirt.","The worst thing is I have my period and I have a cold, and my throat is killing me.","It's like a double whammy."],"exercise":"The first most important thing when you're 在月经期间 is to get as much sleep as possible. I have the most 头发简直是不能再乱了. I think I just 睡得很不安稳 whenever I'm 来姨妈的时候. Taking a really hot shower can help with your 痛经, but honestly, the reason I like taking 很烫的 hot showers is because it's just really comforting to me. I 不再穿 all my jeans and just wear leggings and a 舒适的 sweatshirt. The worst thing is I have my period and I have a cold, and 我的喉咙疼得要命. It's like 双重打击.","vocabulary":[{"id":"47e7c2c8-5a69-4627-a0b4-06e4971573a6","english":"menstrual cycle","ipa":"/'menstrʊəl/","chinese":"月经周期","usage":"1. menstrual cycle abnormal \n月经周期异常\n2. menstrual cycle disorder \n月经周期紊乱"},{"id":"a7b41bb7-4167-4e85-a4c9-97077a136849","english":"bedhead","ipa":"/'bedhed/","chinese":"n. （因为刚起床）一头乱发","usage":"She emerged from the house the next morning with a serious bedhead.\n第二天早上，她走出屋子，头发乱糟糟的。"},{"id":"b27ba6fb-67a8-4b81-a4e6-922b20f78efa","english":"restlessly","ipa":"/'restlisli/","chinese":"adv. 不安地","usage":"1. tumble restlessly in bed\n在床上辗转反侧\n2. I wandered restlessly round my room.\n我不安地在屋子里走来走去。"},{"id":"309b5ab2-97db-406c-b87e-2b693d7a4655","english":"on one’s period","ipa":"","chinese":"月经；生理期","usage":""},{"id":"2ac801eb-59f6-4f45-b7c4-62c5848d233f","english":"period cramps","ipa":"","chinese":"痛经","usage":"It's exhausting to sit through lessons and meetings pretending to be absolutely normal, while internally crying out from intense period cramps.\n假装完全正常地坐着上课和参加会议，同时内心因强烈的经期痉挛而哭泣， 这让人筋疲力尽"},{"id":"9f451e72-7f0e-422f-9d00-4710497337b9","english":"scorching","ipa":"/ˈskɔːtʃɪŋ/","chinese":"a. 酷热的","usage":"He was dizzy with the scorching sun.\n他被炎热的太阳晒得晕头转向。"},{"id":"4c5c4a41-600b-493a-b7e2-a50099cd5ea2","english":"forgo","ipa":"/fɔːˈɡəʊ/","chinese":"v. 放弃，弃绝（想做的事或想得之物）","usage":"No one was prepared to forgo their lunch hour to attend the meeting.\n谁都不愿意放弃午餐时间出席会议。"},{"id":"768bd1ff-53a6-488d-a390-668761ea12cc","english":"comfy","ipa":"/'kʌmfɪ/","chinese":"a.  舒服的；舒适的","usage":"a comfy armchair/bed\n舒适的扶手椅/床"},{"id":"9e377146-3b43-4123-91ae-49819cec8f71","english":"a double whammy","ipa":"","chinese":"双重打击","usage":"The reason is a double whammy of climate change and development.\n原因是气候变化和发展的双重打击。"},{"id":"488b4411-2aac-4eb4-bd00-6215741b1738","english":"whammy","ipa":"/'wæmɪ/","chinese":"n. 晦气；倒霉事","usage":"With this government we've had a double whammy of tax increases and benefit cuts.\n自从这任政府上台以来，我们又是增加税收又是减少补贴，倒了双倍的霉。"}]},{"day":61,"title":"英语积累Day 61","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Lauren Snyder","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/c00055f1778445b49b5b3d3f7c7d1e49","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/N4om5YkLbQw?si=Ghp6dGLUgNpmab5B","audioSize":"434.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-061.m4a","youtubeId":"N4om5YkLbQw","chinese":"我买了几件圆领衫。你们都知道，我对挑选圆领衫很讲究。这件是浅灰色的圆领衫。这款不像那种又厚又大的，更像是面料轻薄的圆领衫。然后这一款是更厚实的针织材质。我经常穿它，因为喜欢它穿起来很合身。我也爱把它搭在长款大衣下面，搭出一种街头风。最后我还买了运动裤，是直筒的象牙白运动裤。","english":"So I got a few crew necks. I'm very particular with my crew necks as we all know. This one is like a light gray crew neck. This one isn't as like heavy and oversized. It's more of like a lightweight type of crew neck. And then this is more of that heavy knit type of material. I'm constantly wearing it because I just love how it fits. Also love how people style these under like long peacoats and stuff and kind of give them a street style look to them. And then the last thing I got were these sweats. They're just straight-legged Ivory colored sweatpants.","sentences":["So I got a few crew necks.","I'm very particular with my crew necks as we all know.","This one is like a light gray crew neck.","This one isn't as like heavy and oversized.","It's more of like a lightweight type of crew neck.","And then this is more of that heavy knit type of material.","I'm constantly wearing it because I just love how it fits.","Also love how people style these under like long peacoats and stuff and kind of give them a street style look to them.","And then the last thing I got were these sweats.","They're just straight-legged Ivory colored sweatpants."],"exercise":"So I got a few 圆领衫. I'm very particular with my 圆领衫 as we all know. This one is like a 浅灰色的 crew neck. This one isn't as like heavy and oversized. It's more of like a 面料轻薄的 type of crew neck. And then this is more of that 厚实的针织材质. I'm constantly wearing it because I just love 很合身. Also love how people 把它搭在 these 下面 like 长款大衣 and stuff and kind of give them a 街头风 them. And then the last thing I got were these sweats. They're just 直筒的象牙白 sweatpants.","vocabulary":[{"id":"6a1dd422-c6ad-4e4e-b2f4-563c6aa6a218","english":"crew neck","ipa":"","chinese":"（套头毛衣等的）圆领，水手领","usage":""},{"id":"00c1d9bd-3465-40ec-ba89-db350ad75b77","english":"light gray","ipa":"","chinese":"浅灰","usage":"His eyes were light gray. His expression was happy and calm.\n他的眼睛是浅灰色的。他的表情快乐而平静。"},{"id":"65222d2c-bfcd-4624-b20c-c3b896671dde","english":"light","ipa":"/laɪt/","chinese":"a. 浅色的；淡色的","usage":"1. light blue eyes\n浅蓝色的眼睛\n2. Lighter shades suit you best.\n较浅色的衣服对你最合适。"},{"id":"f8226b7b-04fb-40ea-b26c-5484c8a33558","english":"lightweight","ipa":"/'laɪtweɪt/","chinese":"a. （布料）轻量的，薄型的","usage":"a lightweight jacket\n轻便的短上衣"},{"id":"63b5d336-3fab-4785-a9ca-95a0a196e96d","english":"heavy knit","ipa":"","chinese":"厚针织物","usage":"Allie wears a red, heavy knit belted cardigan, which would have been accurate for the 1940s.\n- Allie 穿着一件红色、厚实的系腰带针织开衫，这在 1940 年代应该是准确的。"},{"id":"215be77a-7594-4c60-95be-d0f000d93505","english":"fit","ipa":"/fɪt/","chinese":"v. （形状和尺寸）适合，合身","usage":"1. I tried the dress on but it didn't fit.\n我试穿了那连衣裙，但不合身。\n2. That jacket fits well.\n那件短上衣很合身。"},{"id":"19c724c3-db0e-4ebd-9685-92bf0d996508","english":"style","ipa":"/staɪl/","chinese":"v. 把 … 设计（或缝制、做）成某种式样","usage":"1. an elegantly styled jacket\n式样高雅的上衣\n2. He'd had his hair styled at an expensive salon.\n他去一家豪华美容厅做了头发。"},{"id":"d0040864-7a5e-41dc-a852-d250d9cadea6","english":"peacoat","ipa":"/'piːkəʊt/","chinese":"n. 水手短外套（一种厚呢短大衣）","usage":"I combine my peacoat with contrasting gloves and scarves.\n我将我的短大衣与对比鲜明的手套和围巾结合起来。"},{"id":"12dd8781-4006-4ecc-b85f-cd121c380092","english":"long peacoat","ipa":"","chinese":"长款（海军）大衣","usage":""},{"id":"d0c01197-dafa-4c7f-9f54-468350287547","english":"street style look","ipa":"","chinese":"街头风格","usage":""},{"id":"aa0e2724-61bb-43f6-83ad-3a379ea035dd","english":"straight-legged","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 直腿的","usage":""},{"id":"a452905c-a455-4ecf-b54d-cff81655a315","english":"ivory","ipa":"/ˈaɪvəri/","chinese":"n. 象牙色；乳白色","usage":"My shirt is more ivory colour than white.\n我的衬衣与其说是白色的, 不如说是乳白色的"}]},{"day":62,"title":"英语积累Day 62","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Lauren Snyder","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/5861a50ab714457e9576d7794cf29e90","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/N4om5YkLbQw?si=Ghp6dGLUgNpmab5B","audioSize":"352.0KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-062.m4a","youtubeId":"N4om5YkLbQw","chinese":"我刚到美甲店。一直以来，我都是做纯色美甲，再涂一层白色镀铬甲油。这是我可靠的备选方案，也是最常做的首选款式，因为永远不会出错。不过，今天我想换个花样，做一个美甲设计。我也喜欢法式美甲，但是两周左右我就看腻了。今天我一定要试试新花样。那我们就进美甲店，让指甲焕然一新吧。","english":"I just got to the nail salon. For the longest time, I've been just doing like a solid color and then white chrome on top. It's just been my fallback and my go-to because you can't really go wrong with it. However, I think today I'm going to switch it up and do a nail design. I also love French tips as well, but I find with those, I get sick of them after like two weeks or so. But today definitely got to do something fun. So we'll head on in and freshen them up.","sentences":["I just got to the nail salon.","For the longest time, I've been just doing like a solid color and then white chrome on top.","It's just been my fallback and my go-to because you can't really go wrong with it.","However, I think today I'm going to switch it up and do a nail design.","I also love French tips as well, but I find with those, I get sick of them after like two weeks or so.","But today definitely got to do something fun.","So we'll head on in and freshen them up."],"exercise":"I just got to the 美甲店. 一直以来, I've been just doing like a 纯色 and then 白色镀铬甲油 on top. It's just been my 可靠的备选方案 and my 最常做的首选款式 because 永远不会出错. However, I think today I'm going to 换个花样 and do a nail design. I also love French tips as well, but I find with those, I （看）腻了 them after like two weeks or so. But today definitely got to do something fun. So we'll 进美甲店 and 让（指甲）焕然一新.","vocabulary":[{"id":"55fcb25e-6e9c-429b-90f4-e24d8b247999","english":"nail salon","ipa":"","chinese":"美甲店","usage":"His sister Ida owns a nail salon in Bushwick.\n他姐姐艾达在布什维克开了家美甲店。"},{"id":"d6a52f31-2271-4af7-8ace-16a195335c75","english":"for the longest time","ipa":"","chinese":"长久以来","usage":"For the longest time in technology artists imagine so engineers can build.\n长久以来的科技都是艺术家想象，然后工程师开发。"},{"id":"8937c9eb-99e8-4762-9e77-daf82e0e9358","english":"solid color","ipa":"","chinese":"纯色","usage":"It's a solid color, plain green T-shirt, plain red pants.\n它是纯色的，普通的绿色 T 恤，普通的红色裤子"},{"id":"5111b605-b9bf-476d-96e8-8ff9cb88eea1","english":"white chrome","ipa":"","chinese":"白色镀铬","usage":""},{"id":"dee061c8-3f47-4056-ba7f-4fc86744895d","english":"fallback","ipa":"/'fɔːlbæk/","chinese":"n. 应变计划；退路；可依靠的东西","usage":"We need a fallback position if they won't do the job.\n如果他们不干这个工作，我们就需要一个应变的方案。"},{"id":"1aaee6b6-897a-4662-ab15-23e64693a6be","english":"go-to","ipa":"","chinese":"n. & a.最佳选择；最佳人选","usage":"Shawn is my go-to guy for event planning, so he will definitely be able to help you find a caterer.\n肖恩是我活动策划的时候最可以指望得上的人，所以他一定能帮你找一个宴会承办商。"},{"id":"2b25e252-7ffa-4742-b086-fca0c1cd4111","english":"can't go wrong with","ipa":"","chinese":"不会出错","usage":""},{"id":"36dcf07c-673a-48d4-b9ca-9f6162c1b2ce","english":"switch up","ipa":"","chinese":"改变","usage":"Had to switch up look at things different, see the bigger picture.\n换一个不同的角度，看看更广阔的世界。"},{"id":"32fcb8d4-45fe-4157-b2c6-fb873d42703a","english":"get sick of","ipa":"","chinese":"厌倦","usage":"Harry was getting sick of telling people that Hermione wasn't his girlfriend.\n哈利反复跟人解释赫敏不是他的女朋友，他觉得厌烦透了。"},{"id":"9549b83d-2c37-4a8e-80d5-11b3df0f6050","english":"head on","ipa":"","chinese":"迎面地","usage":""},{"id":"0de8139b-a38f-4fc4-b16a-173e6d83587c","english":"freshen up","ipa":"","chinese":"梳洗打扮；使变得焕然一新","usage":"I'll just go and freshen up before supper.\n晚饭前我要去梳洗打扮一番。"}]},{"day":63,"title":"英语积累Day 63","topic":"情感成长","author":"Pick Up Limes","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/be6e98c82c274560baccf6e236e71289","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1-VFShuFJXQ","audioSize":"495.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-063.m4a","youtubeId":"1-VFShuFJXQ","chinese":"压力并不是真正的敌人，我们对压力的看法才是。如果我们认为压力有害，它就会有害。这类似一个自我实现的预言。但只要简单地改变看待压力的方式，我们就能改变整个生理反应。我不再把压力视为阻碍，而是告诉自己：“你遇到了挑战，但你对此充满激情，你能够克服”。这种心态转变虽然小，却带来了巨大的影响。如今压力已经不再是消耗和控制我的东西，而是我的盟友。","english":"Stress isn't the real enemy, but our perception of it is. If we believe stress is harmful, it often will be. It's kind of like a self-fulfilling prophecy. But by simply reframing how we view stress, we can change the whole biological response. Instead of seeing the stress as something that's hindering me, I tell myself, \"You found a challenge, but you're excited about this, you've got this.\" It's a small mindset shift, but it's been transformative. Stress has gone from being something that consumed and controlled me to now actually being an ally.","sentences":["Stress isn't the real enemy, but our perception of it is.","If we believe stress is harmful, it often will be.","It's kind of like a self-fulfilling prophecy.","But by simply reframing how we view stress, we can change the whole biological response.","Instead of seeing the stress as something that's hindering me, I tell myself, \"You found a challenge, but you're excited about this, you've got this.\"","It's a small mindset shift, but it's been transformative.","Stress has gone from being something that consumed and controlled me to now actually being an ally."],"exercise":"Stress isn't the real enemy, but our 看法 of it is. If we believe stress is harmful, it often will be. It's kind of like a 自我实现的 预言. But by simply 改变 how we view stress, we can change the whole 生理反应. Instead of seeing the stress as something that's 阻碍 me, I tell myself, \"You found a challenge, but you're excited about this, 你能够克服\" It's a 心态转变虽然小, but it's been 巨大的影响. Stress has gone from being something that 消耗 and controlled me to now actually being 盟友.","vocabulary":[{"id":"6bbef56e-c78d-448e-9d99-da1c7156524f","english":"perception","ipa":"/pəˈsepʃn/","chinese":"n. 看法；见解","usage":"There is a general public perception that standards in schools are falling.\n公众普遍认为，学校的水平都在下降。"},{"id":"a9714ac7-33cf-4c6a-8b55-be82690f8cf4","english":"self-fulfilling","ipa":"/'selfful'filiŋ/","chinese":"a. （预言等）自我应验的，自我实现的","usage":"If you expect to fail, you will fail. It's a self-fulfilling prophecy.\n你如果预期失败，就会失败。这是一种自我应验的预测。"},{"id":"4774d0ca-976f-4a10-9e78-2c0e490a3e60","english":"prophecy","ipa":"/ˈprɒfəsi/","chinese":"n. 预言","usage":"to fulfil a prophecy (= make it come true)\n实现预言"},{"id":"bdc6e9d3-5634-4a13-a187-9f8ff895d126","english":"reframe","ipa":"/rɪ'frem/","chinese":"v. 重新构造","usage":"I reframed my question.\n我重新表述了我的问题。"},{"id":"0fefd4f2-eed0-42c3-8fed-168e10f77253","english":"biological response","ipa":"","chinese":"生理反应","usage":"That feeling of strain or pressure is a biological response, and under the right circumstances can be a great source of motivation.\n紧张或压力的感觉是一种生理反应，在适当的情况下可以成为动力的重要来源。"},{"id":"ed02ca1b-01c0-44e7-9043-5635df08a82b","english":"hinder","ipa":"/ˈhɪndə(r)/","chinese":"v. 阻碍；妨碍；","usage":"1. a political situation that hinders economic growth\n妨碍经济发展的政治局面\n2. Some teachers felt hindered by a lack of resources.\n有些教师因资源不足而感到困难重重。"},{"id":"9eca6bba-5309-4ed6-9063-c43ac986970c","english":"you've got this","ipa":"","chinese":"你能行的","usage":""},{"id":"8de95725-0b99-4c54-b21b-c1d51d840416","english":"mindset shift","ipa":"","chinese":"心态转变","usage":"It's a mindset shift our universities have to go through.  \n这是我们的大学需要面临的思想转变。"},{"id":"c5265fb2-2e67-485c-b5ca-857377fc12c3","english":"transformative","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 转变的；转折的","usage":"It was a transformative stage of our careers.\n那是我们职业生涯的一个转折阶段。"},{"id":"1eaf5201-100d-4abe-adb3-0478a89b8da6","english":"consume","ipa":"/kənˈsjuːm/","chinese":"v. 消耗","usage":"She was consumed with guilt.\n她深感内疚。"},{"id":"5ff45399-92e4-4922-8ae2-0e8541807b5a","english":"ally","ipa":"/ˈælaɪ/","chinese":"n. 盟友","usage":"a close ally and friend of the prime minister\n首相的一个亲密盟友和伙伴"}]},{"day":64,"title":"英语积累Day 64","topic":"食物","author":"Lauren Snyder","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/6f93a192bbab425289d5890974a7b029","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lBjFxbnQqLc","audioSize":"368.3KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-064.m4a","youtubeId":"lBjFxbnQqLc","chinese":"苹果干缺货了，所以我们买了小香蕉。我超爱吃坚果酱，通常在早上锻炼前，我会把它涂在米糕上，这样可以在锻炼前摄入一些碳水和脂肪，因为我绝对不能空腹运动，那会很糟糕。我现在只想吃一个扎实的美味煎蛋卷，里面要加很多奶酪和火腿，配料都加满。","english":"The dried apples were out of stock, so we went with the baby bananas. I go through nut butter like crazy. And I typically have this on top of a rice cake before my workouts in the morning to get like some carbs and fats before I work out, because I cannot work out for the life of me on an empty stomach. It would be a mess. I'm craving nothing but like a very solid, yummy omelette with lots of cheese and ham, like all the fixings.","sentences":["The dried apples were out of stock, so we went with the baby bananas.","I go through nut butter like crazy.","And I typically have this on top of a rice cake before my workouts in the morning to get like some carbs and fats before I work out, because I cannot work out for the life of me on an empty stomach.","It would be a mess.","I'm craving nothing but like a very solid, yummy omelette with lots of cheese and ham, like all the fixings."],"exercise":"The dried apples were 缺货, so we 买了 the baby bananas. I 超爱吃 nut butter like crazy. And I typically have this on top of a 米糕 before my workouts in the morning to get like some 碳水 and fats before I work out, because I cannot work out 绝对不能空腹运动. It would be a mess. I'm 只想吃 like a very 扎实的, yummy omelette with lots of cheese and ham, like all the 配料.","vocabulary":[{"id":"756846ea-72be-4bc8-930c-0f3029f33f7a","english":"out of stock","ipa":"","chinese":"缺货, 卖光","usage":"I'm sorry, but the dress you want is out of stock.\n对不起，你要的裙子现在没货。"},{"id":"abcd9b27-bc0c-4260-ba3a-85d027b0c1c2","english":"go with","ipa":"","chinese":"（购买时）选…","usage":"I'll go with a salad for lunch.\n我午饭要一个沙拉。"},{"id":"150e590b-9374-4eb3-80e5-69c3a4056274","english":"go through","ipa":"","chinese":"吃…","usage":"We need to go through these leftovers before ordering new meals.\n在订餐之前我们必须将这些剩菜全都吃掉。"},{"id":"6445360d-3208-44fc-a319-f26fd5fc5210","english":"rice cake","ipa":"","chinese":"年糕","usage":""},{"id":"9739a5d6-5bb3-4506-9584-e98af6563e81","english":"carb","ipa":"/kɑːb/","chinese":"碳水化合物","usage":"Then for lunch, I kinda lay off the carbs.\n午餐时，我会少吃碳水化合物。"},{"id":"ea3344d2-750d-4e2b-b63b-10e147e701ea","english":"for the life of me","ipa":"","chinese":"无论如何","usage":"I couldn’t for the life of me remember his name.\n我怎么也想不起他的名字。"},{"id":"9351f5b9-c1bd-4178-af2a-f7865589798c","english":"on an empty stomach","ipa":"","chinese":"空腹","usage":"But how can you conquer the world on an empty stomach?\n空着肚子怎去征服世界？"},{"id":"c432ef19-dfbd-43d5-83ce-0dc2d4b8dbab","english":"crave","ipa":"/kreɪv/","chinese":"v. 渴望","usage":"She has always craved excitement.\n她总盼望得到刺激。"},{"id":"1be68c7f-fd97-41d8-bc99-b96e691aa744","english":"nothing but","ipa":"","chinese":"只；只有；","usage":"Nothing but a miracle can save her now.\n现在只有出现奇迹才能救活她。"},{"id":"71233ae6-8570-4f63-b774-d3bcb278114f","english":"solid","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 无空隙的;实心的;非中空的","usage":""},{"id":"e11b3851-85e2-4900-93f5-e7a81e754931","english":"fixings","ipa":"","chinese":"n. 配料","usage":"a hamburger with all the fixings\n有各种配料的汉堡包"}]},{"day":65,"title":"英语积累Day 65","topic":"生活方式","author":"Zeliha Akpinar","accent":"英音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/c30c9c91ba2a4c5f88a469a3cddf07b4","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A5KZz3TDo1Y","audioSize":"427.5KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-065.m4a","youtubeId":"A5KZz3TDo1Y","chinese":"很多时候，尤其是在假期，我还是会在凌晨三点醒来，然后一口气追完我最喜欢的Netflix剧集。充足的睡眠能让我醒来后神清气爽。所以要避免为了能早起而牺牲睡眠，因为这会带来负面影响。你可以为了早起而缩短几天的睡眠时间，但这样一来，睡眠不足会导致一整天都注意力不集中、焦虑、疲倦，而且这种睡眠模式是难以持续的。如果早起意味着减少睡眠，那还是不要这样做。","english":"There have been many occasions, especially on holidays, where I still wake up at 3:00 a.m. but binge-watch my favorite Netflix show. Getting enough sleep is the key to waking up feeling refreshed. That's why you really want to avoid sacrificing sleep to become an early riser because it will catch up with you. You can cut your sleep short to wake up early for a couple of days, but then sleep deprivation will cause you poor concentration, anxiety, tiredness during the day, and it won't be a sleep routine you can maintain. If early rising means cutting sleep, don't do it.","sentences":["There have been many occasions, especially on holidays, where I still wake up at 3:00 a.m. but binge-watch my favorite Netflix show.","Getting enough sleep is the key to waking up feeling refreshed.","That's why you really want to avoid sacrificing sleep to become an early riser because it will catch up with you.","You can cut your sleep short to wake up early for a couple of days, but then sleep deprivation will cause you poor concentration, anxiety, tiredness during the day, and it won't be a sleep routine you can maintain.","If early rising means cutting sleep, don't do it."],"exercise":"There have been many occasions, especially on holidays, where I still wake up at 3:00 a.m. but 一口气追完 my favorite Netflix show. Getting enough sleep is the key to waking up 神清气爽. That's why you really want to avoid sacrificing sleep to 早起 because it will 带来负面影响 you. You can cut your sleep short to wake up early for a couple of days, but then 睡眠不足 will cause you 注意力不集中, anxiety, tiredness during the day, and it won't be a 睡眠模式 you can maintain. If early rising means cutting sleep, don't do it.","vocabulary":[{"id":"a5bccc46-f607-47a0-9638-d916168db454","english":"binge-watch","ipa":"/ˈbɪndʒ ˌwɒtʃ/","chinese":"v. 连续观看电视节目，刷剧","usage":"We binge-watched an entire season of \"Breaking Bad\" on Sunday.\n我们星期天一口气看完了整季的《绝命毒师》。"},{"id":"20308664-f2e5-494b-a020-fec84e6d13fc","english":"refreshed","ipa":"/rɪˈfreʃt/","chinese":"a. 精神振作的","usage":"I feel so refreshed after that cup of tea.\n我喝了一杯茶，感到神清气爽。"},{"id":"6bd379b4-92c3-4a63-8773-3c0518d00e43","english":"early riser","ipa":"","chinese":"n. 早起者","usage":"So in the early risers, they found that their peak was around about lunch time, around about noon.\n他们发现早起的人的峰值出现在午饭时间，大约是正午。"},{"id":"33f70591-40a1-4d7a-842c-98117c6604e7","english":"catch up with","ipa":"","chinese":"和…算旧账；使…最终尝到苦果","usage":"Although he subsequently became a successful businessman, his criminal past caught up with him.\n尽管后来他成了事业有成的生意人，以前的犯罪前科终究让他尝到了苦果。"},{"id":"f23368f5-c61c-4e47-beb0-dca7ed1bd2be","english":"deprivation","ipa":"/ˌdeprɪˈveɪʃn/","chinese":"n. 缺乏，损失","usage":"the deprivation of war\n战时的物品匮乏"},{"id":"0cda7570-789b-4a40-9558-36854f0b184c","english":"poor concentration","ipa":"","chinese":"注意力不集中","usage":"If you skip breakfast, blood sugar levels drop, fatigue, poor concentration, irritability and lethargy results. \n如果你忽视早餐，则会出现低血糖、疲劳、精力不集中，易怒和昏睡后果。"},{"id":"8b66ed45-7c65-4ad1-beba-896188d115cc","english":"sleep routine","ipa":"","chinese":"睡眠习惯","usage":"A healthy sleep routine begets sound sleep.\n健康的睡眠习惯会带来良好的睡眠。"}]},{"day":66,"title":"英语积累Day 66","topic":"兴趣爱好","author":"Yasmin The Art Person","accent":"英音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/9da697a93acf4d548eff8a9f6d607022","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RrAmtyOD4hU","audioSize":"298.3KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-066.m4a","youtubeId":"RrAmtyOD4hU","chinese":"折纸——这可能听起来是个奇怪的爱好，谁会把折纸作为一种爱好呢？折纸就是你拿一张纸，简单地通过折叠把它变成很酷的艺术作品。不需要用胶水粘，也不需要用剪刀剪，你可以把它送给朋友，也可以用作房间装饰。说实在的，这个过程非常治愈和放松。","english":"Origami—this might sound like a weird one—who gets into origami as a hobby? Origami is where you take a piece of paper and turn it into a cool creation simply by folding it. There's no glue, no cutting. You can gift it to a friend, you can make origami room decor. Honestly, it's so therapeutic and relaxing.","sentences":["Origami—this might sound like a weird one—who gets into origami as a hobby?","Origami is where you take a piece of paper and turn it into a cool creation simply by folding it.","There's no glue, no cutting.","You can gift it to a friend, you can make origami room decor.","Honestly, it's so therapeutic and relaxing."],"exercise":"折纸—this might sound like a weird one—who 爱好 origami as a hobby? Origami is where you take a piece of paper and 把它变成 a cool creation simply by folding it. There's no glue, no cutting. You can 把它送给朋友, you can make origami 房间装饰. Honestly, it's so 治愈和放松c and relaxing.","vocabulary":[{"id":"f9c66056-4860-4fc4-ae14-13ae1fe7b79f","english":"origami","ipa":"/ˌɒrɪ'gɑːmɪ/","chinese":"n. 折纸艺术","usage":"Origami poses a basic yet infinitely complex challenge\n折纸提出了一个基本但无限复杂的挑战"},{"id":"00a2336e-5475-4e40-a376-97a3b4f63416","english":"get into","ipa":"","chinese":"对 … 产生兴趣","usage":"I'm really getting into jazz these days.\n我最近真的开始喜欢爵士乐了。"},{"id":"91fd0b53-82a4-4823-b269-432fe5e9d53a","english":"turn into","ipa":"","chinese":"使（从 … ）变成","usage":"Ten years of prison had turned him into an old man.\n十年大狱使他变成了一个老头。"},{"id":"31a32843-dde8-4e15-976a-63c4a64dca64","english":"gift","ipa":"/ɡɪft/","chinese":"v. （正式）赠送","usage":"The child's grandmother had gifted her £10,000.\n孩子的祖母赠予她一万英镑。"},{"id":"0e2e706d-f948-47c6-ab41-658db1d4a841","english":"room decor","ipa":"","chinese":"房间装饰","usage":"Fortunately for you, I do not think you would complement my sitting room decor.\n对你来说幸运的是， 我认为你不会补充我的客厅装饰。"},{"id":"5674f6c8-c235-4aca-a2c3-d96542de942b","english":"therapeutic","ipa":"/ˌθerəˈpjuːtɪk/","chinese":"a. 有助于放松精神的","usage":"Painting can be very therapeutic.\n绘画可以使人放松。"}]},{"day":67,"title":"英语积累Day 67","topic":"生活方式","author":"Life Of Riza","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/9374a0e96be94e5bbf39986c4a3978cc","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mf9KYXqwaS8","audioSize":"442.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-067.m4a","youtubeId":"mf9KYXqwaS8","chinese":"不开玩笑，昨晚，我在这张床上睡了有生以来最好的一觉，睡得不省人事。我打算今天剩下的时间写点日记，为这一周做打算。我设立“思考周”是为了能把时间完全用在自己的作品上，沉思复杂的想法和问题。来到这里，我感觉有些不堪重负，感觉有无数的事情需要我时刻关注。虽然日常生活中分心很正常，但我感觉或许我只是需要一些时间着眼全局，进行思考。","english":"I kid you not. I had the best sleep of my life on this bed last night. I slept like a rock. So my plan for the rest of the day is I'm gonna go and journal a little bit more, set my intentions for this week. The purpose of my think week was to dedicate time solely to my craft, to ruminate on complex ideas and questions. Coming here, I was feeling a bit stretched thin and felt like a million things needed my attention at all times. And while it's normal to have the distractions of everyday life, I felt like maybe I just needed some time to zoom out and think.","sentences":["I kid you not.","I had the best sleep of my life on this bed last night.","I slept like a rock.","So my plan for the rest of the day is I'm gonna go and journal a little bit more, set my intentions for this week.","The purpose of my think week was to dedicate time solely to my craft, to ruminate on complex ideas and questions.","Coming here, I was feeling a bit stretched thin and felt like a million things needed my attention at all times.","And while it's normal to have the distractions of everyday life, I felt like maybe I just needed some time to zoom out and think."],"exercise":"不开玩笑. I had the best sleep of my life on this bed last night. 睡得不省人事. So my plan for the rest of the day is I'm gonna go and journal a little bit more, 为这一周做打算 The purpose of my 思考周 was to 把时间完全用在 my craft, to 沉思 complex ideas and questions. Coming here, I was feeling a bit 不堪重负 and felt like 无数的事情需要我时刻关注. And while it's normal to have the distractions of everyday life, I felt like maybe I just needed some time to 着眼全局 and think.","vocabulary":[{"id":"3b2846d0-404a-4714-8e56-6722c466f6ea","english":"I kid you not","ipa":"","chinese":"不开玩笑","usage":""},{"id":"ce2a120f-3d34-473b-9946-0d6128b04d7d","english":"sleep like a rock","ipa":"","chinese":"睡得很好、很沉","usage":"My sister sleeps like a rock! I can play loud music in the same room as her, and she doesn’t wake up.\n我姐姐睡得很沉！我在她房间里放吵闹的音乐，她也不会醒来。"},{"id":"3420b470-aeb9-4669-8d8e-3feac4aa6a1d","english":"intention","ipa":"/ɪnˈtenʃn/","chinese":"n. 打算；计划；","usage":"I have no intention of going to the wedding.\n我无意去参加婚礼。"},{"id":"4cf6f635-c93e-4af2-8cb6-e336805e4640","english":"think week","ipa":"","chinese":"思考周","usage":"比尔·盖茨每年都会留出一周从工作中跳出来，让各种各样的思想充满大脑，从而找到未来的方向。这个习惯被称为“思考周”（Think Week）。"},{"id":"56c24b6c-cb87-41eb-b326-717bf68e6f73","english":"dedicate","ipa":"/ˈdedɪkeɪt/","chinese":"v. 致力于","usage":"He dedicated his life to helping the poor.\n他毕生致力于帮助穷人。"},{"id":"74d46517-b616-4f83-8295-723c2b43f18c","english":"solely","ipa":"/ˈsəʊlli/","chinese":"adv. 仅；只；唯；","usage":"She was motivated solely by self-interest.\n她所追求的完全是私利。"},{"id":"28bd2b04-de25-44de-b58d-5da8da2f61fc","english":"ruminate~ (on/over/about sth)","ipa":"/ˈruːmɪneɪt/","chinese":"v. 沉思；认真思考","usage":"It is worth while to ruminate over his remarks.\n他的话值得玩味。"},{"id":"29962c9e-67ff-42b0-b508-cc4def9f2330","english":"stretched thin","ipa":"","chinese":"不堪重负","usage":"During the pandemic, nurses have worked non-stop and are still stretched thin.\n在新冠肺炎期间，护士连轴转工作， 仍然是心有余而力不足。"},{"id":"cc9f2e21-54ad-4a82-bfb9-cd69b33b4cb6","english":"zoom out","ipa":"","chinese":"放大范围，显示更广阔的视野","usage":"Just to zoom out, remind us what is at stake here.\n从全局来看，这其中有何利害关系。"}]},{"day":68,"title":"英语积累Day 68","topic":"生活方式","author":"Nika Erculj","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/4d1121f59c004065b8f8d3fefeac3b16","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lYhv3cVK23Y","audioSize":"689.8KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-068.m4a","youtubeId":"lYhv3cVK23Y","chinese":"今年的第一个收获是，我终于爱上了运动。我尝试过各种的居家锻炼、健身挑战项目、在家做瑜伽，也报过私教、办过健身房会员。老实说，我很难坚持下去，总是一阵一阵的。一开始我很兴奋，然后就完全放弃了。但今年我终于做到了，这可能是我一年中最有成就感的一件事。运动确实让我的生活更加稳定，也让我变得自信和自律。","english":"My first kind of lesson of this year was that I finally fell in love with moving my body. I tried different home workout challenges, programs, at-home yoga, I had a personal trainer, I had a gym membership. It was honestly just so impossible for me to stick to. Like, it was I always came in little spurts. I was really excited, and then I completely fell off. And I finally figured it out this year, and it's honestly been probably the most gratifying part of my year. It's honestly added so much stability to my life. Like, it really builds confidence and discipline.","sentences":["My first kind of lesson of this year was that I finally fell in love with moving my body.","I tried different home workout challenges, programs, at-home yoga, I had a personal trainer, I had a gym membership.","It was honestly just so impossible for me to stick to.","Like, it was I always came in little spurts.","I was really excited, and then I completely fell off.","And I finally figured it out this year, and it's honestly been probably the most gratifying part of my year.","It's honestly added so much stability to my life.","Like, it really builds confidence and discipline."],"exercise":"My first kind of lesson of this year was that I finally fell in love with 运动. I tried different home workout, challenges programs, at-home yoga, I had a 私教, I had a 健身房会员. It was honestly just so impossible for me to 坚持下去. Like, it was I always came 一阵一阵的. I was really excited, and then I completely 完全放弃. And I finally 终于做到了 this year, and it's honestly been probably the most 最有成就感的 part of my year. It's honestly 让我的生活更加稳定 to my life. Like, it really 让我变得自信和自律.","vocabulary":[{"id":"7777b215-f3b1-4973-a146-c21a8af4bd48","english":"personal trainer","ipa":"","chinese":"私人健身教练","usage":"Join a gym or see a personal trainer to stay motivated.\n加入健身馆或者聘用个人教练，让你更有动力。"},{"id":"8c86db8b-5b91-43f9-9cf0-d11a1a3f5bca","english":"gym membership","ipa":"","chinese":"健身房会员","usage":"And you don't need an expensive gym membership or a trainer.\n你也不需要花大量的钱成为健身会员或请教练。"},{"id":"b43194b5-127c-4417-811e-9bcbe364aa9d","english":"stick to","ipa":"","chinese":"坚持（做某事，不怕困难）","usage":"She finds it impossible to stick to a diet.\n饮食老受限制，她觉得受不了。"},{"id":"b86f5fc0-ccce-4145-aecd-3e522df62c0e","english":"in spurts","ipa":"","chinese":"一阵阵地；一股股地","usage":"The water came out of the tap in spurts.\n水急速地从水龙头里喷出来。"},{"id":"ab87f5fa-f44a-42d3-b840-cd6fd942a784","english":"fall off","ipa":"","chinese":"下降；减少","usage":"Membership of the club has fallen off in recent months.\n最近几个月俱乐部的会员人数减少了。"},{"id":"185ef60d-f779-4c29-96c9-fa79b4f5b9e8","english":"figure out","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 弄懂；弄清楚；\n2. 解决","usage":"I can't figure out how to do this.\n我弄不懂怎样做这件事。"},{"id":"28f4b638-d04f-4978-bce7-55d90441d4a3","english":"gratifying","ipa":"/'ɡrætɪfaɪɪŋ/","chinese":"a. 令人高兴的；使人满意的","usage":"It is gratifying to see such good results.\n看到这么好的结果真令人欣慰。"},{"id":"bf41f497-44c8-4e95-8de1-efcb73a0b114","english":"stability","ipa":"/stəˈbɪləti/","chinese":"n. 稳定（性）","usage":"political/economic/social stability\n政治/经济/社会稳定"},{"id":"30de1aac-7051-4f4a-8838-7893732e7296","english":"discipline","ipa":"/ˈdɪsəplɪn/","chinese":"n. 自制力","usage":"He'll never get anywhere working for himself — he's got no discipline.\n他为自己工作是不会有什么成就的，他毫无自制力。"}]},{"day":69,"title":"英语积累Day 69","topic":"情感成长","author":"Nika Erculj","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/60c1582f5e264af7a84428c0a57052e7","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lYhv3cVK23Y","audioSize":"477.2KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-069.m4a","youtubeId":"lYhv3cVK23Y","chinese":"在过去的一年左右，我开始有意专注于我已经拥有的特质和才能，而不是试图融入不适合自己的模式。过去，我总是四处寻觅，却忽略了自己已经拥有的一切，很容易受到外界影响。现在，我关注自己已经拥有的才能，将它们视为我的指路明灯。这是我做过的最爱自己的事之一。随之而来的是，我开始感觉自己像在顺应潮流前行。我不再不停地与某种东西作斗争，也不再逼自己去改变或修复一开始根本就没有损坏的东西。","english":"In the last year or so, I've really started to intentionally focus on the traits and talents I already have, instead of trying to fit a square peg into a round hole. I used to look anywhere but at what I already have. I used to be so impressionable. This focusing on the talents I already have, I treated them like my North Star. And it really ended up being one of the most self-loving things I've ever done. And with that, I started to feel like I was going with the current. I wasn't constantly fighting something and pushing to change or fix what was never even broken in the first place.","sentences":["In the last year or so, I've really started to intentionally focus on the traits and talents I already have, instead of trying to fit a square peg into a round hole.","I used to look anywhere but at what I already have.","I used to be so impressionable.","This focusing on the talents I already have, I treated them like my North Star.","And it really ended up being one of the most self-loving things I've ever done.","And with that, I started to feel like I was going with the current.","I wasn't constantly fighting something and pushing to change or fix what was never even broken in the first place."],"exercise":"In the last year or so, I've really started to intentionally focus on the traits and talents I already have, instead of trying to 融入不适合自己的模式. I used to look anywhere but at what I already have. I used to be so 容易受到外界影响. This focusing on the talents I already have, I treated them like my 指路明灯. And it really ended up being one of the most 爱自己的 things I've ever done. And with that, I started to feel like I was 顺应潮流前行. I wasn't constantly fighting something and pushing to change or fix what was never even broken 一开始.","vocabulary":[{"id":"ab6d6cd8-e661-4357-ba5b-030f716987dc","english":"square peg in a round hole","ipa":"","chinese":"格格不入","usage":"His appearance here is like a square peg in a round hole.  \n他在这里出现，显得有些格格不入。"},{"id":"9c8d7d7a-f4a3-4fa7-9d42-b86e7ce8d8ea","english":"impressionable","ipa":"/ɪmˈpreʃənəbl/","chinese":"a. 易受影响的","usage":"children at an impressionable age\n处于易受外界影响的年龄的儿童"},{"id":"0cd33205-707e-4b20-8150-90817a1dad14","english":"self-loving","ipa":"","chinese":"自爱的","usage":"The world needs more people who are kind-hearted, self-loving, and compassionate.  \n我们的世界，太需要更多富于爱心、爱自己、仁慈的人们了。"},{"id":"6fa514e7-a6f7-458d-a352-d329846139d8","english":"go with the current","ipa":"","chinese":"顺水推舟，顺应事物的发展趋势","usage":"Since they insist on going, we'll simply push the boat with the current and let them go with us. \n既然他们坚持要去，干脆我们就顺水推舟，让他们一同去吧。"},{"id":"0d80a3e5-761d-442d-b7ff-18327eb7549d","english":"in the first place","ipa":"","chinese":"当初","usage":"I should never have taken that job in the first place.\n我当初就不该接受那份工作。"}]},{"day":70,"title":"英语积累Day 70","topic":"工作职场,生活方式","author":"Lydia Violeta","accent":"英音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/c76cb9abc5944ed6b7f93768b81ba560","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vqiheTLtjKA","audioSize":"450.8KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-070.m4a","youtubeId":"vqiheTLtjKA","chinese":"我们下班后去喝了点酒，因为有同事过生日，我喝了两杯玛格丽塔酒，回到家就醉醺醺的。但能和团队在下班后联络一下感情还是挺不错的。我觉得我更加了解了他们，也有机会和一些平时接触不多的人聊天，因为我们的工作没什么交集。总之，那是一段非常愉快的时光。","english":"We went for drinks after work because it was someone's birthday, and I had two margaritas and came home really quite tipsy. But it was nice to have that out-of-office bonding time with the team. I really feel like I got to know them better, and it was also a great opportunity to talk to people that I haven't had as much contact with because we don't work on the same things. So yeah, it was a really nice time.","sentences":["We went for drinks after work because it was someone's birthday, and I had two margaritas and came home really quite tipsy.","But it was nice to have that out-of-office bonding time with the team.","I really feel like I got to know them better, and it was also a great opportunity to talk to people that I haven't had as much contact with because we don't work on the same things.","So yeah, it was a really nice time."],"exercise":"We 去喝了点酒 after work because it was someone's birthday, and I had two 玛格丽塔酒 and came home really quite 醉醺醺的. But it was nice to 在下班后联络一下感情 with the team. I really feel like I got to know them better, and it was also a great opportunity to talk to people that I 平时接触不多 because we 工作没什么交集. So yeah, it was a really nice time.","vocabulary":[{"id":"27181724-aee1-400b-aa58-6d96372c2a67","english":"go out for a drink/drinks","ipa":"","chinese":"去喝酒","usage":""},{"id":"df9667ac-4500-4b7c-bdf3-61e73a0ed53f","english":"margarita","ipa":"/ˌmɑːgə'riːtə/","chinese":"n. 玛格丽特酒","usage":"My favorite cocktail of choice. I like spicy margaritas.\n我最喜欢的鸡尾酒——我喜欢辣的玛格丽塔。"},{"id":"10803dbb-7c8d-4127-9538-64274caae8e7","english":"tipsy","ipa":"/'tɪpsɪ/","chinese":"a. 微醉的；略有醉意的","usage":"You had three glasses and got a little tipsy.\n你喝了三杯 有点醉了。"},{"id":"e1370545-9989-4ec7-93bd-ff6e0d6144f5","english":"bonding","ipa":"/'bɔndiŋ/","chinese":"n. 人与人之间的关系（或联结）","usage":"mother-child bonding\n母子亲情"},{"id":"0a58a47a-008e-4db7-8e9b-3426887793b3","english":"have contact with","ipa":"","chinese":"接触到，和……有联系","usage":"We just have contact with the same eight people.\n我们只会接触同样的8个人。"},{"id":"3ef59b00-3e65-488e-92c2-39d3f1fabc42","english":"work on","ipa":"","chinese":"从事于；工作","usage":"Secondly, we're working on disinformation, independent media.\n第二，我们致力于打击不实信息，发掘独立媒体。"}]},{"day":71,"title":"英语积累Day 71","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Lydia Violeta","accent":"英音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/3b04062f200d4993acaf61ff44b455df","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vqiheTLtjKA","audioSize":"597.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-071.m4a","youtubeId":"vqiheTLtjKA","chinese":"今天的工作穿搭又是一身黑白配。这件背心是几周前从 Dish 买的，我喜欢的不得了。自从买来后，已经穿了很多次，因为它的款式太百搭了。甚至晚上出门时，我也会穿着它。但我也会穿着它去上班，因为领口设计太绝了，我非常喜欢。 下半身我还是穿了一条常穿的黑色长裤，但我很喜欢腰带上那一抹跳脱的金色，这也是几周前从 Dish 买的，我觉得它很好地打破了黑白的单调。","english":"Once again, I've ended up with a very monochrome look for today's work outfit. This is the tank top that I got from Dish a few weeks ago. I am obsessed with it. I've worn it so much since I bought it because the shape of it is just so versatile. Like, I've worn this out on a night out, actually. But I'm also wearing it into work because this neckline is just genius. I love it. I've just got my usual black trousers on, but I'm loving the little pop of gold, this belt I also got from Dish a few weeks ago, and I think it just breaks up the black and white quite nicely.","sentences":["Once again, I've ended up with a very monochrome look for today's work outfit.","This is the tank top that I got from Dish a few weeks ago.","I am obsessed with it.","I've worn it so much since I bought it because the shape of it is just so versatile.","Like, I've worn this out on a night out, actually.","But I'm also wearing it into work because this neckline is just genius.","I love it.","I've just got my usual black trousers on, but I'm loving the little pop of gold, this belt I also got from Dish a few weeks ago, and I think it just breaks up the black and white quite nicely."],"exercise":"Once again, I've ended up with a very 黑白配 look for today's 工作穿搭. This is the 背心 that I got from Dish a few weeks ago. I 喜欢的不得了. I've worn it so much since I bought it because the shape of it is just so 百搭. Like, I've worn this out on a night out, actually. But I'm also wearing it into work because this 领口（设计） is just 太绝了. I love it. I've just 穿了 my usual black trousers on, but I'm loving the little 跳脱的 of gold, this belt I also got from Dish a few weeks ago, and I think it just 打破了 the black and white quite nicely.","vocabulary":[{"id":"ca556aac-df82-46a5-a29f-7c259dfa6085","english":"monochrome","ipa":"/'mɒnəkrəʊm/","chinese":"1. a. 黑白的\n2. 单色的","usage":"1. monochrome illustrations/images\n黑白插图/肖像\n2. a monochromatic colour scheme\n单一色彩的调配"},{"id":"87bbf899-1b52-4e94-986e-78cfacc4cde5","english":"work outfit","ipa":"","chinese":"工作穿搭","usage":"We've been scouring social media and essentially young people are wearing what's being called gross work outfits.\n我们在社交媒体上搜罗，基本上年轻人都穿着所谓的工作恶心穿搭。"},{"id":"c7311036-5f00-42fd-9d64-4db799dca662","english":"tank top","ipa":"","chinese":"1. n. 坎肩\n2. 汗背心","usage":"And just pair it with a simple tank top and boots.\n搭配一件简单的背心和靴子就可以了。"},{"id":"34e09d82-f44c-43a2-a473-65af77657dfa","english":"be obsessed with","ipa":"/əbˈses/","chinese":"痴迷于……","usage":"They will be obsessed with security, lest the Muggles notice anything.\n他们一门心思就想着安全、安全，生怕麻瓜们注意到什么。"},{"id":"ce1f6675-f414-4fee-9a79-fd6a219b3c1c","english":"versatile","ipa":"/ˈvɜːsətaɪl/","chinese":"a. 多用途的；多功能的","usage":"Eggs are easy to cook and are an extremely versatile food.\n鸡蛋容易烹煮，怎么做着吃都行。"},{"id":"ced22487-e9af-47fb-9713-a7ee0cc2007f","english":"neckline","ipa":"/'neklaɪn/","chinese":"n. （女装的）领口，开领","usage":"a dress with a low/round/plunging neckline\n低领/圆领/深 V 字领的连衣裙"},{"id":"af0412aa-311a-4d38-a6e4-aa30c34f7fd1","english":"genius","ipa":"/ˈdʒiːniəs/","chinese":"n. 天才；天资；天赋","usage":"Her idea was a stroke of genius.\n她的主意是聪明的一着。"},{"id":"e9fd10db-aa5b-4f9b-a579-96f010237fd3","english":"have/got sth on","ipa":"","chinese":"穿上","usage":"I loved that dress you had on last night.\n我特别喜欢你昨晚穿的那条裙子"},{"id":"431c3cda-78e0-4883-9af3-bdb2005fec31","english":"pop","ipa":"/pɒp/","chinese":"n. 明亮而吸睛的顏色或物品","usage":"Last season was all about small pops of colour: a turquoise shoe, an emerald bag, or a slash of scarlet lipstick.\n上一季流行的是色彩明亮抓人眼球的小件：一双松石绿色的鞋、一个祖母绿色的包或一抹猩红色的唇膏。"},{"id":"15c40de2-a871-4aa8-aaa7-55a5e1e7e9c7","english":"break up","ipa":"","chinese":"打破；使破碎","usage":"The water was covered with ice, which could sometimes break up without warning. 水面上覆盖着冰，这些冰有时会突然破碎。"}]},{"day":72,"title":"英语积累Day 72","topic":"情感成长","author":"Elena Taber","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/53ecd7d9ffca49c19e7b16cc11a3da5e","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ehn_TYlxe3E","audioSize":"533.4KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-072.m4a","youtubeId":"Ehn_TYlxe3E","chinese":"有人问我：“你在20多岁的时候，是怎么最大限度地过好单身生活的？”我只谈过一次真正意义上的长期恋爱，也有两次断断续续地谈了较长一段时间，还有过很多短暂的暧昧拉扯，有趣的故事足以写进回忆录。所以当有人问我这个问题时，我会说，这可以让你完全自主地安排日程、做出决定、培养兴趣，以及确定人生方向。我认为在这个阶段，能暂时“自私”一点是很重要的，让自己考虑好想走什么样的道路，即使未来想有一段长期恋爱关系，在合适的时机，你也能以更好的伴侣形象出现。","english":"So someone had asked me, \"How do you make the most out of being single in your 20s?\" I've only had one, like, really long-term relationship, and then there's, like, two other people that I dated for a decent amount of time on and off, and then there's been a lot of flings and whatnot and enough interesting stories to fill the memoir one day. So when someone asked me this, I said it allows total autonomy of your schedule, decisions, interests, and direction you're taking in life. I think it's important to be selfish in quotations in this season for a little while to understand what paths you want to pursue, so that you can show up as a better partner down the line when the timing is right if you want a long-term relationship.","sentences":["So someone had asked me, \"How do you make the most out of being single in your 20s?\"","I've only had one, like, really long-term relationship, and then there's, like, two other people that I dated for a decent amount of time on and off, and then there's been a lot of flings and whatnot and enough interesting stories to fill the memoir one day.","So when someone asked me this, I said it allows total autonomy of your schedule, decisions, interests, and direction you're taking in life.","I think it's important to be selfish in quotations in this season for a little while to understand what paths you want to pursue, so that you can show up as a better partner down the line when the timing is right if you want a long-term relationship."],"exercise":"So someone had asked me, \"How do you 最大限度地过好 being single in your 20s?\" I've only had one, like, really long-term relationship, and then there's, like, two other people that I dated for 较长一段时间 断断续续地, and then there's been a lot of 短暂的暧昧拉扯 and enough interesting stories to 写进回忆录 one day. So when someone asked me this, I said it 让（你）完全自主地 of your schedule, decisions, interests, and direction you're taking in life. I think it's important to be “自私” in this season for a little while to understand what paths you want to pursue, so that you can show up as a better partner 未来 when the timing is right if you want a long-term relationship.","vocabulary":[{"id":"1e3aff5c-7b8d-4c4b-add5-0129431ee9ed","english":"make the most out of","ipa":"","chinese":"充分利用","usage":"A good investor can always make the most out of any amount of time.\n好的投资者总是能够充分利用任何时间。"},{"id":"83a79277-469a-47b1-a44d-1eec4cb858c5","english":"a decent amount of time","ipa":"","chinese":"相当多的时间","usage":""},{"id":"dbe7ac87-f7ed-4af7-a348-b835a660327e","english":"on and off","ipa":"","chinese":"不时地；经常；断断续续地","usage":"It rained on and off all day.\n雨断断续续地下了一整天。"},{"id":"14f89320-4153-4f0c-8da9-09ae4fea4c38","english":"fling","ipa":"/flɪŋ/","chinese":"n. 风流韵事；一阵尽情欢乐；一时的放纵","usage":"She claims she had a brief fling with him 30 years ago.   她声称30年前曾跟他有过一段短暂的风流韵事。"},{"id":"f06ef178-1dce-4c6a-9ced-7b2a4259a7ac","english":"whatnot","ipa":"/'wɒtnɒt/","chinese":"n. 不可名状的东西；诸如此类","usage":""},{"id":"bb959d13-5dc7-4276-b42b-3e56a672dd3e","english":"memoir","ipa":"/'memwɑː/","chinese":"n. 回忆录","usage":"She wrote a memoir of her stay in France.\n她写了一篇旅法记事录。"},{"id":"c86706f7-71aa-49b5-b3af-5aa279ccbe64","english":"autonomy","ipa":"/ɔːˈtɒnəmi/","chinese":"n. 自主；自主权","usage":"giving individuals greater autonomy in their own lives\n给个人在生活中更大的自主权"},{"id":"69aa7934-f935-4c6e-8752-fd507fb26a6a","english":"in quotation","ipa":"","chinese":"加引号","usage":""},{"id":"fbec85e6-525b-4f4f-b263-13e2a74201f7","english":"down the line","ipa":"","chinese":"这里的line可以理解为“时间线”，所以down the line就是“顺着时间线”的意思，翻译成中文就是：将来。","usage":"Then several months down the line revisit this exercise and see how you're getting on. 几个月之后再回头看看，自己是不是变了呢？"}]},{"day":73,"title":"英语积累Day 73","topic":"生活方式","author":"Eve Bennett","accent":"英音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/4a9ba5437e354677b26e092e20ec9c4c","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=slorlXu9m9M","audioSize":"511.8KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-073.m4a","youtubeId":"slorlXu9m9M","chinese":"我一次只打扫一个房间，因为我觉得这样更容易搞定。今天的任务是打扫卧室。其实这个房间从来没有这么乱过，都是因为我到处乱扔衣服。我感觉这个周末，其实我并不想其实我并不想忙着打扫或者做其他事情，只想过个轻松愉快的周末，庆祝妈妈的生日。行，咱们开始打扫吧。我已经把这个房间清理干净了。这里积攒的灰尘真的太多了，所以我清理了个遍，把一堆衣服扔进洗衣机，看我从地毯上刮下来了多少灰啊。我觉得今天的打扫确实取得了些进展。","english":"I'm doing it one room at a time because I feel like that makes it a lot more manageable. The job today is the bedroom. It's actually never been this messy just because I've been chucking clothes everywhere. I think just this weekend, I wasn't really all fussed about cleaning or anything. I just wanted to have a chilled, nice weekend celebrating Mom's birthday. Okay, let's give it a go. I've dusted down this. The amount of dust that accumulates in here is really insane. So I've dusted all of this, I've put a load of laundry in, and look how much dust I got from scraping the carpet. I feel like I've definitely made some headway today.","sentences":["I'm doing it one room at a time because I feel like that makes it a lot more manageable.","The job today is the bedroom.","It's actually never been this messy just because I've been chucking clothes everywhere.","I think just this weekend, I wasn't really all fussed about cleaning or anything.","I just wanted to have a chilled, nice weekend celebrating Mom's birthday.","Okay, let's give it a go.","I've dusted down this.","The amount of dust that accumulates in here is really insane.","So I've dusted all of this, I've put a load of laundry in, and look how much dust I got from scraping the carpet.","I feel like I've definitely made some headway today."],"exercise":"I'm doing it one room at a time because I feel like that makes it a lot more 容易搞定. The job today is the bedroom. It's actually never been this messy just because I've been 到处乱扔 clothes everywhere. I think just this weekend, I wasn't really all 忙着 cleaning or anything. I just wanted to have a 轻松的, nice weekend celebrating Mom's birthday. Okay, let's 咱们开始打扫吧. I've 清理干净 this. The amount of dust that 积攒 in here is really 太多了. So I've 清理 all of this, I've put 一堆 laundry in, and look how much dust I got from 刮下来 the carpet. I feel like I've definitely 取得了些进展 today.","vocabulary":[{"id":"b62d0428-1131-4dba-8432-bc831752a7de","english":"manageable","ipa":"/ˈmænɪdʒəbl/","chinese":"a. 可处理的","usage":"Use conditioner regularly to make your hair soft and manageable.\n经常使用护发剂来使你的头发柔软而且易于梳理。"},{"id":"065069f0-375b-4609-9dce-5283fb531907","english":"chuck","ipa":"/tʃʌk/","chinese":"v. 随便或贸然地）扔，抛","usage":"He chucked the paper in a drawer.\n他把那份报纸顺手丢进了抽屉。"},{"id":"05a15dfd-9976-4cd9-b62f-e8bcaf1efab0","english":"fuss about","ipa":"","chinese":"大惊小怪；瞎忙活","usage":"What a lot of fuss about nothing!\n“真是无事瞎忙乎！”"},{"id":"787899ee-57a9-4809-b49b-d5667108013c","english":"chilled","ipa":"/tʃɪld/","chinese":"a. 放松的","usage":"We went home and chilled in front of the TV.\n我们回家坐在电视机前放松。"},{"id":"ff3d7ce5-f3f0-4096-9c27-5a7c0a74b81b","english":"give it a go","ipa":"","chinese":"试试看","usage":"We'll only have 20 minutes left to finish that report, but let's give it a go.\n我们只有20分钟写完这份报告。可不管怎么说先试一试。"},{"id":"688c4aa8-b101-4b10-ad53-77e4dac3970b","english":"dust down","ipa":"","chinese":"除去 … 的灰尘","usage":"Mel stood up and dusted herself down.\n梅尔站起来拍掉了身上的尘土。"},{"id":"5ddfee87-c536-44f9-ad43-349146440169","english":"accumulate","ipa":"/əˈkjuːmjəleɪt/","chinese":"v. 积累；积聚","usage":"I seem to have accumulated a lot of books.\n我好像已经收集了很多书。"},{"id":"f23ffea9-d1e6-48af-bef0-d2ae066cf1f1","english":"insane","ipa":"/ɪnˈseɪn/","chinese":"a. 疯狂的","usage":"This job is driving me insane.\n这份工作快要把我逼疯了。"},{"id":"6e467222-e6fd-4e07-a50e-041c0bc30cad","english":"dust","ipa":"/dʌst/","chinese":"v. 擦去 … 的灰尘；擦灰","usage":"I broke the vase while I was dusting.\n我擦灰尘时将花瓶打碎了。"},{"id":"40a811a4-e857-40e8-935d-7caa1354a65f","english":"a load of","ipa":"","chinese":"大量；许多","usage":"There's also a load of free downloads.\n有很多免费下载的资源。"},{"id":"70ce50ba-6a94-482f-998e-b3b175953414","english":"scraping","ipa":"/ˈskreɪ.pɪŋ/","chinese":"n. 刮除;擦掉","usage":"Use techniques that generate less dust, such as wet sanding or scraping.\n采用不会产生太多灰尘的办法，如湿式打磨或刮削。"},{"id":"b85aae08-2638-4b15-82f3-7cda95208690","english":"make some headway","ipa":"","chinese":"取得进展","usage":"You know, I actually think I'm making some headway on this H.M.O. thing.\n我觉得我在卫生维护组织的问题上有些进展了。"}]},{"day":74,"title":"英语积累Day 74","topic":"生活方式","author":"adelala","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/8384f154229041a1b971c3c03eea0820","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jDNzqilHjlM","audioSize":"464.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-074.m4a","youtubeId":"jDNzqilHjlM","chinese":"在 12 月的某一天，我决定开车去找房，心里没抱任何期待。我能接受各种条件，但有几个硬性要求。其中之一当然是采光要好，这是首要条件。我希望新公寓里能有娱乐设施，比如楼里能有个健身房的话就太赞了。还希望公寓能自带独立的洗衣机和烘干机。我想搬到离商店和咖啡馆不远的地方，步行就能到。另外，能看到美景的大窗户也是必不可少的。","english":"In December, just one random day, I decided to go drive out and go apartment-hunting, not expecting to find anything. I was pretty open to anything. I did have a few non-negotiables. One of them, of course, being a good and natural lighting. This is the top priority. I was hoping that my next apartment would have recreational amenities, like having a gym in the building would be so cool. I wanted the apartment to have an in-unit washer plus dryer. This time I wanted to move into a place that was walking distance to grocery stores, cafes, etc. Big windows with a pretty view were a must.","sentences":["In December, just one random day, I decided to go drive out and go apartment-hunting, not expecting to find anything.","I was pretty open to anything.","I did have a few non-negotiables.","One of them, of course, being a good and natural lighting.","This is the top priority.","I was hoping that my next apartment would have recreational amenities, like having a gym in the building would be so cool.","I wanted the apartment to have an in-unit washer plus dryer.","This time I wanted to move into a place that was walking distance to grocery stores, cafes, etc.","Big windows with a pretty view were a must."],"exercise":"So, in December, 某一天, I decided to go drive out and 去找房, not expecting to find anything. I was pretty 能接受各种条件. I did have a few 硬性要求. One of them, of course, being 采光要好. This is the 首要条件. I was hoping that my next apartment would have 娱乐设施, like having a gym in the building would be so cool. I wanted the apartment to have an 自带洗衣机和烘干机. This time I wanted to move into a place that was 离…不远，步行就能到 to grocery stores, cafes, etc. Big windows with a pretty view were 必不可少.","vocabulary":[{"id":"646803f9-33c7-49a7-aedf-804ce0f3ba31","english":"random","ipa":"/ˈrændəm/","chinese":"a. 随机的，随意的","usage":"He grabbed a pair of random jeans and an old red shirt.\n他抓了一条随意拿到的牛仔裤和一件旧的红衬衫"},{"id":"d121212d-84ca-4e59-b819-2309109300c0","english":"hunting","ipa":"/ˈhʌntɪŋ/","chinese":"构成复合词：找；寻找","usage":"1. We're going house-hunting at the weekend.\n周末我们去找房子。\n2. How's the job-hunting going?\n工作找得怎么样了？"},{"id":"5e262bc8-eefd-445a-a389-d29e019bd87e","english":"open to anything","ipa":"","chinese":"对任何事情都持开放态度：愿意尝试或接受各种可能性或建议。","usage":"Abbott says he's open to anything. He wants to hold a round table early next week to start beginning discussions.\n阿伯特说，他愿意接受各种意见。他希望在下周初举行圆桌会议，开始进行讨论。"},{"id":"c32f0dfb-71cc-43ca-81b5-f8aaf45a9392","english":"non-negotiable","ipa":"/ˌnɒn.nəˈɡəʊ.ʃə.bəl/","chinese":"a. 无商量余地的；无法改变的","usage":"The terms of this agreement are non-negotiable.\n这项协议的条款不容商榷。"},{"id":"0b913ffd-f5c0-448e-8e36-2384f909b373","english":"good and natural lighting","ipa":"","chinese":"采光好","usage":""},{"id":"a0770989-7fde-4313-a4b4-d39dcaff8c58","english":"top priority","ipa":"","chinese":"最先考虑","usage":"In the 21st century convenience is a top priority.\n在 21 世纪，便利是头等大事。"},{"id":"dae9a8b1-a252-40bf-bd9a-91e04c057e33","english":"recreational amenities","ipa":"/ˌrekriˈeɪʃənl/\n/ə'miːnɪtɪ/","chinese":"娱乐设施","usage":"Aquatic recreational amenities\n水上娱乐设施"},{"id":"56e2b95c-d9a5-4431-9814-a8ec6037c9c6","english":"in-unit washer plus dryer","ipa":"","chinese":"内置洗衣机和烘干机","usage":""},{"id":"b6ece190-38df-46ee-b444-962934fcc4d0","english":"walking distance","ipa":"","chinese":"步行距离","usage":"The store is within walking distance of my apartment.\n这家商店离我的公寓只有几步之遥。"},{"id":"d0dd31f7-0e4c-4477-8674-a19ce6a7494f","english":"must","ipa":"/mʌst/","chinese":"n. 必须做（或看、买等）的事","usage":"His new novel is a must for all lovers of crime fiction.\n他的新作是所有犯罪小说爱好者的必读书目。"}]},{"day":75,"title":"英语积累Day 75","topic":"数码产品,生活方式","author":"Hannah Adkins","accent":"英音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/7578d60d8213493d98bec15c175ccdcc","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MeO-favi2bI","audioSize":"588.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-075.m4a","youtubeId":"MeO-favi2bI","chinese":"我一直在推迟使用手机的时间。我并不觉得社交媒体只有坏处。我认为它可以起到积极作用，给人带来启发，让你感觉与他人有所联结。但我确实觉得，我们需要更有意识地选择何时使用社交媒体，不要让它成为一种无意识的自发行为。这是我目前做出的最重要的改变。 而且，早上出门散步能让我以最好的状态迎接新的一天。","english":"I’ve been not on my phone. I have been like putting off going on my phone. Like it will get like 10 a.m. and I'll just think, Oh, I don't even want to pick it up because I've been having such like productive, clear, positive mornings without all of the kind of external noise that comes from your phone. I do not think social media is a bad thing at all. I think it could be a really positive inspirational thing. I think it can make you feel connected to others. I think there are so many, so many benefits. You can learn loads, you can get so much inspiration. But I do think we need to be so much more careful with when we choose to consume social media rather than it being on auto.","sentences":["I’ve been not on my phone.","I have been like putting off going on my phone.","Like it will get like 10 a.m. and I'll just think, Oh, I don't even want to pick it up because I've been having such like productive, clear, positive mornings without all of the kind of external noise that comes from your phone.","I do not think social media is a bad thing at all.","I think it could be a really positive inspirational thing.","I think it can make you feel connected to others.","I think there are so many, so many benefits.","You can learn loads, you can get so much inspiration.","But I do think we need to be so much more careful with when we choose to consume social media rather than it being on auto."],"exercise":"I’ve been 不碰手机. I have been like 推迟 使用 my phone. Like it will get like 10 a.m. and I'll just think, Oh, I don't even want to 拿起它 because I've been having such like productive, clear, positive mornings without all of the kind of  外部干扰 that comes from your phone. I do not think social media is a bad thing at all. I think it could be a really 有到积极作用，能给人带来启发. I think it can make you feel 与他人有所联结. I think there are so many, so many benefits. You can learn 很多, you can get so much inspiration. But I do think we need to be so much more careful with when we choose to 使用社交媒体 rather than 让它成为一种无意识的自发行为.","vocabulary":[{"id":"c192fbf4-36ef-41ef-9279-9c1cfb07e5dd","english":"put off","ipa":"","chinese":"推迟；延迟","usage":"We've had to put off our wedding until September.\n我们只得把婚期推迟到九月。"},{"id":"22aa7a4e-1d4f-4e46-abed-aa71a11f9ddc","english":"pick up","ipa":"","chinese":"拿起，捡起","usage":""},{"id":"4fcd788b-1833-44f7-96e7-4e0c42daff51","english":"external noise","ipa":"","chinese":"外在噪音，外界的干扰","usage":""},{"id":"13b499d9-5f6f-4d26-968e-0f9517c242c0","english":"inspirational","ipa":"/ɪnspɪ'reɪʃ(ə)n(ə)l/","chinese":"a. 启发灵感的；鼓舞人心的","usage":"an inspirational leader\n有感召力的领袖"},{"id":"19aa7fd4-2aa5-4902-9303-84cff787864d","english":"be/feel connected to","ipa":"","chinese":"与…有联系","usage":"They believe that people are connected to their ancestors.\n他们认为人与他们的祖先是有联系的。"},{"id":"99e81e03-fe28-4ba2-a740-6621ccacac6c","english":"loads","ipa":"/ləʊd/","chinese":"n. 大量，许多","usage":""},{"id":"579d7a53-4074-4255-a4e5-995aef1fc361","english":"consume social media","ipa":"","chinese":"使用社交媒体","usage":"There's been a lot said about the dangers of consuming social media.\n关于使用社交媒体的危险，已经有很多说法。"},{"id":"9b6e0386-76f6-4d47-8566-d130e90619a5","english":"on auto","ipa":"/ˈɔː.təʊ/","chinese":"指在完成某项任务时，不需要过多思考，凭借习惯或经验自动完成。","usage":""}]},{"day":76,"title":"英语积累Day 76","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Hannah Adkins","accent":"英音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/887cf608ba1d4583bec104ee8214e13e","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gLxNCgesF58","audioSize":"513.4KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-076.m4a","youtubeId":"gLxNCgesF58","chinese":"这是我最喜欢的套头针织衫。它们真的非常好穿，是非常保暖但又相当轻薄的一层衣物，因为材质是100%纯羊绒。它们在保暖的同时，又不像那种厚重的绞花针织套头毛衣。你可以把它搭在任何衣服下面。有很多不同的颜色，我现在有奶油色、黑色、海军蓝、灰色。这个款式不会过时，老实说，它们今年已经成为了我衣橱里的必备款式，能搭配任何衣服，我觉得它们搭配起来很顺眼，穿起来又非常容易，只需要套进去就行了。也能搭牛仔裤，能搭配任何衣服。","english":"That's my favorite jumper ever. And they are just so handy. It's like a really warm, but still quite lightweight layer because they're 100% cashmere. They still have that kind of warmth but without being a really big chunky, sort of cable-knit jumper. She You can just kind of pop these on underneath anything. They do them in so many different colors. I now have them in cream, black, navy, gray. They're just like timeless, honestly, being an absolute staple in my wardrobe this year. They just go with everything, and I feel like they look put together, but they're so easy to just throw on. They go with jeans, they go with anything.","sentences":["That's my favorite jumper ever.","And they are just so handy.","It's like a really warm, but still quite lightweight layer because they're 100% cashmere.","They still have that kind of warmth but without being a really big chunky, sort of cable-knit jumper.","She You can just kind of pop these on underneath anything.","They do them in so many different colors.","I now have them in cream, black, navy, gray.","They're just like timeless, honestly, being an absolute staple in my wardrobe this year.","They just go with everything, and I feel like they look put together, but they're so easy to just throw on.","They go with jeans, they go with anything."],"exercise":"That's my favorite 套头针织衫 ever. And they are just so 好穿. It's like a really warm, but still quite 轻薄 layer because they're 100% cashmere. They still have that kind of warmth but without being a really 厚重的绞花针织套头毛衣. you can just kind of 把它搭在任何衣服下面. They do them in so many different colors. I now have them in cream, black, navy, gray. They're just like 不会过时, honestly, being an absolute 必备款式 in my wardrobe this year. They just 搭配任何衣服, and I feel like they 搭配起来很顺眼, but they're so easy to just 套进去. They 能搭 jeans, they 搭配 anything.","vocabulary":[{"id":"4d303220-b36f-4504-9f8e-d9fe7faa6c79","english":"jumper","ipa":"/'dʒʌmpə/","chinese":"n. 针织套衫","usage":"Isabel had on a simple jumper and skirt.\n伊莎贝尔穿着素净的针织套衫和裙子。"},{"id":"23a7c5d5-203a-4bfe-b5cc-6e5cd9b34ac7","english":"handy","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 1. 有用的;方便的\n2. 手边的;附近的\n3. 手巧的;有手艺的","usage":"1. Credit cards can be handy — they mean you do not have to carry large sums of cash.\n信用卡很方便，有了它你就不用携带大量现金了。\n2. It would be good to have a pencil and paper handy...\n最好在手边准备好纸和笔。\n3. If you're handy with a needle you could brighten up your sweater with daisies.\n如果你针线活做得好，可以在自己的毛衣上绣几朵雏菊做点缀。"},{"id":"d9ad1c6d-9572-45f7-b4cd-2df1ef5dd195","english":"lightweight","ipa":"/'laɪtweɪt/","chinese":"a. 轻量的；轻质的；比通常重量轻的\nn. 1. 拳击、柔道、赛艇等运动中的轻量级；\n2. 无足轻重的人；无能的人","usage":"1. The company manufactures a range of innovative light-weight cycles.\n这家公司生产一系列的新型轻便自行车。\n2. By the age of sixteen he was the junior lightweight champion of Poland...\n16岁时他已经是波兰的青少年组轻量级冠军。\n3. Hill considered Sam a lightweight, a real amateur.\n希尔认为萨姆无足轻重，是个十足的生手。"},{"id":"b72bb6a8-90f1-4c9d-bf95-d47f3af9b105","english":"cashemere","ipa":"/kæʃ'mɪə/","chinese":"n. 山羊绒","usage":""},{"id":"d5f92ed3-5ed9-43b0-88b0-c8423181e86b","english":"chunky","ipa":"/'tʃʌŋkɪ/","chinese":"a. 粗重的;大而重的;人粗壮的，背阔胸宽的；","usage":"a chunky sweater.\n厚实的套头毛衣"},{"id":"5726030f-77eb-44dd-8c3b-4fa5a4f97ec8","english":"cable-knit","ipa":"","chinese":"adj. 麻花针的","usage":""},{"id":"05e447da-b9cf-4c84-a9c2-1acb751cceb3","english":"pop on","ipa":"","chinese":"迅速穿上：迅速穿上（衣物）","usage":"I'll just pop on a sweater and meet you outside.  我套件毛衣就出来见你。"},{"id":"f623d9aa-65bd-4fe6-aed8-5cf7dbc08620","english":"underneath","ipa":"/ˌʌndəˈniːθ/","chinese":"prep. 在…下面；在…底下","usage":"The device exploded underneatha van.\n该装置在一辆货车底下发生了爆炸。"},{"id":"8b759487-b28d-4307-a21e-d49cc2c2d82f","english":"timeless","ipa":"/'taɪmlɪs/","chinese":"a. 永久的;恒久美好的;不受时间影响的","usage":"There is a timeless quality to his best work.\n他最好的作品不会因时间流逝而逊色。"},{"id":"aa3572b2-35a2-4934-a170-b8b55ead6f45","english":"staple","ipa":"/ˈsteɪpl/","chinese":"a. 1. (食物、产品或活动)主要的，基本的\n2. 主要部分;重要内容\nn. 订书钉","usage":"1. Rice is the staple food of more than half the world's population...\n稻米是全世界一半以上人口的主食。\n2. Political reporting has become a staple of American journalism.\n政治新闻已成为美国新闻报道的主要内容。"},{"id":"7a6a6676-5010-479b-843b-d569419ba0f8","english":"throw on","ipa":"","chinese":"迅速穿上（一件衣物）；套上","usage":""}]},{"day":77,"title":"英语积累Day 77","topic":"生活方式","author":"Cozy K","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/21459049c486449386cc0bc1b22d7e88","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=shB7HqX-2tk","audioSize":"416.3KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-077.m4a","youtubeId":"shB7HqX-2tk","chinese":"生活或许感觉就像朝你袭来，而你却无法暂停。月复一月、年复一年，在单调乏味的日常中飞逝而过，你或许会被迫感到：“难道就是这样吗？这就是生活的全部吗？”我觉得在我们生活的这个疯狂的世界里，有这样的感受是非常正常和健康的。我们似乎注定要像仓鼠一样在小小的滚轮上奔跑，而不是在大自然中与可爱的动物一起嬉戏、狩猎和采集。但我们也应当打破这一循环。","english":"Life might feel like it's just coming at you, and you can't stop it. Months and years are whizzing by in this kind of same monotonous routine, and you might be pushed to feel like, \"Is this it? Is this everything life is?\" I think that's a very normal and healthy thing to feel on this crazy world we live in where we are meant to run on this little hamster wheel instead of just like frolicking in nature with cute animals and hunting and gathering. But we also do deserve to break ourselves out of that loop.","sentences":["Life might feel like it's just coming at you, and you can't stop it.","Months and years are whizzing by in this kind of same monotonous routine, and you might be pushed to feel like, \"Is this it?","Is this everything life is?\"","I think that's a very normal and healthy thing to feel on this crazy world we live in where we are meant to run on this little hamster wheel instead of just like frolicking in nature with cute animals and hunting and gathering.","But we also do deserve to break ourselves out of that loop."],"exercise":"Life might feel like it's just 朝你袭来, and you can't stop it. 月复一月、年复一年 are飞逝而过 in this kind of same 单调乏味的日常, and you might 被迫 feel like, \"Is this it? Is this everything life is?\" I think that's a very normal and healthy thing to feel on this crazy world we live in where we 似乎注定要 像仓鼠一样在小小的滚轮上奔跑 instead of just like 嬉戏 in nature with cute animals and hunting and gathering. But we also do 应当打破这一循环.","vocabulary":[{"id":"7689bc22-3610-4cf4-aa55-38541ec89e0c","english":"come at you","ipa":"","chinese":"走向你；向你扑面而来","usage":"1. It's 3-D, folks. It's coming at you. 这可是三维效果，向你扑面而来。\n2. Just everything coming at you 每件事情都应接不暇\n3. Your life is about to change, and things are about to come at you very fast. 你的生活将迎来改变，事情如潮水般汹涌而来。"},{"id":"0664ceb8-e859-4116-ac00-c1f887625102","english":"whizz","ipa":"/hwiz/","chinese":"飞驰;嗖嗖地移动","usage":"A car whizzed past.\n一辆汽车疾驰而过。"},{"id":"76dac62e-d1ef-45d3-8f99-677de3e72a59","english":"monotonous","ipa":"/məˈnɒtənəs/","chinese":"单调乏味的;毫无变化的","usage":"• It's monotonous work, like most factory jobs...\n与工厂大部分工作一样，这份工作也很单调乏味。"},{"id":"4741356f-9dd6-4d3a-859a-b20604778f0f","english":"be pushed to","ipa":"","chinese":"被迫做某事，没有足够的时间或金钱：指在某种情况下，由于压力或限制，被迫去做某事，而没有足够的时间或金钱。","usage":"Sometimes in life, we are pushed to our limit. 有时在生活中，我们被推到了极限。"},{"id":"7bc237cc-dbc4-4dcb-b48f-281a5abbc7f0","english":"be meant to","ipa":"","chinese":"应该是； 注定要；照理应当，打算要；旨在","usage":"Whenever , wherever, we are meant to be together. 无论何时，无论何地，我们注定会在一起。"},{"id":"125f7b0f-6bc6-4ece-af5d-db71f875d975","english":"hamster wheel","ipa":"/'hæmstə//wiːl/","chinese":"仓鼠轮：一种圆形的笼子，用于养仓鼠或其他小型啮齿动物，当动物在底部奔跑时，笼子会垂直旋转。在引申义上，也可以指一种单调、重复、无法满足的活动，特别是那些没有取得进展的活动。","usage":"Sometimes it feels like we're running on the hamster wheel of life. 有时感觉就像我们在生活的仓鼠轮上奔跑。"},{"id":"687a0faa-1d92-4112-b063-5929e115574f","english":"frolick","ipa":"/ˈfrɒlɪk/","chinese":"嬉戏;嬉闹","usage":"Tourists sunbathe and frolic in the ocean.\n游客晒着日光浴在海水里嬉戏。"},{"id":"05968eb6-764d-4fd7-8f79-4b92ff8821e5","english":"deserve","ipa":"/dɪˈzɜːv/","chinese":"应得;应受;值得","usage":"These people deserve to make more than the minimum wage.\n这些人应该得到比最低工资更高的报酬。"},{"id":"24babe02-4342-4720-b910-e5ef4818b017","english":"loop","ipa":"/luːp/","chinese":"n. 1. 圈, 环, 环状物\n2. 回路, 循环","usage":"These activists don't want to feel out of the loop.\n这些活跃分子不想做局外人。"},{"id":"ed9a4c89-0dda-48ea-bca7-749aa7ddb1b9","english":"break out of","ipa":"","chinese":"改变生活方式; 突破; 摆脱; 逃出;","usage":"She needed to break out of her daily routine and do something exciting.  她需要从日常事务中解脱出来，找点有意思的事做。"}]},{"day":78,"title":"英语积累Day 78","topic":"情感成长","author":"Pick Up Limes","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/0a0c8de0ba6c4382ac7c3a1a12a4a332","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1-VFShuFJXQ","audioSize":"599.5KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-078.m4a","youtubeId":"1-VFShuFJXQ","chinese":"我们都曾在一瞬间冲动地做出过快的反应。也许是同伴出乎意料的一句话，也许是突如其来的交通堵塞，又或者是最后一刻的项目变动。有多少次我们希望在一下子做出回应或反应之前能稍作停顿呢？我们都清楚，反应过快有时会导致判断错误，错失把握全局的机会。因此，我一直积极尝试，在接收信息和做出反应之间留出一些空间，让自己能够消化信息，也让信息沉淀下来。我已经养成了一个习惯，就是每当感到情绪激动时，就深吸一口气。","english":"We've all had moments where we impulsively react too quickly. Maybe it's an unexpected comment from a partner or sudden traffic, a last-minute project change. How many times have we wished that we just took a little pause before diving headfirst into a response or reaction? We all know that speedy reactions can sometimes lead to misjudgments and missed opportunities to understand the big picture. So I've been actively trying to create space between receiving information and formulating a response, giving myself permission to digest and just let the information marinate. I've gotten into the habit of just taking a deep breath anytime I feel emotionally charged.","sentences":["We've all had moments where we impulsively react too quickly.","Maybe it's an unexpected comment from a partner or sudden traffic, a last-minute project change.","How many times have we wished that we just took a little pause before diving headfirst into a response or reaction?","We all know that speedy reactions can sometimes lead to misjudgments and missed opportunities to understand the big picture.","So I've been actively trying to create space between receiving information and formulating a response, giving myself permission to digest and just let the information marinate.","I've gotten into the habit of just taking a deep breath anytime I feel emotionally charged."],"exercise":"We've all had moments where we 冲动地做出反应 too quickly. Maybe it's an unexpected comment from a partner or sudden traffic, 最后一刻的项目变动. How many times have we wished that we just took a little pause before 一下子 a response or reaction? We all know that 反应过快 can sometimes lead to misjudgments and missed opportunities to understand 全局. So I've been actively trying to create space between receiving information and 做出反应, 消化信息 and just let the information 沉淀. I've gotten into the habit of just taking a deep breath anytime I 感到情绪激动.","vocabulary":[{"id":"54e3092c-1203-4c27-89fd-4e755e82acb6","english":"impulsively","ipa":"/im'pʌlsivli/","chinese":"adv. 冲动地","usage":"Impulsively he reached out and took her hand.\n他一时冲动便伸手握住她的手。"},{"id":"df37fe76-3c84-49ea-ae5a-0787e9bf9e76","english":"last-minute","ipa":"/'læst'mɪnɪt/","chinese":"a. 最后一分钟才完成（或决定、安排好）的；","usage":"a last-minute holiday\n最后一分钟定下来的休假"},{"id":"6cdb1893-6def-474e-81b0-ab11b280468b","english":"dive headfirst into","ipa":"","chinese":"头脑发热地做某事","usage":""},{"id":"5000cd39-6ca9-495c-b2b8-9c86c004071e","english":"headfirst","ipa":"/'hedfɜːst/","chinese":"a. 未经深思；轻率；鲁莽","usage":"She got divorced and rushed head first into another marriage.\n她离婚后又仓促再婚了。"},{"id":"8c72c02a-1516-4f6c-a7bc-74bcb6ee6a6c","english":"speedy reactions","ipa":"","chinese":"快速反应","usage":""},{"id":"1a4e4296-4aff-4a29-b801-77c54636c65c","english":"the big picture","ipa":"","chinese":"整个局面；大局","usage":"Right now forget the details and take a look at the big picture.\n现在别管细节问题，先通观全局。"},{"id":"8a88f945-3ef7-460c-a848-bd4fc9776c46","english":"formulate","ipa":"/ˈfɔːmjuleɪt/","chinese":"v. 构想","usage":"to formulate a policy/theory/plan/proposal\n制订政策；创立理论；构想计划；准备建议"},{"id":"a1edb503-3d8d-4bda-8937-282423e65e53","english":"digest","ipa":"/daɪˈdʒest/","chinese":"v. 领会；领悟；理解","usage":"He paused, waiting for her to digest the information.\n他停了一会儿，等她慢慢领会这一信息。"},{"id":"238d8df1-6329-4431-8d4d-53241f3b1f8a","english":"marinate","ipa":"/'mærɪneɪt/","chinese":"v. 1. 用腌汁浸泡;腌泡；\n2. 引申含义：沉淀；耐心等待某事；像“腌制肉一样”地“长期沉浸在特定环境或经历中，让其影响或左右自己的思想、情感或观点。","usage":"He will talk once he’s had time to marinate. 等他有时间沉淀，他会说的。"},{"id":"f7ca6adb-ccef-4a2d-8da8-a4c33875cfee","english":"charged","ipa":"/tʃɑ:dʒd/","chinese":"a. (形势)紧张的，引起强烈感情的","usage":"There was a highly charged atmosphere...\n气氛高度紧张。"},{"id":"696d26f7-f3a4-4d43-9ee3-b0c9423eead2","english":"emotionally charged","ipa":"","chinese":"情绪激动","usage":"A wedding is an emotionally charged situation.  \n婚礼是一个激动人心的场合。"}]},{"day":79,"title":"英语积累Day 79","topic":"生活方式","author":"Call Me Kathi","accent":"英音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/2f40d1790c1947a0aac0d5b098d8b659","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sXDw8-N_Vrw","audioSize":"379.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-079.m4a","youtubeId":"sXDw8-N_Vrw","chinese":"我们今晚要通宵学习。因为我目前的作息时间完全一团糟，再加上我得知大约一周后就要考试，这让我设法给自己找到了通宵的理由。我现在感觉自己快要疯了，就像已经感觉累了，但是又很清醒。我真的不喜欢这种感觉。","english":"We're doing an all-nighter. The reason for this is because my sleeping schedule is currently disastrous, and that in combination with the fact that I know my exams are starting in about a week or so, has somehow made me justify the fact that I can pull an all-nighter tonight. I literally feel like I'm going insane right now. Like, and it feels like I'm tired, but I'm wide awake. I don't really like how this feels.","sentences":["We're doing an all-nighter.","The reason for this is because my sleeping schedule is currently disastrous, and that in combination with the fact that I know my exams are starting in about a week or so, has somehow made me justify the fact that I can pull an all-nighter tonight.","I literally feel like I'm going insane right now.","Like, and it feels like I'm tired, but I'm wide awake.","I don't really like how this feels."],"exercise":"We're 通宵学习. The reason for this is because my 作息时间 is currently 一团糟, and that 再加上 the fact that I know my exams are starting in about a week or so, has somehow made me 找到了…的理由 I can 通宵 tonight. I literally feel like I'm going 疯了 right now. Like, and it feels like I'm tired, but I'm 很清醒. I don't really like how this feels.","vocabulary":[{"id":"6bca054a-089f-43a3-914c-3b3ebad48eba","english":"all-nighter","ipa":"","chinese":"通宵活动（尤指考试前的）通宵学习","usage":"I pulled an all-nighter last night.\n我昨天熬了个通宵学习。"},{"id":"cb4c926c-fb92-40e7-803e-0b5af1b87fb3","english":"sleeping schedule","ipa":"","chinese":"睡眠计划","usage":"Create a sleeping schedule and stick to it.  \n制定一个睡眠计划表，并持之以恒地坚持下去。"},{"id":"3e0d3536-fe47-4bbd-915a-fc7a1f6acda3","english":"disastrous","ipa":"/dɪˈzɑːstrəs/","chinese":"a. 很糟的","usage":"a disastrous report card.\n极糟的成绩报告单"},{"id":"fd576c49-80bc-4c5b-9fba-8aca032c4131","english":"in combination with","ipa":"","chinese":"结合","usage":"The firm is working on a new product in combination with several overseas partners.  \n这家公司与几家海外合伙人在联合开发新产品。"},{"id":"52987347-9c4a-4c1c-a4f1-03449774fd00","english":"justify","ipa":"/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ/","chinese":"v. 证明 … 正确（或正当、有理）","usage":"Her success had justified the faith her teachers had put in her.\n她的成功证明了老师对她的信任是正确的。"},{"id":"a47065aa-e99f-4912-b2ad-198cf6f9149e","english":"pull an all-nighter","ipa":"","chinese":"通宵","usage":"When I was a student in university I would often, when I had a paper due, I would pull an all nighter in order to get it done.\n当我还是一名大学学生时，当我有一篇论文要交时，我经常通宵达旦地完成它。"},{"id":"d6702144-991b-460a-bcc2-bc66dc908f96","english":"insane","ipa":"/ɪnˈseɪn/","chinese":"a. 精神错乱的;精神失常的;疯狂的","usage":"I must have been insane to agree to the idea.\n我肯定是犯傻了，居然同意了这个想法。"},{"id":"058c980f-fa33-43f6-9cde-d7e290eeffdc","english":"wide awake","ipa":"","chinese":"完全清醒的","usage":"Harry sat up, suddenly wide awake.\n哈利坐起身来，一下子完全清醒了。"}]},{"day":80,"title":"英语积累Day 80","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Jillz Guerin","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/941a43f9db474ae5a6a38b0d08cb5304","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CrHjSiJfrgM","audioSize":"318.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-080.m4a","youtubeId":"CrHjSiJfrgM","chinese":"第七个变美秘诀是认真护发。当然，健康饮食对头发的健康至关重要，另外，在使用加热工具如卷发棒或直板夹之前，先使用热保护剂。不要把头发扎成太紧的马尾辫或者太紧的丸子头，因为这样会导致发丝断裂。尽量少漂头发、少染头发，这点非常重要。","english":"The seventh glow-up tip is taking care of your hair. Of course, eating healthy is huge for the health of your hair, but also using heat protectant before you use heat tools like a curling iron or straightener. Not putting your hair in too many really tight ponytails or really tight buns because that can lead to a lot of breakage. Putting as little bleach or dye on your hair as possible, this is a big one.","sentences":["The seventh glow-up tip is taking care of your hair.","Of course, eating healthy is huge for the health of your hair, but also using heat protectant before you use heat tools like a curling iron or straightener.","Not putting your hair in too many really tight ponytails or really tight buns because that can lead to a lot of breakage.","Putting as little bleach or dye on your hair as possible, this is a big one."],"exercise":"The seventh 变美秘诀 is 认真护发. Of course, eating healthy 至关重要 the health of your hair, but also using 热保护剂 before you use heat tools like a 卷发棒 or 直板夹. Not 把头发扎成 too many really tight 马尾辫 or really tight 丸子头 because that can lead to a lot of 断裂. 尽量少漂头发、少染头发, this is a big one.","vocabulary":[{"id":"4cc539bd-6953-4ccd-a5f7-e6dc1e2e22ea","english":"glow up","ipa":"","chinese":"焕发光彩：指一个人在外貌、气质、自信等方面取得显著改善，变得更加美丽、有魅力。","usage":"You get three unique doses of vitamin C. Helps with the brightening of your skin, the glow up of your skin.\n您可以获得三种独特剂量的维生素 C。有助于提亮肤色，让肌肤焕发光彩。"},{"id":"bbcc2b95-b630-4462-b095-e4b060b5dabc","english":"take care of hair","ipa":"","chinese":"打理头发：指对头发进行护理和保养的行为。","usage":""},{"id":"45b0eeec-9373-4830-a14d-e701b1350c52","english":"be huge for","ipa":"","chinese":"对…意义重大","usage":"This single step would be huge for most poor countries, and make very little difference to developed nations.    单单这一步就会对贫穷的国家产生巨大助益，而对发达国家却影响甚微。"},{"id":"741f35f3-db30-4431-9c29-ae1a228920d9","english":"heat protectant","ipa":"","chinese":"在使用吹风机或卷发棒等热工具时，建议使用热保护剂来保护头发免受热损伤。热保护剂可以在头发表面形成一层保护膜，减少热量对头发的损害。","usage":""},{"id":"521ceea2-5670-4922-a337-2f93689ccba2","english":"protectant","ipa":"/prə'tektənt/","chinese":"n. 保护剂；杀虫剂","usage":"UV Protectant 紫外线防护剂；防晒剂"},{"id":"5ac1fe9a-6b54-46f5-a5a0-da156888a7a5","english":"curling iron","ipa":"/'kɜːlɪŋ//ˈaɪən/","chinese":"n. 卷发器，卷发棒","usage":"She burns herself with the curling iron. 她用卷发器烫伤了自己。"},{"id":"81ee9266-5218-4ef0-97cf-5f5847d38c70","english":"straightener","ipa":"/'streitənə/","chinese":"拉直器，直发夹，直板夹","usage":"Can you burn your forehead with a straightener and not complain?  被直板夹烫伤额头你能不吭声吗"},{"id":"4b6d9a62-2ab4-4ef7-813a-7a79ced87d6e","english":"ponytail","ipa":"/'pəʊnɪteɪl/","chinese":"n. 马尾发;马尾辫","usage":""},{"id":"a32ac7b0-a4e9-4aab-9d1e-f04c37264201","english":"bun","ipa":"/bʌn/","chinese":"n. 圆发髻；丸子头","usage":""},{"id":"1b541cdb-af0a-4ed0-8055-49a59811f109","english":"breakage","ipa":"/'breɪkɪdʒ/","chinese":"n. 破损；毁坏","usage":"Brushing wet hair can cause stretching and breakage...\n梳理湿头发会拉抻头发，造成损伤。"},{"id":"eaca0216-f187-48a0-a666-8327ceaacfa3","english":"bleach","ipa":"/bliːtʃ/","chinese":"n. 漂白剂\nv. 漂白；使变白","usage":"Use some bleach on this shirt. 用些漂白剂漂白这件衬衣。"},{"id":"23fde48b-3ab7-493f-a2fc-19e444dff93b","english":"dye","ipa":"/daɪ/","chinese":"n. 染料;染液\nv. 给…染色","usage":"He applied dye to the door. 他给这扇门上色。"},{"id":"9a419d05-009a-4073-a8fb-322175f35d00","english":"as…as possible","ipa":"","chinese":"尽可能地：表示在某种程度或范围内尽量达到最大限度。","usage":"Use cleaning products with harsh chemicals as little as possible.\n尽量少使用含有刺激性化学物质的清洁产品。"}]},{"day":81,"title":"英语积累Day 81","topic":"生活方式","author":"Hannah Adkins","accent":"英音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/0417560e7ac6415dba40c6577c236563","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0l0M4kyMjKA","audioSize":"479.5KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-081.m4a","youtubeId":"0l0M4kyMjKA","chinese":"今早我就随便套了一件卫衣。今天是我这周第一次化全妆，因为说实话，每次来例假的前一周，我都会觉得自信全无。每天早上，我整张脸都水肿得厉害。例假前一周我总是特别水肿，会感觉之前做的普拉提都白费了。不管怎么说，今天我化妆只是为了能找回一点自我。我和妈妈今早要出去逛逛，看看家具。","english":"I've just thrown a hoodie on this morning. I have done my full makeup for the first time this week today. Because honestly, there was just something about the week before your period that just any ounce of self-confidence you might have, gone. My whole face every morning is so puffy. I get such bad water retention in the week before my period, so it feels like everything you've been doing at Pilates is out the window. So anyway, I did my makeup today just to feel a bit more like myself. Mom and I are actually going to pop out and do a little bit of like furniture hunting this morning.","sentences":["I've just thrown a hoodie on this morning.","I have done my full makeup for the first time this week today.","Because honestly, there was just something about the week before your period that just any ounce of self-confidence you might have, gone.","My whole face every morning is so puffy.","I get such bad water retention in the week before my period, so it feels like everything you've been doing at Pilates is out the window.","So anyway, I did my makeup today just to feel a bit more like myself.","Mom and I are actually going to pop out and do a little bit of like furniture hunting this morning."],"exercise":"I've just 随便套了一件卫衣 this morning.  I have 化全妆 for the first time this week today. Because honestly,  there was just something about the week before your 例假 that just 自信全无. My whole face every morning is so 水肿得厉害. I get such bad 水肿 in the week before my period, so it feels like everything you've been doing at Pilates is 白费了. So anyway, I did my makeup today just 找回一点自我. Mom and I are actually going to 出去逛逛 and do a little bit of like 看看家具 this morning.","vocabulary":[{"id":"fe581a62-dc4b-4185-ba80-991d8cf9247d","english":"throw on","ipa":"","chinese":"迅速穿上（一件衣物）；套上","usage":"Let me throw on a jacket before we go. 在我们出门前让我赶快穿件夹克吧"},{"id":"51f22c5c-66ac-4a7d-8f7d-513165984748","english":"full makeup","ipa":"","chinese":"全妆：指化妆品的全部使用，包括底妆、眼妆、唇妆等。","usage":"Michelle dressed for this meeting like an important job interview, in full makeup and blown-out hair.\n米歇尔为这次会议打扮得像一场重要的工作面试，浓妆艳抹，头发蓬松。"},{"id":"741b1960-a527-4fa8-a617-9bf4e97b88c8","english":"period","ipa":"/'pɪərɪəd/","chinese":"n（妇女的）月经，经期","usage":"period pains\n痛经"},{"id":"ee82dc26-4571-42ed-aec4-c4f8314ff947","english":"ounce","ipa":"/aʊns/","chinese":"n. 盎司；少许少量；一点点","usage":"I spent every ounce of energy trying to hide. 我费尽力气想藏起来。"},{"id":"a0317c96-23ac-49da-8b4d-955458e9209c","english":"puffy","ipa":"/'pʌfɪ/","chinese":"a. 尤指脸部肿胀的，浮肿的；","usage":"Her cheeks were puffy with crying. 她哭得面颊浮肿。"},{"id":"0312f966-3811-42cf-b24f-76ae5f87b718","english":"water retention","ipa":"","chinese":"水肿：身体组织中过多的液体积聚，导致局部肿胀和不适。","usage":""},{"id":"6ec352af-8450-46c8-b603-3c55a22b0ebc","english":"retention","ipa":"/rɪˈtenʃn/","chinese":"n. 1. 保持;保留\n2. 记忆力，记性","usage":"1. the soil's retention of moisture.土壤对水分的吸收和保持\n2. Information learned right before bed has greater rates of retention.\n睡前学到的信息记得更牢。"},{"id":"551971c0-d219-4be8-b761-c97b5728838b","english":"out the window","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 变得过时，因情况变化而发生了巨大变化：指计划、想法等因情况的变化而变得无效或不再适用。\n2. 消失了，离开了，不见了：指物体或事物突然不见了或离开了某个位置","usage":"all my efforts went out the window. 我真是白费工夫。"},{"id":"242a4a48-79d0-4b9e-abe5-2aaa891057cc","english":"pop out","ipa":"","chinese":"匆匆出去","usage":"Would you pop out and get some? 你能不能出去买点？"},{"id":"c71c331e-b4e9-4853-b653-efa08b4405c3","english":"hunting","ipa":"/ˈhʌntɪŋ/","chinese":"构成复合词：找；寻找","usage":"We're going house-hunting at the weekend. 周末我们去找房子。"}]},{"day":82,"title":"英语积累Day 82","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Birta Hlin","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/94276f284eaf47b09ece1033261f7b66","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cJhEDmxg6qk","audioSize":"342.7KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-082.m4a","youtubeId":"cJhEDmxg6qk","chinese":"我们有点想吃意大利面，但不知道该去哪吃。而且我不确定能不能在餐厅找到位置。毕竟今天是周六晚上。不知道我们会不会搞砸，也许吧。但我希望能有接受未预定散客的餐厅。好了各位，我们准备好了。Mattha（注：博主的朋友）看起来超赞，穿了这条粉裤子和这双时髦的厚底鞋。","english":"We are kind of in the mood for some pasta, but we don't have a clue where to go. And I'm not sure if we're even going to get a table anywhere. And it's Saturday night. I don't know if we're screwed. Maybe. But I hope that there will be some restaurants that have like walk-ins. Okay, guys, we're ready. So Mattha is looking slay in these pink pants and these very chunky and funky shoes.","sentences":["We are kind of in the mood for some pasta, but we don't have a clue where to go.","And I'm not sure if we're even going to get a table anywhere.","And it's Saturday night.","I don't know if we're screwed.","Maybe.","But I hope that there will be some restaurants that have like walk-ins.","Okay, guys, we're ready.","So Mattha is looking slay in these pink pants and these very chunky and funky shoes."],"exercise":"We are 有点想吃 some pasta, but we 不知道 where to go. And I'm not sure if we're even going to 找到位置 anywhere. And it's Saturday night. I don't know 会不会搞砸. Maybe. But I hope that there will be some restaurants that 接受未预定散客. Okay, guys, we're ready. So Mattha is 看起来超赞 in these pink pants and these very 时髦的厚底鞋","vocabulary":[{"id":"c9871070-4735-4eab-b8cf-2c206244d232","english":"in the mood for","ipa":"","chinese":"想要做某事或拥有某物的心情","usage":"1. I'm just not in the mood for a party tonight. 我今晚就是没心情参加聚会。\n2. After a day of air and activity, you should be in the mood for a good meal. 在户外活动了一天，你应该想好好吃一顿。"},{"id":"90d72ecd-ac27-4b3f-a0f4-38d8afc0d74b","english":"clue","ipa":"/kluː/","chinese":"n. 线索;提示","usage":"Geneticists in Canada have discovered a clue to the puzzle of why our cells get old and die.\n加拿大的遗传学家已经发现了解开细胞衰老、死亡之谜的线索。"},{"id":"7d8a40a3-0b93-4eb1-8ac0-908ed9abe922","english":"don't have a clue","ipa":"","chinese":"一无所知：表示对某事或某物完全不了解或不知道。","usage":"I don't have a clue where she lives.  我完全不知道她住在哪里。"},{"id":"40d0d3b8-efcb-415d-9d33-8199f79a7141","english":"screwed (up)","ipa":"/skruːd/","chinese":"a. 搞砸，完蛋","usage":"1. She thinks she screwed up the exam. 她认为考试考砸了。\n2. Pretending like our lives aren't screwed? 假装我们的生活并没有一团糟？"},{"id":"8710fa86-7d83-4d12-8d07-56f208be8738","english":"walk-in","ipa":"","chinese":"1. adj. 无须事先约定的\n2. n. 未经预约的人\n3. “大的能走进去的...” walk-in closet 步入式衣柜","usage":"1. They told him they didn't take walk-ins and shooed him away. 他们说他们不接待没有预约过的人，然后把他赶走了。\n2. We accept both appointments and walk-ins at our salon.\n预约客户和非预约客户我们都接受。"},{"id":"361fd923-e5f2-4d16-ab39-6bd993e4ce1a","english":"slay","ipa":"/sleɪ/","chinese":"本义指以暴力“杀死；残杀”，引申为“做事或表演格外出色，令人印象深刻“；人或事物看起来“很酷”“很精彩”“很有气场”或者“让人赞不绝口”","usage":"The actors slay me with the quality of their acting. 演员们用演技征服了我。"},{"id":"3dd9bb9f-7672-4b96-9e80-2559dfc93bec","english":"chunky","ipa":"/'tʃʌŋkɪ/","chinese":"a. 1. 人粗壮的，背阔胸宽的\n2. 粗重的;大而重的","usage":"chunky heels 粗跟"},{"id":"50412f94-c751-472e-9b8e-457d7f0294df","english":"funky","ipa":"/ˈfʌŋki/","chinese":"a. 1. 时髦的\n2.  (音乐)乡土爵士乐风格的，放克风格的","usage":"she likes wearing funky clothes.她喜欢穿新奇时髦的服装。"}]},{"day":83,"title":"英语积累Day 83","topic":"食物","author":"Eva Meloche","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/e8b7b77938924adb8e0570e555bb0f44","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/TUNAarlvuCM?si=fMRo7iqh9yGguehR","audioSize":"541.9KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-083.m4a","youtubeId":"TUNAarlvuCM","chinese":"我们先吃了布拉塔奶酪开胃，上面淋了橄榄油，然后都点了披萨作为主菜，非常棒。饼皮很有嚼劲，特别好吃。我真的吃撑到走不动路了，所以找人把我背一段路回家。要不然只能找个人把我“滚”回家了。他们家的肉桂面包卷简直是绝世美味。亨利尝了这款巧克力面包，简直太好吃太过瘾了。晚饭我们去了一家意大利餐厅，有点踩雷。氛围确实很好，但主菜不太好吃。不过饮料超大一杯，甜点也很美味。","english":"We shared burrata to start, which was drizzled with olive oil, and both got pizzas as mains, which were fantastic. The crust was so chewy; it was delectable. I was actually filled to the brim, so I got a certain someone to carry me part of the way home. It was either that or someone was rolling me all the way home. Their cinnamon buns are out of this world. Henry tried this chocolate pastry that was so gorgeous and so decadent. For dinner, we went to this Italian restaurant, which was a bit of a faux pas. The vibe was really lovely, but our main courses weren't great. Drinks, however, were mega-sized, and the dessert was succulent.","sentences":["We shared burrata to start, which was drizzled with olive oil, and both got pizzas as mains, which were fantastic.","The crust was so chewy; it was delectable.","I was actually filled to the brim, so I got a certain someone to carry me part of the way home.","It was either that or someone was rolling me all the way home.","Their cinnamon buns are out of this world.","Henry tried this chocolate pastry that was so gorgeous and so decadent.","For dinner, we went to this Italian restaurant, which was a bit of a faux pas.","The vibe was really lovely, but our main courses weren't great.","Drinks, however, were mega-sized, and the dessert was succulent."],"exercise":"We shared burrata to 开胃, which was 淋了 olive oil, and both got pizzas as 主菜, which were fantastic. The crust was so 嚼劲; it was 特别好吃. I was actually 真的吃撑到走不动路, so I got a certain someone to carry me part of the way home. It was either that or someone was 把我“滚”回家了. Their cinnamon buns are 绝世美味. Henry tried this chocolate pastry that was so 太好吃 and so 过瘾. For dinner, we went to this Italian restaurant, which was a bit of a 踩雷. The 氛围 was really lovely, but our 主菜 weren't great. Drinks, however, were 超大一杯, and the dessert was 很美味.","vocabulary":[{"id":"4ae28238-45c7-4e99-98b4-cedd757c2f24","english":"drizzle with","ipa":"/'drɪz(ə)l/","chinese":"轻轻地滴下：将液体或调味料以细小的滴落方式均匀地撒在食物上。","usage":"1. Drizzle With Butter: 淋上黄油\n2. Drizzle With Olive Oil: 淋上橄榄油"},{"id":"45b6ccc8-e5c6-4691-aec8-2f72373c70c8","english":"mains","ipa":"/meɪnz/","chinese":"n. 主菜","usage":""},{"id":"e3af1718-db31-43ec-9a9b-b9fe572532d6","english":"main course","ipa":"","chinese":"主菜","usage":"The normal practice in America is to eat the salad before the main course.\n在美国的正常生活中，吃沙拉是在主菜之前的。"},{"id":"20efd7ae-c204-432d-9a74-56344c023f1a","english":"chewy","ipa":"/'tʃuːɪ/","chinese":"a. 耐嚼的","usage":"All that gluten makes a nice, chewy bread.\n所有的这些麸质会让面包可口而劲道。"},{"id":"2faebba5-ecf1-461e-9783-39fd9a4ff549","english":"delectable","ipa":"/dɪ'lektəb(ə)l/","chinese":"a. 美味可口的","usage":"the delectable smell of freshly baked bread\n新烤面包的香味"},{"id":"1f94dcda-0534-41dd-aedd-4b9e6265d12e","english":"be filled to the brim","ipa":"","chinese":"充满；填满；装满","usage":"These two wine glasses are filled to the brim. 两只斟满的酒杯"},{"id":"cd73f747-ac76-419c-a4c5-afbf638971cb","english":"out of this world","ipa":"","chinese":"好（或美等）得不得了；非凡一流","usage":"The meal was out of this world.\n这顿饭简直好吃的不得了。"},{"id":"59bde25c-1a80-4519-a487-abfbb2cf60a1","english":"gorgeous","ipa":"/ˈɡɔːdʒəs/","chinese":"a. 极好的, 称心的","usage":"What a gorgeous day it is today!\n今天天气多好啊！"},{"id":"9cdfa255-a288-4be5-851f-ae0d402b1cee","english":"decadent","ipa":"/ˈdekədənt/","chinese":"a. 1. 堕落的，颓废的，贪图享乐的；\n2. 极其令人满意的，十分享受的\n3. 形容食物时，通常用来表达蛋糕甜点味道浓郁、口感厚重。也带有一层夸大表述意思，表示“sinfully good”，即好吃过瘾但又有种罪恶感","usage":""},{"id":"7f48f43a-c7e6-4c9a-be6e-f28303114e4a","english":"faux pas","ipa":"法语 /ˏfəu ˈpɑː/","chinese":"失策；失礼、失态或失言\nfaux 是错误的，false 的意思，而 pas 则是脚步、step 的意思。faux pas 组合起来，就是走错的步伐","usage":""},{"id":"25bd3052-19be-428f-8504-e3a71ed38fc2","english":"vibe","ipa":"/vaib/","chinese":"n. 氛围","usage":"The vibe in the restaurant is pretty laid back, not like ritzier restaurants in Beverly Hills.  \n这家餐厅的氛围很悠闲，不像比弗利山的豪华餐厅。"},{"id":"fe64583a-8b88-48ca-afd3-a72b169f27e6","english":"mega-sized","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 超大型的，巨大的","usage":""},{"id":"4564f223-0f02-44ce-bf12-088219ff3363","english":"succulent","ipa":"/'sʌkjʊl(ə)nt/","chinese":"a.  汁多味美的","usage":"a succulent pear/steak\n汁多味美的梨；鲜美多汁的牛排"}]},{"day":84,"title":"英语积累Day 84","topic":"生活方式","author":"Nil Sani","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/0bb33b63580a48eba8f1664f418f8d70","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ognVDRykuRE","audioSize":"499.5KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-084.m4a","youtubeId":"ognVDRykuRE","chinese":"我打算先列出今天的整体待办清单，然后做些家务。接着，为了真正进入状态，我打算和朋友一起去图书馆学习。我觉得让自己身处工作或学习环境中，还有和朋友一起，会让事情变得更容易些。而且我们目前面临同样的处境。现在我的大脑不再被各个待办事项分散，它们已经被清晰地列出来了。这就是我最高效的工作方式，事情不再在脑海里漂来荡去，而是写在纸上，我可以划掉已完成的事项。","english":"I'm going to make, like, my overall to-do list for today and then do some chores around the house. And then, to really get myself in the zone, I'm gonna go to the library and study there with a friend. I feel like putting myself in a work or school environment, also going with a friend just makes it a little easier. And just, we're both in the same boat. Now that my brain isn't scattered with everything that I have to do and it's like exactly listed out. That's like how I get the most productive when it's not floating in my brain but it's like written on paper and I can, like, cross things off.","sentences":["I'm going to make, like, my overall to-do list for today and then do some chores around the house.","And then, to really get myself in the zone, I'm gonna go to the library and study there with a friend.","I feel like putting myself in a work or school environment, also going with a friend just makes it a little easier.","And just, we're both in the same boat.","Now that my brain isn't scattered with everything that I have to do and it's like exactly listed out.","That's like how I get the most productive when it's not floating in my brain but it's like written on paper and I can, like, cross things off."],"exercise":"I'm going to make, like, my 整体待办清单 for today and then do some chores around the house. And then, to really 进入状态, I'm going to go to the library and study there with a friend. I feel like 让自己身处工作或学习环境中, also going with a friend just makes it a little easier. And just, we're both 面临同样的处境. Now that my brain isn't scattered with everything that I have to do and it's like exactly listed out. That's like how I get the most productive when it's not floating in my brain but it's like written on paper and I can, like, cross things off.","vocabulary":[{"id":"024be6ed-67b4-46cb-af75-2f5c654d8600","english":"overall","ipa":"/ˌəʊvərˈɔːl/","chinese":"a. 总的；总体的；全面的","usage":"Restrictions could actually mean a healthier lobster population overall. 限制捕捞实际上意味着龙虾整个群体会更健康。"},{"id":"812fdaeb-d03b-4327-a9c5-e0cb99c87a68","english":"to-do list","ipa":"","chinese":"待办事项清单","usage":"I have a million things on my \" to do\" list. 我的任务清单上有很多事情要做。"},{"id":"68b8d90c-3856-4f66-8772-52340db6b55a","english":"get in the zone","ipa":"","chinese":"进入状态","usage":"Before you read something you really want to focus on, get in the zone. 在阅读你真正想要关注的内容之前，先进入状态。"},{"id":"eb242559-c1aa-49c3-99f2-749cc6144022","english":"in the same boat","ipa":"","chinese":"处境相同, 面临同样的危险","usage":"This is a horrible economy. We're all in the same boat. 在这种糟糕的经济环境下，大家的处境都是一样的。"},{"id":"fdf7eec6-291e-4dd7-b4f0-64ad447666fa","english":"be scattered with","ipa":"/ˈskætə(r)/","chinese":"散布着，充满","usage":"The ground is scattered withpine needles and hay.  地上铺满了松针和干草。"},{"id":"f14d5d45-d9b4-410b-a7ba-511212e1630b","english":"list out","ipa":"","chinese":"列举出，罗列出：指将事物一一列举出来或按顺序排列出来。","usage":"I would list out the steps and put a quantifiable measurement to as many things as I can. 我会列出这些步骤，并尽可能多地对这些事情进行量化衡量。"},{"id":"96fde858-e4e0-4e0b-ad5a-dce943854594","english":"float","ipa":"/fləʊt/","chinese":"v. 1. 漂;浮\n2. 提出(计划、方案或想法)","usage":"The French had floated the idea of placing the diplomatic work in the hands of the UN.\n法国提出将外交工作交由联合国处理的想法。"},{"id":"8e91a41d-42cb-4179-a254-bb956caa05da","english":"cross off","ipa":"","chinese":"(从名单上)画掉，删掉","usage":"So, cross off each task you complete. 划掉完成的每一项任务。"}]},{"day":85,"title":"英语积累Day 85","topic":"生活方式,食物","author":"Ashley Hetherington","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/0add745614944971962fb4ca181eba0d","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iiGQMTqSt6c","audioSize":"386.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-085.m4a","youtubeId":"iiGQMTqSt6c","chinese":"一天的成功要从前一天晚上开始。所以在晚上，我喜欢回顾当天的经历，并思考：“有没有哪些未完成的任务可以延续到明天呢？”我喜欢在晚上泡一杯茶，让身心得以放松，再吃一些黑巧克力。今晚，我打算只吃妈妈给的饼干，但我晚上通常都会选择一些相对比较健康又美味的甜点来满足自己想吃甜食的欲望。","english":"The success of the day starts the night before. So at night, I like to look at the day and think, \"What did I not get done that I can bring over to tomorrow?\" I love making tea at night to wind down and munch on some dark chocolate. Tonight, I am totally eating this cookie my mom got for me, but I usually have healthy-ish tasteful desserts at night to savor my sweet tooth.","sentences":["The success of the day starts the night before.","So at night, I like to look at the day and think, \"What did I not get done that I can bring over to tomorrow?\"","I love making tea at night to wind down and munch on some dark chocolate.","Tonight, I am totally eating this cookie my mom got for me, but I usually have healthy-ish tasteful desserts at night to savor my sweet tooth."],"exercise":"The success of the day starts the night before. So at night, I like to 回顾当天的经历 and think, \"What did I not get done that I can 延续 to tomorrow?\" I love making tea at night to 让身心得以放松 and 吃 some dark chocolate. Tonight, I am totally eating this cookie my mom got for me, but I usually have 相对比较健康 tasteful desserts at night to 满足自己想吃甜食的欲望.","vocabulary":[{"id":"28b01997-f664-46d8-aaa6-57fc8987c26c","english":"bring over","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 把…带到…\n2. 使转向，使改变立场：指说服某人改变观点或立场，使其支持某种观点或立场","usage":"I'll bring the dog over by nine. 我在九点之前把狗送来。"},{"id":"961176ec-8a30-431c-b745-4d3baa7e7a12","english":"wind down","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 放松;松弛\n2. 摇下(车窗等)\n3. 逐渐减小(工作规模);使逐步停止;使逐渐关闭","usage":"1. I regularly have a drink to wind down. 我经常喝点酒放松一下。\n2. If a stranger stops you, just wind the window down a fraction.\n如果有陌生人拦你的车，把车窗摇下一点点就行。\n3. Things should be winding down around now. 这事应该接近尾声了。"},{"id":"98c050d2-d0f4-4fe3-8214-3123d25e20d4","english":"munch","ipa":"/mʌntʃ/","chinese":"用力嚼;出声地嚼","usage":"Luke munched the chicken sandwiches...\n卢克津津有味地吃着鸡肉三明治。"},{"id":"0473c448-f8a8-481f-81cb-60fb93acc46d","english":"munch on","ipa":"","chinese":"咀嚼，通常是指吃零食或小吃。","usage":"I like to get a big back of small apples and just munch on them whenever I'm hungry.  我经常准备一些小苹果，觉得饿了就大嚼特嚼。"},{"id":"1e19591b-005e-44a9-9610-63cb700a65d6","english":"healthy-ish","ipa":"","chinese":"在非正式口语中，可以把“-ish”放在一些形容词的后面，意思是 “有点…”，“…左右”。“-ish” 也可以用在表示时间、年龄等的数字后面，意思是 “大约，左右”","usage":""},{"id":"fd5461ca-60c9-4334-a157-33844e1eedd8","english":"savor","ipa":"/'seivə/","chinese":"vt. 1. 尽情享受；品尝，欣赏\n2. 使有风味；加调味品于；","usage":"You need to savor this wine to get its full flavor. 要想充分体验这种酒的醇美，你需要慢慢地去品尝。"},{"id":"2ffbde93-eec2-471a-9f42-53a112a63db6","english":"sweet tooth","ipa":"","chinese":"n. 喜好甜食，对甜食的酷爱","usage":"I definitely have a sweet tooth. A bad sweet tooth. 我确实爱吃甜食。超级甜食爱好者。"}]},{"day":86,"title":"英语积累Day 86","topic":"数码产品","author":"Taylor Bell","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/db2e1752b3eb4314b27e4a0c18457c6f","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/Cqg8tQH4U8M?si=JincAUBVdpAcZgx8","audioSize":"480.9KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-086.m4a","youtubeId":"Cqg8tQH4U8M","chinese":"我正要去这里的数码专卖店买个大件。成年后，我很难改变节俭的心态，但我正努力让自己更舍得在真正重要的事情上花钱。这是一台笔记本电脑。几个月前，在我尝试剪视频的时候，电脑突然死机了，我这才意识到，设备不应该成为阻碍。对我来说，不买一台能力范围内最好的设备来工作实在太不明智了。我不想因为这件事而大惊小怪，但买新电脑真的令人兴奋。","english":"I'm about to go make a big purchase inside there at a tech store. It's been kind of hard for me in my adulthood to break free of my frugal mentality, but I really am trying to become more comfortable with spending money on the things that really matter. This is a laptop. And I just realized while my computer was crashing a couple of months ago while I was trying to edit a video, technology should not be bottleneck. It's just silly for me to not have the best possible machine for me to do my job. Anyway, not to make a huge deal out of this, but this is exciting.","sentences":["I'm about to go make a big purchase inside there at a tech store.","It's been kind of hard for me in my adulthood to break free of my frugal mentality, but I really am trying to become more comfortable with spending money on the things that really matter.","This is a laptop.","And I just realized while my computer was crashing a couple of months ago while I was trying to edit a video, technology should not be bottleneck.","It's just silly for me to not have the best possible machine for me to do my job.","Anyway, not to make a huge deal out of this, but this is exciting."],"exercise":"I'm about to go 买个大件 inside there at a tech store. It's been kind of hard for me in my adulthood to 改变 of my 节俭的心态, but I really am trying to become more comfortable with spending money on the things that really matter. This is a laptop. And I just realized while my 电脑突然死机 a couple of months ago while I was trying to edit a video, technology should not be 阻碍. It's just silly for me to not have 能力范围内最好的设备 for me to do my job. Anyway, not to 大惊小怪, but this is exciting.","vocabulary":[{"id":"09c85fa2-997c-4c48-9bd8-526a877b2f8e","english":"make a big purchase","ipa":"","chinese":"进行大额购买：指购买价格较高的商品或服务，需要花费较多的金钱。","usage":"If you are going to make a big purchase. I will cut the price down.  \n如果你将大量购买的话，我想我可以把价格降低一点。"},{"id":"f2ce0678-2b81-4000-8a3a-e53ae32726ec","english":"break free","ipa":"","chinese":"打破（常规）；挣脱束缚","usage":"I have to try to break free from the thoughts in my mind.  我必须试着摆脱心中的那些想法。"},{"id":"efb2b013-93cf-4f64-bcb3-46dcb75ef18b","english":"frugal","ipa":"/ˈfruːɡl/","chinese":"a. （对金钱、食物等）节约的，节俭的","usage":"a frugal existence/life\n俭朴的生活"},{"id":"56a18496-057e-4405-a1a3-7340f07f889e","english":"mentality","ipa":"/men'tælɪtɪ/","chinese":"n. 心态；","usage":"You have to have the correct mentality to be in this industry.\n你必须要有正确的心态进入这个行业。"},{"id":"d063bbfd-abdb-429a-8ffc-7cba05064ac9","english":"crash","ipa":"/kræʃ/","chinese":"n. 机器或系统，尤指计算机或计算机系统的）崩溃","usage":""},{"id":"2c821b89-f5b6-4e07-b2eb-3ad708f86fd3","english":"bottleneck","ipa":"/'bɒt(ə)lnek/","chinese":"n. （尤指工商业发展的）瓶颈，阻碍，障碍","usage":"hit/encounter/run into a bottle neck 遇到瓶颈"},{"id":"85c3f890-aabe-4548-a1b2-8ab27c99e519","english":"make a huge deal","ipa":"","chinese":"大惊小怪；小题大做","usage":"I didn't have time to tell you, and anyway, I didn't want to make a big thing out of it.\n我当时没有时间对你讲，再说了，我也不想把这事闹大"},{"id":"9a55a3dd-c178-423d-b0a5-f3beeccbf84a","english":"out of …","ipa":"","chinese":"因为……而做某事：表示某人做某事的原因。","usage":"I asked out of curiosity.    \n我出于好奇问了问。"}]},{"day":87,"title":"英语积累Day 87","topic":"生活方式","author":"Taylor Bell","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/95684aa4b5c44c03a6e0c9f41867bf71","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/Cqg8tQH4U8M?si=JincAUBVdpAcZgx8","audioSize":"328.9KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-087.m4a","youtubeId":"Cqg8tQH4U8M","chinese":"这是我为什么喜欢纽约的典型例子。天一放晴，你就会偶遇朋友。“嘿，大家好。“这是哈里。我知道我老是这么说，但正是这种人际互动让人觉得纽约就像是成年人的游乐场。对于这样一个大城市来说，却也有种小而紧密的感觉。我和哈里意外在这里溜达了快一个小时。我们现在已经认识快八年了，他人真的很不错。","english":"Okay, prime example of why I love New York. When the sun comes out, you just run into friends. “What's up, guys?” This is Harry. I know I say this all the time, but it's interactions like this that make New York City feel like a playground for adults. For such a huge city, it is incredibly small and compact at the same time. Anyway, Harry and I hung out here unexpectedly for almost an hour. We've been friends for like almost 8 years at this point. He's a very good egg.","sentences":["Okay, prime example of why I love New York.","When the sun comes out, you just run into friends.","“What's up, guys?”","This is Harry.","I know I say this all the time, but it's interactions like this that make New York City feel like a playground for adults.","For such a huge city, it is incredibly small and compact at the same time.","Anyway, Harry and I hung out here unexpectedly for almost an hour.","We've been friends for like almost 8 years at this point.","He's a very good egg."],"exercise":"Okay, 典型例子 of why I love New York. 天一放晴, you just 偶遇 friends. “What's up, guys?” This is Harry. I know I say this all the time, but it's 人际互动 like this that make New York City feel like 成年人的游乐场. For such a huge city, it is incredibly small and 紧密 at the same time. Anyway, Harry and I 溜达了 here unexpectedly for almost an hour. We've been friends for like almost 8 years 现在. 他人真的很不错.","vocabulary":[{"id":"805e0d08-f7de-4540-8d0d-6bdc062c5f60","english":"prime","ipa":"/praɪm/","chinese":"a. 1. 最典型的；最有代表性的\n2. 主要的；首要的；最为重要的","usage":"The prime example is Macy's, once the undisputed king of California retailers.\n最典型的例子是梅西百货，它曾经是加利福尼亚无可争辩的零售巨头。"},{"id":"ad64ad78-9c84-40be-bd4c-278211a5dcf0","english":"run into","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 撞上，碰上：意指偶然遇到或不期而遇。 \n2. 遇到困难，遭遇：指遇到问题、困境或挑战。","usage":"1. What are the odds of running into you here? 好巧，在这儿遇到你\n2. The pilot told the control tower that he'd run into technical trouble.  该飞行员告诉航空站说他遇到了技术问题。"},{"id":"055c4efb-56a4-425b-8e6c-17dfd16c8e07","english":"interaction","ipa":"/ˌɪntərˈækʃn/","chinese":"n. 互动，交流；相互影响，相互作用","usage":"1. Or had a personal interaction with a student? 或者和学生单独交流？\n2. Price is determined through the interaction of demand and supply.  价格是由供求关系的相互作用决定的。"},{"id":"8556b138-b565-441c-84eb-28518622ee02","english":"compact","ipa":"形容词和动词读作 /kəm'pækt/，名词读作 /'kɒmpækt/","chinese":"a. 1. 小而紧凑的\n2. 矮小结实的;矮壮的\nv. 把…压实(或压紧)\nn.  (内有镜子的)化妆粉盒","usage":"Boston is a compact and highly livable city. 波士顿不大，却是极为适合居住的城市。"},{"id":"e7388446-6a6c-40a7-af25-ea6c8fb0d2e8","english":"hang out","ipa":"/hæŋ/","chinese":"闲逛，逗留\n这里的hung是hang的过去式和过去分词","usage":"1. Hang out with friends.  和朋友出去玩。\n2. We can just hang out and have a good time.\n我们可以只是闲逛一下，开开心。"},{"id":"5a4160d0-791d-4906-8dd1-2e667495318c","english":"at this point","ipa":"","chinese":"这时候，此时此刻","usage":"At this point I don't care what you decide to do.  到这个时候，我不在乎你决定要怎么做了。"},{"id":"98193005-97b4-4b53-a300-23a86ac58537","english":"a good egg","ipa":"","chinese":"好人，可靠的人：用于形容一个人非常友善、可信赖、值得信赖。","usage":"Thanks for buying me lunch, you really are a good egg! 谢谢你请我吃午餐，你真是一个好人！"}]},{"day":88,"title":"英语积累Day 88","topic":"旅行","author":"Allison Anderson","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/cafd9490bd2d4bff8645f490baae964b","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Isd7vM8vVl0","audioSize":"475.9KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-088.m4a","youtubeId":"Isd7vM8vVl0","chinese":"另一个让我能充分享受旅行的办法是，把酒店订在想花时间逛的地方。这似乎是理所当然的做法，但在过去几年里，为了省钱，我一直倾向于在市区比较偏远的地方订酒店。如果我计划一大早抵达某个地方，比如去看日出，我必须考虑好一大早是否有公共交通在运营时间？或者是否能在一大早打到出租车？而且我发现自己开始压缩一天中旅行的时间，提前回到酒店。因为我担心出租车会变少，可能就搭不到车了。","english":"Another way I make the most out of my trips is I book hotels in the areas that I want to explore and spend time in. This may seem like a no-brainer, but for years I would book hotels in further out areas of the city to stretch my budget further. If I wanted to be somewhere really early, like for sunrise, I had to think about: is transit even running that early? Or can I get a cab that early? And I found that I started cutting my days shorter. Like I started going back to the hotel earlier. Because I didn't want to wait until cabs thinned out and I couldn't snag one.","sentences":["Another way I make the most out of my trips is I book hotels in the areas that I want to explore and spend time in.","This may seem like a no-brainer, but for years I would book hotels in further out areas of the city to stretch my budget further.","If I wanted to be somewhere really early, like for sunrise, I had to think about: is transit even running that early?","Or can I get a cab that early?","And I found that I started cutting my days shorter.","Like I started going back to the hotel earlier.","Because I didn't want to wait until cabs thinned out and I couldn't snag one."],"exercise":"Another way I 充分享受 my trips is I book hotels in the areas that I want to explore and spend time in. This may seem like a 理所当然的做法, but for years I would book hotels in 比较偏远的地方 the city to 省钱 further. If I wanted to be somewhere really early, like for sunrise, I had to think about: is 公共交通 even running that early? Or can I 打到出租车 that early? And I found that I started 压缩一天中旅行的时间. Like I started going back to the hotel earlier. Because I didn't want to wait until cabs 变少 and I couldn't 搭 one.","vocabulary":[{"id":"a727aad3-2c97-484f-947a-12a652074dfc","english":"make the most out of","ipa":"","chinese":"充分利用","usage":"A good investor can always make the most out of any amount of time.\n好的投资者总是能够充分利用任何时间。"},{"id":"e07dff12-2a6e-4e95-988e-4b22caac5399","english":"no-brainer","ipa":"","chinese":"n. 无需用脑的事；容易的决定","usage":"So Dr. Udell says getting the vaccine is a no brainer.\n所以尤戴尔博士表示接种疫苗一举理所当然。"},{"id":"4cb03f73-f24c-432f-a882-7746e07187c4","english":"further out areas of","ipa":"","chinese":"更远的地区","usage":""},{"id":"9bbd4724-c9b7-4832-a07c-bea981ef9f6e","english":"further","ipa":"/ˈfɜːðə(r)/","chinese":"1. adv. （空间距离）较远，更远\n2. 进一步；在更大程度上；","usage":"1. We had walked further than I had realized.\n在我不知不觉中我们已走得很远。\n2. The police decided to investigate further.\n警方决定作进一步调查。"},{"id":"6c934df6-a633-4d4c-a027-4967af587abe","english":"stretch budget","ipa":"","chinese":"紧缩预算，节省开支","usage":"To stretch her budget, she began putting in vegetables and fruit—everything from strawberry beds to apple trees—and as her first seedlings grew, her spirits lifted.  \n为了节省开支，她开始种植蔬菜和水果——从草莓苗圃到苹果树——当她的第一批幼苗长大时，她的精神振奋起来。"},{"id":"fee1c064-fd59-4ce1-92c3-44ed41156f16","english":"transit","ipa":"/ˈtrænzɪt/","chinese":"n. 交通运输系统","usage":"the city's mass/public transit system\n城市的公共交通运输系统"},{"id":"1e8582b3-364f-4554-ae4b-3aa0a4040fdd","english":"get a cab","ipa":"","chinese":"打车","usage":"I couldn't get a cab, I had to take a train.\n我拦不到出租车，只能乘地铁。"},{"id":"4fbbaa5a-847e-45b5-a7ff-c8cba6458b7f","english":"thin out","ipa":"","chinese":"使稀疏；变少","usage":"NATO will continue to thin out its forces.  \n北约将继续裁军。"},{"id":"6e194610-91cc-4437-af6c-00adec63cf00","english":"snag","ipa":"/snæg/","chinese":"v. 抓住；抢先获得","usage":"I snagged a ride from Joe.\n我截住乔的车搭了一段路。"}]},{"day":89,"title":"英语积累Day 89","topic":"旅行,食物","author":"Allison Anderson","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/c2b81680b6bd45d48b9113b1911d6f8d","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Isd7vM8vVl0","audioSize":"568.8KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-089.m4a","youtubeId":"Isd7vM8vVl0","chinese":"旅行前，我总是先做好餐厅攻略，并提前预订位置。因为最糟的事情莫过于，一天在市区走了两万步，走到差不多该吃晚饭了，才发现没有一家餐厅有空位。在游览一天后，饿得想发飙、匆匆忙忙找地方吃饭可不是什么愉快的事。所以，提前订好餐厅能轻松许多。当然，我并不是说找一家不需要预订的小餐馆就不会有好的体验。但这全凭运气。所以，我现在每次旅行都会至少预订一家餐厅，这样就能确保自己有次愉快的用餐体验。","english":"The next thing I always do before a trip is scope out restaurants and make reservations in advance, because there is nothing worse than walking 20,000 steps around a city all day, finishing around dinner time and realizing no restaurants anywhere have tables available. It is no fun to be hangry and scrambling to find somewhere to eat after a long day of sightseeing. So making a reservation keeps things a lot more relaxed. Not that finding a little hole in the wall spot that doesn't take reservations can't be a great experience as well. But it is kind of hit-and-miss. So now I try to make at least one reservation for a trip so I know I'm guaranteed a good dining experience.","sentences":["The next thing I always do before a trip is scope out restaurants and make reservations in advance, because there is nothing worse than walking 20,000 steps around a city all day, finishing around dinner time and realizing no restaurants anywhere have tables available.","It is no fun to be hangry and scrambling to find somewhere to eat after a long day of sightseeing.","So making a reservation keeps things a lot more relaxed.","Not that finding a little hole in the wall spot that doesn't take reservations can't be a great experience as well.","But it is kind of hit-and-miss.","So now I try to make at least one reservation for a trip so I know I'm guaranteed a good dining experience."],"exercise":"The next thing I always do before a trip is 做好餐厅攻略 and 预订位置 in advance. Because there is 最糟的事情莫过于 walking 20,000 steps around a city all day, finishing around dinner time and realizing no restaurants anywhere 有空位. It is no fun to be 饿得想发飙 and 匆匆忙忙 find somewhere to eat after a long day of 游览. So making a reservation keeps things a lot more relaxed. Not that finding 小餐馆 spot that doesn't take reservations can't be a great experience as well. But it is kind of 全凭运气. So now I try to make at least one reservation for a trip so I know I'm 确保 a good dining experience.","vocabulary":[{"id":"616fc761-41bb-45bc-91b3-36682fd186b5","english":"scope out","ipa":"","chinese":"仔细观察（看某事物／某人是否有趣或具吸引力）","usage":"We scoped out the local area to see if it would be a good place to rent a flat.\n我们仔细观察了一下附近地区，看是否适于在那里租房住。"},{"id":"7335e50b-ca22-4446-bb0e-5d1087c5b8ab","english":"make reservations","ipa":"","chinese":"预定","usage":"make reservations for hotel rooms: 预订旅馆"},{"id":"f78fa389-4b6f-448d-8b0c-c7a8bda77f86","english":"nothing worse than","ipa":"","chinese":"没有比……更糟糕的了：用于强调某种情况或事物是最糟糕的。","usage":"There is nothing worse than having no friends.  \n没有什么事比没朋友更可怕的了。"},{"id":"3cf4ea6e-40d7-451f-af23-8d990242e86e","english":"available","ipa":"/əˈveɪləbl/","chinese":"a. 能找到的；可获得的","usage":"There are three small boats available for hire.\n有3艘小船可供出租。"},{"id":"e96c3cf0-42c4-4910-9f03-d65d61a89af4","english":"hangry","ipa":"","chinese":"饿怒：因感到饥饿而变得愤怒。由hungry（饥饿）和 angry（愤怒）组成的混合词","usage":"People often get hangry when their blood sugar level is low.\n人们往往在血糖水平降低时会变得\"hangry\"。"},{"id":"de8e0f89-3a4e-4b59-8eee-0e7b683997aa","english":"scramble to","ipa":"","chinese":"争先恐后：指急忙行动，争相做某事，通常是因为时间紧迫或资源有限。","usage":"A sudden thought made her scramble to her feet.  \n她突然冒出一个的想法，急忙站了起来。"},{"id":"d9019270-04af-4051-8c22-485553f684a0","english":"sightseeing","ipa":"/ˈsaɪtsiːɪŋ/","chinese":"n. 观光；游览","usage":"to go sightseeing\n去观光"},{"id":"6c8e1ef4-a8dd-434e-9eea-9e257986cb00","english":"hole in the wall","ipa":"","chinese":"小商店；小餐馆；狭小的房子","usage":"It's just a hole in the wall but the food is good.\n虽说只是个小餐馆，但吃的东西还不错。"},{"id":"63e8c256-9531-486e-a8c3-c4ccfdf18e48","english":"hit-and-miss","ipa":"/'hitən'mis/","chinese":"a. 粗制滥造的；时好时坏的","usage":"The coffee at my local cafe is a bit hit and miss.\n我那儿咖啡馆的咖啡有点时好时坏。"},{"id":"2a7c6ef6-92bf-45bf-83e5-1880884de2fc","english":"guarantee","ipa":"/ˌɡærənˈtiː/","chinese":"v. 确保","usage":"These days getting a degree doesn't guarantee you a job.\n如今获得学位并不能保证你有工作。"}]},{"day":90,"title":"英语积累Day 90","topic":"生活方式,兴趣爱好","author":"Malama Life","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/700a475ed8854c36bb66ae5c1f719abc","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/Gzk8CE6PkWY?si=u_VuvIpwhfnHlVej","audioSize":"679.3KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-090.m4a","youtubeId":"Gzk8CE6PkWY","chinese":"当听到“快乐”这个词时，你会想到什么？对我来说，是在阳光明媚的日子里，坐在泳池边读一本好书的感觉，简直是顶级享受。然而，近年来“快乐”的含义已经发生了彻底的演变。它不再只意味着沉浸在那些令人愉悦的时刻，而是变成一种时时刻刻都想感受到的东西，并且衍生出了一些不良习惯：比如在社交媒体上不停地刷负面信息、查看消息通知、网络购物。这并不是我追求的快乐，而是一种随时都可获得的廉价多巴胺。也许我们的大脑天生就渴望一直追寻快乐。","english":"When you hear the word pleasure, what pops into your mind? For me, it's the feeling of sitting by the pool on a sunny day reading a good book. There is no better feeling. But then, pleasure evolved into something entirely different over the years. It was no longer about indulging in these feel-good moments, but something I wanted to feel all the time and it created some bad habits: doomscrolling on social media, checking for notifications, online shopping or online browsing. It's not the pleasure that I was after, but it's a cheap dopamine that's accessible to me at any time. Maybe our brains are wired to always seek pleasure.","sentences":["When you hear the word pleasure, what pops into your mind?","For me, it's the feeling of sitting by the pool on a sunny day reading a good book.","There is no better feeling.","But then, pleasure evolved into something entirely different over the years.","It was no longer about indulging in these feel-good moments, but something I wanted to feel all the time and it created some bad habits: doomscrolling on social media, checking for notifications, online shopping or online browsing.","It's not the pleasure that I was after, but it's a cheap dopamine that's accessible to me at any time.","Maybe our brains are wired to always seek pleasure."],"exercise":"When you hear the word pleasure, what 想到? For me, it's the feeling of sitting by the pool on a sunny day reading a good book. 简直是顶级享受. But then, pleasure 演变something entirely different over the years. It was no longer about 沉浸在 these 令人愉悦的时刻, but something I wanted to feel al the time and  it created some bad habits: 社交媒体上不停地刷负面信息、查看消息通知、网络购物. It's not the pleasure that I was after, but it's a 廉价多巴胺 that's 可获得的 me at any time. Maybe our brains 天生就渴望 always seek pleasure.","vocabulary":[{"id":"a94cdb98-5ea4-40c2-ac60-c53d1fd11936","english":"pop into one's head/mind","ipa":"","chinese":"突然想到；突然产生念头","usage":""},{"id":"30e17e6c-d71b-4d36-a0b7-c8f865081772","english":"There is no better feeling","ipa":"","chinese":"没有比这更好的感觉了","usage":"There is no better feeling than proving someone wrong that said you couldn't achieve something. \n找那些过去说你无法完成这件事的人，证明他们错了，这世上可没有比这再好的感觉了。"},{"id":"388167a4-08de-4368-a754-59f750fbc177","english":"evolve into","ipa":"","chinese":"发展成；演化为","usage":"Eventually, oral reports evolved into written ones.\n最后，口头报告演变成书面报告。"},{"id":"e34f9b6c-5b16-48c4-a076-988793681dc2","english":"indulge in","ipa":"","chinese":"沉湎于，沉溺于","usage":"1. indulges in self-pity 陷入自怜\n2. Indulge in computer games 沉溺于电脑游戏\n3. Indulge in the past 沉迷于过去\n4. Indulge in her beauty 沉迷于她的美貌"},{"id":"c9e76d83-3552-491b-a1bb-9b657c0f4b8d","english":"feel-good","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 使人愉悦的","usage":""},{"id":"1aa82106-1fd8-4ab3-8b8f-57f89f3c2060","english":"doomscrolling","ipa":"","chinese":"指 “人们在智能手机应用中、社交媒体或互联网上不断滚动浏览无数的坏消息”。","usage":"I've been doomscrolling too much and read so much information about coronavirus that I can't sleep at night.\n我读了太多关于冠状病毒的信息，以至于晚上睡不着觉。"},{"id":"8ccf392f-c4d9-4788-bfc7-951ed3abacf7","english":"online browsing","ipa":"","chinese":"在线浏览：通过互联网浏览网页或其他在线内容的活动。","usage":""},{"id":"5f88e6cd-2d62-4e3c-90b4-5df4736aea28","english":"be after","ipa":"","chinese":"寻求，追求","usage":"She's after his money.\n她是为了钱才追求他的。"},{"id":"262b8fe3-1d0a-4637-a1f2-a66951dbe786","english":"dopamine","ipa":"/'dəʊpəmiːn/","chinese":"n. 多巴胺","usage":"Dopamine is released during arousal. \n多巴胺是在兴奋时释放的。"},{"id":"a90c27a6-c698-4d49-8146-23eec037c147","english":"be accessible to","ipa":"","chinese":"容易接近的；可进入的","usage":"People with a phone can document their daily lives and make them accessible to billions of people, free of charge. \n拥有手机的人可以记录他们的日常生活，并让数十亿人免费使用。"},{"id":"e927535a-a181-4904-8330-ba54ad31003b","english":"be wired to","ipa":"","chinese":"与生俱来，生来……；天生，自然就会","usage":"We are wired to crave new information, and new information is interpreted like a reward.\n我们天生倾向于渴望新信息，并把新信息看作奖励。"}]},{"day":91,"title":"英语积累Day 91","topic":"生活方式,购物时尚","author":"Emma Hill","accent":"英音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/5fd5ae453fac42bc977a6c1c29d208f6","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ocXoGND5aD0","audioSize":"584.8KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-091.m4a","youtubeId":"ocXoGND5aD0","chinese":"在20多岁的时候，我经常掉进这样的陷阱：每次要买新东西的时候，就会有种兴奋和购物的快感，我想很多人应该都有过同感。这种兴奋是短暂的，而且对我来说，它导致了过度购物和消费主义，买的很多东西吊牌都没摘。我有太多多余的物品。自从采用了心愿板的方法，并且在购买前考虑得更周到、更仔细之后，我的买东西的数量显著减少。","english":"I fell into this trap so frequently in my 20s, is that when I would buy something new, I would get a little high, a little buzz from shopping, which I think a lot of us can probably relate to. And this buzz is short-lived, and in my case, led to just so much over-buying, so much consumerism, and I had things with the tags still on. I just had so much excess stuff. And since doing my little wishlist board method and being considerate and really carefully thinking about a purchase before I make it, it has had a huge and drastic effect on the amount of items that I buy.","sentences":["I fell into this trap so frequently in my 20s, is that when I would buy something new, I would get a little high, a little buzz from shopping, which I think a lot of us can probably relate to.","And this buzz is short-lived, and in my case, led to just so much over-buying, so much consumerism, and I had things with the tags still on.","I just had so much excess stuff.","And since doing my little wishlist board method and being considerate and really carefully thinking about a purchase before I make it, it has had a huge and drastic effect on the amount of items that I buy."],"exercise":"I  掉进这样的陷阱 so frequently in my 20s, is that when I would buy something new, I would get a little high, a little 快感 from shopping, which I think a lot of us can probably relate to. And this buzz is 短暂的, and 对我来说, led to just so much 过度购物, so much 消费主义, and I had things with the 吊牌 still on. I just had so much 多余的物品. And since doing my little wishlist board method and being 周到 and really carefully thinking about a purchase before I make it, it has had a huge and 显著 effect on the amount of items that I buy.","vocabulary":[{"id":"3ea22ac0-0979-4cfa-8432-b4fb22b3a097","english":"fall into the trap","ipa":"","chinese":"落入陷阱；陷入误区\n*段落中出现的“fell”是 “fall” /fɔːl/的过去式","usage":"It's a trap too many people fall into.\n太多人都掉进了这个陷阱中。"},{"id":"8ce612e4-7e3d-4d40-aec5-bdea35c6f3fa","english":"trap","ipa":"/træp/","chinese":"1.  (捕鸟兽的)陷阱，罗网，夹子，捕捉器\n2. 圈套;诡计;骗局\n3. 困境;窘境","usage":""},{"id":"bd7bf43d-0800-44d0-91ab-ff675eca262b","english":"buzz","ipa":"/bʌz/","chinese":"n. 1. 短暂的快乐，兴奋\n2. 嗡嗡的说话声\n3. 热闹有趣的气氛；时尚氛围","usage":"He got a buzz from creating confrontations.\n制造冲突让他感到幸灾乐祸。"},{"id":"9bd43593-55bd-4c1c-ab53-06c89135cfd5","english":"short-lived","ipa":"/'ʃɔ:t'livd/","chinese":"短暂的;昙花一现的","usage":"Chantal told Martine about her short-lived marriage.\n尚塔尔跟马丁内谈起她短暂的婚姻"},{"id":"6ac4dedd-f0e6-4f3c-9398-ed94b7ef0767","english":"in my case","ipa":"","chinese":"就我而言，我的情况是","usage":"In my case, those were the times I found myself learning and developing the most. 在我看来，那些时刻给予我了更多学习和发展的机会。"},{"id":"04d927d3-bc07-424f-9fec-49a9d550f290","english":"over-buying","ipa":"","chinese":"过度购买","usage":""},{"id":"1083168b-f5f9-41bc-9407-ffc6d55da0fc","english":"consumerism","ipa":"/kənˈsjuːmərɪzəm/","chinese":"消费主义（Consumerism）指相信持续及增加消费活动有助于经济的意识形态。创造出在生活态度上对商品的可欲及需求（多消费是好事）让资本主义可以提高工资及提高消费。","usage":"They have clearly embraced Western consumerism. 很明显他们已经接受了西方的消费主义观念。"},{"id":"af38b448-3451-4c25-bdc8-0511fd44650b","english":"tag","ipa":"/tæɡ/","chinese":"n. 标签;标牌","usage":"1. price tag 价格标签\n2. Staff wore name tags.\n工作人员都佩戴姓名牌。"},{"id":"8d2505a9-8439-4a93-b98e-2b56d3d9a3f2","english":"excess","ipa":"/ɪkˈses/","chinese":"a. 过量的;过多的","usage":"After cooking the fish, pour off any excess fat...\n烹完鱼后，倒掉多余的油。"},{"id":"022e6587-c848-4559-8ad3-351b69322a10","english":"excess stuff","ipa":"","chinese":"多余的东西：指不必要或过多的物品或材料。","usage":"Get rid of excess stuff.  清除家里多余的东西。"},{"id":"5d77554e-6302-4f60-a03c-1614b073c4af","english":"considerate","ipa":"/kənˈsɪdərət/","chinese":"a. 体贴的, 体谅他人的，周到的","usage":"They have been extremely considerate, polite, and cooperative. 他们考虑极其周到，很有礼貌，非常配合。"},{"id":"4751d23f-134c-467a-ac1d-82984d180e44","english":"drastic","ipa":"/ˈdræstɪk/","chinese":"a.  变化激烈的，巨大的","usage":"Elderly people are not in a position to make drastic changes at this stage of their life.\n上了年纪的人在他们这个人生阶段不会再有什么实质性的改变。"}]},{"day":92,"title":"英语积累Day 92","topic":"旅行","author":"Eva Meloche","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/ea275772be024bfaadac8bc905f6cbc7","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZQGhp3ccSbk&t=9s","audioSize":"448.3KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-092.m4a","youtubeId":"ZQGhp3ccSbk","chinese":"从踏上欧洲大陆的那一刻起，我们就期待着抵达意大利，因为这是我全家最喜欢的度假胜地，也是我的毕业旅行目的地。意大利在我心里占有一席之地，每次去都会感到很治愈。我们住在Plus Hostel，我强烈推荐这家旅馆，因为它靠近市中心，干净整洁，工作人员也非常友好。为了吃到第一口正宗意大利冰淇淋，我们步行去了La Caraya。晚餐后，我们开始游览这座城市，步行去了大教堂，教堂看起来十分气派，在夜色中熠熠生辉。","english":"From the moment we set foot on European soil, we were all anticipating arriving in Italy as my family's favorite vacation destination, as my grad trip location. Italy holds a sweet place in my heart and brings me so much comfort to visit. We stayed at the Plus Hostel, which I highly recommend for its proximity to the city center, its cleanliness, and its friendly staff. Wanting to get our first fix of many of Italian gelato, we walked to La Carraia. After dinner, we set out to explore the city and walked to the Duomo, which was such a majestic sight. It glowed in the night.","sentences":["From the moment we set foot on European soil, we were all anticipating arriving in Italy as my family's favorite vacation destination, as my grad trip location.","Italy holds a sweet place in my heart and brings me so much comfort to visit.","We stayed at the Plus Hostel, which I highly recommend for its proximity to the city center, its cleanliness, and its friendly staff.","Wanting to get our first fix of many of Italian gelato, we walked to La Carraia.","After dinner, we set out to explore the city and walked to the Duomo, which was such a majestic sight.","It glowed in the night."],"exercise":"From the moment we 踏上欧洲大陆, we were all 期待 arriving in Italy as my family's favorite 度假胜地, as my 毕业旅行目的地. Italy 在我心里占有一席之地 and brings me so much 治愈 to visit. We stayed at the Plus Hostel, which I highly recommend for its 靠近市中心o the city center, its 干净整洁, and its friendly staff.  Wanting to get our 第一口 many of Italian gelato, we walked to La Carraia. After dinner, we 开始 explore the city and walked to the 大教堂, which was 看起来十分气派. It 在夜色中熠熠生辉.","vocabulary":[{"id":"8a9a3982-a4b0-439e-8a43-5fdea046ab09","english":"set foot on","ipa":"","chinese":"进入，访问，参观（某地）","usage":"the first man to set foot on the moon\n第一个登上月球的人"},{"id":"c8f8b208-77ea-400b-b475-0fe7f3fd6ac9","english":"soil","ipa":"/sɔɪl/","chinese":"n. 国土；领土；","usage":"it was the first time I had set foot on African soil.\n那是我第一次踏足非洲大地。"},{"id":"4e5ed2ec-e96e-4b59-8ac7-23c7956aba12","english":"anticipate","ipa":"/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/","chinese":"v. 期盼；期望","usage":"The more I anticipated arriving somewhere, the more disappointed I was.\n我越期盼在某方面有所成就，就越失望。"},{"id":"b123fb9a-dbc8-4e8a-b4ba-dcc0e762ce43","english":"vacation destination","ipa":"","chinese":"度假胜地","usage":"The Spanish archipelago is a popular vacation destination for European travelers.\n这个西班牙群岛是欧洲游客的热门度假胜地。"},{"id":"c23bc7bd-28eb-4189-bd98-343532dc9b3d","english":"grad trip location","ipa":"","chinese":"毕业旅行目的地","usage":""},{"id":"745000be-7553-40c5-98d5-51b7d2cd7754","english":"hold a place in heart","ipa":"","chinese":"在心中占有一席之地","usage":"You hold a place in my heart no other woman can fill.  \n你在我心目中的地位是任何女人都无法代替的。"},{"id":"01588769-0666-457d-9472-938a2e851fab","english":"comfort","ipa":"/ˈkʌmfət/","chinese":"n. 安慰；慰藉；","usage":"to take/draw comfort from sb's words\n从某人的话中得到安慰"},{"id":"4ca09301-1a7e-4862-a619-12923ddfdf4d","english":"proximity to","ipa":"/prɒkˈsɪməti/","chinese":"接近，邻近","usage":"The town grew thanks to the proximity to a railroad.\n由于靠近铁路，城镇发展繁荣。"},{"id":"dc33723c-44fd-43ec-9afa-fc97706d1ed3","english":"cleanliness","ipa":"/ˈklenlɪnɪs/","chinese":"n. 清洁；干净","usage":"Some people are obsessive about cleanliness.\n有些人有洁癖。"},{"id":"1c097244-a0d2-4542-8be8-e830eecb313b","english":"fix of","ipa":"","chinese":"(维持身体或心理需要所需的)一个剂量，一定数量；(致瘾的东西，尤指毒品的)一次用量。\nan amount of sth that you need and want frequently","usage":"l need a fix of coffee before l canface the day.\n我总需要喝足咖啡才有精神应付一天的工作。"},{"id":"264747f6-7eee-432c-bc13-f9d78820ec2d","english":"set out to","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 打算\n2. 着手\n3. 开始\n4. 出发去","usage":"In 2019, researchers set out to do just that.\n2019 年，研究人员开始做这样的测试。"},{"id":"fea89b99-5ed7-4657-a8fa-b948ab5965df","english":"Duomo","ipa":"/'dwəuməu/","chinese":"杜奥莫大教堂（Duomo），位于米兰市中心，有人称这是世界第三大教堂。","usage":"It's full of art and the Duomo is the greatest part.\n那里充满艺术气息，最棒的就是大教堂。"},{"id":"4f8e9a06-6873-49f2-a2ee-309797157898","english":"majestic","ipa":"/məˈdʒestɪk/","chinese":"a. 雄伟的；威严的；壮观的","usage":"a majestic castle/river/view\n雄伟的城堡；壮丽的河流/景色"},{"id":"37e95481-98f1-42f5-9eba-43ef607f949e","english":"glow","ipa":"/ɡləʊ/","chinese":"v. 发出微弱而稳定的光；","usage":"The embers still glowed in the hearth.\n余烬仍在炉膛里发出暗淡的光。"}]},{"day":93,"title":"英语积累Day 93","topic":"旅行,购物时尚","author":"Eva Meloche","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/c670541a862a41e89b390589a9f08683","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZQGhp3ccSbk&t=9s","audioSize":"444.0KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-093.m4a","youtubeId":"ZQGhp3ccSbk","chinese":"我们发现，佛罗伦萨不仅历史悠久，也是一座购物之城。通往大教堂和博物馆的每条街道上都是设计师店铺，让人很难在不购物的情况下畅游这座城市。我们看到了佛罗伦萨最迷人的景色，真是风景如画，就像那张明信片上印的一样。佛罗伦萨大教堂和它标志性的巨大橙红色穹顶高高耸立，整个城市的景象美得令人惊叹。之后，我们去逛了二手商店。但我没有找到特别喜欢的，所以空手而归。","english":"We discovered that as much as Florence holds a lot of history, it is also a shopping city. All the streets leading to the Duomo and the museums are packed with designer storefronts, making it almost impossible to glide through the city without making a purchase. We enjoyed the most stunning view of Florence. It was picturesque. The view resembled that of a postcard, with the Cathedral of Florence and its iconic huge rust-orange dome standing high. The sight of the city was breathtaking. Afterwards, we went thrifting. But I didn't find anything that stood out to me, so I left empty-handed.","sentences":["We discovered that as much as Florence holds a lot of history, it is also a shopping city.","All the streets leading to the Duomo and the museums are packed with designer storefronts, making it almost impossible to glide through the city without making a purchase.","We enjoyed the most stunning view of Florence.","It was picturesque.","The view resembled that of a postcard, with the Cathedral of Florence and its iconic huge rust-orange dome standing high.","The sight of the city was breathtaking.","Afterwards, we went thrifting.","But I didn't find anything that stood out to me, so I left empty-handed."],"exercise":"We discovered that as much as Florence 历史悠久, it is also a shopping city. All the streets leading to the Duomo and the museums 都是 设计师店铺, making it almost impossible to 畅游 the city without making a purchase. We enjoyed the most 迷人的景色 of Florence. It was 风景如画. The view 就像 that of a postcard, with the Cathedral of Florence and its iconic huge 巨大橙红色穹顶 standing high. The sight of the city was 美得令人惊叹. Afterwards, we went 二手商店. But I didn't find anything that 特别喜欢的, so I 空手而归.","vocabulary":[{"id":"8c2f82ad-7aed-46b7-b771-2a5ccafac4c7","english":"hold","ipa":"/həʊld/","chinese":"vt. 持有；保存；拥有","usage":"holds a great deal of property.拥有一大笔财富"},{"id":"93846cfa-fd7c-4e90-9071-7a881452aec7","english":"be packed with","ipa":"/pæk/","chinese":"挤满；塞满","usage":"It's packed with vitamins, fibre and minerals.\n里面富含维生素、纤维和矿物质。"},{"id":"12f618bd-9c1f-4fe6-98ac-8180b86b6341","english":"storefront","ipa":"/'stɔːfrʌnt/","chinese":"(临街的)店面，铺面","usage":"Main Street is lined with small storefronts and restaurants.\n主街两侧林立着许多小的店铺和餐馆。"},{"id":"40a08f22-29ad-4ba3-89c9-d27a0f233cc4","english":"glide through","ipa":"/ɡlaɪd/","chinese":"滑过；轻松地完成某事：毫不费力地完成某项任务或活动。","usage":"No venomous snake glides through the thicket, no crocodile lurks in the swamp.\n在那里没有毒蛇在丛林中游弋，也没有鳄鱼在沼泽里潜伏。"},{"id":"70069061-28ad-4716-8403-c36011724d27","english":"stunning","ipa":"/ˈstʌnɪŋ/","chinese":"a. 极有魅力的；绝妙的；","usage":"a stunning view of the lake\n无比优美的湖光水色"},{"id":"6cc81f65-f83a-4c1e-aaeb-693700ad52c2","english":"picturesque","ipa":"/ˌpɪktʃəˈresk/","chinese":"a.  美丽的，风景如画的","usage":"a picturesque cottage/setting/village\n画儿一般的小屋/环境/村落"},{"id":"d650cbc8-d7b5-4099-b23f-edb5d163d84a","english":"resemble","ipa":"/rɪˈzembl/","chinese":"v. 看起来像；显得像；像","usage":"So many hotels resemble each other.\n许多酒店看上去都差不多。"},{"id":"75092fe6-c4bb-447d-a35f-3d8bf218b1c7","english":"rust-orange","ipa":"","chinese":"铁锈橙，橙红色","usage":""},{"id":"c8f5f201-5012-4b75-9875-0e1497740d9e","english":"dome","ipa":"/dəʊm/","chinese":"穹顶;圆屋顶","usage":"the dome of St Paul's cathedral.\n圣保罗大教堂的圆顶"},{"id":"ca7223ab-d888-4e66-89dd-52346bc173b1","english":"breathtaking","ipa":"/'breθteɪkɪŋ/","chinese":"令人兴奋的；激动人心的；壮观的；","usage":"The house has breathtaking views from every room...\n这所房子的每个房间都能看到令人惊叹的美景。"},{"id":"4b3bb1f2-a5a4-4208-ae3c-a4340c1c5fbe","english":"go thrifting","ipa":"","chinese":"去淘二手货\nthrift store二手商店","usage":""},{"id":"793217be-6b8f-4057-91cd-22096187c777","english":"stand out","ipa":"","chinese":"引人注目;显眼；突出","usage":"Yeah, so that stood out for me. 是啊，这让我印象深刻。"},{"id":"1e36f621-ed65-4106-96ea-8ed2d141a8a8","english":"empty-handed","ipa":"","chinese":"adj. 空手的；徒手的","usage":"She visited every Sunday and never arrived empty-handed. 她每个星期天都来拜访，没有哪一次不带礼物。"}]},{"day":94,"title":"英语积累Day 94","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Emma Hill","accent":"英音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/51b13a1ac67442d597f329b15e9abfb2","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ocXoGND5aD0","audioSize":"470.4KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-094.m4a","youtubeId":"ocXoGND5aD0","chinese":"这些是我新添置的首饰，和我其他大部分通常是素金的首饰不太一样。其中几件有一些漂亮的黑尖晶石珠，和金块形成了对比。我之前提到过，我喜欢金色饰品配黑色衣服。我觉得这些首饰非常漂亮，打算之后日常佩戴，也许可以衬托凸显我的基础款服装，比如一件简单的衬衫，甚至是一件基础背心或T恤，然后再在上面套一件夹克外套。这是我在春季最常穿的搭配。","english":"These are my new additions, and they're a little bit different from most of my other jewelry, which is usually plain gold. I have a couple of pieces here which have these beautiful black spinel beads, which contrast with the gold nuggets. And I've mentioned before that I love gold jewelry worn against or worn with black clothing. And I think these are really beautiful pieces which I'll be using for day-to-day wear, perhaps to amp up my basics, so maybe wearing with a basic shirt or even a basic vest or t-shirt and then layering over a blazer on top, which is very much a go-to outfit of mine throughout the spring season.","sentences":["These are my new additions, and they're a little bit different from most of my other jewelry, which is usually plain gold.","I have a couple of pieces here which have these beautiful black spinel beads, which contrast with the gold nuggets.","And I've mentioned before that I love gold jewelry worn against or worn with black clothing.","And I think these are really beautiful pieces which I'll be using for day-to-day wear, perhaps to amp up my basics, so maybe wearing with a basic shirt or even a basic vest or t-shirt and then layering over a blazer on top, which is very much a go-to outfit of mine throughout the spring season."],"exercise":"These are my 新添置的首饰, and they're a little bit different from most of my other jewelry, which is usually 素金.  I have a couple of pieces here which have these beautiful black spinel beads, which 形成了对比 the 金块. And I've mentioned before that I love gold jewelry worn against or with black clothing. And I think these are really beautiful pieces which I'll be using for 日常佩戴, perhaps to 衬托凸显 my basics, so maybe wearing with a basic shirt or even a basic vest or t-shirt and then 套一件夹克外套 on top, which is very much a 最常穿的搭配 of mine throughout the spring season.","vocabulary":[{"id":"12a8b967-7a4a-424b-9ac2-83221bbf3a64","english":"new addition","ipa":"","chinese":"新添加的东西：最近添加到其他事物中的东西。","usage":"Would you like to see the newest additions to our collection first, Catherine?\n凯瑟琳，你想先看看我们的最新藏品吗？"},{"id":"3f5ecfef-8358-4e1c-a2b5-54954a5e9832","english":"plain","ipa":"/pleɪn/","chinese":"1. 单色的；素色的；无花纹或图案、字迹的\n2. 朴素的；简朴的\n3. 明显的；明白的；清楚的","usage":"In general, a plain carpet makes a room look bigger.\n一般来说，单色的地毯使房间显得更宽敞。"},{"id":"1b45147e-9a07-42e3-90be-11aee3b9ee87","english":"plain gold","ipa":"","chinese":"素金：指未经镶嵌或装饰的纯金饰品或物品。","usage":""},{"id":"e3cf582a-0053-4be1-bc70-aac7d97ba7fc","english":"contrast with","ipa":"","chinese":"与……形成对比","usage":"Contrast these foreign goods with the domestic products.\n把这些外国货和本国货比较一下。"},{"id":"415776f2-3cd8-4299-a3b5-b60d5d76ad59","english":"nugget","ipa":"/'nʌgɪt/","chinese":"小块东西;(尤指)小金块","usage":"1. a nugget of food. 一小块食物\n2. But who actually invented chicken nuggets?\n但究竟是谁发明了鸡块呢？"},{"id":"05b87bf7-6f3f-4328-95dc-9b6178826383","english":"day-to-day","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 每天的;日常的","usage":"She has charge of the day-to-day running of the business.  她负责掌管日常业务"},{"id":"18735d34-5d04-440d-8fac-1bc83720ba41","english":"amp up","ipa":"/ˌeɪemˈpi:/","chinese":"增强，增加（某物）的功率、兴趣、强度、音量等：指通过增加某物的功率、兴趣、强度、音量等来使其更强大、更有影响力。","usage":"I also have some tomato paste, which is just gonna amp up that tomato flavor even further.\n我还准备了一些番茄酱，让番茄的味道更浓郁一些。"},{"id":"77c724c6-ff3c-4aa8-8c5b-aa14dec83f18","english":"layer over","ipa":"/ˈleɪə(r)/","chinese":"覆盖：在某物上面加上一层物质或材料","usage":""},{"id":"a6049fbf-f576-4539-a11e-cc16b0d30806","english":"blazer","ipa":"/'bleɪzə/","chinese":"运动夹克，运动上衣","usage":"And I need my white shirt, my red tie and my blue blazer. 我还要我的白衬衫，红领带和蓝色夹克衫。"},{"id":"60c577cb-31ca-4bae-af04-966a8a0dff7d","english":"go-to","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 首选的，最佳的","usage":"Shawn is my go-to guy for event planning, so he will definitely be able to help you find a caterer.\n肖恩是我活动策划的时候最可以指望得上的人，所以他一定能帮你找一个宴会承办商。"},{"id":"47fcb8f0-90c6-45d5-9c1e-727c1ad8c1a8","english":"outfit","ipa":"/ˈaʊtfɪt/","chinese":"n. 全套服装","usage":""}]},{"day":95,"title":"英语积累Day 95","topic":"工作职场","author":"Cass Thompson Career Advice","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/eaa4f2c9f13049c8964466470f900d6e","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U0YdO6zGSH","audioSize":"470.8KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-095.m4a","youtubeId":"U0YdO6zGSH","chinese":"第三个问题：你最大的缺点是什么？在回答这个问题时，绝对不要把一个优点说成是缺点。所以绝对不能说，“哦，我是一个完美主义者。” 这样的回答我们现在都已经看破了。回答这个问题，需要一些技巧，你要做的是给出一个真正的弱点，但这个弱点不直接关系到这个职位的核心技能。所以，我经常提及的一个弱点是我非常固执己见。我对所有事情都有自己的看法，包括要去哪家快餐店，即使这是件无关紧要的小事。","english":"Question three: What's your greatest weakness? You never want to use a strength as a weakness. So you're never going to be like, \"Oh, I am such a perfectionist.\" Like, we all see through that now. What you want to do with this one—and it takes some finessing—is give an actual weakness, but one that is not directly related to the core skills of this position. So one of the weaknesses I give a lot is that I am highly opinionated. I have an opinion on everything, including which fast food restaurant to go to, even though it doesn't really matter to me.","sentences":["Question three: What's your greatest weakness?","You never want to use a strength as a weakness.","So you're never going to be like, \"Oh, I am such a perfectionist.\"","Like, we all see through that now.","What you want to do with this one—and it takes some finessing—is give an actual weakness, but one that is not directly related to the core skills of this position.","So one of the weaknesses I give a lot is that I am highly opinionated.","I have an opinion on everything, including which fast food restaurant to go to, even though it doesn't really matter to me."],"exercise":"Question three: What's your 最大的缺点? You never want to use a strength as a weakness. So you're never going to be like, \"Oh, I am such a 完美主义者.\" Like, we all 看破 that now. What you want to do with this one—and it 需要一些技巧—is give an actual weakness, but one that is not directly related to the 核心技能 of this position. So one of the weaknesses I give a lot is that 我非常固执己见. I 对所有事情都有自己的看法, including which fast food restaurant to go to, even though 这是件无关紧要的小事.","vocabulary":[{"id":"268f2e61-6482-41df-8ca0-ac001ec484e6","english":"perfectionist","ipa":"/pəˈfekʃɵnɪst/","chinese":"n. 完美主义者","usage":"Perfectionists may also hurt team cohesiveness.\n完美主义者也可能会破坏团队凝聚力。"},{"id":"3f018b2d-a6ba-4dd4-8d25-760ebdb456cd","english":"see through","ipa":"","chinese":"看透；识破","usage":"I can see through your little game \n我看透了你的小把戏。"},{"id":"35c8edb5-7987-4d57-a9ef-ccca831d2acc","english":"finesse","ipa":"/fɪ'nes/","chinese":"n. & v. 手腕；策略；手段","usage":"Handling conflict takes finesse and thought.\n处理冲突需要策略和思考。"},{"id":"768e05f0-6c2d-4fbb-bf74-335f75689800","english":"core skills","ipa":"","chinese":"核心技能","usage":"Schools have to deliver the core skills.\n学校必须传授基本的技能。"},{"id":"d9d52f3d-29c8-4c3e-9677-4b93fb70f25e","english":"outreach","ipa":"/aʊt'riːtʃ/","chinese":"n. 外展服务（在服务机构以外的场所提供的社区服务等）","usage":"1. an outreach and education programme\n外展服务及教育计划\n2. outreach workers\n外展服务人员"},{"id":"df21e711-9128-4866-a69b-25bcdd4b59a9","english":"opinionated","ipa":"/əˈpɪnjəneɪtɪd/","chinese":"a. 固执己见的；顽固的","usage":"an arrogant and opinionated man.\n一个傲慢固执的人。"},{"id":"b4d94523-5a65-46b7-bcac-2342bdf8a281","english":"have an opinion on everything","ipa":"","chinese":"对每件事都有自己的看法","usage":""}]},{"day":96,"title":"英语积累Day 96","topic":"工作职场","author":"Indeed","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/df7b82dad65146f6b2291a2bbf5418fe","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bx9bTbN5wH0","audioSize":"603.0KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-096.m4a","youtubeId":"bx9bTbN5wH0","chinese":"薪资谈判错误一：率先透露具体的工资数额。在面试过程中，你肯定想表现得热情随和，但在这种特定情况下，要把这个问题反过来问面试官。让我们来看一个真实示例。假如雇主在初步电话面试时问你：“您对薪资有何预期要求？”你可以简单地回答：“现在还在面试初期，我还在了解这个岗位的职责，所以目前我的薪资预期比较灵活。另外，在加入一家新公司时，除了薪酬，我还会考虑很多其他因素。”然后你可以反问他们：“这个岗位的薪资预算是多少？”","english":"Salary negotiation mistake number one: being the first to disclose a specific dollar amount. You, of course, want to be obliging in the interview process, but in this particular instance, go ahead and flip that question back to the interviewer. So, let's take a look at a real-world example here. Let's say an employer is doing initial phone screening with you, and you're asked, \"What are you looking for for pay?\" Now, you can go ahead and just respond with something as simple as, \"It's so early in the process that I'm still learning what the role and responsibilities are, so my expectations are flexible at the moment. Plus, there are many other considerations that I make when it comes to joining a new company beyond pay.\" But flip then question to them and say, \"What have you budgeted for the role?\"","sentences":["Salary negotiation mistake number one: being the first to disclose a specific dollar amount.","You, of course, want to be obliging in the interview process, but in this particular instance, go ahead and flip that question back to the interviewer.","So, let's take a look at a real-world example here.","Let's say an employer is doing initial phone screening with you, and you're asked, \"What are you looking for for pay?\"","Now, you can go ahead and just respond with something as simple as, \"It's so early in the process that I'm still learning what the role and responsibilities are, so my expectations are flexible at the moment.","Plus, there are many other considerations that I make when it comes to joining a new company beyond pay.\"","But flip then question to them and say, \"What have you budgeted for the role?\""],"exercise":"Salary negotiation mistake number one: being the first to 透露 a specific dollar amount. You, of course, want to 热情随和 in the interview process, but 在这种特定情况下, go ahead and 把这个问题反过来问面试官 the interviewer. So, let's take a look at 真实示例 here. Let's say an employer is doing 初步电话面试 with you, and you're asked, \"您对薪资有何预期要求?\" Now, you can go ahead and just respond with something as simple as, \"现在还在面试初期 that I'm still learning what the role and responsibilities are, so my expectations are 灵活 at the moment. Plus, there are many other considerations that I make when it comes to joining a new company 除了薪酬.\" But 反问 them and say, \"What have you 这个岗位的薪资预算?\"","vocabulary":[{"id":"51a76ef4-d694-4470-abdc-d94276825466","english":"disclose","ipa":"/dɪsˈkləʊz/","chinese":"v. 透露","usage":"I cannot disclose what we discussed.\n我不能泄露我们讨论的内容。"},{"id":"0bad47c4-79f2-46f8-83cf-60331d26a377","english":"obliging","ipa":"/əˈblaɪdʒɪŋ/","chinese":"a. 乐于助人的；热情的","usage":"They were very obliging and offered to wait for us.\n他们非常热情，主动提出等候我们。"},{"id":"3b7568d0-ec6c-49f2-a452-c59a28e18892","english":"in this particular instance","ipa":"","chinese":"在这种特定情况下","usage":""},{"id":"f7931142-7079-4af4-9826-7645cd9e2c18","english":"flip question back to","ipa":"","chinese":"反问","usage":""},{"id":"65ae7432-ea21-4107-ba43-af54367b6aa0","english":"flip","ipa":"/flɪp/","chinese":"v. （话题、活动或意见）突然改变，突然转换","usage":""},{"id":"4c18d5b4-deb5-4424-87a0-8f1fe01e7eab","english":"real-world","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 存在于现实世界的；真实的","usage":"Teachers need to prepare their students to deal with real-world situations outside the classroom.\n教师应该让学生做好应对课堂以外的现实世界的准备。"},{"id":"0a22c3b6-9031-44ae-99d8-f0df4f199aa7","english":"initial","ipa":"/ɪˈnɪʃl/","chinese":"a. 最初的；开始的","usage":"My initial reaction was to decline the offer.\n我最初的反应是婉言谢绝这个提议"},{"id":"9b39ff40-c23b-41dd-b5d8-b0827e25113a","english":"phone screening","ipa":"","chinese":"电话面试","usage":"Take a deep breath and remember you've already passed the first test, generally a phone screening.  \n做一次深呼吸，记住你已经通过了第一轮的电话面试。"},{"id":"5de4e50f-dd19-48c2-906e-880eb2680c51","english":"screen","ipa":"/skriːn/","chinese":"v. 审查；筛选","usage":"I use my voicemail to screen my phone calls.\n我用语音信箱筛选打来的电话。"},{"id":"a947ad40-aef4-465d-b93a-05daa4f39776","english":"look for","ipa":"","chinese":"期望；期待；盼望","usage":"We shall be looking for an improvement in your work this term.\n我们期待你这学期功课有进步。"},{"id":"7eff594b-7362-4fe8-a497-a5c7d417104e","english":"flexible","ipa":"/ˈfleksəbl/","chinese":"a. 能适应新情况的；灵活的；","usage":"1. a more flexible approach\n更灵活的方法\n2. flexible working hours\n弹性工作时间"},{"id":"263b25fd-ffdb-4f37-90c6-c7fbd79901b4","english":"plus","ipa":"/plʌs/","chinese":"conj. 而且；此外；况且","usage":"I've got too much on at work. Plus my father is not well.\n我工作负担太重了，而且我父亲身体也不好。"},{"id":"f37cee6d-a451-424e-8e4a-295558d902a6","english":"beyond","ipa":"/bɪˈjɒnd/","chinese":"prep. 除 … 之外","usage":"She's got nothing beyond her state pension.\n除了政府发的养老金外，她就什么都没有领取。"},{"id":"7343e493-1e04-4c3d-ba46-8949e12658da","english":"budget","ipa":"/ˈbʌdʒɪt/","chinese":"v. 安排开支; 把 … 编入预算","usage":"I've budgeted for two new members of staff.\n我已经把两名新职员名额编入预算。"}]},{"day":97,"title":"英语积累Day 97","topic":"购物时尚","author":"Steph Bohrer","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/5c196d55a07d4b67b23dc9f7b1923a0d","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QfbG3qgqqkY","audioSize":"656.3KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-097.m4a","youtubeId":"QfbG3qgqqkY","chinese":"我不用粉底，只用这款遮瑕膏。我会把它涂在鼻周泛红或有瑕疵的地方。这款遮瑕膏和我的肤色完美匹配，你可能根本看不出我涂在哪里，因为它几乎和我的肤色一模一样。然后我会用平头刷把它均匀推开。这就是我不用粉底液也能均匀肤色的方法。这是我用过的最好的眼下遮瑕，能很好地遮盖我的黑眼圈。我的眼下有比较明显的细纹，这款遮瑕膏能遮住它们，并且只要定妆就不会卡纹。在上完遮瑕还没卡纹之前，我会用这个三角形粉扑和这款Huda Beauty散粉。我不知道散粉的色号，我会取一点粉轻轻按压在眼下。","english":"I don’t use foundation, I just use this concealer. I put this on any like redness or spots around my nose. This is like an exact skin tone match. You can probably not even see where I’m putting it because it is almost identical to my skin tone. And then I take a brush. This is a flat head brush and I kind of like just blend it out everywhere. This is just how I even out my skin tone rather than using a foundation. It’s just the best under-eye concealer I’ve ever used. It covers up my dark circles so much. I have pretty defined creases under my eyes, and it covers them and it doesn’t crease as long as you set it. Right after I do that, before it creases, I take this triangular powder puff and use this Huda Beauty powder. I don’t know what shade it is, and I pack it in under my eyes a little bit.","sentences":["I don’t use foundation, I just use this concealer.","I put this on any like redness or spots around my nose.","This is like an exact skin tone match.","You can probably not even see where I’m putting it because it is almost identical to my skin tone.","And then I take a brush.","This is a flat head brush and I kind of like just blend it out everywhere.","This is just how I even out my skin tone rather than using a foundation.","It’s just the best under-eye concealer I’ve ever used.","It covers up my dark circles so much.","I have pretty defined creases under my eyes, and it covers them and it doesn’t crease as long as you set it.","Right after I do that, before it creases, I take this triangular powder puff and use this Huda Beauty powder.","I don’t know what shade it is, and I pack it in under my eyes a little bit."],"exercise":"I don’t use 粉底, I just use this 遮瑕膏. I put this on any like 泛红 or spots around my nose. This is like an 和我的肤色完美匹配. You can probably not even see where I’m putting it because it is almost 一模一样 my 肤色. And then I take a brush. This is a flat head brush and I kind of like just 均匀推开 everywhere. This is just how I 均匀肤色 my skin tone rather than using a foundation. It’s just the best 眼下遮瑕 I’ve ever used. It 遮盖我的黑眼圈 so much. I have pretty 明显的细纹 under my eyes, and it covers them and it doesn’t 卡纹 as long as you 定妆. Right after I do that, before it creases, I take this 三角形粉扑 and use this Huda Beauty powder. I don’t know what 色号 it is, and I 按压在 under my eyes a little bit.","vocabulary":[{"id":"ac3e8379-48e4-4643-a88f-45e1f99f9ee2","english":"foundation","ipa":"/faʊnˈdeɪʃn/","chinese":"n. （化妆打底用的）粉底霜","usage":""},{"id":"832cbcb3-e1e6-4271-8332-4c5691f3ac39","english":"concealer","ipa":"/kənˈsiːlə/","chinese":"n. 遮瑕膏；遮瑕粉；","usage":"And if you order right now, I'll throw in some extra concealer for half off.\n如果你现在下单，我额外把下一支遮瑕膏算你半价。"},{"id":"1392f6a6-eef4-41b7-9baf-7bae2cca392f","english":"redness","ipa":"","chinese":"n. 泛红；红肿","usage":"1. skin redness 皮肤发红\n2. You may notice redness and swelling after the injection.  \n注射后会出现红肿。"},{"id":"ac2ed0f8-a389-4a6f-8f5b-e07a4ed164b6","english":"skin tone","ipa":"","chinese":"肤色","usage":"If you skip foundation, your skin tone will be uneven.\n如果你不用粉底，你的肤色会不均匀。"},{"id":"ca06d131-d263-4abf-8465-f5ba4469831d","english":"be identical to","ipa":"/aɪˈdentɪkl/","chinese":"a. 相同的","usage":"Her dress is almost identical to mine.\n她的连衣裙和我的几乎一模一样。"},{"id":"97a8b661-ba67-4806-8ed8-471f1291fe71","english":"blend it out","ipa":"","chinese":"晕开","usage":"Next, apply eye shadow from the root of the lash all the way to the brow. Concentrate more shadow at the lash roots, then blend it out.\n接着，从睫毛根部到眉毛，一路都涂上眼影。在睫毛根部要重点刷上眼影，然后晕开。"},{"id":"acfc83ed-6937-4a10-8b43-69fdb7b57a0c","english":"even out","ipa":"","chinese":"均匀肤色","usage":"You might choose a foundation or tinted lotion to even out your skin tone.\n你可以选用一款粉底或提亮肤色的润肤露来均匀肤色。"},{"id":"01e72919-1ea1-47bc-8a54-68d6f4982a00","english":"under-eye concealer","ipa":"","chinese":"眼部遮瑕霜","usage":""},{"id":"1af9bf19-47dd-4794-ace1-4219e95146f4","english":"cover up","ipa":"","chinese":"遮瑕","usage":"Makeup helps conceal or cover up those imperfections, like scars or acne.\n化妆可以帮助遮瑕，比如遮住疤痕或粉刺。"},{"id":"67b2a779-824d-4a58-85e7-3f0e02eaf461","english":"dark circle","ipa":"","chinese":"黑眼圈","usage":"Susan observed that Doris had lost a lot of weight and often had dark circles under her eyes.\n苏珊发现多莉丝瘦了很多而且经常出现黑眼圈"},{"id":"825dc8ac-3737-469c-8d2b-7d8233ddba24","english":"defined","ipa":"/dɪ'faɪnd/","chinese":"a.  轮廓分明的，外形清晰的","usage":"gentle hills that were defined against the sky.\n在天空的衬托下显得轮廓分明的丘陵"},{"id":"0f57a087-d9ad-4e90-ace6-05fee28b4405","english":"crease","ipa":"/kri:s/","chinese":"1. n. （皮肤上，尤指脸上的）皱纹\n2. v. （皮肤）皱起；使起皱纹","usage":"1. creases around the eyes\n眼睛周围的皱纹\n2. A frown creased her forehead.\n她一皱眉，额头显出了皱纹。"},{"id":"b8d396ef-5707-492c-803b-2436ee2d6931","english":"set","ipa":"","chinese":"v. 定妆","usage":"setting spray 定妆喷雾"},{"id":"37e23a13-45a1-49cc-808c-738bf2552344","english":"powder puff","ipa":"/ˈpaʊdəˌpʌf/","chinese":"粉扑","usage":"So a powder puff would pat the powder on, not brush it.\n粉扑是把粉拍上去而不是刷上去。"},{"id":"ab4e6c86-3ddb-424b-9a04-4ed674cb8275","english":"shade","ipa":"/ʃeɪd/","chinese":"n. 色号","usage":"CHANEL launched a new eye shadow collection, which contained many stunning shades.\nCHANEL推出了新的眼影系列，里面有很多很惊艳的色号。"},{"id":"2cc7f5bc-ae63-4504-9dfd-6a98241eab6a","english":"pack","ipa":"/pæk/","chinese":"v. 压实","usage":"Pack the earth down around the plant.\n把植物周围的泥土压实。"}]},{"day":98,"title":"英语积累Day 98","topic":"旅行","author":"Macerly","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/970eb4c6f87a438f94bd579707d64953","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kuR5QJ8gdUU","audioSize":"496.5KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-098.m4a","youtubeId":"kuR5QJ8gdUU","chinese":"让我们来聊聊为什么你应该首先考虑轻装出行。我认为最显而易见的原因是，这样能省钱。目前，大多数航空公司都会对托运行李收取额外费用，所以只携带随身行李就能为你省下一笔钱。此外，带行李还会面临潜在的压力：行李可能会在机场、飞行途中或中途的某个地方丢失；有人可能会在行李托运处误拿你的行李。而我只需带着随身行到达机场，直接过安检，然后登机——不用排队托运行李。一旦你开始像这样轻装出行，就真的再也不想回到以前那种出行方式了。","english":"Let's talk about why you should even want to pack light in the first place. And I think the most obvious one is the fact that it will save you money. Most airlines nowadays will have you pay extra for checked-in baggage. So, bringing just a carry-on will save you money. But there's also the potential stress that comes with bringing luggage: it could be lost either at the airport or during the flight or somewhere in between; someone could accidentally take your luggage at baggage drop. I just got to the airport with my luggage, go straight through security, and then onto the plane—no waiting in lines to drop off my luggage. Once you start traveling and packing like this, there's truly no going back.","sentences":["Let's talk about why you should even want to pack light in the first place.","And I think the most obvious one is the fact that it will save you money.","Most airlines nowadays will have you pay extra for checked-in baggage.","So, bringing just a carry-on will save you money.","But there's also the potential stress that comes with bringing luggage: it could be lost either at the airport or during the flight or somewhere in between; someone could accidentally take your luggage at baggage drop.","I just got to the airport with my luggage, go straight through security, and then onto the plane—no waiting in lines to drop off my luggage.","Once you start traveling and packing like this, there's truly no going back."],"exercise":"Let's talk about why you should even want to 轻装出行 in the first place. And I think the most obvious one is the fact that it will save you money. Most 航空公司 nowadays will have you pay extra for 托运行李. So, bringing just a 随身行李 will save you money. But there's also the 潜在的压力 that comes with bringing luggage: it could be lost either at the airport or during the flight or 中途的某个地方; someone could accidentally take your luggage at 行李托运处. I just got to the airport with my luggage, 直接过安检, and then onto the plane—no waiting in lines to 托运 my luggage. Once you start traveling and packing like this, 就真的不想回到以前那种出行方式了.","vocabulary":[{"id":"b0ed6c7e-1870-482e-89ee-67210090970d","english":"pack light","ipa":"","chinese":"轻装出行","usage":"If you must fly, be sure to pack light to cut down the plane's load.  \n如果你必须坐飞机，一定要轻装上阵，减少飞机的载重。"},{"id":"0979c15c-95a1-4cde-aa65-e5870ae076c8","english":"airline","ipa":"/ˈeəlaɪn/","chinese":"n. 航空公司","usage":"1. international airlines\n国际航空公司\n2. an airline pilot\n航空公司飞机驾驶员"},{"id":"848459d1-a74a-425c-8cfc-b68b51724249","english":"checked-in baggage","ipa":"","chinese":"托运行李","usage":"Your checked-in baggage will be tagged to your final destination.  \n您的托运行李将被标记为您的最终目的地。"},{"id":"2341c081-29d7-42d4-b859-fd6ad15bc0f0","english":"carry-on","ipa":"/'kæriɔn/","chinese":"n. （可随身携带上飞机的）小包，小行李箱","usage":"1. Only one carry-on is allowed.\n随身只能携带一个小包。\n2. carry-on baggage\n随身携带的行李"},{"id":"13048f38-a0ce-4b4e-9330-d9126438b07f","english":"somewhere in between","ipa":"","chinese":"介于两者之间","usage":"Does the truth lie somewhere in between?  \n真相会不会就在这两者之间？"},{"id":"fa9ad62c-1fe1-419e-a883-bb877070cf16","english":"baggage drop","ipa":"","chinese":"行李托运","usage":""},{"id":"c810214f-64cd-4dcc-a0fc-61e6e943ac6e","english":"go straight through","ipa":"","chinese":"径直通过","usage":"This train goes straight through to New York\n这班火车直达纽约。"},{"id":"5c6725be-228a-4892-b6a3-ce89eddb6174","english":"security","ipa":"/sɪˈkjʊərəti/","chinese":"n. 保护措施；安全工作","usage":"Security Check 安全检查"},{"id":"e6ff4970-f96b-4d21-b8ea-369266ecad5e","english":"drop off","ipa":"","chinese":"放下","usage":"Anonymously dropped off at the front desk.\n有人匿名放在了前台。"},{"id":"feba470e-10a1-4a50-8f73-31d5aa31c002","english":"there's truly no going back","ipa":"","chinese":"没有退路 ; 无法回头","usage":"We said we would do it—there can be no turning back.\n我们说过要干这事，不能反悔。"}]},{"day":99,"title":"英语积累Day 99","topic":"生活方式","author":"Birta Hlin","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/7118bb0d2d864a318fa8f2adb2ee3386","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JP8JP8oZ1zw","audioSize":"578.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-099.m4a","youtubeId":"JP8JP8oZ1zw","chinese":"我打算化个妆，然后出去找一家不错的早餐店。我真的很想喝点好咖啡，我觉得自己对咖啡有点上瘾了。倒不是因为我需要提神，我甚至都察觉不到咖啡能让我精力提升。更多是因为喝咖啡的感觉太惬意了，就像每天早上来一杯咖啡，你会对此有所期待。但我有些怀疑我对咖啡上瘾了，因为我甚至在酒店房间都要冲速溶咖啡。","english":"I am gonna throw on some makeup, and then I guess I'm gonna go out and try and find a nice breakfast spot. I am really craving some good coffee. I feel like I'm becoming a bit more addicted to coffee. It's not that I need the energy boost. I don't really even notice that it gives me any energy boosts. It's more the fact that it's just so cozy. Like having a morning coffee, you have something to be excited about. But I've had some suspicion that I might be addicted to coffee from the fact that I actually make instant coffee at hotel rooms.","sentences":["I am gonna throw on some makeup, and then I guess I'm gonna go out and try and find a nice breakfast spot.","I am really craving some good coffee.","I feel like I'm becoming a bit more addicted to coffee.","It's not that I need the energy boost.","I don't really even notice that it gives me any energy boosts.","It's more the fact that it's just so cozy.","Like having a morning coffee, you have something to be excited about.","But I've had some suspicion that I might be addicted to coffee from the fact that I actually make instant coffee at hotel rooms."],"exercise":"I am gonna 化个妆, and then I guess I'm gonna go out and try and find a nice 早餐店. I am really 很想 some good coffee. I feel like I'm becoming a bit more 上瘾了 coffee. It's not that I 需要提神. I don't really even notice that it 让我提升精力. 更多是因为 it's just so cozy. Like having a morning coffee, you have something to be excited about. But I've 有些怀疑 that I might 上瘾 coffee 因为 I actually 冲速溶咖啡 at hotel rooms.","vocabulary":[{"id":"61ca930d-1224-4617-9925-2a92dfd7f93f","english":"throw on makeup","ipa":"","chinese":"化妆","usage":""},{"id":"967f2312-e3a6-42ce-819e-6e38155b63ec","english":"breakfast spot","ipa":"","chinese":"早餐店","usage":"We always go to the same breakfast spot so let me take you there.\n我们总是去同一家早餐店，我带你去吧。"},{"id":"28337563-1063-4621-948c-4d817b9c1ed8","english":"crave","ipa":"/kreɪv/","chinese":"v. 渴望","usage":"She has always craved excitement.\n她总盼望得到刺激。"},{"id":"681be5f1-bd0b-4d5b-887d-71cb1b4d9232","english":"be addicted to","ipa":"","chinese":"对…上瘾；沉溺于","usage":"I was addicted to reading and writing poetry.\n我沉迷于阅读和写诗。"},{"id":"d08fab7b-6ef5-464b-bfd1-6a38d2ea2d16","english":"energy boost","ipa":"","chinese":"能量提升：指通过某种方式增加身体或精神的能量水平，以提高活力","usage":"Of course, sugary food tastes nice, it can help lift our mood, and the glucose in it can give us an energy boost.当然，含糖食物味道不错， 可以帮助我们提神，其中的葡萄糖可以让我们精力充沛。"},{"id":"7bfb821b-eec0-46d5-ab79-bd4ac04ed352","english":"It's more the fact that","ipa":"","chinese":"更重要的是","usage":""},{"id":"22dd1fec-e1ba-4176-95ed-2158b47fd151","english":"have some suspicion","ipa":"","chinese":"有些怀疑","usage":"However, in recent years, the public have an increasing suspicion of specialists' opinions.\n但是最近几年，公众对专家的意见产生了越来越多的怀疑。"},{"id":"12b11b70-56cd-4c72-a6c7-55c4e57ad4cd","english":"suspicion","ipa":"/səˈspɪʃn/","chinese":"n. 怀疑；嫌疑","usage":"I have a sneaking suspicion that she's not telling the truth.\n我暗自怀疑她没讲实话。"},{"id":"d2f16d08-80bd-468f-8b3c-d6067e3ce7b5","english":"instant coffee","ipa":"","chinese":"速溶咖啡","usage":"He spooned instant coffee into two of the mugs.  \n他用勺把速溶咖啡舀进了两个杯子里。"}]},{"day":100,"title":"英语积累Day 100","topic":"生活方式,旅行","author":"Elena Taber","accent":"美音","period":"51-100期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/3b42dce3ce514ae0b14e60d21ce44795","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3TclNeETcso","audioSize":"580.8KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-100.m4a","youtubeId":"3TclNeETcso","chinese":"我收拾行李的秘诀是使用收纳袋。这些是我的背心和睡衣。我总是尽量把所有衣物都卷得整整齐齐：连衣裙、运动服、罩衫、内衣，并把它们分门别类地收纳好，这对长期旅行非常有帮助。在另一边，我放了两个包和这次旅行的鞋子，有乐福鞋和跑鞋、沙滩拖鞋、晚上穿的小高跟鞋，还有一双适合走路的凉鞋。接下来我要向你们展示一下我是多么有条理。","english":"My key to packing is packing cubes. These are my tank tops and pajamas. Everything else I always try to roll as neatly as possible: dresses, workout clothes, cover-ups, undergarments, and having it sectioned off is such a game changer when you're traveling for long periods of time. And then on this side, we have two purses, my shoes for the trip, which are loafers, pair of running sneakers, little beachy slides, little heels for a night out, as well as a pair of walking sandals. And I'm gonna reveal to you guys how type A I can truly be.","sentences":["My key to packing is packing cubes.","These are my tank tops and pajamas.","Everything else I always try to roll as neatly as possible: dresses, workout clothes, cover-ups, undergarments, and having it sectioned off is such a game changer when you're traveling for long periods of time.","And then on this side, we have two purses, my shoes for the trip, which are loafers, pair of running sneakers, little beachy slides, little heels for a night out, as well as a pair of walking sandals.","And I'm gonna reveal to you guys how type A I can truly be."],"exercise":"My key to packing is 收纳袋. These are my 背心 and 睡衣. Everything else I always try to roll as neatly as possible: dresses, 运动服, 罩衫, 内衣, and 把它们分门别类地收纳好 is 非常有帮助 when you're traveling for long periods of time. And then on this side, we have two purses, my shoes for the trip, which are 乐福鞋, pair of  跑鞋, little 沙滩拖鞋, little heels for a night out, as well as a pair of walking 凉鞋. And I'm gonna reveal to you guys how 有条理 I can truly be.","vocabulary":[{"id":"14863f97-12b3-43db-9be3-50935438c27b","english":"packing cube","ipa":"","chinese":"旅行收纳包","usage":""},{"id":"8cd92eea-eb2c-4673-ad60-1f97b84ed935","english":"tank top","ipa":"","chinese":"背心","usage":""},{"id":"c2c17783-9318-42be-a5ec-770e9471454b","english":"pajama","ipa":"/pə'dʒɑ:mə/","chinese":"n. 睡衣","usage":"pyjama bottoms\n睡裤"},{"id":"7c85f0e3-f991-40f8-a3ff-fd35fee5bd40","english":"workout clothes","ipa":"","chinese":"运动服","usage":"So my 2-minute rule was putting on my workout clothes and stretching.\n所以我的“两分钟规则”就是穿上运动服做拉伸运动。"},{"id":"16cb8fa2-9207-4b58-8161-7e679615c4b3","english":"cover-ups","ipa":"","chinese":"穿在泳装外面的一件罩衫","usage":""},{"id":"50c90925-5d67-4ce1-8f66-51e94c3c0698","english":"undergarment","ipa":"/'ʌndəgɑːm(ə)nt/","chinese":"n. 内衣","usage":"Undergarments, t-shirt, and shorts, usually, and I barely wear a shirt when I'm there, or try not to.\n通常是内衣、T 恤和短裤，我在那里的时候几乎不穿衬衫，或者尽量不穿。"},{"id":"41215934-9e68-4f51-a5c3-5eee91d571b5","english":"section off","ipa":"","chinese":"隔出；划出","usage":"Parts of the town had been sectioned off.\n城市的部分地区被划了出去。"},{"id":"95954ed2-9570-4fb4-a78a-f555f2ae6067","english":"game changer","ipa":"","chinese":"游戏规则改变者（指彻底改变事态发展的人、理念或事件）","usage":"And, you know, technology is really a game changer, I think, in urbanisation.\n我觉得科技在城市化中处于力挽狂澜的角色。"},{"id":"d66d95ff-6742-42de-9932-84618e88f0e7","english":"loafer","ipa":"/'ləʊfə/","chinese":"n.  平底便鞋；乐福鞋","usage":"Sorry. You and he have the same loafers.\n抱歉，你跟他穿了同款乐福鞋。"},{"id":"804dee7c-294e-4e28-9aaa-7595e5826fd1","english":"running sneakers","ipa":"","chinese":"跑鞋","usage":""},{"id":"3a311031-adb8-431c-943d-aef3faebf96a","english":"sneaker","ipa":"/'sniːkə/","chinese":"n. 运动鞋；便鞋","usage":"He wore old jeans and a pair of sneakers.\n他穿一条旧牛仔裤，脚蹬运动鞋。"},{"id":"c61289f3-13b6-4b67-b846-e9ca5532eb06","english":"slides","ipa":"","chinese":"n. 能外穿的拖鞋","usage":""},{"id":"5afffef3-b8f8-439d-9c4f-8c1633af58df","english":"sandals","ipa":"/sændlz/","chinese":"n. 凉鞋","usage":"Yes, it's just sandals for you and sports trainers for me.\n是的，你只穿凉鞋，我只穿运动鞋。"},{"id":"2e05599b-b21b-479a-8841-9b8e8732156c","english":"type A","ipa":"","chinese":"type A personality A型人格","usage":"The hypothesis describes Type A individuals as outgoing(外向), ambitious(有野心), rigidly organized(有严谨的条理), highly status-conscious(高度重视地位), impatient(急躁), anxious(焦虑), proactive(积极主动), and concerned with time management(注重时间管理). People with Type A personalities are often high-achieving workaholics(工作狂).\n\nA型人格其实是指一种特定的行为模式，而不是个体的整个人格面貌。这种行为模式最早在20世纪50年代末期，由迈耶·弗里德曼(Meyer Friedman)和瑞·罗森曼(Ray Rosenman)两位心脏病学家首次提出。这种被称为A型行为的模式包括如下特征：\n（1）一种要达到个人目的的强烈而持久的内驱力；\n（2）在所有情况下都有一种热衷于竞争的倾向；\n（3）一种想得到别人的承认和不断超越自我的持久的欲望；\n（4）不断卷入有最后期限的事务之中；\n（5）习惯于风风火火地完成各种活动；\n（6）心理和生理上的过分敏感。"}]},{"day":101,"title":"英语积累Day 101","topic":"生活方式","author":"Sanne Vloet","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/a646bbb6e03f40ab803c130d826df629","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W1LDbwqN1X4&t=2s","audioSize":"498.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-101.m4a","youtubeId":"W1LDbwqN1X4","chinese":"锻炼前，我会先快速补充水分。随着秋天天气转凉，我感觉周围的人都在生病。上周我也有点流鼻涕。让我们开始运动吧。在做任何运动前，我都会先用泡沫轴拉伸。我很清楚自己的痛点在哪里。这样做有助于让我的身体更协调，这样在之后的训练中，我能够调用正确的肌肉，还能消除肌肉结块和紧张感，所以这对身体恢复非常有帮助。","english":"Before I work out, I'm quickly hydrating myself. I have been feeling like everyone around me is getting sick with the fall weathers. I had a little bit of sniffles too last week. Let's go. Before I do anything, I will always grab my foam roller and stretch. I actually have a few videos on my app as well, but I have been doing this for so long that I know exactly where my pain points are. It really helps align my body, so when I do the training after, I'm actually able to activate the right muscles, and it also gets rid of any knots and tension I have, so it's amazing for recovery.","sentences":["Before I work out, I'm quickly hydrating myself.","I have been feeling like everyone around me is getting sick with the fall weathers.","I had a little bit of sniffles too last week.","Let's go.","Before I do anything, I will always grab my foam roller and stretch.","I actually have a few videos on my app as well, but I have been doing this for so long that I know exactly where my pain points are.","It really helps align my body, so when I do the training after, I'm actually able to activate the right muscles, and it also gets rid of any knots and tension I have, so it's amazing for recovery."],"exercise":"Before I 锻炼, I'm quickly 补充水分 myself. I have been feeling like everyone around me is getting sick with the fall weathers. I had a little bit of 流鼻涕 too last week. Let's go. Before I do anything, I will always 用泡沫轴拉伸. I actually have a few videos on my app as well, but I have been doing this for so long that I know exactly 痛点在哪里. It really helps 身体更协调, so when I do the training after, I'm actually able to 调用 the right muscles, and it also gets rid of any 肌肉结块和紧张感 I have, so it's amazing for 身体恢复.","vocabulary":[{"id":"8a4d1210-bd72-4c3a-b690-88e51f9bbda0","english":"work out","ipa":"","chinese":"锻炼身体；做运动","usage":"I work out regularly to keep fit.\n我经常做运动以保持健康。"},{"id":"ce3a2497-b16e-4ca7-9912-8dc42d629967","english":"hydrate","ipa":"/haɪˈdreɪt/","chinese":"v. 使吸入水分","usage":"He's got diarrhea, so we're hydrating him.\n他腹泻 所以我们要给他补水"},{"id":"5050112c-42f9-401a-867f-b2084b4ad068","english":"sniffle","ipa":"/'snɪf(ə)l/","chinese":"v. （尤指因哭泣或患感冒）抽鼻子","usage":"get, have, etc. the ˈsniffles 患轻感冒"},{"id":"fda016dd-41bf-4c10-bb8c-d6908dd1260b","english":"foam roller","ipa":"","chinese":"泡沫轴","usage":"Using a foam roller is simple, but working some areas may take a bit of practice and some body contortion. You start by finding a relatively open area with some floor space. \n使用泡沫轴很简单，但是要让它对身体一些部位的起到锻炼作用还需要一些练习和身体的柔韧性。"},{"id":"f9205eb8-4718-4533-801f-7080636a6907","english":"stretch","ipa":"/stretʃ/","chinese":"v. 伸展；舒展","usage":"The exercises are designed to stretch and tone your leg muscles.\n这些活动目的在于伸展和增强你的腿部肌肉。"},{"id":"0cda3f8e-d68f-4baf-8d1e-40847e7f5750","english":"pain point","ipa":"","chinese":"痛点","usage":"For example, we're better at detecting the two pain points on the shoulders than at the wrists.\n比如，我们对肩部两点的疼痛感知会比手腕附近的两点要更灵敏。"},{"id":"f4b8897a-20b1-4a1b-9c84-c52680ef47a2","english":"body alignment","ipa":"","chinese":"舞蹈用词：身体对齐，身体正位","usage":"主要体现在三个方面：\n1.肌肉的调动顺序\n2.肌肉能力的动态和谐\n3.原动肌和拮抗肌的制衡"},{"id":"7c4f81cd-12d8-4659-999f-ee9c1d6ef2a7","english":"align","ipa":"/əˈlaɪn/","chinese":"v. 排列整齐；使对齐；（尤指）成一直线","usage":"Make sure the shelf is aligned with the top of the cupboard.\n务必使搁架与橱柜顶端靠齐。"},{"id":"43c9814d-469c-4202-89fe-9bbb49937e50","english":"activate","ipa":"/ˈæktɪveɪt/","chinese":"v. 使活动；激活；","usage":"1. The burglar alarm is activated by movement.\n这防盗警报器一动就会响。\n2. The gene is activated by a specific protein.\n这种基因由一种特异性蛋白激活。"},{"id":"14fe7120-a09e-41f9-9387-9122e7472b03","english":"knot","ipa":"/nɒt/","chinese":"n. （由紧张、恼怒等引起的胃、喉等的）痉挛，郁结，哽咽，哽塞","usage":"His forehead knotted in a frown.\n他眉头紧锁。"},{"id":"c5bc2f5c-625e-44c6-9d5c-5150a842bca1","english":"tension","ipa":"/ˈtenʃn/","chinese":"n. 拉伸；张力；拉紧状态；绷紧程度","usage":"The elimination of neck tension can relieve headaches.消除颈部的压力可以减轻头痛。"},{"id":"1ca1de04-e30e-4aa0-a59c-488a7d1def5a","english":"recovery","ipa":"/rɪˈkʌvəri/","chinese":"n. 恢复","usage":"to make a remarkable/quick/speedy/slow, etc. recovery\n恢复显著、很快、迅速、缓慢等"}]},{"day":102,"title":"英语积累Day 102","topic":"生活方式","author":"Elena Taber","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/c6d6a217e332496091d07234cae24da7","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W1LDbwqN1X4&t=2s","audioSize":"662.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-102.m4a","youtubeId":"W1LDbwqN1X4","chinese":"最近几个月，我的睡眠质量前所未有的好，感觉压力在慢慢消退。我认为这个地方的特别之处还在于周围质朴的自然环境。阳光穿过这些美丽的树木，鸟叫声此起彼伏，你还可以闻到玫瑰和茉莉的芳香。这里的活动选择不多，有一种宁静的氛围。就像回到了童年的夏天，除了工作之外，就是骑自行车、读书、玩游戏、远足、探索森林。我很想就这样过上一两个月，一边远程工作，一边体验这种不同的生活方式。","english":"I've been sleeping better than I have in months and just feel the stress leaving my body. I think what’s so special about it is you’re so surrounded by a simple kind of nature. These beautiful trees, light falling through, the constant sound of birds, and you can smell like the roses and jasmine. There's this kind of peace that with almost having so few options of what to do. It's almost like being a kid in summer again where outside of work, it's bike rides, reading books, playing games, going for long walks, and exploring forests. I would love to do this for a full month or two, and just work remote(ly) and kind of experiencing this different style of living.","sentences":["I've been sleeping better than I have in months and just feel the stress leaving my body.","I think what’s so special about it is you’re so surrounded by a simple kind of nature.","These beautiful trees, light falling through, the constant sound of birds, and you can smell like the roses and jasmine.","There's this kind of peace that with almost having so few options of what to do.","It's almost like being a kid in summer again where outside of work, it's bike rides, reading books, playing games, going for long walks, and exploring forests.","I would love to do this for a full month or two, and just work remote(ly) and kind of experiencing this different style of living."],"exercise":"最近几个月，我的睡眠质量前所未有的好 and just feel 压力在慢慢消退. What makes this place so special is the simple kind of nature surrounding us. There are beautiful trees 阳光透过树叶洒下来，鸟叫声此起彼伏, and the air 弥漫着玫瑰和茉莉的芳香. There's a peace that 因而 having so few 选择 of what to do. It's almost like 回到了童年的夏天—除了 work, it's bike rides, reading books, playing games, going for long walks, and exploring forests. I would love to do this for a full month or two, 远程工作 and experiencing this different style of living.","vocabulary":[{"id":"eb2e417e-4cb0-4eee-b2a0-718f58952ea0","english":"constant","ipa":"/ˈkɒnstənt/","chinese":"a. 连续发生的；不断的；重复的","usage":"a constant stream of visitors all day\n整天络绎不绝的游客"},{"id":"f127d69b-d8e0-45ee-a215-5be340eee4b3","english":"jasmine","ipa":"/'dʒæzmɪn/","chinese":"n. 茉莉","usage":"a spray of jasmine was twined in her hair.\n她头发上编着茉莉。"},{"id":"2bc0789c-22c8-4c99-9a1a-169db95d4f5f","english":"option","ipa":"/ˈɒpʃn/","chinese":"n. 可选择的事物；选择；","usage":"There are various options open to you.\n你有多种选择。"},{"id":"89ed62cd-b27b-4926-b869-3ea76021eded","english":"outside of","ipa":"","chinese":"除…之外","usage":"Outside of love, the best thing you can give a child is attention. \n除了爱，你能给予孩子的最好的东西就是关心。"},{"id":"a085dfa5-add7-4901-ad2c-20921ec8a9bb","english":"remote work/ work remotely","ipa":"","chinese":"远程工作","usage":"The pandemic and remote work gave us that flexibility.\n疫情和远程工作为我们提供了这种灵活性。"}]},{"day":103,"title":"英语积累Day 103","topic":"生活方式","author":"Holly B Fitness","accent":"英音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/5d6b6b38021547c29fb624142871066b","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nw0_p5Pp5HI","audioSize":"408.5KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-103.m4a","youtubeId":"nw0_p5Pp5HI","chinese":"最近总感觉有些不对劲，但我不喜欢依赖“天哪，我在水逆”这样的说法，因为我感觉一旦你知道这些，就会立刻想“好吧，接下来几周会过得很糟糕”。过去大约六周里，我感觉自己一直在按部就班地生活，机械地应付每一天。总感觉事情有些不太对劲。不过，现在感觉我已经安定下来了，准备重新投身于我的目标并专注于实现它们。","english":"Something has just been in the air, and I don't like to lean into things like, \"Oh my God, Mercury's in retrograde,\" because I feel like if you see those things, you just immediately like, \"Oh well, I'm gonna have a bad few weeks.\" For the past, potentially like, six weeks, I just feel like I've kind of been on autopilot, going through the motions. I just kind of feel like something hasn't really been clicking. However, I do now feel like I'm settled. I feel like I'm ready to get back to my goals, I’m really kind of like tunnel vision in on them.","sentences":["Something has just been in the air, and I don't like to lean into things like, \"Oh my God, Mercury's in retrograde,\" because I feel like if you see those things, you just immediately like, \"Oh well, I'm gonna have a bad few weeks.\"","For the past, potentially like, six weeks, I just feel like I've kind of been on autopilot, going through the motions.","I just kind of feel like something hasn't really been clicking.","However, I do now feel like I'm settled.","I feel like I'm ready to get back to my goals, I’m really kind of like tunnel vision in on them."],"exercise":"最近总感觉有些不对劲, and I don't like to 依赖 things like, \"Oh my God, 我在水逆,\" because I feel like if you see those things, you just immediately like, \"Oh well, I'm gonna have a bad few weeks.\" For the past, 大约 like, six weeks, I just feel like I've kind of 按部就班地生活, 机械地应付每一天. I just kind of feel like something 不太对劲. However, I do now feel like I'm 安定下来. I feel like I'm ready to 重新投身于 my goals, I’m really kind of like 专注于 on them.","vocabulary":[{"id":"2932e67e-74cd-4699-ab12-e9ed671a14cd","english":"in the air","ipa":"","chinese":"在传播中；流行；可感觉到","usage":"There's romance in the air.\n有种浪漫的气氛。"},{"id":"8eaa32fc-b563-4168-af2c-12976b0118d8","english":"lean","ipa":"","chinese":"vi. 倾斜；倚靠；倾向；依赖","usage":"I now lean towards sabotage as the cause of the crash.\n我现在倾向于认为坠机原因是蓄意破坏。"},{"id":"0aa2b769-12b6-49e3-9176-8e16ec4e560f","english":"Mercury Retrograde","ipa":"","chinese":"“水逆”，即“水星逆行”","usage":"是指占星学上的水星逆行导致运势低迷的情况。虽说信则有不信则无，当遇事不顺、运气不佳的时候，“水逆”一词就逐渐成为了当代人情绪的调节剂。\nDon’t start anything when Mercury is retrograde. 水逆时不要开始任何事。"},{"id":"a4a93571-e3da-40a5-89cf-325aa55e4d1f","english":"potentially","ipa":"/pəˈtenʃəlɪ/","chinese":"adv. 潜在地;可能地","usage":"All polling methods are potentially open to abuse.\n所有的民意调查方法都有可能被滥用。"},{"id":"a81b620b-3e2d-46d6-b7c3-c01d20a6e942","english":"be on autopilot","ipa":"","chinese":"做某件事没有专注，也没有思考，好像无人机的驾驶模式，随着无意识或潜意识模式而动。\n无脑（不用太多的脑力劳动）、机械性的状态。可以形容某种习惯累积而有的潜意识行为","usage":"I was supposed to pick up my niece but instead heading to workplace when I drived on autopilot\n 我本来要去接侄女，但一开车就不由自主地习惯性往公司去。"},{"id":"5448b2d2-d5b9-4bc2-ad0b-70add51e7cdb","english":"go through the motions","ipa":"","chinese":"敷衍了事；走过场；装样子","usage":"I was simply going through the motions, without direction nor a purpose.   \n我只是完任务，没有方向和目标"},{"id":"466a8bdc-e01d-46b9-85a4-19faad7e8b73","english":"something hasn't really been clicking","ipa":"","chinese":"有些事情不太对劲。","usage":""},{"id":"dd3ffdc8-0b4d-4eb9-981e-588d3a393228","english":"click","ipa":"/klɪk/","chinese":"vi.  配合默契；运作协调","usage":"The team don't seem to have clicked yet.\n这支队伍好像还没有配合默契。"},{"id":"73f39877-4946-422f-a886-893a87f02532","english":"be settled","ipa":"","chinese":"(最终)决定,确定,安排好","usage":"It's all settled —we're leaving on the nine o'clock plane.\n一切都定下来了——我们乘九点的航班走。"},{"id":"e8f48473-c1d7-4682-ad05-5dae7f1e67d2","english":"get back to","ipa":"","chinese":"回到…","usage":"Anyhow, I'd better get back to work.\n好了，我得回去工作了。"},{"id":"19b51600-7452-4a95-bc48-a78351dafbc5","english":"tunnel vision","ipa":"","chinese":"“隧道视觉”。这是指在隧道中驾驶时，驾驶员的视觉区域被大幅度缩小到前方的狭小空间上。\n可指极度专注于一件事或一件事的一部分。","usage":""}]},{"day":104,"title":"英语积累Day 104","topic":"生活方式","author":"Faye Bate","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/7d9b86d2b7794a63b8192ac1f215b679","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ytgQBifuZbw","audioSize":"699.8KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-104.m4a","youtubeId":"ytgQBifuZbw","chinese":"近几年，注意力缺陷多动障碍（ADHD）受到了媒体的广泛关注。对我来说，替身策略是一根救命稻草。ADHD患者会采用这种策略，即在别人的陪伴下完成任务，从而保持专注。我不确定这一策略是否已经被科学完全证实，但我个人推测，只要有别人在场，我就会得到某种刺激。另一个推测是，人类的思维方式其实非常简单。我觉得替身策略可能迎合了我们希望在别人面前表现得好的需求。因此不论如何，这绝对是我这几年应对ADHD的神级策略。","english":"ADHD has seen a lot of media coverage over the past few years. Body doubling is a lifesaver for me. Body doubling is a strategy implemented by people with ADHD to ancrhor them to a task where they complete the task alongside someone else. I'm not sure if the science is completely understood. But My personal hypothesis is that I get a certain element of stimulation from just being in the presence of someone else. Another hypothesis I have is that as human beings, we're very simple-minded. I think maybe body doubling is pandering to our need to feel like we look good in front of other people. So anyway, body doubling is just an absolute god-tier strategy that I've had in my ADHD toolkit for the past few years.","sentences":["ADHD has seen a lot of media coverage over the past few years.","Body doubling is a lifesaver for me.","Body doubling is a strategy implemented by people with ADHD to ancrhor them to a task where they complete the task alongside someone else.","I'm not sure if the science is completely understood.","But My personal hypothesis is that I get a certain element of stimulation from just being in the presence of someone else.","Another hypothesis I have is that as human beings, we're very simple-minded.","I think maybe body doubling is pandering to our need to feel like we look good in front of other people.","So anyway, body doubling is just an absolute god-tier strategy that I've had in my ADHD toolkit for the past few years."],"exercise":"注意力缺陷多动障碍 has 受到了媒体的广泛关注 over the past few years. 替身策略 is a 救命稻草 for me. Body doubling is a strategy 采用 people with ADHD to 保持专注 a task where they complete the task alongside someone else. I'm not sure 这一策略是否已经被科学完全证实. But My personal 推测 is that I get a 某种刺激 from just 在场 someone else. Another hypothesis I have is that as human beings, we're very 思维方式（其实）非常简单. I think maybe body doubling is 迎合 our need to feel like we look good in front of other people. So anyway, body doubling is just an absolute 神级 strategy that I've had 应对ADHD for the past few years.","vocabulary":[{"id":"fcdd8e04-ea24-417d-8b27-3985a5001969","english":"ADHD-Attention-Deficit/Hyperactivity Disorder","ipa":"","chinese":"注意缺陷多动障碍：一种常见的神经发育障碍，会影响患者的注意力、记忆、决策等能力，导致他们出现注意力不集中、多动和冲动等行为和情绪问题。\nADHD有两个亚型，一个是注意力缺陷，表现为无法控制注意力，另一个则是无法控制行为和情绪，就是多动。","usage":""},{"id":"1804e865-b695-4131-b5ce-a56f810ae23c","english":"media coverage","ipa":"","chinese":"媒体报道","usage":"She said she never expected her research to get media coverage.\n她表示，没想到媒体会报道自己的研究成果"},{"id":"90cfdca4-a5ce-4016-8405-ff6f0b9e6063","english":"Body doubling","ipa":"","chinese":"身体替身：源于对注意力缺陷/多动障碍患者的临床治疗。指的是和朋友做一项需要集中注意力的任务，让自身保持专注。","usage":""},{"id":"7cc85dcd-09bd-467b-9746-e707f1afdce6","english":"lifesaver","ipa":"/'laɪfseɪvə(r)/","chinese":"n. 救命稻草，救助物；救命物","usage":"So travel insurance can be a lifesaver.\n旅行保险可以成为救命稻草。"},{"id":"0cfaebd1-6816-4953-89c1-620af4b3e3f2","english":"implement","ipa":"/ˈɪmplɪment/","chinese":"v. 执行；实施","usage":"to implement changes/decisions/policies/reforms\n实行变革；执行决议/政策；实施改革"},{"id":"50f29828-a209-43b0-8c64-42523b948475","english":"anchor to","ipa":"/ˈæŋkə(r)/","chinese":"锚定","usage":"The child seat belt was not properly anchored to the car. \n儿童坐椅的安全带并未在车上固定到位。"},{"id":"548594d2-0b14-42f0-a038-8b84e4bad119","english":"hypothesis","ipa":"/haɪˈpɒθəsɪs/","chinese":"n. （凭空的）猜想，猜测","usage":"It would be pointless to engage in hypothesis before we have the facts.\n在我们还没掌握事实之前瞎猜是毫无意义的。"},{"id":"22a9a6ed-3a4a-4c7c-987b-1b781437d032","english":"certain","ipa":"/ˈsɜːtn/","chinese":"a. （不提及细节时用）某事，某人，某种","usage":"For certain personal reasons I shall not be able to attend.\n由于某种个人原因，我将不能出席。"},{"id":"38ffa1ab-4a97-4bd7-b164-db8418d9c03f","english":"stimulation","ipa":"/ˌstɪmjuˈleɪʃn/","chinese":"n. 刺激","usage":"sensory/intellectual/sexual/visual/physical stimulation\n感官/智力/性/视觉/身体刺激"},{"id":"f6cd59df-329e-47b7-913e-c6245413aba1","english":"be in the presence of","ipa":"","chinese":"在…面前","usage":"You no longer needed to be there in the presence of the medium.\n你不再需要出现在媒体面前。"},{"id":"545edbe5-3daf-464c-b7a0-741ea43c2836","english":"simple-minded","ipa":"/ˌsimpl'maindid/","chinese":"a. 头脑简单的","usage":"1. a simple-minded person\n头脑简单的人\n2. a simple-minded approach\n笨方法"},{"id":"9291b9b2-0584-4da9-8ced-4f861f5577e3","english":"pander to","ipa":"/ˈpændə(r)/","chinese":"迎合；奉迎；投其所好","usage":"books which don't pander to popular taste\n不迎合大众口味的书"},{"id":"53ea41de-2f4b-4dc4-adb1-bda25d29baf4","english":"god-tier","ipa":"","chinese":"神级","usage":""},{"id":"50abbed7-043d-46d2-b9c6-0f4202dcd80f","english":"tier","ipa":"/tɪə/","chinese":"n.  阶层；等级","usage":"a two-tier system of management\n两级管理制"},{"id":"611698bf-0223-469d-ba9d-45491eaf3b7b","english":"toolkit","ipa":"/'tulkɪt/","chinese":"n. 一套工具；工具箱；工具包","usage":"And in fact was a toolkit for focus.\n事实上，这是一个集中注意力的工具包。"}]},{"day":105,"title":"英语积累Day 105","topic":"生活方式","author":"Ellen Miller","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/a68bc2e863e74b9489934804c69fbc7d","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Jr4OvHN_frc&t=1s","audioSize":"489.0KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-105.m4a","youtubeId":"Jr4OvHN_frc","chinese":"我是周二感冒的，现在是周六。所以今天是感冒的第五天。这次感冒很严重，我原以为它会持续几周。每当生病时，我都尽量放一些轻松愉快的节目，让身体充满快乐的荷尔蒙，以此来欺骗身体，让它感觉比实际情况好一些。今晚我要早早上床睡觉，优先保证睡眠是非常重要的。没有什么比让身体得到充分休息更重要的了，这样它才能在感觉不佳时更好地恢复。","english":"My cold hit on Tuesday, and it's now Saturday for me. So, this is day five. My cold was so bad, I really thought that it was gonna be one to stick around for a couple of weeks. I always try and put on something light-hearted when I'm feeling sick to help flood my body with happy hormones to trick my body into feeling better than it actually is. Tonight, I'm gonna go to bed super early, and prioritizing your sleep is so important. There's nothing more important than giving your body plenty of rest in order for it to recuperate while it's not feeling its best.","sentences":["My cold hit on Tuesday, and it's now Saturday for me.","So, this is day five.","My cold was so bad, I really thought that it was gonna be one to stick around for a couple of weeks.","I always try and put on something light-hearted when I'm feeling sick to help flood my body with happy hormones to trick my body into feeling better than it actually is.","Tonight, I'm gonna go to bed super early, and prioritizing your sleep is so important.","There's nothing more important than giving your body plenty of rest in order for it to recuperate while it's not feeling its best."],"exercise":"我是周二感冒的, and it's now Saturday for me. So, 第五天. My cold was so bad, I really thought that it was gonna be one to 持续几周. I always try and 放节目 something 轻松愉快的 when I'm feeling sick to help 让身体充满快乐的荷尔蒙 to 欺骗 feeling better than it actually is. Tonight, I'm gonna go to bed super early, and 优先保证 your sleep is so important. There's nothing more important than 让身体得到充分休息 in order for it to 恢复 while it's not feeling its best.","vocabulary":[{"id":"5aef7b84-8a70-4df0-b1cb-e6c65deb8dc7","english":"hit","ipa":"/hɪt/","chinese":"v. 产生不良影响；打击；危害","usage":"1. The tax increases will certainly hit the poor.\n增税肯定会加重穷人的负担。\n2. His death didn't really hit me at first.\n他的死起初并没有对我产生影响。"},{"id":"73da4048-8128-47a7-baba-dee3f2f1a58b","english":"stick around","ipa":"","chinese":"不走开；逗留, 停留","usage":"Stick around a while and see what develops.  \n稍呆一会儿，看看会发生什么。"},{"id":"d692c172-9a10-46de-9194-a151d4a29aef","english":"put on","ipa":"","chinese":"播放（磁带、CD、DVD 等）","usage":"Do you mind if I put some music on?\n我放点音乐你不介意吧？"},{"id":"bbb47bd5-934a-485e-9793-db7e30b8d775","english":"light-hearted","ipa":"/'lait'hɑ:tid/","chinese":"a.  轻松的；愉快的","usage":"a light-hearted speech\n轻松愉快的讲话"},{"id":"2998474c-ff1d-46fe-8555-2478bb4a6d50","english":"flood with","ipa":"","chinese":"淹没，充斥","usage":"Being frightened makes your brain flood with healthy chemical substances that excite your mood and release feelings of great excitement. \n受惊吓时会让你的大脑充满一些健康的化学物质，能刺激你情绪，让你十分兴奋。"},{"id":"03701ca2-6425-4fc0-ac58-2c47920d4379","english":"hormone","ipa":"/'hɔ:məun/","chinese":"n. 激素；荷尔蒙","usage":"1. growth hormones\n生长激素\n2. a hormone imbalance\n激素失调"},{"id":"ba421c1d-09cd-4faa-820c-d3421ca29773","english":"trick sb ˈinto sth/into doing sth","ipa":"","chinese":"骗…做某事","usage":"He tricked me into lending him £100.\n他骗我借给了他 100 英镑。"},{"id":"b113764a-04af-498c-b426-6d1ce48c0d6b","english":"prioritize","ipa":"/praiˈɔritaiz/","chinese":"v. 按重要性排列；划分优先顺序","usage":"You should make a list of all the jobs you have to do and prioritize them.\n你应该把所有要做的事都列出来，并按轻重缓急排个顺序。"},{"id":"97ed6992-b295-4bc8-b7a9-a48d46e40822","english":"recuperate","ipa":"/rɪˈkuːpəreɪt/","chinese":"v. 康复；恢复；恢复健康","usage":"He's still recuperating from his operation.\n他动了手术，还在恢复。"}]},{"day":106,"title":"英语积累Day 106","topic":"情感成长","author":"Dr Izzy Sealey 凯琦","accent":"英音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/e26b2100829a4525bed55d926a7004a4","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6RLdRauWegI","audioSize":"483.0KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-106.m4a","youtubeId":"6RLdRauWegI","chinese":"我去了洗手间，坐下来哭了一会儿，因为压力已经累积到让我感到不堪重负的地步。我不认为需要休息一下来处理自己的情绪，或者让情绪表露出来并充分感知情绪有什么可羞耻的。因为我意识到，一次又一次地压抑情绪实际上不是一种可持续的处理方式。工作中难免会犯错，我们会有做错事情的时候，但关键是要为此承担责任，并确保你已经尽全力去纠正错误。","english":"I went to the restroom, and I just sat down and honestly had a little bit of a cry because the levels of stress are just boiled up to the point where actually I felt overwhelmed. I don't think there’s any shame in having to take a break to deal with your emotions or let them come to the surface in that way and experience them fully because suppressing emotions over and over again is actually, I've realized, not a sustainable way to deal with them. Mistakes are going to happen at work, and you're going to get things wrong, but it's just about taking responsibility for that, being accountable for it, and making sure that you've done everything in your power to correct it.","sentences":["I went to the restroom, and I just sat down and honestly had a little bit of a cry because the levels of stress are just boiled up to the point where actually I felt overwhelmed.","I don't think there’s any shame in having to take a break to deal with your emotions or let them come to the surface in that way and experience them fully because suppressing emotions over and over again is actually, I've realized, not a sustainable way to deal with them.","Mistakes are going to happen at work, and you're going to get things wrong, but it's just about taking responsibility for that, being accountable for it, and making sure that you've done everything in your power to correct it."],"exercise":"I went to the restroom, and I just sat down and honestly had a little bit of a cry because the levels of stress are just 累积到 to the point where actually I 感到不堪重负. I don't think there’s any shame in having to take a break to deal with your emotions or 让情绪表露出来 in that way and 充分感知情绪 because 压抑情绪 over and over again is actually, I've realized, not 一种可持续的方式 to deal with them. 工作中难免会犯错, and you're going to get things wrong, but it's just about taking responsibility for that, being 承担责任 it, and making sure that you've 尽全力 to correct it.","vocabulary":[{"id":"28a7f59a-ad13-440e-84c7-a8369b435e69","english":"have a cry","ipa":"","chinese":"哭一场","usage":"It’s good to have a cry sometimes. 有时候哭一哭倒是有好处。"},{"id":"2ff05f36-2d9b-4738-8790-cb1bc9cc4c6e","english":"boil up","ipa":"/bɔɪl/","chinese":"（局势、情绪等）进入危急关头，令人担忧","usage":"I could feel anger boiling up inside me.\n我感到怒火中烧。"},{"id":"82a88ea3-1583-494d-ac7d-4fc9a5a59b41","english":"overwhelm","ipa":"/ˌəʊvəˈwelm/","chinese":"v. （感情或感觉）充溢，难以禁受","usage":"She was overwhelmed by feelings of guilt.\n她感到愧疚难当。"},{"id":"8086f78d-9ef2-48e0-b7a4-c186f3333c21","english":"shame","ipa":"/ʃeɪm/","chinese":"n. 羞耻；羞愧；惭愧","usage":"put to shame 使蒙羞；使自愧不如\nin shame 因为耻辱；因为害羞\nbring shame on 抹黑，使……蒙羞\nsense of shame 羞耻感\nwhat a shame 多可惜；真丢脸\nshame on you 你太无耻\nfor shame 真不害臊；不要脸\nsuch a shame 真羞耻"},{"id":"d853577c-936c-4503-b9cf-c540ca99530d","english":"take a break","ipa":"","chinese":"休息一下","usage":"Let's take a break. I need to freshen up.\n我们休息一会儿吧，我想调整一下。"},{"id":"7d9fd981-6353-489b-8ca5-a5f03287dbab","english":"come to the surface","ipa":"/'sɜːfɪs/","chinese":"1. 浮出水面：指从水下上升到水面，通常用于描述潜水员、鱼类或其他水生生物的行为。 \n2. 显露出来：指隐藏的事物或情感逐渐暴露出来，通常用于描述问题、情感或秘密等。","usage":"The bad news surfaced the day before.\n坏消息前天浮出水面。"},{"id":"8ae03f8c-2913-4c08-a398-f8dcc204e2c1","english":"suppress","ipa":"/səˈpres/","chinese":"v. 抑制；控制；忍住","usage":"1. to suppress a smile\n忍住没笑\n2. She was unable to suppress her anger.\n她按捺不住怒火。"},{"id":"f86e92b2-e796-4cc3-a093-0a7b8746885b","english":"sustainable","ipa":"/səˈsteɪnəbl/","chinese":"a. 可持续的","usage":"sustainable economic growth\n经济的可持续增长"},{"id":"271df050-5c48-49a7-8f88-03c27eef163a","english":"accountable for","ipa":"/əˈkaʊntəbl/","chinese":"对……负责","usage":"We need somebody accountable for this process.\n我们需要一个人对这个过程负责。"},{"id":"48c46e90-f9d8-4977-bc5b-fd7e9ed85744","english":"do everything in your power","ipa":"","chinese":"尽一切努力","usage":"When you're the new girl at work, you do everything in your power to stay on your best behavior. \n当你还是一名职场上的新人时，你在方方面面都尽力做到最好。"}]},{"day":107,"title":"英语积累Day 107","topic":"宠物","author":"Caroline Manning","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/bdd135f39628439587360df11630883f","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fQvZzBA7v0M","audioSize":"489.4KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-107.m4a","youtubeId":"fQvZzBA7v0M","chinese":"就是今天！我现在兴奋得不得了。我要带我可爱的宝贝回家了，它是一只小约克夏犬。简直不敢相信，从今天起，我的生活将发生改变。我现在有了照顾一个小生命的责任。在某种程度上，这让我有些紧张，但我也觉得我有种母性特质。我还是不敢相信，我真的要养一只狗了。今天我就要把它接回家，我的脑子还有点反应不过来。","english":"Today is the day! I am over the moon right now. I'm taking my sweet little baby home. It's a baby Yorkie. I just can't get over the fact that my life is about to change from this day forward. I now have a responsibility to take care of a mammal. In a way, it's kind of nerve-wracking, but I also feel like I just have a very maternal personality. I just cannot believe that I'm literally getting a dog. I'm taking him home today and I just don't think my brain can, like, wrap around that statement.","sentences":["Today is the day!","I am over the moon right now.","I'm taking my sweet little baby home.","It's a baby Yorkie.","I just can't get over the fact that my life is about to change from this day forward.","I now have a responsibility to take care of a mammal.","In a way, it's kind of nerve-wracking, but I also feel like I just have a very maternal personality.","I just cannot believe that I'm literally getting a dog.","I'm taking him home today and I just don't think my brain can, like, wrap around that statement."],"exercise":"Today is the day! I am 兴奋得不得了 right now. I'm taking my sweet little baby home. It's a baby 约克夏犬. I just can't 简直不敢相信 my life is about to change 从今天起. I now have a responsibility to take care of a mammal. 在某种程度上, it's 让我有些紧张, but I also feel like I just have a very 母性特质. I just cannot believe that I'm literally getting a dog. I'm taking him home today and 我的脑子还有点反应不过来.","vocabulary":[{"id":"2048792c-2b14-4574-b13a-a25cd7bae54b","english":"over the moon","ipa":"","chinese":"欣喜若狂","usage":"She was over the moon with her new bike.\n她骑着她的新自行车，喜出望外。"},{"id":"78076bd2-caae-4545-bcc3-ddfac07accd0","english":"Yorkie","ipa":"/jɔ:ki/","chinese":"n. 约克夏（狗狗品种）","usage":""},{"id":"733d45c6-6175-42be-a5a8-c6abe3a350a2","english":"get over","ipa":"","chinese":"接受某事","usage":"You need to get over the fact that he is married.\n你必须接受他已经结婚了的事实。"},{"id":"b04e7356-6f20-45b5-bbbd-8924dc5c42eb","english":"from this day forward","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 未来\n2. 从今天起","usage":"From this day forward the world is filled with endless possibilities.\n从今天起，世界充满无限可能。"},{"id":"c459d5d5-f287-4168-a1f1-e1a194042e92","english":"mammal","ipa":"/ˈmæml/","chinese":"n. 哺乳动物","usage":"The whale is the largest mammal in creation.\n鲸鱼是所有哺乳动物中最大的。"},{"id":"cc5489c2-c883-4b23-b90f-11d35fe0372f","english":"in a way","ipa":"","chinese":"在某种程度上；不完全地","usage":"In a way, I appreciated the directness. \n在某种程度上，我欣赏这种直率。"},{"id":"60fc13bf-6b4e-4774-a71e-ac0b7cc9ddc2","english":"nerve-wracking","ipa":"/'nə:v,rækiŋ/","chinese":"a. 令人十分紧张的；伤脑筋的","usage":"Blind dates can be so nerve wracking, you know. 你知道的，相亲真是让人伤脑筋。"},{"id":"bd1cc140-a92b-435e-bbc9-e8f40c90cbe3","english":"maternal","ipa":"/məˈtɜːnl/","chinese":"n. 母亲的；母亲般慈爱的","usage":"1. She didn't have any maternal instincts.\n她没有一点做母亲的天性。\n2. maternal love\n母爱"},{"id":"e0ccc018-2d7e-4481-ae4a-cde9cab09bc8","english":"wrap one's head / mind /brain around","ipa":"","chinese":"（对不熟悉或复杂问题的）理解、弄清楚”","usage":"I know that I'm leaving a lot out here, and that, especially this last tip is kind of hard to wrap your brain around.  \n我知道我这里省略了好多东西，特别是最后一点，很难让你让你们掌握。"}]},{"day":108,"title":"英语积累Day 108","topic":"生活方式","author":"Meadows & Mountain","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/515ed275aac243b1aa2cf22e72e9bcdf","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-a6u-1j5W9M","audioSize":"408.8KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-108.m4a","youtubeId":"-a6u-1j5W9M","chinese":"上周初天气转变，整个星期都很冷、潮湿且阴沉。这种天气变化严重影响了我的情绪，也拖慢了我的工作效率。但今天，我要扭转局面，确保下周能大大好转。所以我们今天要花一天处理完上周堆积起来的事情，比如洗衣和打扫。每当我情绪低落时，制定一个计划对我很有帮助。","english":"The weather took a turn at the beginning of last week, and it's been cold, wet, and gloomy all week. This change in weather has put a serious damper on my mood, and it's really taking a toll on my productivity as well. But today, I want to steer the ship around and make sure that next week will be a whole lot better. So, we're gonna spend the day getting some things done that I have left piled up over the week, such as laundry and cleaning. Anytime I'm in a slump, it really helps me to make a plan.","sentences":["The weather took a turn at the beginning of last week, and it's been cold, wet, and gloomy all week.","This change in weather has put a serious damper on my mood, and it's really taking a toll on my productivity as well.","But today, I want to steer the ship around and make sure that next week will be a whole lot better.","So, we're gonna spend the day getting some things done that I have left piled up over the week, such as laundry and cleaning.","Anytime I'm in a slump, it really helps me to make a plan."],"exercise":"The weather 转变 at the beginning of last week, and it's been cold, wet, and 阴沉 all week. This change in weather has 严重影响 my mood, and it's really 拖慢 on my productivity as well. But today, I want to 扭转局面 and make sure that next week will 大大好转. So, we're gonna spend the day getting some things done that I have left 堆积 over the week, such as laundry and cleaning. Anytime I'm 情绪低落, it really helps me to make a plan.","vocabulary":[{"id":"8777b1e9-9bc8-41f5-8bc6-a44bd52f03dd","english":"take a turn","ipa":"","chinese":"发生某种变化；转变(转机；变更)；","usage":"The scandal took a new turn over the weekend. 周末时丑闻有了新的发展。"},{"id":"f4ca934c-e09d-491f-b238-bd985cd6d47c","english":"gloomy","ipa":"/ˈɡluːmi/","chinese":"a. 阴暗的；幽暗的","usage":"1. a gloomy room/atmosphere\n昏暗的房间；阴沉沉的气氛\n2. It was a wet and gloomy day.\n那一天下着雨，阴沉沉的。"},{"id":"10feecfd-b6e4-44ba-87f7-6b4be28cf587","english":"put a damper on sth","ipa":"/'dæmpə/","chinese":"抑制；使扫兴；使沮丧","usage":"The cold weather put a damper on our plans\n寒冷的天气给我们的计划泼了冷水。"},{"id":"a757f241-9c7b-46e7-af76-909328ba1f6e","english":"take a toll","ipa":"","chinese":"描述某种负面影响或损害对某人、某事物或某群体产生的影响。","usage":"The stressful job began to take a toll on her mental well-being.\n紧张的工作对她的心理健康产生了负面影响"},{"id":"08864466-2863-4012-aee3-59c0f578dd2c","english":"steer","ipa":"/stɪə(r)/","chinese":"v. 驾驶（船、汽车等）；掌方向盘","usage":"He steered the boat into the harbour.\n他把船开进港。"},{"id":"145181c8-f949-4ed2-89b1-6675d58fe479","english":"be a whole lot","ipa":"","chinese":"非常，很","usage":"Whole 是形容词，意为“整体的，全部的”等，它只作前置定语，此时可以在 a lot of 中加 whole 来表示“许许多多，大量”，相当于 a large amount/ number of；a lot 还可以作副词，修饰动词、形容词或副词，意为“非常，很”，相当于作副词的 much，因此 a whole lot 也有类似的用法，也意为“非常，很”\nThings were about to get a whole lot worse.\n事情会变得更糟。"},{"id":"73009de3-d366-4125-9943-f3f2e28aecbc","english":"pile up","ipa":"","chinese":"堆积；积压","usage":"Work always piles up at the end of the year.\n年底总是积压一大堆工作。"},{"id":"44197a94-f00a-4a98-a217-81bc1f99bc6b","english":"in a slump","ipa":"/slʌmp/","chinese":"处于低迷期，状态不佳","usage":"She is in a slump in her career.\n她处在事业的低谷。"}]},{"day":109,"title":"英语积累Day 109","topic":"生活方式","author":"Meadows & Mountain","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/4fc61ecfc4b9434cb9fbce50c048e746","originalVideoUrl":"https://youtu.be/-a6u-1j5W9M?si=oY-3XFKhiG-J3OzX","audioSize":"361.4KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-109.m4a","youtubeId":"-a6u-1j5W9M","chinese":"当我感觉精力不足时，运动往往是最不想做的事情。但其实运动是摆脱低迷状态的有力工具。因为运动会触发内啡肽的释放，内啡肽也被称为 “快乐荷尔蒙”。虽然这似乎有悖直觉，但运动实际上可以提升精力，因为它可以增强心脏功能，提升耐力，并改善睡眠质量。","english":"When I'm feeling low in energy, moving my body is often the last thing I want to do. But working out can actually be a powerful tool to get you out of a rut because exercise triggers the release of endorphins, also known as feel-good hormones. Even though this might seem counterintuitive, exercise can actually increase your energy because it strengthens your heart, increases your endurance, and improves the quality of your sleep.","sentences":["When I'm feeling low in energy, moving my body is often the last thing I want to do.","But working out can actually be a powerful tool to get you out of a rut because exercise triggers the release of endorphins, also known as feel-good hormones.","Even though this might seem counterintuitive, exercise can actually increase your energy because it strengthens your heart, increases your endurance, and improves the quality of your sleep."],"exercise":"When I'm feeling 精力不足, moving my body is often the last thing I want to do. But working out can actually be a powerful tool to 摆脱低迷状态 because exercise 触发内啡肽的释放, also known as 快乐荷尔蒙. Even though this might seem 有悖直觉, exercise can actually increase your energy because it strengthens your heart, 提升耐力, and improves the quality of your sleep.","vocabulary":[{"id":"04aa91b0-86a4-4411-abc2-88877fbe1561","english":"get out of a rut","ipa":"","chinese":"逃离单调的无聊的工作轨道或生活轨道","usage":"In order to get out of a rut, you should do new things.  \n为了摆脱枯燥乏味，你应该做新的东西。"},{"id":"37ff6053-dd64-4cc4-8861-f560979f89a3","english":"trigger","ipa":"/'trɪgɚ/","chinese":"v. 发动；引起；触发","usage":"Nuts can trigger off a violent allergic reaction.\n坚果可以引起严重的过敏反应。"},{"id":"f5b2c661-a76f-4e7b-9d9f-d51c15f1d664","english":"endorphin","ipa":"/enˈdɔːfɪn/","chinese":"内啡肽（内分泌激素，有镇痛作用）","usage":"Get some exercise, which is a major source of endorphins!\n做些运动，运动是内啡肽的重要来源！"},{"id":"2727b13c-3267-4d80-a7a6-7bf2d924771d","english":"feel-good","ipa":"","chinese":"a. 使人愉悦的","usage":"a feel-good movie\n令人愉悦的电影"},{"id":"d257a690-2a25-4031-8ad4-533ada8f0c22","english":"counterintuitive","ipa":"/ˌkaʊntərɪn'tjuːɪtɪv/","chinese":"a.  反直觉的；与正常预期相反的","usage":"These results seem counter-intuitive.\n这些结果似乎与预料的相反。"},{"id":"3d545135-ea3a-4fbd-911e-f3da216139c4","english":"endurance","ipa":"/ɪnˈdjʊərəns/","chinese":"n. 忍耐力；耐久力","usage":"He showed remarkable endurance throughout his illness.\n他在整个生病期间表现出非凡的忍耐力。"}]},{"day":110,"title":"英语积累Day 110","topic":"生活方式","author":"Holly B Fitness","accent":"英音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/f7c45611a4c74fc598b11838e47a8f79","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H3hjvvuGm54","audioSize":"479.9KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-110.m4a","youtubeId":"H3hjvvuGm54","chinese":"我有好几次在跑步的时候，虽然人已经外出跑步了，但大脑完全不在状态。感觉就像身体在跑，但脑子却在另一个频道上。所以我在这个过程中总结出来了几个小技巧和窍门，当我有这种感觉时，它们能让我坚持下去。首先是准备一个好听的歌单。选一些你熟悉的歌曲做成歌单，在脑海中哼唱，跟着音乐放空自己是分散注意力的好方法。我还喜欢想出三句激励自己的话或者是显化的语句，反复在心里默念。","english":"I've been on so many runs where I've got out and my head is just not in it. It's almost like my body is going but my brain is like on a completely different wavelength. So I just have a few little tips and tricks that I've kind of picked up along the way that keep me going when I do feel like that. So one is having a really good playlist. Make a playlist with songs that you know, singing along in your head and zoning out to them is a really good way to kind of distract yourself. I also like to think of three kind of motivational sentences or almost like manifestations I kind of chant to myself over and over again.","sentences":["I've been on so many runs where I've got out and my head is just not in it.","It's almost like my body is going but my brain is like on a completely different wavelength.","So I just have a few little tips and tricks that I've kind of picked up along the way that keep me going when I do feel like that.","So one is having a really good playlist.","Make a playlist with songs that you know, singing along in your head and zoning out to them is a really good way to kind of distract yourself.","I also like to think of three kind of motivational sentences or almost like manifestations I kind of chant to myself over and over again."],"exercise":"I've been on so many runs where I've 外出跑步 and 大脑完全不在状态. It's almost like my body is going but 脑子却在另一个频道上. So I just have a few little 小技巧和窍门 that I've kind of 在这个过程中总结出来 that keep me going when I do feel like that. So one is having a really good 歌单. Make a playlist with songs that you know, singing along in your head and 跟着音乐放空自己 is a really good way to kind of 分散注意力 yourself. I also like to think of three kind of 激励自己的话 or almost like 显化的语句 I kind of 反复在心里默念。","vocabulary":[{"id":"fc712cb5-5499-4333-9965-e55a13e19cc8","english":"be on the same wavelength | be on sb's wavelength","ipa":"/'weɪvleŋθ/","chinese":"具有（与他人）相同的思路；合拍；与 … 所见略同","usage":"when we met we hit it off immediately—we're on the same wavelength .\n我们见面时很快就相处得很好——我们志趣相同。"},{"id":"c47a924c-4170-4918-b375-8d627a7950b4","english":"tips and tricks","ipa":"","chinese":"技巧和窍门","usage":"It is not just a little trick you can pick up in half an hour.\n这不是你半个小时就能学会的小窍门。"},{"id":"81eada56-fa7e-4765-a641-985c85e23966","english":"trick","ipa":"/trɪk/","chinese":"n. 窍门;诀窍;技巧","usage":""},{"id":"cc22f53b-f227-4e1d-b033-107264c7d70d","english":"pick up","ipa":"","chinese":"（偶然）得到，听到，学会","usage":"Here's a tip I picked up from my mother.\n告诉你一个窍门，是我从妈妈那里学来的。"},{"id":"327b1d8c-7012-41cd-b4d5-5be8c149a9ec","english":"playlist","ipa":"/ˈpleɪlɪst/","chinese":"n. （电台节目的）音乐播放清单","usage":"Sotify delivers a personalized playlist of 30 new songs every Monday to its users.\nSpotify \n每周一都会向用户提供包含 30 首新歌的个性化播放列表。"},{"id":"295b8eec-3dd7-4b11-8a11-ebfe86b32c1f","english":"zone out","ipa":"","chinese":"失去知觉；走神","usage":"Instinct is also at work on those occasions when people have completely zoned out.\n当人们完全思想游离的时候，本能也在起作用。"},{"id":"46e2f598-b9b9-4e6c-b27b-93e28738db54","english":"distract","ipa":"/dɪˈstrækt/","chinese":"v.  转移（注意力）；分散（思想）；使分心","usage":"It was another attempt to distract attention from the truth.\n这又是企图分散人们对事实真相的注意力。"},{"id":"e5711fc2-6acc-4726-9ca5-533e88228e33","english":"motivational","ipa":"/ˌməuti'veiʃənəl/","chinese":"a. 动机的；激发性的；","usage":"I'm not really a motivational words kind of gal.\n我并不是那种喜欢说激励性话语的人。"},{"id":"24bd6873-cfdc-48dc-8fcd-af1954cb907e","english":"manifestation","ipa":"/ˌmænɪfeˈsteɪʃn/","chinese":"n. 显化：精神疗愈领域用词，指通过意念将想要的东西带进你的生命中来。这个强大的心理工具有助于实现内心深处的愿景，将内心所想转化为现实。","usage":""},{"id":"d7c50231-c0c6-4e0d-a703-78dc93d5571e","english":"chant","ipa":"/tʃɑːnt/","chinese":"v. 反复唱；反复呼喊","usage":"The crowd chanted their hero's name.\n人群不断地呼唤着自己英雄的名字。"}]},{"day":111,"title":"英语积累Day 111","topic":"生活方式","author":"Zeliha Akpinar","accent":"英音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/9f44b200d2444693b85f63fe1de15d21","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UwVwDOkZV4s","audioSize":"351.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-111.m4a","youtubeId":"UwVwDOkZV4s","chinese":"我的通勤时间包括坐火车和步行回家，总共要花半个小时。这段时间足够我听几段医学院的语音笔记或者追一期播客。有意思的是，在通勤期间，我会强烈感觉自己应该明智地利用这段时间。可能因为知道，相比于那些不用每天通勤的人，我已经处于劣势，所以我会努力做一些对自己有益处的事情。","english":"My journey, including the 坐火车 and walk back home, takes half an hour. It's enough time to listen to a few Medical School 语音笔记 or 追一期播客. Interestingly, 在通勤期间 , I 强烈感觉自己应该 明智地利用这段时间. Maybe it's because I know I'm already 处于劣势（相比于） people who doesn’t need to travel daily to work or school, so I make an effort to do 一些对自己有益处的事情.","sentences":["My journey, including the 坐火车 and walk back home, takes half an hour.","It's enough time to listen to a few Medical School 语音笔记 or 追一期播客.","Interestingly, 在通勤期间 , I 强烈感觉自己应该 明智地利用这段时间.","Maybe it's because I know I'm already 处于劣势（相比于） people who doesn’t need to travel daily to work or school, so I make an effort to do 一些对自己有益处的事情."],"exercise":"My journey, including the 坐火车 and walk back home, takes half an hour. It's enough time to listen to a few Medical School 语音笔记 or 追一期播客. Interestingly, 在通勤期间 , I 强烈感觉自己应该 明智地利用这段时间. Maybe it's because I know I'm already 处于劣势（相比于） people who doesn’t need to travel daily to work or school, so I make an effort to do 一些对自己有益处的事情.","vocabulary":[{"id":"f7258c5f-3d5e-4417-b0a8-9e381180c384","english":"train ride","ipa":"","chinese":"坐火车","usage":"The idea for Harry Potter came to her in 1990 during a train ride. \n1990年，在一次火车旅行中，她产生了创作《哈利·波特》的想法。"},{"id":"c1e82d4a-1526-45ac-9414-72e703e9c51b","english":"voice note","ipa":"","chinese":"语音笔记","usage":"We'll be playing some of your voice notes on the show.\n我们将在节目中播放您的一些语音笔记。"},{"id":"6c105fde-2552-4b97-8b04-c4f915fc0ea0","english":"catch up on","ipa":"","chinese":"补做（未做的事）；赶做；补上","usage":"I have a lot of work to catch up on.\n我有许多工作要补做。"},{"id":"ab9b4f32-e40a-49d4-8770-bdbf2d0591a5","english":"commute","ipa":"/kəˈmjuːt/","chinese":"n. 上下班路程\nv. （乘公共汽车、火车、汽车等）上下班往返，经常往返（于两地）","usage":"1. I have only a short commute to work.我上班的路程很短。\n2. She commutes from Oxford to London every day. 她每天上下班往返于牛津与伦敦之间。"},{"id":"8f12b5c9-672e-48d0-9c73-da151bdaba75","english":"sense of…","ipa":"","chinese":"…的感觉","usage":"sense of humour幽默感\nsense of security安全感\nsense of belonging归属感\nsense of accomplishment成就感\nsense of failure挫败感\nsense of self-doubt自我怀疑感\nsense of social responsibility社会责任感"},{"id":"c0901b94-2cab-4902-bf80-3d6f2df39675","english":"wisely","ipa":"/'waizli/","chinese":"adv. 明智地","usage":"He wisely decided to tell the truth.\n他明智地决定实话实说。"},{"id":"15573ec2-0f63-4c6b-9229-4437fa758c73","english":"disadvantaged","ipa":"/dɪsəd'vɑːntɪdʒd/","chinese":"a. 处于不利地位的；","usage":"Children living in inner-city areas may be educationally disadvantaged.  \n居住在市中心贫民区的孩子在教育方面可能处于不利的地位。"},{"id":"b03c5669-5537-4aff-afa2-db8827b42123","english":"against","ipa":"","chinese":"prep. 反对；与 … 相反","usage":"She was forced to marry against her will. 她被迫违背自己的心愿嫁了人。"},{"id":"903d186b-3b3e-4970-beef-4c2d1437bddb","english":"make an effort to","ipa":"","chinese":"努力做某事","usage":"He made an effort to collect himself.\n他挣扎着想使自己平静下来。"},{"id":"fc6dc07a-e1b8-49ed-8276-a4346dbd6e16","english":"beneficial","ipa":"/ˌbenɪˈfɪʃl/","chinese":"a. 有利的；有帮助的；有用的","usage":"A good diet is beneficial to health.\n良好的饮食有益于健康。"}]},{"day":112,"title":"英语积累Day 112","topic":"生活方式","author":"Zeliha Akpinar","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/90bde0522b59485a8e93e986cfce6b0f","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UwVwDOkZV4s","audioSize":"307.4KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-112.m4a","youtubeId":"UwVwDOkZV4s","chinese":"坦白说，我一走进卧室，本能反应就是躺在床上休息。但我一直在努力把它转变为对自己的提醒，让自己迅速打开书包，并清理干净书包和口袋里的垃圾。当我摒弃不良习惯，一进房间就立刻做一些有益的事情时，会给我带来积极的动力，让我更容易完成晚上剩余的任务。","english":"Honestly, my first instinct when I come to my room is to lie on my bed, but I've been trying to turn that instinct into a reminder to quickly unpack and clean out any rubbish in my bag or pockets. When I skip unhelpful habits and do something good as soon as I get into my room, it sets a positive momentum and makes it easier for me to tackle the rest of my evening tasks.","sentences":["Honestly, my first instinct when I come to my room is to lie on my bed, but I've been trying to turn that instinct into a reminder to quickly unpack and clean out any rubbish in my bag or pockets.","When I skip unhelpful habits and do something good as soon as I get into my room, it sets a positive momentum and makes it easier for me to tackle the rest of my evening tasks."],"exercise":"","vocabulary":[{"id":"70340599-1878-4d16-a27d-1562443070cd","english":"first instinct","ipa":"/ˈɪnstɪŋkt/","chinese":"本能","usage":"His first instinct was to run away. \n他的本能反应就是逃跑。"},{"id":"71d7db79-b09a-43bb-9106-7d26957b0426","english":"turn sb/sth (from sth) ˈinto sth","ipa":"","chinese":"使（从 … ）变成","usage":"The prince was turned into a frog by the witch.\n王子被女巫变成了一只青蛙"},{"id":"f1b8db19-3805-469d-a9d0-829cd2e2b633","english":"skip","ipa":"/skɪp/","chinese":"v. 跳过（正常的步骤等）；略过；漏过","usage":"You can skip the next chapter if you have covered the topic in class.\n下一章，你要是在课堂上已经讲到了，就可以跳过。"},{"id":"765d7d46-36ff-4c06-b2e3-0e22b48f1d07","english":"momentum","ipa":"/məˈmentəm/","chinese":"n. 推进力；动力；势头","usage":"The fight for his release gathers momentum each day.\n争取使他获释的斗争声势日益加强。"},{"id":"c96ec395-fca4-4f8c-952e-1bf61fc95903","english":"tackle","ipa":"/ˈtækl/","chinese":"v. 应付，处理，解决（难题或局面）","usage":"The government is determined to tackle inflation.\n政府决心解决通货膨胀问题。"}]},{"day":113,"title":"英语积累Day 113","topic":"生活方式","author":"simply by christine","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/4b736eb6d7144b719057d8147dc33220","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AEt6Sw3Hyi4","audioSize":"667.3KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-113.m4a","youtubeId":"AEt6Sw3Hyi4","chinese":"拥有更多物质并不等同于幸福。我曾花费大量时间网购新衣服和新产品，而要想找到下一个最好的商品会耗费许多精力。但当我冷静下来思考时，很快就意识到，其实我什么都不缺。这种思维习惯就像肌肉需要不断锻炼培养，我会尽量在购物时有意识地展开思考，而不是一时冲动而情绪化购物。当我真的需要买东西的时候，我会尽量选择二手商品，如果需要购买全新的，我会选择质量更高或可持续生产的商品。虽然会比价格低廉、批量生产的商品成本更高，但与之前的消费习惯相比，我认为自己还是节省了不少。","english":"More stuff doesn't equate to happiness. I used to spend lots of time looking online for new clothing or products to purchase, and it took a lot of energy to find that next best thing. But when I took a step back, it didn't take long to admit that I have everything I need. Doing so is a mental muscle I need to continue to exercise, but I do my best to consciously think through purchases instead of buying things on impulse and pure emotion. When I do buy something, I do my best to purchase products secondhand, or if I buy new, I try to look for products that are higher quality or sustainably made. While they do cost more than cheaply mass manufactured goods, I would say that I am saving quite a bit compared to my previous spending habits.","sentences":["More stuff doesn't equate to happiness.","I used to spend lots of time looking online for new clothing or products to purchase, and it took a lot of energy to find that next best thing.","But when I took a step back, it didn't take long to admit that I have everything I need.","Doing so is a mental muscle I need to continue to exercise, but I do my best to consciously think through purchases instead of buying things on impulse and pure emotion.","When I do buy something, I do my best to purchase products secondhand, or if I buy new, I try to look for products that are higher quality or sustainably made.","While they do cost more than cheaply mass manufactured goods, I would say that I am saving quite a bit compared to my previous spending habits."],"exercise":"拥有更多物质并不等同于幸福. I used to spend lots of time looking online for new clothing or products to purchase, and 耗费许多精力 find that next best thing. But when I 冷静下来思考时, it didn't take long to admit that I have everything I need. Doing so is a 思维习惯就像肌肉 I need to continue to exercise, but I do my best to 在购物时有意识地展开思考 instead of buying things 一时冲动 and 情绪化(购物). When I do buy something, I do my best to purchase products 二手, or if I buy new, I try to look for products that are higher quality or 可持续生产的. 虽然 they do cost more than cheaply 批量生产的 goods, I would say that I am saving quite a bit compared to my previous spending habits.","vocabulary":[{"id":"65a6f551-65cb-4f58-902d-6a204bc5ad82","english":"equate to sth","ipa":"/iˈkweɪt/","chinese":"相当于；等于","usage":"To sum up, I think a higher education doesn't always equate to a better career.\n总而言之，我认为更高等的教育并不总是等同于更好的职业生涯。"},{"id":"fb13db23-c53f-46c9-b9af-71c17c89266f","english":"It takes sb. time / money / energy to do sth.","ipa":"","chinese":"某人花时间或精力做某事","usage":"It takes a lot of energy to listen to another person and enter sympathetically into their experiences.\n倾听他人得耗费极大的心力并怜悯地设身处地着想。"},{"id":"f110e1a0-2379-460c-b6a4-c339b11ce83c","english":"take a step back","ipa":"","chinese":"退一步（讲/看）；停下来思考，试图从不同的角度来看待问题。","usage":"If you feel stressed by responsibilities at work, you should take a step back and identify those of greater and less importance.   如果你因为工作中的职责而感到有压力，你应该停下来思考，确认什么事情更重要，而什么事情不那么重要。"},{"id":"61269db0-77bb-4722-a65b-121eea034067","english":"mental muscle","ipa":"/ˈmentl/  /ˈmʌsl/","chinese":"心理肌肉","usage":"心理学家Jim Taylor在研究体育运动员的过程中发现，虽然身体上的肌肉力量对于运动员的表现至关重要，但运动员的自信水平、注意力集中的程度等等，同样会影响表现。因此他提出了“心理肌肉”（Mental Muscle）理论，认为自信、专注力等特质是每个人身上都有的“心理肌肉”，我们可以像锻炼身体上的肌肉一样，通过训练来加强我们的自信。"},{"id":"4d85c317-fe3a-469a-a3b0-8e65e78476af","english":"consciously","ipa":"/ˈk ɔnʃəslɪ/","chinese":"adv.  有意识地","usage":"She realized how tense she was and consciously relaxed.\n她发觉自己很紧张，于是有意识地放松了一下。"},{"id":"acd474d5-cb76-4032-ab37-e84752f752c3","english":"think through","ipa":"","chinese":"充分考虑；全盘考虑；想透","usage":"I didn't think through the consequences of promotion.  \n我没有充分考虑到晋升带来的各种结果。"},{"id":"b8958322-598e-4ec4-a91e-1deab0d3ea9b","english":"on impulse","ipa":"/ˈɪmpʌls/","chinese":"一时兴起，心血来潮","usage":"On impulse, I picked up the phone and rang her.  \n一时心血来潮，我拿起电话给她打了过去。"},{"id":"267a0685-f439-4cd2-a7ef-e3a65a3f994f","english":"pure","ipa":"/pjʊə(r)/","chinese":"a. 完全的；纯粹的","usage":"She laughed with pure joy.\n她由衷地笑起来。"},{"id":"bf693566-0e48-4ce8-b191-16d6fe6c1c87","english":"secondhand","ipa":"/ˈsekəndˈhænd/","chinese":"a. 旧的；用过的；二手的","usage":"I bought a secondhand chair which is as good as new.\n我买了一把二手货椅子,它如同新的一样。"},{"id":"12e8d551-56bd-4a33-b9c8-2753d2041db4","english":"sustainably","ipa":"/səˈsteɪnəbl/","chinese":"a. 可持续的","usage":"The aim is to keep visits sustainable and access fair.\n目的是保持参观的可持续性和公平准入"},{"id":"2622ca48-6fca-4dc0-aae1-9970cee85fa7","english":"while","ipa":"/wail/","chinese":"conj. （用作句首）虽然；尽管","usage":"While I am willing to help, I do not have much time available.\n尽管我愿意帮忙，但是没有多少时间。"},{"id":"6061937f-f4a1-4287-8441-108ed83ab462","english":"mass manufacture/production","ipa":"/ˌmænjuˈfæktʃə(r)/","chinese":"大量生产；大量制造","usage":"In the mass production era, multinational firms tended to centralize their operations.  \n在大规模生产时期，跨国公司倾向于集中运营。"}]},{"day":114,"title":"英语积累Day 114","topic":"情感成长,生活方式","author":"TheCottageFairy","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/6597b2c5d6564311b497654bec24359e","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AhPGS0RCn6Y","audioSize":"714.6KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-114.m4a","youtubeId":"AhPGS0RCn6Y","chinese":"上大学时我非常争强好胜，一心追求财富。我把财富和随心所欲的自由生活联系在一起。然而讽刺的是，尽管我努力工作，既没有赚到很多钱，也没有实现我的梦想。结果就是，我一直活在对未来的憧憬中。而日复一日的生活就像一个奇怪而无意义的循环，没有尽头。搬到这里后，我用了很长时间才走出迷雾，真正睁开眼睛，欣赏到周围环境的奇妙和美丽。这是一个回归内在灵魂的过程。","english":"I was a very competitive university student, and I was addicted to the pursuit of wealth. I connected wealth to freedom to live how I wanted. And the irony of it was that neither was I making much money, even though I was working hard, but I was also not living my dream. And consequently, I was constantly living in the future. Day-to-day life felt like a strange, meaningless cycle in which there was no end. After moving here, it took quite a long time to pull myself out of the haze and to really open my eyes and appreciate the wonder and beauty of where I lived. It was a process of coming home to my inner spirit.","sentences":["I was a very competitive university student, and I was addicted to the pursuit of wealth.","I connected wealth to freedom to live how I wanted.","And the irony of it was that neither was I making much money, even though I was working hard, but I was also not living my dream.","And consequently, I was constantly living in the future.","Day-to-day life felt like a strange, meaningless cycle in which there was no end.","After moving here, it took quite a long time to pull myself out of the haze and to really open my eyes and appreciate the wonder and beauty of where I lived.","It was a process of coming home to my inner spirit."],"exercise":"I was a very 争强好胜 university student, and 一心追求财富. I 把财富和随心所欲的自由生活联系在一起. And 讽刺的是 neither was I making much money, even though I was working hard, but I was also not 实现我的梦想. And 结果就是, I was 一直活在对未来的憧憬中. 日复一日的生活就像一个奇怪而无意义的循环 in which there was no end. After moving here, it took quite a long time to 走出迷雾 and to really open my eyes and appreciate the wonder and beauty of where I lived. It was 回归内在灵魂的过程。","vocabulary":[{"id":"008c05cb-5025-47f3-b066-8ccc4915ab4a","english":"competitive","ipa":"/kəmˈpetətɪv/","chinese":"a. 努力竞争的；一心求胜的","usage":"You have to be highly competitive to do well in sport these days.\n如今你必须有强烈的竞争意识才能在体育运动中取得好成绩。"},{"id":"7493c24a-8a3f-4cea-85dc-5e168b72f71a","english":"be addicted to","ipa":"/əˈdɪktɪd/","chinese":"沉溺于","usage":"More net users means more chances to be addicted to the Internet.  \n网络使用者越多，网络成瘾的机会越大。"},{"id":"2aaf8de1-f11f-4bb2-ba55-ad92ca0fb0ba","english":"pursuit","ipa":"/pəˈsjuːt/","chinese":"n.  追求；寻找","usage":"1. the pursuit of happiness/knowledge\n对幸福/知识的追求\n2. She travelled the world in pursuit of her dreams.\n她走遍天下，追寻她的梦想。"},{"id":"1593371c-52b0-4e49-9135-c01903ebb12c","english":"irony","ipa":"/ˈaɪrəni/","chinese":"n. 出乎意料的）奇异可笑之处；有讽刺意味的情况","usage":"The irony is that when he finally got the job, he discovered he didn't like it.\n讽刺的是，当他最终得到那份工作时，他发现自己并不喜欢它。"},{"id":"cc9e49b4-8743-4b99-a2bd-664c18f2f3e1","english":"live one's dream","ipa":"","chinese":"实现梦想：追求并实现自己的梦想或理想生活。","usage":"But I was stressing, but I did end up get a record contract and yeah, as I said I'm living my dream.\n但我压力很大， 但我最终还是得到了一份唱片合同，是的，正如我所说， 我正在实现我的梦想。"},{"id":"d20b1930-b498-4f5d-a52e-37906f1d59a7","english":"consequently","ipa":"/ˈkɒnsɪkwəntli/","chinese":"adv. 因此；所以\n＝ As a consequence","usage":"This poses a threat to agriculture and the food chain, and consequently to human health.\n这会对农业和食物链造成威胁，由此而危及人的健康。"},{"id":"f5fd2afa-09e1-4097-80c5-34e2e674d558","english":"constantly","ipa":"/ˈk ɔnstəntlɪ/","chinese":"adv. 始终；一直；重复不断地","usage":"1. Fashion is constantly changing.\n时尚总是日新月异。\n2. Heat the sauce, stirring constantly.\n加热调味汁并不停地搅动。"},{"id":"1bf36332-a2ed-434c-a0cf-fd15a35339dc","english":"day-to-day","ipa":"/'deitə'dei/","chinese":"只用在名词前\na.  按日计划的；逐日的；每天的","usage":"I have organized the cleaning on a day-to-day basis, until our usual cleaner returns.\n我已逐日安排好清洁工作，直到我们的清洁工回来为止。"},{"id":"7e877ace-5570-4954-8490-128b646fc06a","english":"cycle","ipa":"/ˈsaɪkl/","chinese":"n. 循环","usage":"The World's Health Organization calls it a vicious cycle.\n世界卫生组织称其为恶性循环。"},{"id":"2d12485b-16e2-4233-b955-7a9a7722afc4","english":"pull (oneself/a part of body)","ipa":"/pʊl/","chinese":"v. 挣脱；移开；抽出","usage":"Hughes pulled himself slowly to his feet.\n休斯慢慢站了起来。"},{"id":"2d248139-5fd6-44f8-ba42-87dba8250898","english":"pull out of","ipa":"","chinese":"退出；拉出，取出","usage":"France was going to pull out of NATO.  法国准备退出北大西洋公约组织。"},{"id":"6af3f245-7345-4092-8df6-c4d126b146c4","english":"haze","ipa":"/heɪz/","chinese":"n. 阴霾、雾霭; 迷糊、懵懂","usage":"1. They vanished /'væniʃd/ into the haze near the horizon /həˈraɪzn/.\n他们消失在天边的雾霭中。\n2. His mind was a haze of fear and confusion.\n由于害怕和困惑，他当时处于一种混沌状态。"},{"id":"e78f04be-0d48-44b8-b8ca-ef437f39c196","english":"inner","ipa":"/ˈɪnə(r)/","chinese":"a. 内部的;里面的;内心的","usage":"Loving relationships will give a child an inner sense of security.\n亲昵关系会给予孩子内心一种安全感。"},{"id":"37bf8a45-cf93-4bcb-b69d-f1cfbe798dd8","english":"spirit","ipa":"/'spɪrɪt/","chinese":"n. 精神;心灵;灵魂","usage":"Marian retains a restless, youthful spirit, in search of new horizons.\n玛丽安怀着一颗年轻、不断进取的心去寻求新的天地。"}]},{"day":115,"title":"英语积累Day 115","topic":"生活方式","author":"Malama Life","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/ee1d3fafe08a436fbcd1a93eb5618c0e","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=adYxEtp-pkM","audioSize":"612.4KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-115.m4a","youtubeId":"adYxEtp-pkM","chinese":"你知道吗？美国人平均每天会看大约4000到10000个广告。我觉得大多数人对此已经习以为常，甚至注意不到它们的存在，但这并不意味着我们没有一直暴露在广告的影响下。每当我们刷手机、看电影、出门，算法都会根据我们的兴趣，推送个性化广告。难怪我们会忍不住在一些根本不需要的东西上挥霍钱。最近这种感觉尤其强烈，特别是在衣服、护肤品和化妆品方面，因为我猜测我正好是这个市场的目标受众。","english":"Did you know that the average American sees around 4,000 to 10,000 ads each day? I think most of us have become so used to it that we don't even notice it anymore. That doesn't mean that we're not exposed to it all the time. Every time we scroll on our phones, watch a movie, step outside of our houses, and now the algorithm picks up on our interests and personalizes the ads for us. No wonder we feel so tempted to splurge on things that we don't even need. It honestly feels like too much more than ever lately, especially when it comes to clothes, skincare, and makeup, because I guess I am the target audience for this market.","sentences":["Did you know that the average American sees around 4,000 to 10,000 ads each day?","I think most of us have become so used to it that we don't even notice it anymore.","That doesn't mean that we're not exposed to it all the time.","Every time we scroll on our phones, watch a movie, step outside of our houses, and now the algorithm picks up on our interests and personalizes the ads for us.","No wonder we feel so tempted to splurge on things that we don't even need.","It honestly feels like too much more than ever lately, especially when it comes to clothes, skincare, and makeup, because I guess I am the target audience for this market."],"exercise":"Did you know that 美国人平均 sees around 4,000 to 10,000 ads each day? I think most of us 已经习以为常 that we don't even notice it anymore. That doesn't mean that we're not 暴露在广告的影响下 all the time. Every time we 刷手机, watch a movie, step outside of our houses, and now the 算法 根据我们的兴趣，推送个性化广告. No wonder we 忍不住 挥霍钱 things that we don't even need. It honestly feels like too much more than ever lately, especially when it comes to clothes, skincare, and makeup, because I guess I am the 目标受众 for this market.","vocabulary":[{"id":"dde11948-ab23-425b-a103-4f6743c08932","english":"be used to sth/doing","ipa":"","chinese":"习惯于","usage":"1. be used to doing的to是介词，所以后面接名词、代词或者动名词。这里的be也可以用get替换，变成get used to doing。另外，used也可以被替换为accustomed，变成be accustomed to doing。都表示“习惯于做·······”\neg. In the West, many were used to staying home and receiving financial support from the government throughout the pandemic. As a consequence, they are not used to working now. \n在西方，许多人习惯了在疫情期间待在家里得到政府的经济补偿。因此，他们现在不习惯出去工作了。\n2. be used to do这里的to是不定式，所以后面接动词原型。表示“被用来做······”。\neg. Science is supposed to be used to help us to live a better life, but relunctantly, it has been also used to harm us.\n科学应该是用来帮助我们生活得更好，但是不幸的的是，它也一直被用来去伤害我们。"},{"id":"28ec23b4-3ef6-42f6-821e-2964d9932170","english":"be exposed to","ipa":"/ɪkˈspəʊz/","chinese":"暴露于；接触；受到…影响","usage":"1. We should allow children to be exposed to new ideas.\n我们应当让孩子们接触新思想。\n2. exposed themselves to disease; exposed their children to classical music.\n使他们受到疾病的影响；使他们的孩子们受到古典音乐的影响"},{"id":"7274fb6f-1dce-4426-a5e7-f9ee4bf1fb4e","english":"scroll","ipa":"/skrəʊl/","chinese":"v. 滚屏；滚动","usage":"1. scroll on the phone 刷手机\n2. Scroll down to the bottom of the document.\n向下滚动到文件末尾。"},{"id":"78d8152d-2b17-43fc-911d-01f4b2579fd4","english":"algorithm","ipa":"/'ælgərɪð(ə)m/","chinese":"n. 算法；计算程序","usage":"So we use a lot of smart software algorithms.\n所以我们使用了很多智能软件算法。"},{"id":"11860dd4-4818-4a65-806e-fa1ed1573878","english":"pick up on","ipa":"","chinese":"领略，意会，意识到","usage":"I failed to pick up on the humour in his remark.\n我没有领悟到他话中的幽默。"},{"id":"ff5993ec-bde3-4c25-8615-f9abe6b53d0c","english":"personalize","ipa":"/'pɜːs(ə)n(ə)laɪz/","chinese":"v, 为个人特制（或专设）；个性化","usage":"All our courses are personalized to the needs of the individual.\n我们的全部课程都是针对个人需要设计的。"},{"id":"0c4f8e7e-70a7-4b7f-b6f7-28d1a857d76e","english":"feel/be tempted to","ipa":"/tempt/","chinese":"忍不住，憋不住，极想","usage":"He was tempted to smoke during the flight but the warning of the stewardess held him back. 坐飞机飞行的过程中，他忍不住想抽烟，但被空姐的警告让他憋住了。"},{"id":"dd1d1436-7d27-45a2-a327-25bcda3b51ee","english":"tempt","ipa":"/tempt/","chinese":"1. v. 引诱；诱惑\n2. 劝诱；鼓动；怂恿；","usage":"1. I was tempted by the dessert menu.\n甜食菜单馋得我垂涎欲滴。\n2. How can we tempt young people into engineering?\n我们怎么才能吸引年轻人学习工程学呢？"},{"id":"9aea9b71-ddfe-4eb8-afb8-dac09bf6eb07","english":"splurge sth/on sth","ipa":"/splɜːdʒ/","chinese":"乱花钱；糟蹋钱；挥霍","usage":"We'll splurge on a trip in France next year.  \n明年咱们去法国挥霍玩个痛快。"},{"id":"310514a5-6698-4c94-ae9d-059e4e2dbeb9","english":"target audience","ipa":"/ˈtɑːɡɪt/ /ˈɔːdiəns/","chinese":"目标受众：某个事物（通常是广告活动）旨在吸引的主要人群。","usage":"The target audience for this advertisement was mainly teenagers. \n这个广告的对象主要是十几岁的青少年观众。"}]},{"day":116,"title":"英语积累Day 116","topic":"工作职场","author":"Abbey Robins","accent":"英音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/474bbbbe14dd4bac8368de2afa16c5c1","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0CHBRDr4r54","audioSize":"360.7KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-116.m4a","youtubeId":"0CHBRDr4r54","chinese":"工作方面，我刚开始做一个新项目，所以今天不怎么忙。我们目前还没有紧迫的截止日期，但还是要立即展开工作，确保跟上进度，一忙起来能有所准备。在项目期间，每天早上第一件事就是召开“站立会议”，项目团队会一起对齐当天的任务和前一晚传达的任何事宜。","english":"At work, I have just started a new project, and so my day is going to be moderately busy. We don't have any pressing deadlines just yet, however, we are really trying to hit the ground running, make sure we are up to speed and ready to go as soon as the rush begins. When on a project, we have a meeting called stand-up first thing every morning, and this is where the project team get together and we align on our tasks for the day, anything that came through overnight.","sentences":["At work, I have just started a new project, and so my day is going to be moderately busy.","We don't have any pressing deadlines just yet, however, we are really trying to hit the ground running, make sure we are up to speed and ready to go as soon as the rush begins.","When on a project, we have a meeting called stand-up first thing every morning, and this is where the project team get together and we align on our tasks for the day, anything that came through overnight."],"exercise":"At work, I have just started a new project, and so my day is going to be 不怎么忙. We don't have any 紧迫的截止日期 just yet, however, we are really trying to 立即展开工作, make sure we 跟上进度 and ready to go as soon as the 一忙起来 begins. When on a project, we have a meeting called 站立会议 first thing every morning, and this is where the project team get together and we 对齐 for the day, anything that 传达 overnight.","vocabulary":[{"id":"0bed29d2-eac1-469c-96a7-bd62a108d477","english":"moderately","ipa":"/ˈmɒdərətli/","chinese":"adv. 一般地","usage":"1. a moderately successful career\n还算成功的事业\n2. She only did moderately well in the exam.\n她这次考试成绩还好。"},{"id":"1e5cf389-a771-4824-a5c3-dfb9175e479e","english":"pressing","ipa":"/ˈpresɪŋ/","chinese":"a. 紧急的；急迫的","usage":"I'm afraid I have some pressing business to attend to.\n很抱歉，我有些急事需要处理。"},{"id":"08b1fd92-a6d9-405e-8eaf-acb5daf38c94","english":"deadline","ipa":"/ˈdedlaɪn/","chinese":"n. 最后期限；截止日期","usage":"I prefer to work to a deadline.\n我喜欢按规定的期限完成工作。"},{"id":"4c545b96-e7be-481b-af9e-f4319ad2932b","english":"hit the ground running","ipa":"","chinese":"立即开始行动：立即开始并全力以赴进行某项活动或任务","usage":"Boris Johnson will have to hit the ground running.\n鲍里斯必须快速进入角色。"},{"id":"741f4d11-d5c8-4195-a9ff-618cf10d2976","english":"up to speed","ipa":"","chinese":"了解最新情况；跟上形势","usage":"Here to get you up to speed on current events.\n我们会让你足不出户快速知晓天下事。"},{"id":"3f10d910-9b49-4f5c-ad81-f8210470e227","english":"rush","ipa":"/rʌʃ/","chinese":"n. 忙碌；繁忙","usage":"The evening rush was just starting.\n繁忙的夜晚才刚开始。"},{"id":"247dd41e-8462-487a-8f2d-2c731478c9a9","english":"stand-up meeting","ipa":"","chinese":"站会：每天进行的会议旨在在组队成员之间进行状态更新。\n这种会议通常是限定时间的，长度大概在五至十五分钟并且保持站立以提醒与会人员控制会议的时间专注在会议的主题上。","usage":""},{"id":"d0397bbd-9f3c-46f6-abc2-c3cfc8e0ac18","english":"align","ipa":"/əˈlaɪn/","chinese":"v. 使对齐；将某个事物与另一个事物进行比较，以达到一致性","usage":"We need to align our marketing strategy with our business goals. 我们需要将我们的营销策略与我们的业务目标保持一致。"},{"id":"7993c20f-ef9a-49f5-9031-9dda062ad39f","english":"come through","ipa":"","chinese":"1. 传达，传递：指信息或声音成功地被传达或传递\n2.做到，完成：指按照需要或期望做到或完成某事。","usage":"A message is just coming through.\n有消息刚传来。"}]},{"day":117,"title":"英语积累Day 117","topic":"数码产品,兴趣爱好","author":"MaybeHeilly","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/6f77520b1f14497eb80f98d3acde0ee0","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JuL4KLFL76c","audioSize":"520.5KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-117.m4a","youtubeId":"JuL4KLFL76c","chinese":"我是个iPad迷。自从我发现了拆箱游戏、烹饪游戏、家居装饰类游戏，就玩个不停。手指像这样在屏幕上滑动，Apple Pencil到处点，我渐渐上瘾了。我开始陷进iPad游戏无法自拔。不知为何，这些游戏给我带来了不一样的体验。这些是我目前迷上的游戏。这款游戏是让你清理别人的房子，修理各种东西，然后倒卖出去。但最让我欲罢不能的还是披萨游戏。我很爱它的画风，也喜欢经营自己的披萨店。我会尽量多看广告，因为这样会额外给我一些钻石道具。","english":"I'm an iPad adult. Ever since I discovered unpacking games, cooking games, home decor kind of games, yeah, I'm playing. Fingers are moving like this, pencils all over in the air, I'm addicted, little by little. I started going down the rabbit hole of iPad games. For some reason, they hit different. These are the current games that I have a crush on. This is a game that you literally just clean up somebody's house and like fix things and all that kind of stuff and you flip the house. But the game that has me hooked is Pizza. I love the look of it and I love my own pizza shop. As much as I wanna to watch the ad because I'll watch it if you're going to give me some extra diamonds.","sentences":["I'm an iPad adult.","Ever since I discovered unpacking games, cooking games, home decor kind of games, yeah, I'm playing.","Fingers are moving like this, pencils all over in the air, I'm addicted, little by little.","I started going down the rabbit hole of iPad games.","For some reason, they hit different.","These are the current games that I have a crush on.","This is a game that you literally just clean up somebody's house and like fix things and all that kind of stuff and you flip the house.","But the game that has me hooked is Pizza.","I love the look of it and I love my own pizza shop.","As much as I wanna to watch the ad because I'll watch it if you're going to give me some extra diamonds."],"exercise":"I'm an iPad迷. Ever since I discovered 拆箱游戏, cooking games, 家居装饰类游戏, yeah, I'm playing. Fingers are moving like this, Apple Pencil到处点, I'm 上瘾了, little by little. I started 陷进iPad游戏无法自拔. 不知为何 they 给我带来了不一样的体验. These are the current games that 迷上的. This is a game that you literally just clean up somebody's house and like 修理各种东西 and you 倒卖出去. 但最让我欲罢不能的 is Pizza. 我很爱它的画风 and I love my own pizza shop. As much as I wanna to watch the ad because I'll watch it if you're going to 额外给我一些钻石道具.","vocabulary":[{"id":"26b5f87d-c386-4d38-baae-ab297b4a632a","english":"iPad adult","ipa":"","chinese":"沉迷于iPad的成年人，iPad迷；源自英文俚语 iPad kid: A child who is always on a tablet 总是玩平板的小孩","usage":""},{"id":"67376a7b-09e2-49e2-b832-4afba5d1237f","english":"unpacking games","ipa":"","chinese":"拆箱游戏：开箱整理物品类小游戏","usage":""},{"id":"8c93b988-79dc-4b79-a0ee-fa675865eff7","english":"decor","ipa":"/ˈdeɪkɔ:/","chinese":"n. 装饰布局，装饰风格","usage":"1. interior decor\n室内装饰风格\n2. the restaurant's elegant new decor\n餐馆内部别致的新装潢"},{"id":"591d2be7-56f7-4a46-a96c-1eb6ffe32614","english":"addicted","ipa":"/əˈdɪktɪd/","chinese":"a. 上瘾；入迷","usage":"He's addicted to computer games.\n他迷上了电脑游戏。"},{"id":"6fbee717-2b7a-42be-ba51-e08a29724896","english":"go down the rabbit hole","ipa":"","chinese":"陷入新奇、复杂、吸引人的情况\n来源于《爱丽丝梦游仙境》，小女孩儿掉进了兔子洞，进入了奇幻世界","usage":"After watching the first episode of the new series, I was completely hooked and went down the rabbit hole, binge-watching the entire season in one weekend.\n在新剧的第一集之后，我完全被吸引住了，陷入了追剧的漩涡，在一个周末就刷完了整季。"},{"id":"98b9d963-c1dc-4bef-bd1d-9cce7dd956d5","english":"hit different","ipa":"/hɪt/","chinese":"感觉不同；格外触动","usage":"That love song was amazing – it really hits different – it makes me feel a bit sentimental. 那首情歌太棒了——格外触动我，让我有点感伤。"},{"id":"3a013bde-b376-4d53-a454-2a050fc59055","english":"for some reason","ipa":"","chinese":"出于某种原因；\nsome在这里意思是“某个；某些”，强调不确定到底是为什么","usage":"I had a bad night; I went to bed early enough, but for some reason I couldn't fall asleep.\n昨天晚上我没睡好, 上床相当早, 可是不知道为什么睡不着。"},{"id":"80dd0ef7-bfd6-4891-9cb2-284ac3ae8758","english":"have a crush on","ipa":"","chinese":"迷恋","usage":"He has a crush on a girl in our class.\n他暗恋我们班上的一个女生。"},{"id":"794dabd8-b0c0-489f-8ffb-e635ca5c9251","english":"fix","ipa":"/fɪks/","chinese":"v. 修理","usage":"The car won't start — can you fix it?\n这辆车发动不起来了，你能修理一下吗？"},{"id":"9a76dd94-afcb-4581-87e8-be04de229c68","english":"flip the house","ipa":"/flɪp/","chinese":"倒手/转卖房子：通过低买高卖，或者买进来后重新装修再高价卖出","usage":"I am going to take three weeks' vacation and flip this house. 我要休假三个星期，稍微装修一下这个房子然后卖掉。"},{"id":"168962a1-ee59-44e0-b42c-58d56a46d7c1","english":"hook","ipa":"/hʊk/","chinese":"n. 钩子 v. 吸引","usage":"I was hooked by John's radical zeal.\n我被约翰的狂热吸引住了。"},{"id":"b07b0811-13b1-446a-8f40-c24c7759b8a3","english":"extra","ipa":"/ˈekstrə/","chinese":"a. 额外的；","usage":"The conference is going to be a lot of extra work.\n这次会议将有很多额外工作。"}]},{"day":118,"title":"英语积累Day 118","topic":"生活方式","author":"haley<3","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/0f762313151c49c28248949ec261067d","originalVideoUrl":"[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U5e4ZB0jdS](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U5e4ZB0jdSk)","audioSize":"372.0KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-118.m4a","youtubeId":"U5e4ZB0jdSk)","chinese":"带妆过夜容易堵塞毛孔，导致皮肤冒痘，还可能引起皮肤干燥和发炎。洗完澡后要擦身体乳，有助于滋润全身肌肤。每周做一到两次去角质，这样可以去掉让皮肤感觉干燥的死皮。确保每周只做一到两次，因为如果过度去角质会破坏皮肤屏障。","english":"Leaving makeup on overnight clogs your pores and causes breakouts. It can also cause dryness and irritation to your skin. Always apply lotion after a shower. This will help to moisturize all of your skin. Exfoliate your skin one to two times a week. It removes dead skin cells that make your skin feel dry. Make sure you only do this one to two times a week because if you over-exfoliate, it can damage your skin barrier.","sentences":["Leaving makeup on overnight clogs your pores and causes breakouts.","It can also cause dryness and irritation to your skin.","Always apply lotion after a shower.","This will help to moisturize all of your skin.","Exfoliate your skin one to two times a week.","It removes dead skin cells that make your skin feel dry.","Make sure you only do this one to two times a week because if you over-exfoliate, it can damage your skin barrier."],"exercise":"Leaving makeup on overnight 堵塞毛孔 and causes breakouts. It can also cause （皮肤）干燥 and 发炎 to your skin. Always apply 身体乳 after a shower. This will help to 滋润 all of your skin. 去角质 your skin one to two times a week. It removes 死皮 that make your skin feel dry. Make sure you only do this one to two times a week because if you 过度去角质, it can damage your 皮肤屏障.","vocabulary":[{"id":"528ce376-7af0-49a9-828c-da9ee53020db","english":"clog","ipa":"/klɒɡ/","chinese":"v. （使）阻塞，堵塞","usage":"Tears clogged her throat.\n她哽咽了。"},{"id":"223c4939-9a3b-464a-8ef6-aec4712ec607","english":"pore","ipa":"/pɔː/","chinese":"n. （皮肤上的）毛孔","usage":"The pores of your body secrete sweat.\n身上的毛孔分泌汗液。"},{"id":"581fc1af-c8bc-473f-8121-7e839dd32c98","english":"clog pores","ipa":"","chinese":"堵塞毛孔","usage":"The sweat causes dirt to accumulate and clog pores, thus causing acne. \n汗水的原因污垢积累和阻塞毛孔，从而造成痤疮。"},{"id":"16ce3be5-0dc8-40ff-8007-04d794f55fd2","english":"dryness","ipa":"/'draɪnɪs/","chinese":"n. 干燥","usage":"He was advised to spend time in the warmth and dryness of Italy. \n他被建议在意大利的温暖和干燥中过些日子。"},{"id":"d0ca45da-9c28-471c-a1d8-529e45a49668","english":"irritation","ipa":"/ˌɪrɪˈteɪʃn/","chinese":"n.刺激","usage":"a skin irritation\n皮肤发炎"},{"id":"cd9aedc1-8984-4cbc-830a-a23e236f4f0b","english":"lotion","ipa":"/ˈləʊʃn/","chinese":"n. 洁肤液；护肤液；润肤乳","usage":"1. (a) body/hand lotion\n护肤/护手乳液\n2. suntan lotion\n防晒露"},{"id":"03bfe607-c4ec-44af-ad53-348ebea04687","english":"moisturize","ipa":"/ˈmɔɪstʃəˌraɪz/","chinese":"v. 使皮肤湿润","usage":"a product that soothes and moisturizes\n使皮肤柔软湿润的产品"},{"id":"c790c929-1525-4e4d-9b1b-597b0b5d3845","english":"Exfoliate","ipa":"/ɪks'fəʊlɪeɪt/","chinese":"v. 使表皮剥脱","usage":"In a matter of minutes you can completely exfoliate your skin. \n短短几分钟就可以使你的肌肤焕然一新。"},{"id":"42957a3f-3cb5-4531-bbf2-859a3a4b0395","english":"dead skin cell","ipa":"","chinese":"死皮","usage":"The dead skin cells peel off, revealing healthy skin cells underneath.\n死皮细胞脱落，露出健康的皮肤细胞来。"},{"id":"ddad235b-9926-4065-b509-cc8f5b62a487","english":"skin barrier","ipa":"","chinese":"皮肤屏障","usage":"Once that protection is lost, and the integrity of the skin barrier disrupted, skin becomes dry. \n一旦保护层丧失，皮肤的整体屏障就受到破坏，皮肤变干。"}]},{"day":119,"title":"英语积累Day 119","topic":"情感成长","author":"oliSUNvia","accent":"美音","period":"101-150期","sourceUrl":"https://marsh-princess-35f.notion.site/8510ba7925444e76a4669a037c333e35","originalVideoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jcbEiZQ9B7o&t=96s","audioSize":"549.1KB","audioUrl":"audio/day-119.m4a","youtubeId":"jcbEiZQ9B7o","chinese":"我有点反感刷到现在一些有关恋爱关系的帖子。倒不是因为我是个愤世嫉俗的人，或者觉得公开示爱很尴尬。其实我很看重爱情，我认为爱情应该是我们生活中很重要的一部分。但是，网络上广为流传的一些恋爱观点让我感到不适。弗洛姆指出，大多数人都持有一种被动的爱情观。仿佛爱情只是在某处等着我们偶然发现。因此，人们专注于尽可能地让自己更讨人喜欢。我们总是很在意自己是否被爱。","english":"Scrolling through posts about romantic relationships nowadays, I kind of hate it. Not because I'm a cynic or I find PDA to be cringy. In fact, I love love; I think it should be central to the way we live our lives. But there are several beliefs about romantic relationships that I see commonly floating around on the internet that bug me. Fromm notices that most people view love through a passive lens. Love is somehow out there waiting for us to stumble upon, and so people focus on making themselves as lovable as possible. We're always so concerned with being loved.","sentences":["Scrolling through posts about romantic relationships nowadays, I kind of hate it.","Not because I'm a cynic or I find PDA to be cringy.","In fact, I love love; I think it should be central to the way we live our lives.","But there are several beliefs about romantic relationships that I see commonly floating around on the internet that bug me.","Fromm notices that most people view love through a passive lens.","Love is somehow out there waiting for us to stumble upon, and so people focus on making themselves as lovable as possible.","We're always so concerned with being loved."],"exercise":"刷到 帖子 about 恋爱关系 nowadays, I kind of hate it. Not because I'm a 愤世嫉俗的人 or I find 公开示爱 to be 尴尬. In fact, I love love; I think 爱情应该是我们生活中很重要的一部分. But there are several beliefs about romantic relationships that I see commonly 广为流传 on the internet that 让我感到不适. Fromm notices that most people 都持有一种被动的爱情观. Love is 只是在某处 waiting for us to 偶然发现, and so people focus on 尽可能地让自己更讨人喜欢. We're always 很在意 being loved.","vocabulary":[{"id":"af94c2b2-3a46-48b2-afcf-8a5c2c6941c4","english":"scroll through","ipa":"","chinese":"浏览","usage":"Yet I found myself spending that precious time slack-jawed, scrolling through my social media feeds.\n然而，我发现自己把那段宝贵的时间用于发呆，浏览我的社交媒体。"},{"id":"c06ad0b7-8698-4b5d-9f3a-800e086c4fe6","english":"scroll","ipa":"/skrəʊl/","chinese":"v. 滚屏；滚动","usage":"Use the arrow keys to scroll the list of files.\n用箭头键滚动文件目录。"},{"id":"243961b2-c71b-4c28-aa9e-8b4a0ac06973","english":"post","ipa":"/pəʊst/","chinese":"n.（发送到互联网讨论组的）帖子，信息；博文","usage":"The forum does not allow posts from non-members.\n该论坛不允许非会员发帖。"},{"id":"a7d20bae-3f65-4974-855c-1026bfb17767","english":"cynic","ipa":"/ˈsɪnɪk/","chinese":"n. 愤世嫉俗者；悲观者","usage":"1. That's the problem with being a cynic. It blinds you.\n这就是愤青的毛病所在 它蒙蔽了你。\n2. Cynics will say that there is not the slightest chance of success.\n悲观的人会说根本不可能取得成功。"},{"id":"e52e6e7c-4840-4619-87b6-fd156f81953c","english":"PDA","ipa":"","chinese":"网络用语：Public Display of Affection 在公共场合展示亲昵行为","usage":""},{"id":"c03104ce-7044-4d5d-aa2e-dc0c25f49260","english":"cringy","ipa":"","chinese":"指情况尴尬得让人浑身不自在","usage":"This performance is just so cringy.\n这个表演看得我尴尬癌都要犯了。"},{"id":"da797b06-7a76-4dd2-8b0d-78af67159c2b","english":"central","ipa":"/ˈsentrəl/","chinese":"a. 最重要的；首要的；","usage":"She has been a central figure in the campaign.\n她一直是这场运动的主要人物。"},{"id":"34c1784a-a3a4-4595-9aba-84c24e1416ed","english":"float around","ipa":"/fləʊt/","chinese":"（思想等）传播，流传( 通常用于进行时)","usage":"Chances are, rumours and gossip are always floating around your school or community.\n流言和闲话很有可能充满着你的学校或社区。"},{"id":"3e49bc24-7894-4067-b108-dbcc3bafea9c","english":"bug","ipa":"/bʌɡ/","chinese":"v. 使烦恼；使恼怒","usage":"It's something that's been bugging me a lot recently.\n那事使我最近一直大伤脑筋。"},{"id":"551ccd42-3324-4232-af4f-1e5ea0db51b3","english":"view sth through a …lens","ipa":"","chinese":"看待……的角度","usage":"One reason why we should learn a foreign language is that it provides a lens through which to view cultural differences.\n学外语是因为语言能让我们用不同的角度看待文化差异"},{"id":"6ca6455a-59f3-49e9-9d34-bbde4b842450","english":"somehow","ipa":"/ˈsʌmhaʊ/","chinese":"adv. 不知什么缘故;不知怎的","usage":"She somehow got lost.她不知怎的竟迷了路。"},{"id":"ca678c75-afc0-46b9-be63-ea77dd41c998","english":"stumble upon","ipa":"/ˈstʌmbl/","chinese":"意外发现；偶然遇见","usage":"Police have stumbled across a huge drugs ring.\n警方无意中发现一个庞大的贩毒集团。"},{"id":"b8f38467-c098-47d9-9bcf-bebaa7f059e2","english":"be concerned with","ipa":"/kənˈsɜːnd/","chinese":"在意；关心；","usage":"Don't be too concerned with the opinions of others.\n不要太在意别人的意见。"}]}];
